{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/205196-ic-zodiac-beasts","id":205196,"title":"IC Zodiac Beasts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T11:57:24-07:00","id":205196,"title":"IC Zodiac Beasts","content":"Recruitment Thread is located here: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/206054-recruitment-thread-zodiac-beasts-ooc\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/g...iac-beasts-ooc</a><br /> <br /> <br /> I know I posted this in the Story Hooks section, but damn it sounded like a pretty cool set up to me! Anyways, this game is designed for up to 13 people (12 players + 1 Story Teller) to take part in. The players will be one of the 12 Chinese Zodiac beasts, which consists of Dragon, Goat, Rooster, Dog, Snake, Rat, Monkey, Pig, Tiger, Ox, Rabbit, and Horse. Roles are first come, first serve.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Rules 1 - No one liner posts, about 1 paragraph each (4 or 5 lines) would be an acceptable amount.<br /> <br /> Rule 2 - Don't be a dick OOC. In character dickishness is perfectly acceptable.<br /> <br /> Rule 3 - This is a semi-durance RP, meaning you're inside Arcadia, and your Keeper (preferably played by the ST), has more power than you do. That being said, you need to find a way back home, while at the same time doing whatever tasks he commands of you. The other players are in the same boat as you, maybe you can work together to formulate a plan.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rule 4 - OOC chat should be done in ( ) in order to let players know what is part of your activity, and what you wish to address outside the story. Don't think I have to actually mention this, but thought I'd do it anyways.<br /> <br /> <br /> Dual Kiths are encouraged. Not a rule, just an advisement.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Collecting figurines has been a hobby of yours, and your last purchase was from some Chinese gift shop. You bought a golden figurine of your Zodiac animal, thinking it would be pretty cool for your collection. After putting it on your bedside and going to sleep last night, you awaken to find two things amiss. One, you're inside a cold, metal cage instead of your nice warm bed. And two, you've become your Zodiac animal! Thankfully you seem to be some manner of hybrid, rather than a full beast, and therefor have access to your digits. Maybe you can open the cage from the inside out! As your senses begin to flare, the image of the store owner from yesterday appears before you, holding the figurine you bought with one hand, and stroking it with the other... &quot;Now I have the full set!&quot; he says, as you notice you're not the only cage in the room.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-24-2014, 09:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T18:59:11-07:00","id":206731,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Jessica Sparks' mind rebelled at </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">the reality of the situation. Having two human parents, she simply could not really be an ox hybrid. It was impossible. Clearly, she was but in the grasp of an odd dream. For long moments, she expected to wake up next to Curtis or one or more of their cats. Those moments and more passed, and Jessica remained where and wherever she was imprisoned.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">As the image of the store owner faded away, Jessica tried to open the cage she was in from the inside. She was a locksmith by trade, and felt confident she could let herself out. The coldness of the cage seemed as unnatural to her as her new oxen body. It took an effort of will to continue trying to free herself. However, the very strangeness of the cage's metal strengthened her resolve to escape. Who could even image what prolonged to this bizarre metal could do?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">In the end, Jessica opened the door and tumbled out onto a floor of small emerald green tiles. Behind her, a strange voice radiated out from the cage from which she had escaped. The cage itself shook with the voice. It said, &quot;For taking thine leave from inside me without mine consent, thou may with confidence count me as your foe eternal.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The cage's grandiose threat triggered a battle within Jessica between fear and something not unlike amusement. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  To go from pig to ox! 07-24-2014, 05:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T17:09:13-07:00","id":207736,"title":"","content":"Something was definitely off about this place. It wasn't just the talking cage, everything in the room felt 'alive' somehow. The tiled floors vibrated under Jessica, almost as if they were shuddering at her touch, and the shadows on the walls shifted, as if the walls and ceiling were looming over her now, anticipating her next action. The floor was cool to the touch, and had a texture like that of polished stone. A closer inspection would reveal the floor was made from real jade, which would have probably cost a fortune. Soon the floor began to speak as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;If you smudge or crack me in any way, I will make your life a living hell!&quot; it threatened, &quot;He gets angry when I'm not flawlessly shined!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Soon the rest of the room began to chime in with a chorus of voices, each of which threatening them if they disturbed anything about the neatly organized structure contained within. Thousands of voices communicating in unison, it was impossible to make out more than a few words at a time as they all seemed to be trying to talk over one another.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Get back in your cage!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You'll get us all in trouble!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You'd better not be shedding, Beast!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You break it, he breaks you!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T17:44:15-07:00","id":207754,"title":"","content":"The chorus of commands almost drove Jessica back into the cage from which she had just escaped. The multitude of orders seemed to call for obedience like a physical force, like a river of sound sweeping her bodily to where it wanted her to go. She almost could not even entertain the idea that she could actually resist the commands engulfing her. At that point, merely breathing proved disturbingly challenging. She was just a woman before something mighty and uncanny. How could she possibly resist?<br /> <br /> Then Jessica remembered something. In this strange place, she was not just a woman. Was she not also partly an ox? That which could overcome a person might not vanquish an ox. With this thought, she started to move away from her screaming former prisoner. Ignoring the storm of voices around her and heaving jade floor beneath her, Jessica trod where she would walk. She would be free, if she could manage it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T21:02:04-07:00","id":207884,"title":"","content":"Max Layton sat there a while, grappling with his new condition. He knew he wasn't dreaming. He'd tried pinching himself awake a bit earlier, and wound up with only pain and the discovery that there really were a lot of little bristles all over his new pink flesh. <i>&quot;How does something like this</i> happen<i>? And why?&quot;</i> he wondered, poking and prodding at his new self, in bewilderment and horror at what he finds. It was as though he hoped against hope to discover he was in some sort of suit. <i>&quot;There's gotta be a zipper somewhere... Or or or where do these things detach?&quot;</i> Of course, prosthetic snouts, ears, and curly tails shouldn't <i>hurt</i> when he tugged at them or move when he willed them to move (or when he didn't).<br /> <br /> The young man would have just sat there for a while longer, had Jessica's actions not drawn his attention off of himself. Max had noticed the other cages, but didn't take stock of their residents until he heard the tinking sound. He jerked his head over to see what looked like a... cow-lady picking at the lock. And getting it open. To which it gave archaic-sounding criticism. Well. That helped snap him back awake. He was still very much out of it, and deathly worried about what had happened. But there were better places to be out of it and deathly worried than in a cage.<br /> <br /> Climbing shakily to his hooves -- and never more thankful for his hands -- Max went to the door and tried fiddling with the latch. Aaaand accomplished a great deal of nothing. Unlike Jessica, his only professional experience with locks was closing up shop at the end of a late shift. He grunted in annoyance.<br /> <br /> And then the cacophony began. Wincing, he brought his hands to his ears and staggered back from the noise. He'd sort of breezed past the talking cage -- it almost seemed... whimsical -- but <i>everything in the room</i> shrieking commands and complaints was too much. He found himself trembling and just wishing everything would just stop being horrible for five minutes. He watched the bovine stranger begin to retreat to her own cage, and then decide better of it. She seemed like she planned to leave, sending a new wave of desperation through him. &quot;W-Wait,&quot; was lost in the din. &quot;Stop,&quot; fared little better. &quot;D-Don't leave!&quot; she might just barely have heard. &quot;<i>Help me please!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The last one was piercing enough to get through. Still, it was an open question whether anyone could make out the words: it had sounded more like an animal squealing than a human screaming. Max felt a bit sick. If anyone wondered whether pigs could blush, well, his face held the answer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 07-25-2014, 12:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T21:24:39-07:00","id":207894,"title":"","content":"Despite all he noise, Jessica did hear Max. She turned toward him and tried to make her way over to his cage. The floor heaved, and she tumbled. With a grunt, she got to her feet and tried again. This time she made it. She said to the trapped porcine figure, &quot;I'll try to get you out. If I can.&quot;<br /> <br /> To this, the cage snarled, &quot;You will not find me such easy prey to your skill. My charge I am keeping.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica did her best to ignore the cage. Even so, the cage resisted all her efforts. &quot;See?&quot; mocked the cage. &quot;You are a failure! You cannot beat me, like you did my flawed peer!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey!&quot; exclaimed Jessica's cage. &quot;I heard that!&quot;<br /> <br /> Rage filled Jessica, but she knew anger would do nothing to help her. She decided to change tactics with Max's cage. Instead of trying to force it open, she tickled the door as best as she could with her new hands. The metal felt so wrong, but she persisted in her efforts. Luckily, the cage started to laugh. The laughter was eerie and wrong, but Jessica took full advantage. Swiftly, she pulled open the laughing cage's door and pulled Max out to relative freedom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  Forgot a line 07-25-2014, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T22:33:26-07:00","id":207924,"title":"","content":"Max sighed in relief as she started over. He was luckier than she when the floor decided it wasn't being enough of a jerk, catching the bars of his cage to keep from falling. Though he did get an earful from the bars for getting his grubby hands all over them. Feeling bolder, he told them, &quot;Oh, shut up.&quot;<br /> <br /> He watched the stranger as she drew near, and nodded to her words. &quot;Thank you,&quot; he said, flashing a nervous smile and letting her work. Then began what Max could only describe as a comedy sketch between cages.<br /> <br /> Still, otherworldly as the situation was, his boastful cage seemed to mean it: Jessica wasn't having much luck. At which point he thought of being a more active player. He took stock of his legs again. They were very different than they had been, but he thought he could work with them. Holding a bar of the cage to steady himself, Max lifted one unfamiliar leg and chambered it for a side kick. &quot;Okay. Stand back, and let's see if this...&quot;<br /> <br /> The swinish youth then stared as Jessica began to tickle the cage. &quot;Hunh. Or... Or that.&quot; Fortunately, most else in the room seems roughly as dumbfounded, and the racket has dulled to a murmur. Max set down his leg in time for his rescuer to get the door open and pull him out of there. It was amazing how much better it felt just being out of there. He turned to face her with an impressed smile. &quot;Phew! Thank you. Just... thank you! That was brilliant!&quot; His happiness and relief were only dented by the bizarre feeling of his tail swishing back and forth behind him. Yes, Max could really have done without that.<br /> <br /> Still, ignoring it, Max tried to give his savior all due courtesy. &quot;Uh... I really owe you one. The circumstances are awful, but I'm glad to meet you. I'm Max.&quot; He held out a hand. &quot;I... guess you're human, too?&quot; This won the room a fresh bundle of decibels from the various not-so-inanimate objects, this time to the tune of laughter. &quot;Oh, that is just <i>precious</i>!&quot; rang one voice. &quot;They think they're people!&quot; called another, to more guffaws. The student groaned and snorted. &quot;Great. The peanut gallery has an opinion...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T04:15:03-07:00","id":208113,"title":"","content":"&quot;What is going on in here?&quot; a voice asked in a calm, yet menacing tone. The voice seemed to come from all directions at once, making its source impossible to pinpoint. The voice itself was recognizable however, it was the shop keeper's. And as he spoke, the entire room went dead silent, all except for the two cages who began to flip their shit and scream at the escapees to return to their cells as fast as possible. They didn't get the chance, however, because moments after the question was asked, the containers heated up to a brilliant orange and began to dissolve into puddles of molten metal. This quickly reduced their screaming pleas to cries of agony as their voices bubbled and gurgled as if they were drowning.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe I need to reforge you with stronger materials...&quot; the voice said, the malice in its voice escalating slightly, it sounded like it was losing its temper. &quot;The calender is all wrong, it's not the year of the Pig or Ox. I'm going to have to make some... corrections.&quot; the voice continued, before footsteps sounded off in the distance, gently patting against the jade tiles. Something was approaching them, and was taking a leisurely pace in doing so. &quot;One of you gets let out of your cage on a 12 year rotation schedule, that's how the Zodiac works. But now somebody decided to break the rules and ruin the authenticity. I do so hate when my collections are unorganized!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-25-2014, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:08:39-07:00","id":208266,"title":"","content":"Jessica opened her mouth to speak, but then she closed it. One had to select her words with care when dealing with someone who could melt talking cages at a whim. Fear forced her to take her present utterly surreal situation seriously. She glanced over to the pig man who had introduced himself as Max. She took a deep breath and then she said, &quot;I'm sure Max will agree with me in saying that neither of us meant to offend you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica then tried to offer the shop keeper her best smile, the same one she had used a few months ago to get out of a speeding ticket. She could but hope for the best. What else could she do? Absurdly, she wondered if the extra set of breasts she had gained with her new oxen body would help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:33:34-07:00","id":208290,"title":"","content":"Max's heart skipped a beat at the voice. It was the last thing he remembered hearing when he awoke, and a stark reminder that their condition was by someone's design. And, as the cages bubbled away in agony, that someone wasn't limited to turning people into animals. He felt some pity for the poor things. Particularly since life in a cage just might be preferable to no life at all.<br /> <br /> Trembling, he nodded a frantic agreement to Jessica's words and tried to follow her lead. &quot;Y-Yeah! N-No question here. We didn't mean to make you angry, we just... We didn't know what was going on.&quot; Max might not be able to work the same kind of... appeal that his bovine companion might, but it wouldn't be the first time he'd pulled off a &quot;wide-eyed innocent&quot; routine. Though that admittedly usually went over better with a less nervous smile. &quot;M-Mmaybe you could tell us how we got here and... got like this? Er, so we don't offend you again, I mean.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T08:12:24-07:00","id":208333,"title":"","content":"The foot steps seemed to grow closer and closer, and finally came to an abrupt halt. The voice began to speak once more, but this time it was clearly focused in a specific area. As it spoke, the shop keeper's image faded into view as if slowly materializing out of thin air.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;You are here because of a contract.&quot; he said. His arms were crossed behind his back, and the old man was dressed in a dark green vest and black pants, he also looked to be quite elderly, possibly mid 70's. &quot;I'm a collector, you see, and I'm particularly fond of birth signs.&quot; he explained, holding out both hands, one showing the golden figurine of the pig, and the other of the ox. &quot;The first customer to purchase one of my figurines would join my realm as part of my collection.&quot; he went on, &quot;It took a long time, everybody wants the cool animals like Dragon or Snake, not many wanted to buy Pig and Ox. Collecting the full set was quite a chore, and I'd really hate to have it lost or damaged.&quot; he went on.<br /> <br /> <br /> The cages were not dead, because their voices still bubbled and gurgled even in their melted state.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Quiet, or I'll consider mixing iron into you!&quot; he ordered.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> He turned back to his two escapees and with a flick of his hand, the figurines vanished and he moved his arms behind his back again before continuing to speak.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;My real name would take 3 hours for you to pronounce, so you will simply address me as Keeper, or more preferably Master.&quot; he introduced himself before glaring at the two of them, &quot;Since it's your first offense, I'm going to be lenient this one time and only give you a mild punishment. But if you cross me like this again, I'll revoke your privilege to remain animated.&quot; he threatened, &quot;I would prefer live models, they're so much more fun, but I'm not opposed to pouring molten gold over you and adding some new statues to my home!&quot; With that, he seemed to stand up straight as if he were adjusting his posture and looking down upon them.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Now as for your punishment.&quot; he began, &quot;You will spend 3 hours in the slaughter house, providing meat for my more obedient slaves.&quot; he ordered.<br /> <br /> <br /> With that, the sound of clanking chains and rushing air filled the room as two meat hooks swung down from the ceiling towards the confused beasts, their speed evident they were intending to impale them on impact.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T11:08:34-07:00","id":208483,"title":"","content":"Jessica tried to escape and shove Max out of the way. She failed. The swinging meat hook took her through her chest. Pain prevented her from seeing clearly what happened to Max as she was carried of to the keeper's slaughter house. The overpowering scent of blood and rotting meat almost made her gag. Only the meat hook impaling her prevented it.<br /> <br /> Inside the slaughter house, as promised, Jessica provided meat to the keeper more obedient slaves. The sliced off pieces of her with knives or simply tore her flesh with their teeth. As her flesh was eaten, new flesh took its place. The pain of it all staggered the imagination.<br /> <br /> The slaves that the keeper deemed more obedient than her represented a diverse lot. Only a couple of them looked like normal humans. Other things ate from her she simply could not comprehend. One looked like it was made out of living glass, while another seemed fashioned out of drunken butterflies. Despite knowing her ordeal was to last only three hours, Jessica soon found herself yearning for death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typo 07-25-2014, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:07:15-07:00","id":208797,"title":"","content":"Max fared no better. His ears pricked up in time for him to jerk his head up at the hooks, but he was too horrified by &quot;Keeper's&quot; decree to do more than stare stupidly. He managed only a single step, unsure even where to move, before it ran through his back. He opened his mouth to scream, but no sound came, and he merely gaped as it pulled him up and away, watching &quot;Keeper&quot; and ten cages fade from sight. He had his definition of &quot;true pain&quot; redefined in that moment. And not for the last time in those next three hours.<br /> <br /> The stench of blood and rot hit like a punch to the face. The anguished cries of men and beasts and things both or neither were just as overwhelming. Max had no chance to recover before the butchers were on him. He perceived none of them clearly, aside a few laughs, a few grumbles about his being scrawny, and perhaps even a quiet, &quot;Sorry.&quot; He mostly just felt their knives -- and fangs and fires and claws -- rip away every bit of his flesh. And when it returned, they did it again. Hundreds of times over they stripped him to the bone -- when they didn't cut through -- and hundreds of times his body mended itself for them. He joined the cacophony with his anguished screams and squeals, and before long found he could not distinguish the two. Time quickly lost all meaning.<br /> <br /> The wall before him held a chart. A diagram of all the cuts on a pig. Each segment flashed in time with the pain of the corresponding flesh taken from him, or outlined the grisly gashes where a butcher hadn't managed or cared for a clean cut. Max had not looked long before the pain alone clamped his eyes shut. But the agony had already seared the image of it into his eyelids.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T16:31:19-07:00","id":208821,"title":"","content":"To call the place a slaughter house could not have been anymore accurate. The place wreaked of blood and viscera, and was filled with the sounds of creatures being massacred. They were not the only two who had been placed on the menu today, it seemed. Dozens of other beast morphs such as themselves were hanging from the ceiling, some even being upside down as the hooks were embedded in their ankles or knee caps. Others were being force fed through a grinder, only to appear above it again and fall back in like they were trapped in some kind of time loop. Monsters, humanoids, animals, and creatures the human tongue had no words for were consuming the meat as it was produced. Some ate it raw off the plate, others appeared to wait for it to be properly cooked and prepared before dining.<br /> <br /> <br /> Some of the methods for harvesting the food appeared legitimate, but others appeared specifically designed to fulfill some kind of sadistic pleasure. The sight of a deer getting bludgeoned repeatedly by meat tenderizers being one of the least shocking methods to behold. Thankfully, time eventually passed and the hooks that held them prisoner in this hell hole began to carry them away back towards their previous location, leaving behind many others who apparently had a longer (or perhaps even permanent) duration on their service in the slaughter house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T22:56:10-07:00","id":209110,"title":"","content":"As the hook whisked Jessica from the slaughter house back toward her previous location, she tried to pull herself free. The thought of seeing the keeper again filled her with dread. Better to simply drop into whatever lay below, whatever that might be. Nothing could be worse than the monster who could inflict such agony. As she tried to pull herself off the hook, her thoughts drifted back to the slaughter house.<br /> <br /> One memory in particular haunted Jessica. She remembered watching a dog-thing eat her left shoulder blade, the one tattooed with the red racing car, early in her time in the slaughter house. Later, she saw her left shoulder blade eaten again. However, the second time her shoulder had been unadorned by any image of car. The process that had restored her flesh had not brought back her tattoo. Its lose had hit her surprisingly hard. It seemed a minor thing in the midst of all this horror. She supposed it was a link to who she had been before her present nightmarish situation. Now it was gone, leaving her new, unnatural body with no trace other than gender of who she had been before the keeper had taken her. She now truly was a new creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T03:24:49-07:00","id":209254,"title":"","content":"Max was too swept up in a world suddenly free again of pain -- well, aside from the hook still in his back. There were no especially deep thoughts; something like a protective catatonia had set in. Even so, there was an underlying dread that mirrored Jessica's own: their so-called &quot;Keeper&quot; might well be waiting, perhaps thinking up another torment the next time they displeased him. Though that gave the Keeper too much credit. He would likely give them no thought at all until he wished to admire his collection or they stepped &quot;out of line,&quot; and then might casually resign them to suffer without batting an eye.<br /> <br /> The ox's time in the slaughterhouse had wrenched away some of her human identity. The pig's had done likewise to his sense of personhood. &quot;Ribs... Tenderloin... Tusks... Oink... Bacon... Ham...&quot; he mumbled, mindlessly tracing out the proper lines of each cut on his body. Pain was a powerful teacher, and had on some level buried the cruel diagram in his self-image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T06:47:12-07:00","id":209286,"title":"","content":"The hooks were no more tender in releasing them than they had been catching them. Like a child on a swing set, they came to a very abrupt halt, practically flinging the two off their blades and onto the floor. They were back in the cage room, and the two cages that had melted before were replaced with shinier new models. It made them stand out among the older and worn out cages the rest of the Zodiac were trapped in. Apparently the Keeper had fulfilled his intention of having them reforged, instead of simply discarding them.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh good, I just finished installing the new cages.&quot; said the Keeper's voice as he faded into view with his back facing towards them. He turned around smiling as he watched the last remains of the hook wounds mending themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Slaughter House is where I place my disobedient Beasts.&quot; he said, &quot;I have other punishments for other types of servants. These two just got back from The Foundry where I break down and remold my Elementals in the searing heat, pounding hammers, and boring drills.&quot; he smiled then as a far off expression came to his eyes. He seemed actually proud at having designed such a torment &quot;I don't believe they will be letting you two back out anytime soon. But just to be sure, I've added 2 additional locks on the door.&quot; the Keeper mused as the doors opened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T09:35:35-07:00","id":209370,"title":"","content":"Jessica said nothing to the keeper. With a nod to Max, she went into the newly forged cage set out for her. She wanted to fight, but knew that there was nothing she could do. Once she stepped into the cage, the door slammed shut. Jessica sat down. She tried her best not to cry, but failed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T11:15:59-07:00","id":209428,"title":"","content":"Max realized he'd been staring at the ox when she gave a nod. He guessed he hoped she had come up with some idea or plan to throw into action, but alas, if she had, it was something less immediate. He sunk a bit and began to slink back toward his freshly minted cage. As he neared the open door, he paused. Maybe it was just the endorphins roaring through him with no more pain to mend (other than the phantom variety), but a fancy took its hold. He took a long, deep breath. He would just enter immediately or shut up if commanded.<br /> <br /> &quot;Th-These are... very nice cages you've made for us,&quot; he said, laying a hand on his own, and trying to sound impressed. &quot;I-I mean, I'm no expert, but the... the craftsmanship speaks for itself.&quot;<br /> &quot;The 'craft' speaks for itself, too,&quot; he heard the cage mutter, caked through with bitterness.<br /> Max swallowed and forged on. &quot;Yeah, just... You spared no expense. N-Nothing but the best for us, right? Th-Th... Thank you.&quot; He couldn't express how much he wanted to break in those slightly hoof-like hands of his by punching himself in the face.<br /> <br /> &quot;But-- A-And I'm n-not meaning any disrespect here!&quot; he said, turning toward the Keeper with what he hoped was a winning smile. And looked down near the man's feet. Even the turn to face him had brought the twinge of the hook in his back. His porcine body locked in a cringe, Max pressed on, &quot;But I-I was thinking about that 'one a year' thing you said. I've heard people and... well... animals locked in cages all the time just get tired and stringy. Haggard. Just... Just not presentable at all, y'know? With all the trouble you went through, I'd... hate you to be disappointed when you came to... to admire us, or... show us off.&quot;<br /> <br /> He swallowed. This was the tricky bit. &quot;So... maybe there could be times when we're... y'know, out and about. Just a little!&quot; A bit of a squeal slipped into that last bit. &quot;Just... Just for exercise and, and... some recreation and things to do. That stuff. Like, uh... Free-range! I-I mean, you said it yourself: live models are more fun. Wouldn't you get more... more fun out of us moving around like that? I-I-If you think you could find some way to do it.&quot; Max raised his arms, as though he feared being struck. He dared to lift his eyes to the man's shins, and began to laugh nervously. &quot;A-Again, you know best! I'm... I'm just a... a... just a Beast.&quot; His voice cracked at the word. Max's world spun a moment; there was something powerful about actually saying it. But he'd come too far.<br /> <br /> He coughed to get his bearings and forced himself to say the last word. He needed it. But could not imagine having anything more vile in his mouth. &quot;M-M-Master...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T12:50:14-07:00","id":209475,"title":"","content":"The Keeper looked down at the pig as he continued to plead. Indeed, the man's height seemed to have shifted without them noticing before, he gently placed a hand upon Max's cheek and smiled at him as if he were adorable in some fashion.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh you still don't get it, do you?&quot; he asked, smiling cheerfully. &quot;You're not in that boring old human world anymore. You're in my realm, and whatever I say goes.&quot; he patted his cheek before continuing. &quot;I could lock you up in a 5X5 sized box for 50 years, and you'd still be just as pretty and strong as I want you to be.&quot; he boasted. &quot;Everything you see in this realm belongs to me. The furniture, the animals, the people, the monsters, the very landscape, I am lord of this domain and the laws of reality are subject to my will.&quot; he moved his hand away and quickly struck the pig in the face with an open palm.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;That's for not following orders immediately.&quot; he said, &quot;But you bring up an interesting point, it's not really very entertaining to just have you sit around all day. Doesn't really capture the essence of the Zodiac unless you get to show off a bit.&quot; He thumbed his chin a bit in thought, &quot;I could have a ranch constructed, I suppose.&quot; he muttered, tilting his head at the idea. &quot;And since you enjoy my work so much, I'll let you in on a little secret.&quot; he said, leaning in and pointing around the room. &quot;Everything in this room that can talk... used to be a person. I can turn you into more than just animals. I want you to remember that.&quot; he finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T14:00:32-07:00","id":209513,"title":"","content":"Jessica listened to the exchange between the keeper and Max. She shook her head. Her situation was hopeless. What could she do? Thinking of no other possible escape or action, she tried to go to sleep. Naturally, slumber proved elusive. However, in time, sleep found her. She dreamed that was lost in a vast forest filled with terrible monsters, but that her three cats were dutifully searching for her. In her dream, she prayed that they would find her before it was too late.<br /> <br /> Jessica woke up with a start, and tried to return to sleep. It took some time, but managed to do it. This time her dream offered no comfort. This time, she dreamed that Curtis was sleeping with a woman who thought was her. Her cats knew the truth, but had no way of alerting Curtis. This time when Jessica awakened, she gave up the idea of escaping through sleep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T16:25:07-07:00","id":209564,"title":"","content":"Max squealed and staggered back from the slap. The chilling picture the Keeper had painted had left the student spellbound, and the gentle touch on his cheek (swifter than he could flinch from) had lowered his guard. Needless to say, hand on his cheek, he got into the cage as quick as his hooves allowed, the door slamming behind him. The slap was hardly the most painful event of even the last five minutes, but the surprise gave it extra heft. As did the confirmation that his little effort to improve things had failed. Worse, the seed he had planted might actually be growing into something horrible in the alien soil of their Keeper's mind. And given what the shopkeeper had already done...<br /> <br /> The pig felt his legs buckling and managed to sit before they gave way altogether. &quot;I... I will...&quot; he told the terrifying being before him, barely managing a whisper. The conversation seemingly over, he simply sat there, decompressing.<br /> <br /> Then all the insanity hit Max in a rush. That this was his life now, this was the new normal. And with no sign that things were going to get better. And it might very well get a lot worse. That he would never see any of his friends and loved ones ever again, and they might never know. He had no more luck than Jessica in holding back the tears and sobs. He cried himself half to sleep.<br /> <br /> He looked up when his tears had run dry, some time later. He saw his 'partner in crime' curled up, somehow managing to sleep. He still didn't even know her name, but didn't want to disturb her. The sleep didn't look restful, on the floor of her cage. The cage he now knew to be as much a person as they were. Like his own.<br /> <br /> At which point Max decided on something he could do, at least. Something decent. And something to get out of his own head. Unsure how to address it, he set a hand on the door of his cage and said to it, &quot;I'm... I'm sorry. You shouldn't have gone through that. Or be like this. If it was anything like the...&quot; He trembled just to think of the slaughterhouse. &quot;... like what we went through then I... I just...&quot; He gave up trying to articulate the thoughts around it. &quot;I'm just so sorry.&quot;<br /> <br /> A few moments passed in silence, the cage not responding, for whatever reason of its own. Max respected that. Perhaps it was asleep, too; how would he know? Still, on the off-chance it wasn't, he asked it a question he suspected it hadn't been asked in a while. &quot;So... what's your name?&quot;<br /> <br /> With or without an answer, it wasn't long after that his new ears told him the ox was waking. &quot;Ah, you're up, too? Didn't catch your name either, earlier.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T17:13:35-07:00","id":209585,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Jessica Sparks introduced herself to Max. She explained that was a locksmith from Mankato, Minnesota. </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">She also told him how she had lived with her three cats and Curtis. &quot;Now I might never see him or my cats again,&quot; Jessica said. &quot;I wish had treated him better.&quot;<br /> <br /> While she said nothing more, Jessica remembered flirting with one of her clients when she had gone to change his locks. At the time, she had thought almost nothing of it. The man had been too cute to ignore. Now that she might never see Curtis again, she regretted it. </span></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T18:29:54-07:00","id":209647,"title":"","content":"Max nodded and went through the &quot;Pleased to meet you&quot;s, but Jessica gave him pause when she mentioned her home state. &quot;Wait, wait, Minnesota? Really? 'cause I came here from San Antonio, Texas myself... What kind of reach does this guy have?&quot; It wasn't even the most extreme indication of the power their Keeper commanded -- their own bestial forms were nearer the mark -- but it was another reminder.<br /> <br /> That aside, Max's heart went out to her. &quot;I definitely hear you on the regret. But... At least you were together before. Even if you don't again, you <i>had</i> something that close. Tonight was the first...&quot; It again struck him how they had no means of tracking the passage of time. &quot;... I mean, I was just about to take Karen out on our first date. We've been close since we were little, but until college it just... I wish I'd had the guts to ask her out when I knew how I felt. Heh, she even asked what took me so long.&quot; He gave a snort, starting to get a bit worked up. &quot;Can't imagine she'll be wild about dating me looking like <i>this</i>, though. Even if we do get outta here...&quot; And lo, did he return to being a sad sack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T18:55:37-07:00","id":209672,"title":"","content":"Jessica attempted to smile. She said, &quot;Max, who can say we won't turn back to normal one day? Maybe this can end as suddenly as it started. We must try not to give up hope.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica wondered if her words were more for herself or Max. In reality, she had little hope. Even so, it seemed proper to try to be brave for Max. In a sense, what he suffered in the slaughter house was because of her If she had left him in his cage, he would never have suffered that horror. She owed. However, she had learned at great cost to take great care in the help that she offered him. She would need to be careful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-26T21:25:14-07:00","id":209799,"title":"","content":"Max found himself smiling back. &quot;Thanks. You're right.&quot; Regardless of how Jessica felt, she had given off just the impression he needed to see. &quot;We didn't know anything like... all of this was possible. There's a lot else we might not know. I know we can't just give up.&quot; His smile faded just a bit. &quot;But... Man, this sure would be easier on both of us if I was as strong as you. So... Thanks again for not just leaving me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ironically, Max had his own sense of guilt and indebtedness over her helping him. Jessica could have left him in his cage, and might have even found a way out on her own. Even if she had been caught, perhaps their Keeper's inscrutable calculations would have punished her more lightly if she hadn't helped another. He worried that he'd been dead weight, and she'd suffered trying to haul him out. <i>'I've gotta get stronger,' </i>he thought,<i> 'I can't let this happen again.'</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-27T02:32:15-07:00","id":209973,"title":"","content":"Time began to pass, though it was impossible to tell how long in... in wherever the hell they were. The two prisoners would find themselves frequently losing track of time, having conversations that seemed to last only a few minutes, and then discovering several hours had passed by. When their Keeper finally announced the ranch had been completed, they had no way of knowing if it took a few days, or several years, such was the maddening power of this realm.<br /> <br /> <br /> As the cages were wheeled out to the ranch, it was a shocking sight to behold. It did not resemble any ranch the human world had ever known. It actually looked <i>beautiful</i> compared to everything else they had experienced so far. Fluorescent plants illuminated the landscape in hues of purple, blue, pink, and turquoise, the sky was perfectly cloudless and displayed the image of a starry nebula expanding into the vastness of outer space, complete with planetary bodies and swirling galaxies. There was little room to wonder how they were able to see entire galaxies in the distance without a telescope, it certainly wouldn't be the strangest thing they'd come across here.<br /> <br /> <br /> It was clear their Keeper had gone to a great deal of trouble in order to create the majestic beauty of celestial beings like the Chinese Zodiac. Although just how many bushes, trees, and blades of grass were actual plants, and how many were fellow prisoners? For that matter, how many stars were actual stars, and not just somebody he had pinned to the sky? What were the limits of their Keeper's power; did he even have any? Was he really just some shop keeper, or some kind of forgotten pagan god? So many questions for Max and Jessica to ponder in their time here.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Release your contents, slaves.&quot; the Keeper ordered, and the doors to the cages popped right open. The other members of the Zodiac crawled out and took their first steps on the illuminating grass beneath their feet. &quot;Welcome to your new habitat!&quot; the Keeper said to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T09:11:11-07:00","id":211303,"title":"","content":"Aside from Max, Jessica had seen only glimpses of the other zodiac prisoners. She took the chance to covertly examine them from where she stood. The incredible vista all around them served as an ideal distraction. Each of them looked as she and Max did: humanoid animals. She noticed that there was no horse. This suggested to her that it was still 2014, and whoever the keeper had forced to play the horse still had his or freedom. Jessica tried vainly to remember how long it was until the next year of the ox","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T23:34:35-07:00","id":212193,"title":"","content":"Max had discussed with Jessica concerns and trepidations about the &quot;ranch.&quot; But this? Frankly? The sight of it all took his breath away. He had seen fantastic locales in movies and games, and imagined them from books. The luminous beauty around put them all to shame. Unselfconscious, he got some mileage out of his new snout, snuffling at the aromas of the place, trying to drink in as much of it all as he could. Just being there made him feel <i>good</i>. For a moment, he forget it all: the abduction, the transformation, the torture... None of it mattered. But just for a moment.<br /> <br /> He shook his head to clear it, ears flopping about comically. <i>'This is the most amazing place I've ever seen, but it's still a prison.'</i> Max kept telling himself that. He tried to distract himself by stretching his legs. Like Jessica, he turned his focus to the other zodiac members. Despite knowing it was horrible what had happened to everyone, he found it fascinating to see these living blends of human and animal. Still, it did feel a little... unseemly. Not just because clothing consisted of whatever few scraps and rags remained after the change, but looking at people who were -- if anything like the Pig -- still very uncomfortable in their own skins. Indeed, he still felt embarrassed just to be seen as he was. And he couldn't be alone in that. All of this kept him from going over to say 'hello,' or staring too much.<br /> <br /> Still, there were some he couldn't help keeping an eye on: chiefly the Tiger and the Dragon, a bit less so the Snake and Dog. <i>'I don't need to worry. It's normal for a human to feel like this when he sees a wild animal,'</i> he told himself, <i>'even if I know they're still people, whatever they look like.</i> <i>They won't hurt any of us. How I feel is normal, and I'll calm down. Yeah. Normal.' </i>Max tried not to wonder whether there were claws or jaws like those that had taken turns stripping meals off him. Or whether he was picking up their scents, aware they were picking up his, and some part of him that was now prey was having a very natural reaction to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T05:00:33-07:00","id":212349,"title":"","content":"&quot;I hope you will better behave yourselves here.&quot; The Keeper addressed his two hoofed prisoners, &quot;You saw for yourself there are even worse ways to feed you to my slaves than simply hanging you from the ceiling.&quot; he warned, placing a hand slowly on both their heads as he said it.<br /> <br /> <br /> The foliage was more than simply illumination, it looked like it would provide some decent shelter too. The grass was long enough to reach mid shin, and many of the bushes were tall enough to stand over their heads, their thick leaves hanging over to provide shade, or perhaps cover from the weather. Patches in between the tree branches provided the glimpses of the night sky, making it even more enchanting than a simple open meadow would.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Sadly, the contract only allowed the figurines to work on the first customers who bought them.&quot; Keeper explained, &quot;Replacing any of you would be quite difficult for me, not to mention expensive. And you're such prized collector pieces...&quot; he removed his hand from their scalps as he once more folded his arms behind his back, it seemed to be his preferred stance when he wasn't using them for something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-29T21:11:50-07:00","id":213134,"title":"","content":"The keeper's words about the contract only allowing the figurines to work on the customers who bought them rolled around in Jessica's mind. It seemed to suggest that the keeper had limitations, or at least rules he deigned to recognize. She wondered if that could be used somehow. Slowly, a plan stated to take shape in her mind. She had no idea if it would work, or make things worse. For her plan to work, she would need Max's help.<br /> <br /> Later, Jessica took Max aside under a towering tree. &quot;Max, I might have a plan to get us out of this. But it might it not. In fact, it might make matters worse.&quot; Jessica went on to remind Max how the keeper had said that the figurines only would work on the first customers who bought them. She then explained that it occurred to her that they might sell each other their figurines and then resell them back to each other. Jessica said that she hoped that this would make them the third rather the first owners of their respective figurines. She concluded, &quot;Then, if the keeper is telling the truth and my reasoning is sound, our figurines will no longer have any power over us. Of course, I could be totally wrong. Maybe being the third owner or customer does nothing to change that we were the first ones. Maybe I'm seeing hope where there is none. It might well be doing this will do nothing but make the keeper mad at us for trying to escape. What do you think, Max?&quot; .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T13:24:33-07:00","id":215015,"title":"","content":"Nate had been silent during their change of scenery. In fact, he had been a loner for days. Like all the zodiacs, he had freaked out when he woke up in the cage, and like almost all of them, he got to experience the Keeper's punishments for rebellion. He had tried to avoid speaking to the other Beasts. He didn't know why, but he felt uneasy conversing with the Dragon, the Snake or the Tiger. As for the Rooster or the Rabbit...well, they were too ridiculous to take them seriously. He liked talking with the Horse, it felt natural to him. A shame he disappeared.<br /> <br /> The last few days, he had watched the Oxen and the Pig. He was somewhat happy to have been born under the sign of the Ram, at least he didn't become fat with a curly tail and a pink skin. However, he felt that his animal side called out to them. Must be this domesticated animal kinship or something. It was easy to ignore this call when they were imprisoned, but now that they were on the ranch, well... Sheeps are social animals, aren't they?<br /> <br /> So when Jessica and Max went alone under a tree, he decided to follow them, and called them out. &quot;Hey guys. What are you doing here alone? Hope you're not planning to escape. We all saw how <i>well</i> it went last time.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T18:17:36-07:00","id":215384,"title":"","content":"Nate's arrival startled Jessica. Giving a Max a warning look, she forced a laugh. She had no idea if she could trust the Ram. However, she did want to automatically assume the worst about him. She would simply have to get to know him better. Maybe he could join them on their escape attempt, if he proved trustworthy and they dared even to attempt her plan. Smiling, she asked, &quot;How could we escape? If only we could!&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica then offered her hand and introduced herself to Nate.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-31T21:58:55-07:00","id":215546,"title":"","content":"After hearing Jessica's plan, Max raised a hand to his chin, thinking it over. He was grateful to discuss some way of getting out; he hadn't come up with any good ideas himself. Still, the trip to the Slaughterhouse and the other threats had him very nervous about trying anything. &quot;That's... actually a really clever idea. I just don't know if--&quot; His ears pricked up at the sound of cloven hooves heading toward them through the grass. He put on a smile as he turned to face the Sheep, catching Jessica's expression as he did so. The young man got the picture. Still, he wondered at any ability they had to keep a discussion truly to themselves: the &quot;ranch&quot; wasn't the biggest of places, and if any other of the bestial prisoners' ears were half as sharp as his own -- and he was sure they were -- then &quot;private conversation&quot; was sort of a theoretical concept.<br /> <br /> &quot;We definitely don't want to go through... <i>that</i> again,&quot; Max said with a shudder. &quot;Or worse.&quot; He followed Jessica's offered handshake and introduction with his own.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sorry we're just meeting for the first time. I mean, if we're all in this together, we should at least get to know each other. Especially since it's been...&quot; Max paused, remembering how that train of thought went nowhere, &quot;... Well, however long it's been.&quot; He made himself smile despite the reminder, offering a shrug. &quot;Not much else to do here but wander around, sleep, or chat, anyway.&quot; This was mostly true. The student had done quite a bit of all three, but had also tried to get a little privacy now and then to keep his skills sharp. His body was still very unfamiliar, but he'd made great strides in adapting his martial arts training to its needs. These efforts stemmed in part from not wanting those skills to atrophy and knowing he'd need every advantage he could get. Well, and a bit of vanity: Nate's assessment of &quot;fat&quot; might have been a bit much, but Max's porcine transformation <i>had </i>put some pounds on him. Pounds he hoped to shed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor edits. 08-01-2014, 01:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T01:43:41-07:00","id":215677,"title":"","content":"He shook their hands and flashed a smile. &quot;The name's Nate. And you're right, you don't want to go through that again. We can't escape.&quot; Memories of his own tortures flashed back in his mind, and he tried to do his best to look confident in front of the two. He remembered the Keeper tying him up with a prickled chain and leading him to some sort of stock-market, where he had waited in the mud and the filth with other animals for god knows how long. He remembered potential buyers examining him unceremoniously, looking at his teeth, his ears, and all that made him part goat. He remembered being bought and brought to a slaughterhouse, where he had being flayed alive, his skin destined to be leather, before he got chopped up and died... Only to wake up in the same pen with the same mud and the same animals, over and over.<br /> Yeah. He didn't want to remember that, thank you very much, brain.<br /> <br /> &quot;Listen up, you two. When we were in our cages, we each had our problems, but the Keeper kept us separated. Now that we can properly interact with each other, I'm pretty sure he's gonna switch to group punishment, and none of us want to get hurt by your fault. You already did that to your cages, but they were people! So don't try anything weird, and be nice Beasts for the Keeper, alright? And after the Horse, I'm the next one to go out, so you'd better not screw me up.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":".  Minor corrections 08-01-2014, 06:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T12:00:42-07:00","id":216068,"title":"","content":"Jessica realized that Nate must have heard everything. She could hardly fault him for not wanting the two of them to try to escape. She thought he might well be right about the keeper switching to group punishment. She said, &quot;Nate, the last thing I want is to bring trouble to you or anyone else, and I'm very sorry about what happened to those cages. I'll consider your words very carefully.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica had not totally abandoned the idea of escape, but thought it prudent to allay Nate's fears.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T15:19:23-07:00","id":216196,"title":"","content":"The Sheep certainly wasn't very... well, sheepish. Max didn't know what had happened to Nate when the Keeper had taken him away, but made the safe assumption of &quot;torment.&quot; He understood where Nate was coming from. He himself waffled between trying for a way out and simply trying to minimize his own suffering -- and those of others, as the horned man noted. Max wasn't so sold on their Keeper employing group punishment; he wasn't sure the horrible <i>thing</i> that had taken them understood people well enough for that. But given what had become of their cages, it might amount to the same thing. &quot;Hmm... And even if he doesn't, if he thinks someone <i>should</i> have stopped an escape attempt, that someone's gonna be in just as much hot water...&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, Max did have an issue with Nate's reasoning -- aside from how much the idea of letting the Keeper win made his hackles rise. &quot;Why do you think the Horse is doing better than any of us? I mean, yeah, maybe the day-to-day treatment is <i>different</i>, but the Keeper's been very consistent: he sees us as collectibles and doesn't care about us being happy.&quot; He took a breath to keep himself calm, but got swept away a bit in the rant. &quot;That just doesn't mean we get to leave for it, it just means we're not right here. Having it be 'your' year could just mean you sit in a display case. Or maybe you spend more one-on-one time around the Keeper. What a treat. I'm sure none of us would stumble into <i>any</i> little rules to break.&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, the rant brought Max to a helpful place. &quot;Which, when you get down to it, is the whole problem: we don't know the rules. We picked our pieces for this game and didn't even know there <i>was</i> a game. And we still don't know most of the rules, but at least we know there <i>are</i> rules. We need to know if there's more to that contract. Or more to how this whole place works than just 'the whim of the Keeper.'&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Missed a 'made' in there. 08-01-2014, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T16:11:41-07:00","id":216235,"title":"","content":"Nate was taken aback by Max's reasoning. He thought he had scared them enough so they wouldn't be a pain anymore, but it looked like little piggy still had a fight in him.<br /> &quot;Well... I...&quot; This wasn't good. His plan was falling apart. &quot;You're saying the Keeper doesn't care about us being happy, but you don't know. After all, you only met him when you were trying to escape, of course you pissed him off and got punished! I'd do the same to my pets!&quot; If he had stopped here, maybe he would have realized what an humiliation this was. &quot;He can be kind! Look, you asked him nicely, and he gave us this beautiful ranch! If we cooperate and behave, I'm sure he'll reward us.&quot;<br /> <br /> He tried to appear sincere, but he realized something that scared him. Deep inside, he didn't need to try. His animal instinct believed it was true, life would be easier if he would simply obey the Keeper and play his part in this collection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T20:29:19-07:00","id":216389,"title":"","content":"Jessica shook her head. &quot;We can't think that way. I admit that I can't understand the mind of the keeper. But I'll bet if the keeper rewards us, it's to control us, to keep us passive. Don't you even want to get back to your old life, Nate?&quot;<br /> <br /> As she asked this question, Jessica thought heard something. Looking, she thought she saw one of the other captives, maybe the tiger, creeping closer to them through the surreal foliage. The marrow of her bones went cold. Was the tiger trying to stalk them? She looked again to make sure, but saw nothing. Maybe she was just imagining things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T21:55:35-07:00","id":216430,"title":"","content":"(This looks like a good time to get back in, was looking for a way to integrate this anyways!)<br /> <br /> <br /> The creature who had been noticed by Jessica was not the Tiger she had assumed at first. It was, however, a fairly large cat, and as it began to make it's presence noticed, it was clear the creature was a hybrid animal like them. A Lion, to be precise, a fierce and regal looking cat man who displayed an heir of nobility. Judging from his appearance, he was stark naked, but everything below the waist was cleverly hidden behind the leaves of one of the fluorescent bushes he had been crouched under. Regardless, the muscle tone on his arms and torso was clear indication he was at least twice as strong as any of them if it came to a fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, so he's moved onto the Chinese Zodiac?&quot; the lion asked nobody in particular. As he leered at the trio of farm animals, he licked his lips as if savoring the moment, before regaining his composure. &quot;I'm a member of the western Zodiac, I represent Leo.&quot; he introduced himself, &quot;And I couldn't help but overhear you're trying to escape.&quot; he grinned, flashing those long, predatory teeth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T22:37:47-07:00","id":216488,"title":"","content":"Fighting her fear, Jessica took forward. &quot;And if we were? I really don't see what business it is of yours!&quot; <br /> <br /> Jessica ran out of words, and she felt her breath catch in her thought. Her heart pounded. She realized that she found herself attracted to Leo, despite the fear he inspired in her. He just looked stunning. Her feelings did not bother her. She actually thought her attraction was a good sign. If her thinking had become completely like that of an ox, she would never have any desire for anything like a lion. Her absurd longing for Leo proved that she was still at least part human. Pangs of hunger from multiple stomachs undercut the comfort given to her by realization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T23:02:28-07:00","id":216515,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh, I just thought you'd be interested in hearing the rules of your contract.&quot; the lion said with a shrug, &quot;But if you're going to be rude, I'll just let you figure them out on your own. Maybe I'll pay you a visit at the slaughterhouse next time you step out of line.&quot; he mocked, licking his lips again as he eyed the ox, probably thinking of her as a juicy steak. His hands went to rest on his hips, his tail swaying behind him, rustling nearby bushes.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;These things always have loop holes... if you're smart enough to notice them, that is.&quot; he stated, leering his eyes and grinning wider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-01T23:19:59-07:00","id":216532,"title":"","content":"Max was distracted from the discussion. The sudden appearance of a newcomer would have done it at the best of times. When said newcomer looked like he could break any of the three in half and eat them -- and might be mulling over just that -- it sort of swept all other matters to the side. He gulped, took a step back -- reflexively falling into a defensive stance (for all the good it would do him) -- and tried to get a handle on the fear rushing through him. He'd be sweating buckets, if he still had sweat glands.<br /> <br /> Still, the mention of loopholes caught him by surprise. &quot;W-Wait!&quot; The pig half-squealed, waving his arms a bit. He was quite unsure what to do. &quot;W-We're sorry for any rudeness. We want to hear what you have to say.&quot; He paused and then coughed. &quot;And, uh... Again, no disrespect, but if you could... m-maybe see your way to not looking at us like a buffet line? That would be great, too.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor edit! 08-02-2014, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T00:51:27-07:00","id":216589,"title":"","content":"Nate began to answer Jessica's question. &quot;Of course I'd want to go back, but we can't! I'd rather--&quot; He interrupted himself when the Leo emerged from the delicious grass -<i>wait, what?!</i>- and began taunting them. He had to shut down the little bleating voice in his mind urging him to bolt to the nearest tall tree. Instead, he gulped but stood his ground, and tried to make himself bigger, wielding his horns as a threat. Yeah, you're not a mere sheep, you're the Ram, another voice said, maybe his, he wasn't sure.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, looks like you've quite adjusted to your part in your Zodiac. Do all your colleagues feel the same way?&quot;<br /> <br /> He was glad to have been chosen for the Chinese collection, as he was a Cancer. Better being a ram than being part crab. Some part of him wanted to meet them. Maybe they would feel more at ease, hearing what older prisoners have to say. And he could meet the Aries, a kin! And of course, he couldn't wait to bump into the Virgo...it's been so long since he had seen a truly female human body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-02-2014, 07:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T03:05:35-07:00","id":216631,"title":"","content":"&quot;The longer you stick around, the more influence this place has on you.&quot; Leo replied to Nate, &quot;Suffice it to say, I've been here long enough to take up permanent residence.&quot; he crossed his arms, turning his attention back to Max before continuing.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Unfortunately for me, if he's building a new Zodiac, it means he's losing interest in my group. The special treatment we've been getting is likely to come to a halt. So rather than be thrown away like some used hand-me-down, I'm going to give you a chance to escape.&quot; he explained, once more licking his lips.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The terms for the contract are as follows, and I suggest you listen to my words very carefully.&quot; he began, &quot;The first customers to buy the Zodiac figurines agrees to come to Arcadia and take on their forms. That is the terms of agreement you unknowingly signed when you bought your figurines.&quot; he said. His tail swished the bushes again, his lower regions still being hidden behind the leaves.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Take a while to mull it over, I'm sure the answer will become clear to you...&quot; he commented.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T04:36:15-07:00","id":216650,"title":"","content":"Nate didn't care for riddles. He'd always hated them, but the Pig and the Oxen seemed to be interested in finding loopholes. Good for them, good for him. They would do his job, he'll just have to follow them. Although...<br /> <br /> &quot;...I don't trust you.&quot; He said to Leo, a cocky smile on his face. &quot;If you know the answer to get out of here, what stopped you from leaving? The Keeper's just finished building this ranch, so it's not just because you like running nude in the high grass, right? And if you want us to go, why don't you give us a straight answer, instead of riddling us?&quot; He didn't notice, but he instinctively bared his teeth, showing animal aggressiveness to the Lion. &quot;You're just doing this to mess with our heads, so we can fail and become prey for you!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T06:03:05-07:00","id":216709,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's like I said,&quot; the Lion replied matter of factly, &quot;You being here is a sign that the Keeper is losing interest in the rest of us, and I don't want that to happen. Whether you live in paradise or hell is entirely up to how much he likes you.&quot; he explained, &quot;And just because I know a loop hole in the contract, doesn't mean I can find the exit.&quot; he added. &quot;Reality is an illusion here, the world is constantly shifting. Becoming... lost... is very easy.&quot; he grinned mischievously as he hesitated to say the word.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;And I can't just flat out tell you the answer, if word got out, I'd be in trouble. Best to let you solve the mystery on your own.&quot; he turned his back to them, winking at them as he did so before crouching beneath the leaves and slinking off to wherever it was he had come from. The leaves barely rustled as he did so, it was no wonder he had crept up so easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T13:14:49-07:00","id":216841,"title":"","content":"Max understood that bit about 'more influence.' He'd had some strange and distressing thoughts every now and then, so knowing it wasn't just him was a help. Also a harm. &quot;S-so... We're just going to think more and more like our animals the longer we stay here?&quot; It was bad enough <i>looking</i> like a pig. Just earlier that day he'd found a little mud pool and had been tempted to go roll around in it. That these inclinations might get worse was very unwelcome news. To say nothing of the other animals: the lion was clearly holding himself back, and this was just a few minutes for a chat! Even if, say, the tiger had an iron will, it would only take a moment's slip-up. And they'd be in close quarters a <i>lot</i> longer than just a few minutes.<br /> <br /> So Max took the lion-man's advice and listened to every word. <i>'Arcadia... So that's where we are?'</i> He rolled the words around in his head, hoping to turn something up as he nodded. &quot;Thanks for the help. And the risk.&quot; He didn't know what sort of tortures the guy had gone through, but didn't need more than guesses like &quot;becoming countless lion skin rugs&quot; or &quot;spending ages as a head mounted on a wall.&quot; Still, while more than he'd like to admit was glad to see the maned predator leave, he had another question. He took a deep breath and tried to calm himself as he stepped forward. <i>'Oh, quit shaking! It's not... not <b>that</b> scary...'</i> he told himself, completely unconvinced before the terrified squealing in his heart. The snoutful of the carnivore's scent would do that to the poor little piggy.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just uh... Just a moment more. How'd you get here, anyway?&quot; It had puzzled Max. &quot;I tried looking for the road that brought us here and the next thing I knew I was on the other side of the ranch. Is there some kind of trick to it?&quot; Another thought then struck him, ears visibly perking. He wasn't actually sure he wanted to know the answer, but, well... Knowledge was power, and they needed every bit they could get.<br /> <br /> &quot;A-And... One last thing. It was the year of the Horse when we were taken and...&quot; He didn't want to refer to any of them as animals, but he had no other name. &quot;... and we haven't seen the Horse in a long time. You guys are on a shorter cycle, right? So...&quot; The pig's eyes drifted toward Nate's for a moment. &quot;... So what happens when it's time for your sign?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Paragraph break! 08-02-2014, 04:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T13:31:19-07:00","id":216856,"title":"","content":"Jessica hoped that Leo would return Max's questions. As waited, she wondered if her solution was right. It seemed to fit the wording of the contract. Yet, even if they become the third customer, would they not still be the first? However, any other solution seemed to elude her. If Leo did not return, maybe the three of them should try to follow him. At that moment, she wished that she had the keen nose of a pig. At least she had read somewhere that pigs had senses of smell greater than those of even dogs. It was how they hunted truffles, if she remembered right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-02T15:04:54-07:00","id":216981,"title":"","content":"&quot;There's always a path, don't trust your first impressions!&quot; Leo's voice replied, it was growing fainter, indicating he was spanning the distance away from them. &quot;When it's your turn, you get to wander the realm, and that's when the real fun starts.&quot; he laughed at the end as his voice faded away completely, he was gone, leaving them to ponder his words. One could only wonder what the lion man would have considered to be fun, considering what they had glimpsed of this place so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T03:15:41-07:00","id":217308,"title":"","content":"Nate eased up at Leo's departure, but wondered about his words. What did he mean by wandering the realm? What realm? Arcadia? Suddenly, he wasn't sure about wanting to go next. Leo was right : his urges were getting stronger and stronger; and he didn't want to risk losing himself to the brain-washing magic of this world. Although, the little bleating voice in his head tried to reassure him. That's right, he thought. For all the madness and horror in this place, there is also wonder. He just had to look around him : this ranch was gorgeous. He wouldn't mind staying here. He didn't have to chance to explore it yet! They should lay low for a while, and wait for a window of opportunity, but for now, they should enjoy it. They were seeing things an human wouldn't ever dream of! <br /> <br /> &quot;I still don't trust him&quot;, he said to his two hoofed colleagues. &quot;He's clearly getting desperate to get the Keeper's attention again, just like a cat wanting to get petted. If he's losing interest in them, that means we're safe as long as we behave, and there's no need to rush ourselves, we'd only run into more troubles and tortures. We should play along for now, and be the nice Beasts the Keeper wants us to be.&quot; Yeah. This plan felt right. Just play along for now. &quot;Of course, we'll have to focus on keeping our humanity. But as long as we're aware of this place's influence on our mind, that shouldn't be a problem.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T15:11:05-07:00","id":217597,"title":"","content":"Max likewise relaxed with the Leo's exit; he hadn't realized he'd had his legs tight as a coiled spring, ready to bolt. Perhaps it was the new feeling of calm that made Nate's suggestion seem more palatable than it otherwise might. He certainly bristled at the thought of doing what the Keeper wanted and just being good little animals, but well... Things had been so hard, and it would be <i>so</i> <i>easy</i> not to rock the boat, now that it was out of stormy waters. They'd suffered so much; didn't they deserve a little happiness? Just for a bit? &quot;I...&quot; he began uncomfortably, &quot;I... don't know if I agree with <i>everything</i>, but I see a point. I mean, after all we've been through, we're all really stressed out. I think we <i>should</i> grab some R&amp;R while we can. It'll clear our heads, make it easier to think of a way out. It's... it's just for a while, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> The pig visibly relaxed further. He didn't quite pick up on how &quot;laze about and indulge&quot; was the basic plan in question, nor how it perfectly lined up with his subtle swinish inclinations. &quot;But I think we can trust the guy. It sounds a lot like what the Keeper was saying before. The way out might be something like Jessica's idea -- pretty sure you caught that one.&quot; Max looked at Nate's large ears, and flopped his own pair for emphasis. &quot;If we're waiting, we can just mull it all over.&quot;<br /> <br /> At this point, he took a deep breath. The air smelled just as good here as it had when he'd arrived, and he was actually glad to have such a keen nose. As Jessica quietly suspected, he could even smell generally where the lion had gone off, but was mostly focused on how much nicer it smelled without him. Actually, around here, it was even more appealing than before. He worked his snout a moment more, and managed to zero in on the particular. Distracted and unthinking, Max turned his head away from the other two farm animals and began sniffing at the air, toward a tree. Or, more precisely, something growing near its roots. Jessica had also been quite right about pigs and truffles. Though this little piggy wasn't finding it so much of a blessing, as a trickle started to drip down from the side of his mouth.<br /> <br /> Catching himself with a grunt, Max shook his head and swallowed the excess saliva. He blushed at this embarrassing display. &quot;Aw, man...&quot; he groaned. &quot;I... I don't know how easy keeping our humanity is gonna be here...&quot; He tried not to think about the fungi, but his snout still sang its treacherous siren song. &quot;I'm... really scared about that.&quot; He looked between the Ox and Sheep, as though for support. &quot;H-Have you guys gone through anything like... like that?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T20:32:39-07:00","id":217841,"title":"","content":"Jessica thought about Max's question. After a moment, she said, &quot;I think I'm still all right. I don't think I'm thinking like an ox. For example, I had rather un-oxen thoughts about Leo. He was hot! Still, I'd be the first to admit that I really don't know much about how oxen think. I'm a city girl, not a farm girl. I'm really not sure. Still, my new body is weird. I'll admit that. As to waiting, I'm not sure that's a good idea.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica shook her head. Were oxen stubborn, or was that just donkeys and mules? Maybe she was thinking like an ox, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typoes 08-03-2014, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-03T22:03:25-07:00","id":217883,"title":"","content":"Nate scoffed at Max's inquiry. &quot;Come on man, you're human. You can't be seriously thinking about rolling in the mud or whatever pigs do.&quot; He was putting on a brave facade, even lying to himself. &quot;As for me, no, I'm not feeling weird impulses. I mean, sure, I have to chew my food for what seems forever and I could really use a haircut, but I'm feeling sane in my mind. I'm stronger than you think.&quot; He hoped that thinking this would shield him against any brainwashing attempt. The body's a plaything of the mind, or whatever, right? Goat were stubborn too, so bring it on, Keeper.<br /> <br /> He frowned at Jessica's remark. &quot;You're finding a lion-man hot? What are you, a furry or something?&quot; Tch, typical. He couldn't trust the female. She just wanted another male. You'd think she'd prefer the Taurus, though. Wait a minute, was he jealous? Maybe he was, yeah, but jealousy's a human feeling, right? That ought to be good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-04-2014, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T15:41:46-07:00","id":218573,"title":"","content":"Blushing, Jessica retorted, &quot;Whatever, Nate. Leo was hot, and my seeing that means that I'm not thinking like an ox, but a woman.&quot;<br /> <br /> With that, Jessica started off. She realized neither of them were yet willing to risk her plan. Fighting with them about it just risked drawing the keeper's notice. She shook her head. Her plan might not have worked anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T16:04:38-07:00","id":218592,"title":"","content":"Seemingly out of nowhere, the high pitched tingling of a bell could be heard throughout the ranch and shortly afterward, something began to appear out of the ground in front of the collected Zodiac. It appeared to be feeding time, because the objects that emerged were definitely food. However it wasn't exactly people food, so much as animal food. Raw slabs of meat appeared for the carnivorous members of the collection, still wet with fresh blood, it was probably best not to think about where the meat had come from.<br /> <br /> <br /> To Jessica and Nate, a pair of feed bags appeared at their feet -or rather hooves- with straps to fasten them around their faces while they ate. For max, a feeding trough appeared to be filled with an assortment of so many different samples of food, it coalesced into a brownish slop, making it nearly impossible to discern one ingredient from the other. Apparently their Keeper intended to feed them like beasts, as well as make them look like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T22:07:11-07:00","id":218849,"title":"","content":"Nate openly laughed at Jessica's exit, seems like he had struck a nerve. He was cut short by the bell, and gulped out of nervousness when their respective meals appeared. Looking at Max's trough, he wrinkled his nose a bit in disgust, and had, for once, a little bit of compassion for the poor guy. Nate opened his own bag, and saw a mix of leaves and grass. It looked good, like a big salad, and he soon remarked that it smelled really good too. He crouched down, and picked two leaves from the bag, before looking at poor Max.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dude, I'm sorry, but we have to do this. You know the Keeper's watching us right now, and this is a test. If we want to survive and not get punished, we have to force ourselves. Besides, if we don't eat, we'll likely starve or be too weak to escape potential danger.&quot;<br /> <br /> He looked around, and instinctively lowered his head, feeling as if the Collector was watching them. &quot;Look, just think about something typically human to focus on while eating. Like...I don't know, maths, grammar, law, or a tv show or whatever.&quot; As he said that, he put the leaves in his mouth and started to chew. He followed his own advice, and chose to focus on music theory. He tried to remember his favourite song from his band, the Wild Exhibit --<i>Oh, the irony</i>--, and began to mentally rehearse it.<br /> After chewing for quite a long time, he gulped, and found that it hadn't been so terrible. He could do this. Being a musician could help in this realm, who knew? He took more forage, and slowly began to empty his bag. He wouldn't put the straps though. Eating this was humiliating enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-04T22:43:56-07:00","id":218859,"title":"","content":"Jessica's revealed attraction surprised him a bit. 'How... How do you think about having the hots for someone at a time like this?' The idea also made Max wonder, just a bit, whether she wasn't being as honest with herself about her bestial side affecting her. Animals weren't exactly shy about making their affections known. Which he felt, on second thought, was maaaaaybe a bit sexist. <i>' &quot;Oh, a woman getting attracted quickly? Clearly animal urges at work!&quot; Ugh, the hell am I thinking...'</i> He did feel better about rolling his eyes at the Sheep, though. &quot;Oh, for crying out loud, Nate, just--&quot;<br /> <br /> But that was as far as Max got before they all heard &quot;the dinner bell.&quot; He looked around, curious what was coming. Also concerned; part of him had been waiting for the other shoe to drop. He smelled it before he saw it, and couldn't smell much of anything else. A great trough, full of... Yeah, he really didn't want to think. It looked vile. He could hardly imagine anything more unpleasant trying to pass itself off as food. His food. Which made it particularly uncomfortable that much as it smelled as foul and overpowering as it looked... Part of him also found it fascinating. Comfortable. Right.<br /> <br /> &quot;... No,&quot; Max told... well, the universe itself at this point. &quot;No no no. No. Just... No. You have got to be kidding me.&quot; The protests were a bit hard to swallow, of course. His snout was plainly intrigued by the contents. Nate's counsel didn't do much for his resolve, either. &quot;... I... I know.&quot; He trembled. &quot;And... And that's not bad advice. I'll try that. Thanks. Let's uh, just... get through this.&quot; A bubble drifted up from the brown sludge. He shuddered. &quot;Bon app\u00e9tit...&quot; he said sardonically, taking a seat at the edge of the trough. &quot;Just, uh... Do me a solid, ah? H-Hit me if I look like I'm enjoying this.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max looked down at his meal. There was a faint temptation to plunge his face into it, but he held strong, there. Not that he was sure of how to eat it. He glanced at Nate's efforts and felt a twinge of envy. <i>'It's like he's just eating a bag of chips...'</i> He dipped his hand in, hesitantly, and found some resistance in places. He pulled out what looked like most of a carrot, still dripping brown. <i>'Okay... Okay... You got this. Just. Think of Black Adder annnnnd one, two, ... three.'</i> Max bit into it. It was the mushiest carrot he'd ever had, likely half-rotten. And significantly tastier than it had any right to be. <i>'... Dammit.'</i> He finished the rest of that handful quickly, nearly licking his fingers. He then cupped an especially liquid section in his hands and awkwardly tipped it into his mouth. Much messier, but again, not half-bad. Enough for him to repeat the maneuver twice more, before the line, &quot;A man with a small, painted, wooden duck on his head,&quot; brought him back to himself. He licked his chops and checked his progress. The trough was still quite full. <i>'This is gonna be a loooooong meal...'</i> he thought with a sigh, picking out what appeared to be a corn husk. He decided it beat out the tamales at his roommate's favorite restaurant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T05:49:34-07:00","id":218981,"title":"","content":"After a bit, Jessica picked up her feed bag. Her extra stomachs gave her little choice. She had to eat. It was not what she was used to eating, but it hardly bothered her. She realized that she found the thought of eating meat sickening. Maybe it was because of her slaughter house experience, but it might also be the result of being part oxen. Either way, she felt better after she ate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T13:12:30-07:00","id":219377,"title":"","content":"Halfway through his meal, Nate took a short break, and reflected on this experience. Compared to Max, he certainly had it easy. At least he didn't have any rotten food in his bag. He did found some snails, but he picked them up and threw them away, before realizing that they may be people too. He didn't feel especially for them. Sucks to be them, but he couldn't apologize and be compassionate to everything in this place, he wouldn't dare lift a finger otherwise!<br /> <br /> His internal singing relaxed him, and took his mind away from this ordeal. In fact, he noticed that he had absent-mindedly synchronized his mastication with the beats of the music. It wasn't so bad. Sure, it got boring pretty quickly, especially with all the chewing, but it was pretty peaceful. In fact, it even reminded him of a vegetarian restaurant Valerie took him to. He'd hated it back then. But now that he had this newfound aversion for meat...<br /> <br /> He let out a bleating sigh and looked up at his dining neighbour. &quot;How are you holding up, buddy?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-05-2014, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T21:30:35-07:00","id":219822,"title":"","content":"Max had also gotten to around his halfway mark by this time. He'd also probably already eaten a greater volume than Nate's or Jessica's feedbags held in total. Maybe even combined. There was just... a <i>lot</i> of slop in there. It struck him as extraordinarily unfair; he was a city boy, but he'd always thought a full trough was usually intended for several pigs at once. In a fair world, Max would have already... ... No, scratch that. In a fair world, Max <i>wouldn't have had to eat any</i>. Nor would any of them for that matter.<br /> <br /> But alas, the world wasn't so fair. And so not only did Max eat the horrible stuff, he ate at quite a rapid pace, looking all the more so next to Nate's. Anything solid he pulled out disappeared within a few bites. As for the liquid, well... The poor Pig had kept to his aim of not gorging snout to trough in true porcine fashion -- though the practicality and temptation yet lingered. But anyone who hadn't been looking might at first assume otherwise, what with the splashes and speckles of slop-water on his face and front.<br /> <br /> He'd also unfortunately found his thoughts drifting away from British comedies, mental course reviews, and other strictly human things. He'd instead gone with an almost perverse fascination to deciphering what was in his trough, like some sort of puzzle. It would have been impossible for anyone without his snout, and Max actually found himself impressed. Despite how thoroughly mashed up all the food (and &quot;food&quot;) had become, he could still pick out individual scents if he tried. If noses were computers, it was as though he'd had his human model replaced with one that had abandoned all sense of style for raw power. <i>'It <b>better</b> be good for that,'</i> he thought morosely. <i>'It's certainly using enough facial real estate...'</i><br /> <br /> Lost in his thoughts, Max was shaken out of it by Nate's question. The Pig had a big mouthful of... oh, something that had probably been green and leafy, long ago. Suddenly self-conscious, he awkwardly swallowed it down, and wound up coughing a bit for his trouble. Breathing deep, he appreciated the excuse to turn from the trough and talk to someone. &quot;Sorry. Um, oh, you know...&quot; he said, putting on a brave face, &quot;I'm doing alright.&quot; He felt something stuck on his face, just outside his lower jaw. He brought a slop-stained finger to the site and found a leaf had gotten stuck in one of his little tusks. With a porcine grunt of annoyance, he plucked it free and flicked it away. &quot;It's... pretty disgusting. But it really doesn't taste as bad as it looks. It... honestly doesn't taste that bad at all...&quot; He coughed again, the brave face eroding a bit. &quot;I'm... I'm sorta deciding whether that's a good thing or not... And really hoping I don't have to eat <i>all</i> of it...&quot; He licked his chops. A groan with a hint of a squeal made clear how he wished he hadn't.<br /> <br /> &quot;Anyway!&quot; Max forged on, eager to not to dwell on it. &quot;Thanks for asking. Really. I know this can't be easy for any of us, so... Uh, so, how about you? How are you handling this?&quot; The concern was genuine, even if he also welcomed the chance to get out of his own head. Or pick up another coping mechanism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 08-06-2014, 12:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-05T22:30:38-07:00","id":219847,"title":"","content":"Nate found himself looking intently at the little leaf falling from Max's tusks, before sitting down and shrugging.<br /> &quot;I guess it's not so bad. You know, I was used to smoking weed, but I've never thought I would be eating buckets of it!&quot; He forced himself to laugh at his own joke, but the bleating that came out was somewhat sad.<br /> &quot;I...I don't like what I'm about to say but... I could get used to that. I... I like chewing this stuff.&quot; He rubbed his head, ashamed, but when the Ram inadvertently touched one horn, he jerked and brought his hands back to his furry knees, which wasn't actually better, as it was a reminder of how natural his fur felt.<br /> &quot;Weirdly enough, eating this reminds me of my girlfriend. She was a vegetarian. I guess I can kinda see the appeal now...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-06-2014, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-06T21:31:56-07:00","id":220722,"title":"","content":"Max forced a laugh of his own at the joke, with roughly as sincere a smile. He certainly wasn't going to <i>discourage</i> an attempt to lighten the mood. Even if the sound of Nate's bleat of a laugh had been, well, maybe a little depressing. Still, there was a bit of relief mixed in with the younger man's sympathy. <i>'At least I'm not the only one making animal noises.'</i><br /> <br /> The next remarks and physical display held Max's full attention. The ram had previously struck him as fairly untouchable, with all that bravado in the way. He found a very different story in the look of disgrace at his admission of enjoyment and clear discomfort with his own body. &quot;I... I think I know the feeling.&quot; From his seat, he pulled his knees near to his chest, and wrapped his arms around them. He tilted his head toward the trough. &quot;Just thinking about this... this stuff, well, kinda makes me wanna puke. And it should. I mean, it's <i>actual</i> <i>swill</i>.&quot; The indignant tone went as quickly as it had come. &quot;But, but more than that... I... Part of me wants to... just...&quot; His voice cracked a moment. &quot;... just dunk my head in and eat until I've licked the damn thing clean.&quot; The pig shook as he apparently tried to bury his guilty face in his knees. &quot;So... I think I get you.&quot;<br /> <br /> The next bit got a wince out of Max. &quot;Ouch, you've got a girl back home? That's ...&quot; He gave up on finding the right word. There wasn't one, just something in the ballpark. &quot;That's terrible. You must--&quot; Aaaand the little swine stopped himself there. He tried to figure out how to backpedal from a direction that could only depress them both. His tactic of choice involved jumping at another question, further away. &quot;I mean... What's her name?&quot; Yes, pigs were not especially well known for their long jump.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor tweaks. 08-07-2014, 01:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T11:39:26-07:00","id":221146,"title":"","content":"After she finished eating, Jessica came to regret her show of temper. It made all the sense in the world that Nate would look with askance at her attraction to Leo. The lion man was obviously dangerous. Desiring him made no sense. Jessica also realized she had made another mistake. She disclosed too much to Nate too soon after meeting him. She should have shown more caution. One had to be wary.<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe I am starting to think like an ox,&quot; mused Jessica, dismayed by her timid thoughts. <br /> <br /> Perhaps to strike out in the opposite direction, Jessica started to wonder if she should try her escape idea with another of the prisoners. If it worked, Nate and Max would be free to use it themselves. Only Nate's theory about group punishment held her back.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T13:37:36-07:00","id":221247,"title":"","content":"&quot;Technically, you're wrong. I <i>had</i> a girl back home, but I dumped Valerie the day I got the figurine.&quot; He had felt some remorse then, but now... &quot;She lied to me.&quot; Nate shrugged. He didn't need to tell Max about the kid. What was the point? Besides, she could do fine on her own, she should be motherly enough. <i>Like all females should be</i>, the voice in his mind added. He didn't argue with it, or even tried to slap himself out of it. The voice was kinda right after all, wasn't it?<br /> <br /> He changed the subject. &quot;Anyway, about the food, I get you too. Well, somewhat. I don't want to throw myself into a trough of forage, but... when I eat this, the mastication relaxes me so much that I almost want to doze off.&quot; Looking at the straps, he wondered if one day he would be too far gone to not refuse putting these around his head. He shueddered but tried to make a brave face. &quot;Almost. I won't, of course. Being aware of the animal influence on our minds is the first step to resisting it, so it's good that you admit that. You're not like this oxen-girl, who's clearly confused. If we follow her plan, we'll likely fail due to her weakening willpower. She's going nuts man.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-08-2014, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-07T14:27:58-07:00","id":221267,"title":"","content":"While the three of them may have been pacing out their meals, the carnivores were not so hesitant. But then again, that may have been due to their species not having to chew for so long. Already the piles of fresh meat were nearly gone, some of them beginning to squabble over the last slices. It seemed their hesitation to enjoy their meals would cost them a full stomach, because once the last shred of meat vanished down the tiger's throat, meal time seemed to be finished. The trough began to recede back into the ground and the feed bags started to fade away into nothingness, along with their remaining contents!<br /> <br /> <br /> The message seemed to be rather obvious, adhering to polite manners would only lead to starvation. A message they would have to keep in mind during the next feeding, whenever that may be!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T00:50:27-07:00","id":222931,"title":"","content":"When the bags started to fade, the Ram's eyes widened, and he desperately tried to grab a handful of leaves but failed, as his hand passed through his past meal. He looked around frantically to see if he didn't spill any anything from the bag earlier that could have remained here, but soon even those bits of forage had disappeared. <i>No no no no no, I'm still hungry!</i> The Beast took a quick scan around him and relaxed slightly. That's right, he was in an open field, he could just munch on the grass around here. He'd almost decided to go on four legs to the nearest bush, but when he laid eyes on Max, Nate woke up from his hungry trance, cursed himself, and got up. What had just <i>happened</i>?! He was horrified at how strong the instincts had been. His four stomachs were groaning, and he somehow knew that this hunger would be at the forefront of his mind all day, unless he took care of it.<br /> But not right here. Not in front of the kid. He had just been boasting about being strong, shielding your mind, yadda yadda, but it was simply bullshit. He couldn't let the piggy see it.<br /> &quot;Well, mealtime's over. Looks like we'll need to be quicker next time. Was nice speaking with you, Max. I'm gonna take a walk, and explore the ranch. See ya around!&quot; And with that, he leaved his friend, hoping to put some distance between them, so he could indulge in his hunger with the minimum amount of shame.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T04:39:32-07:00","id":223124,"title":"","content":"Max winced again on hearing about the breakup over deception. He couldn't really think of anything to add but a sympathetic look, so such was all he did. Though Nate still had things to say. Most of them made sense, and honestly had Max feeling a bit relieved. Thinking there was someone having similar urges, but with the strength to defy them -- and the belief that <i>he</i> could defy them, too -- gave him more hope than he'd had. &quot;You're right,&quot; he said, smiling a bit, &quot;If we stare the animal side head-on, it can't take over so easy. Thanks.&quot; Though the bit about Jessica did make him wrinkle his snout a bit. &quot;Well... Yeah, she's confused. But who isn't, here? Her plan's risky, but her idea's pretty--&quot;<br /> <br /> Max turned in time to see his trough sinking. Like Nate with his bag, he lurched toward it and tried to shovel a last few scoops of slop down his throat. Also like Nate, he found his hand brushing the grass on the other side. <i>'Aww, c'mon! No warning?'</i> He took a deep breath and let out a sigh. Part of it was frustration at the meal getting away, while the rest was relief. He wouldn't wind up shoving his head into that garbage today. And surely he would be fine until the next feeding: he'd never eaten nearly as much in one sitting. Only one issue... <i>'... Why don't I feel very full?'</i> Perhaps the full trough really <i>was</i> a serving size to his new swinish appetite. In a moment's panic, Max was grateful he'd been a messy eater. He began scooping up what slop detritus he could off of snout, stomach, and limbs, and into his mouth. It was maybe a third of a mouthful altogether, and quickly swallowed. Getting something more in him helped enough to calm down.<br /> <br /> Still, even if Max wasn't especially hungry, he knew it wouldn't be as long as he'd like before his stomach was rumbling for more. <i>'Aw, man... Pleeease don't let me root around in the dirt for truffles...'</i> he asked of any who might have listened. He then noticed Nate looking his way. It was an odd look; Max had no idea how to place it. Without thinking, he found himself tilting his head to one side at Nate, like a questioning puppy (or piglet). To be answered with a surprise notice of departure.<br /> <br /> &quot;Huh? Uh.&quot; He turned his gaze toward where he knew the truffles were buried. &quot;W-Wait!&quot; Max said, scrambling back up onto this hooves. Moving felt a bit awkward after all he'd eaten, but he made it up just fine, and followed after Nate a bit. &quot;Hey, uh, n-no reason we've gotta part ways right away, r-right? I mean, uh...&quot; He took a breath. &quot;I'm sorry. I-I don't mean to be a burden. It's just, you're so strong.&quot; The pig turned his gaze down and away. &quot;And I'm really, <i>really</i> not. I... I need help.&quot; He looked up to Nate cautiously, putting on a nervous smile. &quot;You know I still mean what I said before, right, about smacking me upside the head if I started to go a little... h... h-hog wild?&quot; The kid tried for a forced laugh after the 'joke,' but the emerging oinks worked about as well as Nate's laugh-turned-bleat. It only further revealed the anxiety he was already not hiding especially well. &quot;Just... It would really help to have someone sop me where I need it. C-Could I tag along? Please?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor adjustment. 08-09-2014, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T15:59:31-07:00","id":223677,"title":"","content":"Nate gritted his teeth. He had brought this upon himself, making himself so strong in front of the kid. He didn't want to be near him right now. But he needed help, and what could he say? No, don't follow me, I don't want you to see me devour some bushes? Strangely enough, it was Max's oinks that got to him. Someone was counting on him. Besides, he didn't really want to be alone if he encountered the Tiger or Leo again.<br /> &quot;...alright, you can come. Let's try to find something nice around here, like, I dunno, a spring, an orchard...a place we can claim as our headquarters, you know?&quot; For the first time since he came to Arcadia, he offered a sincere smile to someone, trying to encourage Max. He needed the Pig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-09T21:30:14-07:00","id":223846,"title":"","content":"Max let out a heavy sigh of relief and smiled back. &quot;Thanks. I can't tell you how much that helps.&quot; He nodded as he caught up to Nate, the suggestions cheering him. &quot;And good idea. There's gotta be more to this place than we've seen. If we find some good fruit trees or something, that should have us set for food. And I don't know about you, but I'm kinda thirsty after all that.&quot; He could also do with a bath, frankly. It bugged him to have little lingering traces of slop. His nose might have been more sensitive than the others', but he figured the stuff would still smell foul enough to them -- on top of any other natural odor he'd picked up. If the Sheep was being nice enough to let him tag along, he could at least not make it an unpleasant olfactory experience.<br /> <br /> Speaking of smells, as they walked, Max figured he might as well put his snout to good use. Well, reluctantly. Still, he owed Nate for the help, so he wanted to do what little he could. &quot;Uh... Look, this is kind of embarrassing, but... I'm gonna... sniff around a little. I-It might help us find fruit or water or something.&quot; Smiling sheepishly, he patted the bridge of his snout. &quot;Heh, I mean, as long as I've got this stupid thing, we might as well get <i>some</i> use out of it, right? Just... call me on it if I get a little too interested in anything I shouldn't, okay?&quot; He'd just keep on alert, sniffing the air from time to time, steering them toward anything that might interest them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 08-10-2014, 12:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T05:20:25-07:00","id":224045,"title":"","content":"After a time, Jessica decided to go see how Max and Nate were doing. It may have been rude for her to wander off from them. She needed to control her temper, if she could. She decided she should also look for some water. Before she found Nate or Max, she found a babbling brook. The water looked perfectly clear, allowing her to see tiny fish every color of the rainbow darting about in the swift current. She even saw equally colorful crayfish lurking among the rocks at bottom. She took a long drink. Never in her life had water tasted so perfect. The more she drank, the less escaping seemed important to her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T07:30:59-07:00","id":224094,"title":"","content":"The Ram tried to repress a laugh at Max's idea. The kid had a good point, but Nate couldn't help but find it silly. Still, it was better than nothing, and he wondered if his new body offered him some new skills. He had already figured out he could wield his horns as a threat, and he was pretty sure he could do some ugly damages with it. What else? His fur might keep him warm in winter, but that wasn't really useful in this ranch. He remembered that he once saw a picture of goats climbing impressive moutain peaks, maybe his legs and hooves would make him a great climber? He didn't really have a way to know, in this grassy field.<br /> <br /> He let Max lead the way through their search. Nate didn't have a keen nose, although he could clearly smell the pig's BO. Strangely enough, that didn't bothered him so much. Sure, Max stank, but he figured that so did he. Their bodies must have been producing a natural musk. He wondered if he could now emit some pheromones, and chuckled at the idea. Unfortunately, his fit of levity was interrupted by the groaning of his stomachs. He needed to eat something, <i>right now</i>. Looking at his fee...hooves, he felt the urge to just drop on all fours and eat all the forage he could see. But with Max around, he couldn't allow that. So he figured out a compromise. He decided to walk slightly behind the kid, and let his hand catch some high grass to slip discreetly in his mouth, like a light snack. Between two chews, he asked Max. &quot;So. What were you doing, back there, in the real world?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-10-2014, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T10:40:16-07:00","id":224261,"title":"","content":"Max caught the amused look on Nate's face and blushed a bit. Not that he blamed the Ram. It <i>was</i> a silly solution, even if it was promising. <i>'Seriously. &quot;Let's follow my nose and find delicious fruit!&quot; Who am I, Toucan Sam?'</i> His shnozz <i>was </i>certainly big enough now. In any case, it was reassuring Nate didn't see an angle that made it too bestial a thing to do. So, much as the sound of his own snuffling about didn't thrill him, he got to it.<br /> <br /> He didn't think much about Nate hanging back just a bit. If Max's snout was taking point, it made sense for him to go in front. Honestly, it was probably for the best. That made it easier for him to pick out promising scents, as Nate <i>did</i> have a powerful smell, now that Max thought about it. All of the Zodiac did. Still, while impossible not to notice and not exactly pleasant, it didn't bother the Pig any more than the Sheep. They were just smells. <i>'I guess you can just get used to everyone having a strong odor to them?</i> <i>Animals don't seem bothered, unless it's a skunk or something.' </i>So, while more suggestions that his mind was changing in ways he hadn't noticed was a touch worrying, well... He'd gladly take <i>this one</i> over gagging through any interaction with the other captives.<br /> <br /> Max might have noticed Nate's sneaking a meal if he'd been trying, but he was focused on what his nose was telling him, not his ears. Though he did hear the question clear enough. &quot;Oh, nothing much. I'm in college, so I was having a lotta fun there. I mean, I'm not much of a party anim-- party <i>guy</i>, but I love the atmosphere. Lotsa cool people and a ton of cool stuff I'm learning. I mean, no idea what I wanna <i>do</i>, but still, fun.&quot; His enthusiasm went up a bit, even if there was a hint of wistfulness. &quot;As for what I was doing the day of... this, well... I'm kinda shy, but I'd finally asked out someone I'd had a crush on for years. It was actually gonna be our first date.&quot; He smiled sadly just thinking about her. &quot;Heh. Honestly, if it weren't for that, I probably wouldn't be here... The little statue was going to be a gift. We've got the same sign, and she's always thought pigs were cute.&quot; He gave another squeal of a sigh. &quot;Pretty sure she wouldn't think a pig is <i>boyfriend</i> material, though.&quot;<br /> <br /> Interrupting Max's resurgent moping, his nose had quite a message for him around then. He slowed, turning his head. He felt kind of ridiculous, but he snuffled thoroughly in the particular direction. His mouth also began to water. &quot;Uh... G-Guess the metal detector's beeping?&quot; he joked, swallowing. &quot;I smell something kinda sweet this way. Let's check it out.&quot; And off he started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T11:51:55-07:00","id":224332,"title":"","content":"<i>Oh, just great. Don't tell me I also have to manage the romantic life of a teenage pig?</i> Nate almost rolled his eyes at Max's plight. Good thing he was behind him. He couldn't just ignore the kid, though. He needed to have allies in this world. So he obliged himself to put an arm around his shoulder in a friendly gesture, he tried to not show his disgust for the pig's body, and he spoke in a reassuring tone. &quot;Come on, man. There's plenty of fish in the sea, they say. And I don't mean fish-women!&quot; He forced a bleating laugh. &quot;So you've changed and she would dump you with your new body. Women are fickle and superficial, Max, that's to be expected. But who cares! I'm sure you'll find a girl who enjoy a man with a spare tire! That's why we have what we call love handles man!&quot; Well, that was a rhetorical we. Nate was used to be fit, and he was seriously glad that his goat body didn't store fat, but even brought some muscles with him. Although there was the fur and the hooves, of course.<br /> When Max found a lead, the Ram patted him on the back and removed his arm. &quot;Good! Now focus on the scent. We can't really do a thing about our girls back home, so why bother?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-11-2014, 12:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T12:32:28-07:00","id":224373,"title":"","content":"((By the way, I check in on this every day. I just pop in when I think there's an opportunity to introduce some ST elements.))<br /> <br /> <br /> The sweet scent would lead them through the bushes to come upon a completely unexpected sight. There in front of them was what appeared to be an oasis, complete with a bathing pond and a water fall cascading down into it from the top of a cliff. Where the waterfall was drawing itself from was a complete mystery, because there didn't seem to be any rivers leading up to it. Surrounding the edge of the pond were rows and rows of various sized mushrooms, and frolicking around the oasis was a collection of enchantingly beautiful women. Women who the boys quickly noticed, were not wearing any clothing to speak of!<br /> <br /> <br /> Those who were on the dry land had pale green skin tones, and hair that was the same vibrant shades as the plants that dotted the landscape. Their ears were pointed like those of an elf, and their bodies were unnaturally lithe and beautiful like they belonged more in a painting than real life. Those who were in the water had a more amphibious appearance, with light blue scales covering their bodies, fin-shaped ears, webbed digits, and hair the color of sea weed. They too had unnaturally beautiful figures and appeared to be having a splash fight with each other while the green women danced about the mushrooms!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T13:51:09-07:00","id":224434,"title":"","content":"Nate literally stood gaping for about a minute, before bursting into a cheerful and vibrant laugh. &quot;Oh man! Max, you have the best nose ever! This is <i>so much</i> better than just finding some fruits!&quot; Everywhere he looked, he saw heaven. He felt a stirring in his loins, and couldn't help himself. He <i>had</i> to have those women. &quot;Watch and learn, kid, watch and learn.&quot; He took off his shirt, did his hair as well as he could manage, groomed his facial hair into some sort of goatee (<i>of course)</i>, and strutted toward the nymphs. He turned up the charm, and he didn't have any problem feel confident, <i>as I should</i>. Unknowingly, he proudly raised his head, displaying his horns for all to see.<br /> &quot;Hello, ladies. I am truly sorry to interrupt your beautiful dance, but my friend and I just arrived in this realm, and we're looking for some nice place to rest. Could we join you? I'm sure we'll have a <i>delicious</i> time together.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-10-2014, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T20:32:39-07:00","id":224796,"title":"","content":"Max did honestly appreciate Nate's gesture. Just... not some of the specifics. &quot;I... What? I-I'm not fat. I'm not! ... Am I?&quot; He looked down at his pink belly. It had been pretty flat before, even had some muscle, and was now... well, less so. Granted, some of it could be chalked up to the huge meal, but aside that, there were simply more pounds on his frame. Even so, he was still positively svelte for a pig. Just... Well, most wouldn't regard the standard as all that high. And, in any case, this was Arcadia: symbolism, assumption, and perception could play much bigger roles than something as petty as objective reality. &quot;... I'm not <i>that</i> fat...&quot; Max mumbled, not enjoying the new source of insecurity. <i>'... I need to train harder...'</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Anyway, I meant less... that, and more... everything else.&quot; Max moved a hand up and down the length of himself for emphasis. &quot;I don't think 'fickle and superficial' is totally fair. Like...&quot; Max tried for an example. &quot;Say you were really into someone. And then she got kidnapped, and came back with, oh, I don't know, horns and hooves. Or, or a... a snout and curly tail. How would <i>you</i> take it?&quot; Still, he nodded at the last bit of advice: there wasn't anything to be done about Karen or anyone else back home for now. Of course, in all fairness -- and only a bit of sour grapes -- Max somehow didn't see a guy with horns, goat legs, and a bleating laugh doing <i>that</i> much better with the ladies than himself, anyway.<br /> <br /> And, wouldn't you know it, the realm then saw fit to provide testing grounds for this hypothesis! The Pig joined the Sheep in gaping at the unclad women. And also in being a bit... interested. Max was certainly blushing more than Nate -- in that he was blushing at all -- and with a somewhat dopey, guilty expression, agreed, &quot;My nose <i>is</i> pretty awesome.&quot; Hell, he even forgave how part of him was really digging the smell of those mushrooms. He barely noticed a bigger part of him that told him how sensuous the lovely ladies smelled. Which isn't to say he was all on board. One voice acidly wanted to remind him of Karen. Another little voice of reason in him took one look at the situation and decided, &quot;This is a trap. Leave this place. Now.&quot; The voices then likely wondered why no action was taken on these urgent matters. Largely because all other voices had abandoned their posts to press their faces up against the window at the loveliness.<br /> <br /> Max watched, but it was questionable what he learned. He ran a hand through his hair, pushing it back in a more presentable fashion, decided that was as good as he'd get, and then awkwardly followed Nate after a bit, smiling bashfully. &quot;Uh, yeah! It's been a long day for us, but... Well, what better place to take a rest than with all this beauty around? Uh, natural -- and otherwise.&quot; Maybe they were big on adorkable in that gathering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-10T21:23:13-07:00","id":224837,"title":"","content":"When Jessica finally had her fill of water, she laid down for a nap. Once again, she dreamed of her three cats searching for her. The dream was oddly comforting. When she woke up, a sudden thought about the contract struck her like lightning. The key to escaping was not what she had thought. No matter how many times her little oxen changed hands, she would still be the original buyer. Her plan was flawed. To escape, she needed to literally change her identity. The one way she knew to do that - at least theory - was through marriage. If she successfully married someone, she would have a identity. In some ways - she hoped enough! - she would no longer be the woman who bought the oxen from the keeper. The contract would be broken.<br /> <br /> Could she do that to Curtis? Jessica shook head. She had no idea. Even if she could betray Curtis, who would she marry? Pondering these things, she started to follow the brook upstream. In time, she came to the same oasis that Max and Nate had discovered earlier. The scandalous tableau that greeted her caused the ox woman to gasp in surprise. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T03:36:15-07:00","id":224966,"title":"","content":"(And the shit now hits the fan!)<br /> <br /> <br /> There before her were Max and Nate laying dazed on the ground after having stuffed their bellies on shrooms and satisfied their base lusts with the many women that surrounded them. Judging by the vacant expressions, the mushrooms had been hallucinogenic, and not the harmless kind you'd put on salads. Only the women were no longer the buxom beauties they had been before. The ones in the water had become hideous fish-women who's fingernails grew into curved claws, their teeth like daggers, and their eyes solid black. The green women proved to be nothing more than bushes which had been sculpted into erotic imagery. As the fish women climbed out of the pool, they advanced upon the exhausted and well fed boys with the obvious intention of devouring them being seen as they clacked their jaws together and hissed with anticipation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-11-2014, 06:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T05:06:54-07:00","id":224983,"title":"","content":"Screaming for Max an Nate to wake up, Jessica charged into the aquatic women. Not at all a fighter, she hoped her new oxen body would aid her. Luckily, it did. Her first blow sent on of the fish women flying to the ground. However, her triumph was short lived. Two of the fish women brought her down to together. Jessica tried to throw them off her. With her oxen strength, she might even have managed it in time. Before she could find out, a third fish women joined the other two in holding her down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  Misread 08-11-2014, 12:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T05:38:02-07:00","id":224995,"title":"","content":"((The green women are just bushes. Basically, they had sex with plants <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ))<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;This one's female!&quot; hissed one of the fish women who was attempting to restrain Jessica, &quot;The spores only affect males.&quot; having trouble matching her physical strength, she began to dig her claws into the oxen's shoulders, hoping that pain would make her more cooperative.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;It matters not!&quot; hissed another, &quot;We outnumber her, and these two are well intoxicated.&quot; there were a total of four of the women, and with three holding her down, that left the last one free to move about. She sauntered her way over to Max and passed a glance back to Jessica. Grinning sadistically, she allowed two claws to playfully dance their way up the boy's chest and to his throat. Clearly she was savoring the moment before the kill, though whether this was a habit of hers or something brought on by having an audience was unknown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T07:12:31-07:00","id":225930,"title":"","content":"((Alright, time for a quick revision due to issues with the time skip))<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>A couple hours earlier at the oasis...</b><br /> <br /> <br /> The ladies gasped in surprise as they turned to see Max and Nate had entered the scene, but after they realized what was going on, they calmed down. In fact, they seemed more than friendly as they giggled and beckoned them over. Two of the green women approached and wrapped their arms around the two as they lead them closer to the pool.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh if you're looking to relax, you've come to the right place!&quot; they said, &quot;The mushrooms are edible, and the water is safe for drinking. You'll also find the grass is very comfortable!&quot; they explained. The blue women seemed to be admiring the pair of them now, having ended their splash fight as they subtly teased them with their exposed bodies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T11:55:01-07:00","id":226172,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh, that's so nice of you!&quot; Nate didn't resist at all, and let himself be led by the green woman. &quot;We're really exhausted, you see. We've been looking for comfort for days!&quot; His gaze was focusing on the women, and especially the one near him. He realized that his bestial nose was also very active, and he could <i>smell</i> the girl's excitement as well as his own. His tail twitched madly, and he almost skipped in glee at the situation. He put his arm around her, and started to grope her slightly. &quot;You know, where I come from, we don't have women as beautiful as you...&quot; By the way where did he come from? He remembered a town, but...well, it certainly didn't matter right now. &quot;We should get to know each other. I can't wait to get intimate with you...&quot; he said, leaning in for a kiss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-13-2014, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T20:53:13-07:00","id":226762,"title":"","content":"Max was more reticent than his hircine companion, but, well, that wasn't a high bar to straddle. His tail, his nose, his eyes, and... other things were doing a lot of the same, the touch of his respective green woman sending a tingle through him. &quot;Ahahahah. Uh, yes. That sounds great.&quot; Not that he was taking much initiative, aside from being led. One drop-dead gorgeous woman swept up to him with a smile. &quot;Well, someone's cute,&quot; she told him, running a finger along his chest. As a shiver went through him, his face turned beet-red as he stammered, &quot;I-I-I-I... I try?&quot; which was met with giggles from the ladies around him. &quot;And funny,&quot; another woman remarked, smile widening. The little pig was <i>well</i> out of his depth, here. Part of him was squealing at him to go for something, but he mostly just went along with a stupid look on his face.<br /> <br /> Max needed guidance. <i>Some</i> kind of an idea what to do. He spotted the Ram's horns over one beauty's shoulder. <i>'Well, he said to watch and learn...'</i> So he turned his head, and watched and learned of Nate's fondling technique. The guy was eager. <i>Really</i> eager. Like, 'starving man with sandwich' eager. It... broke the spell just a bit, seeing that kind of half-naked animal lust. &quot;H-Hey, c'mon, man. It's been, like, ten seconds, and, and--&quot; His meager protests were cut off as the original woman shifted into his line of sight, wearing a pouty expression. &quot;You don't want me...?&quot; Max's face fell. For a moment, he seriously had to think about that one -- if what he did with all those hormones raging could be called &quot;thinking.&quot; He gulped. <i>'God, she's beautiful... Maybe it wouldn't be so wrong to... But there's gotta be...'</i> He tried to laugh it off. &quot;H-How, I... Ha ha, w-what kind of question is that, ha ha?&quot; He grinned at her. &quot;J-Just, y'know, w-w-where's the rush, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> She glanced over her shoulder at Nate, and then turned back with a sultry smirk. &quot;Well, that seems to suit <i>him</i>. But you're right.&quot; Max gave a sigh of relief. &quot;Besides,&quot; she said, giving him a gentle push, with just enough force to knock him back... into other green and blue arms to ease him onto the grass. &quot;I can think of <i>plenty</i> of ways to show you a good time, until -- or if -- you find your nerve,&quot; she said. She dipped in to scratch gently along the top and side of his snout. He let out a grunt of pleasure, feeling a lot of tension leave him; it felt too good for it to really hit him that she was stroking his face like an animal at a petting zoo. &quot;Ooh...&quot; was all he had to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T22:11:13-07:00","id":226791,"title":"","content":"And with that kiss, Nate's mind was literally gone. He couldn't remember how to speak, not that he wanted to. When the woman fondled his long goatee, he broke the kiss and couldn't help but bleat happily. &quot;Oh my, someone's excited!&quot; She giggled. And she wasn't exactly right. Excited was too weak a word to describe the Ram right now. She grabbed his horns, and that feeling sent him over the hedge. The Beast swept her off her feet, eliciting a surprised squeal, and lowered her to the ground, where he straddled her. He started to explore her body quite thoroughly, alternating between fondles and hungry kisses. It was an act so <i>raw</i>, it was only driven by pure instinct, a primal need to breed. The woman's moans were only answered by his grunts and bleats. Both of them were quite noisy indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-13-2014, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T07:37:08-07:00","id":227001,"title":"","content":"The blue women were noticeably - or rather unnoticeable- hanging back from the display. While they were flirting and teasing the two males, they seemed content to let their green companions have all the real fun for the moment. Perhaps they couldn't leave the water, or perhaps they were simply waiting their turn. Whatever the case, the pig and goat were receiving plenty of attention from the collecting of green women.<br /> <br /> <br /> There were 6 of them in total, as well as 4 blue women. Max and Nate were soon tended by 3 green women each as more approached to pet and stroke Max, or join Nate in his debauchery. Realizing Max wasn't interested in sex, they instead offered him another temptation, plucking one of the mushrooms from the ground and wiggling it over his face like a slave girl would offer grapes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T11:03:44-07:00","id":227156,"title":"","content":"The Ram welcomed the two other women in the same way he had been treating the first. One, two or three, it didn't matter. He was the alpha male of the flock, they were only showing him proper respect. He smelled their heat, and that gave him every right to take advantage of them. Why wouldn't he? It was his role to breed them. In his frenzy, he somehow managed to notice the women surrounding the Pig. He wasn't breeding them properly? Fine by him. As soon as he finishes with those three, the Ram will go assert his dominance on the others females. And if the piggy refused to hand them over, the Ram wouldn't hesitate to fight him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-13-2014, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T21:19:11-07:00","id":227571,"title":"","content":"Max was likewise losing himself in a different sort of pleasure. He let every muscle go limp and just lay there with his eyes closed, curly tail swishing and grunting in pleasure as they lavished him with tender caresses and pet every inch of him. He loosed a squeal that bordered on ecstasy when they started in on rubbing his ears. While the Ram was much more active, the Pig had little more use for human words. He simply enjoyed the sound of their cooing over him, like they would over an adorable pet. He should have found it all humiliating, but it just felt <i>so good</i>.<br /> <br /> Still, something did manage to stir Max, as his nose sniffed at the object coming near. A most tantalizing object. He opened his eyes and saw the most beautiful mushroom he'd ever seen, still with soil clinging to it, and in the hands of an even more beautiful lady. Though there was something odd to its smell, too; not exactly <i>bad</i>, but he'd have likely taken longer to snatch it up if it had been further from his face. But snatch it up he did, quick enough that only the girl's reflexes spared her fingers. Ohhh, yes, but <i>that</i> was a good mushroom. This swiftness and contented chewing elicited a chorus of giggles and aww's and ohhh's and some words, probably about how cute and clever he was; he really was beyond language, but the voices using it sounded just so <i>pleased</i> with him. It made him happy all on its own.<br /> <br /> And it got better, as Max smelled another mushroom! Even closer than the first, as they'd balanced it on his snout. He snatched it up in one bite, rewarded with applause, laughter, and ear rubs. He could get used to this... Another mushroom pulled him up a bit. He snapped at it, but this time it danced away. The girl holding it beamed down at him and said something, and then said it more forcefully when he made a go for it. The third time his brain fired up to find a way to get at it and identified the command for him: &quot;Stay.&quot; This brief brush with human thought brought a faint sense of humiliation with it, but, well, c'mon, mushroom! He obediently tilted his snout down, earning a new trill of laughter, the deliverance of the mushroom and a, &quot;Good piggy!&quot; as she wrapped her arms around him, even now earning more satisfaction from him than shame. &quot;Ohh, maybe we'll even get to keep you~&quot; A pause, at which the temperature seemed to fall, suddenly. &quot;I said 'maybe,'&quot; the girl said again, as though defensive.<br /> <br /> Max turned his head to look at her, puzzled by implications presently too complicated for him. Even beyond the simple encroachment of the pig, the mushrooms were getting started. His metabolism might have been good at managing the effects, but each one was mighty potent on its own. In turning his head, he chanced on the other trio of green women, and a goat giving all he had. <i>'W-Wai... Nnnnate...?'</i> No, he supposed not. Sure, Nate was a bit goatish, and had been there earlier, but he didn't even see anything human about the <i>animal</i> grinding and bleating away over there. Perhaps the angle simply made it seem so to him, or perhaps the mushrooms were having a side-effect... or perhaps the forces of Arcadia had decided one should be as much a beast in body as one was in mind. A single look at Max would say just how true that last one was.<br /> <br /> Regardless, he did look around a bit to see where Nate had gotten off to. Until something more important brushed his snout. The command that meant &quot;stay,&quot; came again, and so he waited. Then the mushroom went sailing a short ways off, accompanied by an encouraging push and a call of, &quot;Go geddit!&quot; The Pig needed no encouragement, squealing in delight as he bolted after on all-fours, and then gobbled the fungus up off the grass. His expedition proved especially rewarding when a few seconds of nosing about found him another, which he quickly ate without using his hands. Just as he found another, though, the hysterical laughter from the girls had given way to calling him back. Max felt torn, but compromised: he only took a bite of part of it before returning to their loving hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T15:08:51-07:00","id":228492,"title":"","content":"((Ending Flashback))<br /> <br /> Such had been the previous scene before Jessica's arrival, with Nate indulging his more primal instincts, and Max being cooed over like a domestic hog. But now things were quite the opposite, as their oxen companion had discovered.<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe we can have some more fun with this one. Save her for later, perhaps?&quot; asked one of the fish women who was holding her down. She grabbed Jessica's head and forced it to the side as she licked along her neck, &quot;I haven't had steak since I was taken!&quot; she whined. The others appeared to salivate at the suggestion, before the one who was teasing Max clacked her jaws together and drew their attention once again.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Focus, ladies!&quot; she ordered, &quot;We don't want them escaping like last time!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-04-2015, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T23:06:33-07:00","id":228836,"title":"","content":"The shouting nearby brought the Ram back to his senses. Well, at least a little. He saw the fight between a cow and attractive blue females. What was that bovine doing here? Bah, the reason didn't matter. However, those blue nymphs looked like prime breeding material. And the Beast didn't smell any male on them. Good. Time to increase the flock.<br /> He suddenly bolted out of the green women's reach, who let out a shrill of surprise, and he ran on all four charging the women on the ox, horns on display. He crashed into the pile of blue female, sending some tumbling, and immediately leaped on one, well decided to mate with her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-15-2014, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T23:11:17-07:00","id":228838,"title":"","content":"((Once again, the green women are just illusions. The blue fishy women are the only real ones. :P ))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T23:46:44-07:00","id":228844,"title":"","content":"((Yeah, I know, that's why they didn't resist and tried to catch him when he jumped away. ))","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-15-2014, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T20:03:30-07:00","id":229883,"title":"","content":"Max was quite oblivious to the fishy woman threatening his life. He presumed she was simply going to stroke his chest and then his chin. And that would be nice. But really, what wouldn't be nice? He'd known the ladies were still doing nice things, but he couldn't really tell what they were. Unless they were mushrooms. The mushrooms were nicest of all. Still, into a fog that thick, The shouting of his name cut through like a searchlight. Somewhat. At least enough for him to turn his attention and his head in its direction, even if it felt like doing so from a thousand miles away. There he saw several women holding Jessica down. Though he supposed that couldn't be. She didn't look like she had the horns or the tail or the hooves or... any of the bovine traits he'd come to associate with Jessica. Nevertheless, the apparently human woman still gave a sense of... Jessica-ness to him and his nose, so he could work with that.<br /> <br /> Still, interesting a sight though it was, Max couldn't perceive a reason he should move for it. Not when it was so comfortable where he was, after all. He was sure Jessica would understand. Of course, he got a reason quick enough when that goat from earlier charged, and scattered the blue women like bowling pins. <i>That</i> got an emotion to focus him through the fungal daze. First was shock. And then anger. Ironically, both he and Nate -- had they been able to articulate their feelings -- would have regarded the women as &quot;theirs.&quot; But while the Goat saw them through the lens of domination, the Pig saw them as a pet might see its masters. And this pet was going to protect them.<br /> <br /> With an enraged squeal, Max twisted away from the fish woman threatening him. Surprised, by the sudden movement, her grasp came late, though she did grab one of his legs. With no thought beyond that he needed to remove the impediment to getting where he needed to go, he whirled his head around and sank his teeth into her wrist. She screamed something inhuman as the bite broke the skin and her wrist, and released her grip. And then he was off, charging at the goat on all-fours. He needed to because... Because... He couldn't remember. The fog had gone red.<br /> <br /> Yet something else was different about the swine, even if it was only a trick of the spores still circulating. Max seemed... bigger. There was less pink and more in the way of a bristly brown, less baby fat than hard muscle, and less of large floppy ears than short sharp ones. Most of all, while he himself sometimes forgot he had a pair of dinky little tusks, there was no chance of that with the new prominent pair. Well... Sometimes it <i>is</i> called the Year of the Boar...<br /> <br /> <i>This</i> was the Max that barreled into the goat, likely doing extensive harm to the woman Nate had mounted. To say nothing of at least one of the others, rolled over as they were by the big ball of raging horns, tusks, and hooves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 08-15-2014, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T21:00:55-07:00","id":229915,"title":"","content":"Nate and then Max's actions had freed Jessica. On her feet, she started to stomp one of the blue fish women. However, Max's transformation into a boar distracted her enough for another of the blue woman to wrap an arm around her neck from behind. Jessica struggled to toss the attacker off her, but found herself unable to manage it. Desperate for air, the ox woman threw herself backwards, slamming her would-be strangler hard into the ground. The tactic worked, and the fish woman lost her grip. Jessica again got to her feet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T21:53:43-07:00","id":229954,"title":"","content":"Judging by the confusion, the fish women were accustomed to easy meals and did not have much opportunity for a real fight. They were scrambling, trying to regain their composure as they snapped and clawed at the three companions. However, before the two parties could tear each other to pieces, an echoed voice rang out, loud enough to pierce even the dizzying fog of the spores.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;STOP this at once!&quot; the voice commanded, and the women immediately obeyed, lowering their claws and turning to see who had issued the command. There, standing in the pool were a pair of new figures. One male, one female, yet similar enough to be identical twins. They were bare naked, revealing that from the waist down they had large fish tails like that of mer folk. A chain was shackled to the ends of their tails, binding the two of them together. Their upper bodies were covered in scales, but otherwise appeared human in shape. Their heads were bald, and their ears pointed and finned.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Gemini!&quot; hissed one of the blue women before the twins spoke together in perfect unison.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;These are no mere farm animals, they are members of the Chinese Zodiac. Part of the master's collection, you will release them immediately!&quot; they commanded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-16-2014, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T02:29:17-07:00","id":230083,"title":"","content":"The Ram didn't foresee the Pig, well, the former Pig barreling into him, and he was sent sprawling to the ground a few meters away. Ooooh, it was on. A rival male wanted to be the head of the herd? Not on this Ram's watch. He recovered and assessed his opponent. It seems like he had been underestimated. While he had looked like a submissive beta before, the Boar that now stood before him seemed quite strong. Still, how could he pretend to be an alpha male when he didn't have the proper horns to display his status to all? He'd show him! He'd show them all!<br /> <br /> The Goat grunted and snorted aggressively, preparing to charge. His curling horns seemed to be getting bigger, each of them gaining another spiral. As he stamped to the ground on all fours, one could notice his bare hands changing. The nails looked...darker, and rougher, as if hooves started to form. But the most disturbing change might have been his eyes. His pupils narrowed, and became horizontal, while his irises became yellowish. He snorted one last time and charged, crashing and locking his horns into the Boar's tusks, effectivly headbutting him. Now he just had to hold his ground and push the other into submission, so that he could claim all the females of the --<br /> <br /> &quot;STOP this at once!&quot;<br /> <br /> It was like a bucket of cold water had been doused on Nate's mind. What...What was he doing? He was fighting Max! Or...what seemed to be Max, anyway. They were on all fours, like vulgar farm animals! He looked into his friend's eyes, trying to offer an mute apology. But...he couldn't give up the fight. He wasn't dominated by his instinct anymore, or at least he thought so, but he couldn't just lose to Max. It seemed that it wasn't just the Ram's mind speaking, there was also Nate's own pride. He stopped pushing, not wanting to hurt the kid, and just hold his ground.<br /> <br /> &quot;Please Max...&quot; He whispered. &quot;Just...give up. Let me have this. Please.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-16-2014, 07:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T21:18:40-07:00","id":230976,"title":"","content":"Ohh, the Boar <i>loved</i> a good fight. There was an elation undercutting the rage when the Goat stood and began pawing the ground, ready for a scrap. It got even better when the beast underwent a change of its own. Hardly an even fight against the bristled engine of destruction, but still. Fury against fury in bodies to match. One would soon be crumpled and bleeding while the other stood in triumph. <i>Nothing</i> could be more right and proper. The Boar snorted, bellowed his ferocity, and lowered his head. They charged in perfect synchronicity. Their aims and approaches proved just different enough that, try though the Boar did, he failed to gore or slash his adversary. He caught the headbutt and dug in his heels. If the Goat thought the Boar was going to yield even an inch, he had another thing com--<br /> <br /> A twin-voiced shout rang out.<br /> <br /> Max came back to himself in as big a rush as Nate. Or... the person he was pretty sure was Nate. As he had with Jessica, Max wasn't seeing any of the animal traits through the mushroom haze. Which... limited the degree to which he was fully back to himself. The situation appeared to be that he had his head pressed against another naked guy's, and they were both trying not to lose ground. And it seemed really important to Nate that he win. Just as the kid had felt the very same thing a moment ago. The rage had been hanging around, formless and undirected. But it was quickly chased out as the whole situation struck a drugged-up Max as <i>incredibly hilarious</i>. The boar laughed, grunts and snorts finding their ways in. His body shrank, the bit of chub replacing the muscle. The pink flesh, the floppy ears, and curly tail made their returns as the tusks and bristles took their leave.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nate... Naaaaaate... Ha ha! We <i>could not</i> look stupider right now!&quot; The Pig was... jovial. &quot;I mean. We're human, right. But. But we're naked. And on all-fours. Pushing at each others' heads. Like animals! Ha ha! Oink! Baaa! Ha!&quot; More giggling, as his little tail wagged behind him. &quot;And in front of people!&quot; He turned their collective heads to the rest of the entourage. And waved excitedly at them with one hand. &quot;Hi Jessica! Hi ladies! Hi important-looking twin-person!&quot; It was Masks all around, to his eyes, everyone looking human. He turned their heads back toward one other, and then coughed from laughing too hard. &quot;And... and you want me to give up, now? Ha! Dude, no way. I'm not giving up!&quot; He grinned. &quot;<i>We're</i> giving up! Because this is too dumb for us!&quot; There was a bit of uncontrollable snickering. &quot;So... So, c'mon. Count of three. We drop this. And do something less stupid. Or more! I'm cool. Okay? Okay? Okaaay! Ooooone... Twwwoooo... Three.&quot; He started to get to his feet.<br /> <br /> And that was how mushrooms allowed Max to disentangle himself from what should have been a tense encounter, likewise putting off the heaping servings of crushing humiliation and depression. The chemicals were unlikely to last <i>too</i> much longer. But for now, things seemed as fine to him as they possibly could.<br /> <br /> (Note: As may or may not be apparent, I have <i>no</i> experience with recreational drugs. I thus can't place whether this works as a portrayal or is dumb as hell. xD Oh well.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  OOC disclaimer and minor edits. 08-17-2014, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-16T22:20:06-07:00","id":231033,"title":"","content":"(I would imagine it's fairly accurate for magic shrooms as I also have no such experience beyond what hippy music videos tell us.)<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Ridiculous.&quot; The twins said, &quot;How much Goblin Fruit did you give these two?&quot; they leered at the patch of mushrooms and scoffed. One of the fish women hissed angrily at the twins, but with a flick of their wrists, a torrent of water erupted from the pool and knocked her flat on her back. &quot;We said enough!&quot; they commanded, the pool now churning as if ready to attack again should the twins will it. This seemed to get the women to back down.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;This isn't fair, Gemini!&quot; one of the women exclaimed, &quot;We can't travel far from the pond, we need food!&quot; the twins scoffed at her and gestured to the mushrooms.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The Keeper has been very kind in leaving you this Goblin Fruit, you show disrespect by demanding for more. That's why you're not beautiful anymore, he thought you needed a humility lesson, so now you look like the creature from the black lagoon!&quot; the twins chastised the women who shrieked at their insults and fell to their knees sobbing like maniacs.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Pathetic, to think you were ever considered trophy wives.&quot; the twins said before turning to the three companions. &quot;We suggest you leave now and return to the ranch. This confrontation is finished!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T00:03:27-07:00","id":231134,"title":"","content":"Nate nervously smiled at Max's delirious behavior, and chucked without any conviction. Seems like they weren't going to be any bad blood between them, but he <i>still</i> couldn't give up. So when the Pig decided to get up, Nate slowly pushed again, with just enough force to make him step back. <i>Now</i> he could let go of their fight. His body had changed to display his dominant instinct. If he had gave up, would he have gained the softer characteristics of a obedient sheep? Nate hadn't be ready to find out, and he certainly wasn't eager to experience it. He got up and looked around him, the fog of drugs clearing his mind.<br /> He saw Gemini, and was puzzled by their look. Did the Keeper took one person? Two? Could the twins even remember the truth? He then saw the erotically-shaped bushes. Was he...Oh wow. He had tried to mate with<i> that</i>? He had fornicated with some <i>plants</i>?! The shriek of the blue women drew his attention, and he couldn't help but shiver in disgust at their bodies. He wanted to puke. This was wrong, so wrong. He should feel repulsed. <i>So why am I still aroused?</i><br /> Some parts of his body were still betraying him. Speaking of his body, he looked at his hands and cringed. His fingers were harder to bend now. Could he still play guitar with them? He tried to ignore the fact that he'd already need to remember how to play the chords, and checked his horns. They were bigger alright. They didn't really feel heavier though. Seemed like he had gained some neck muscles to support them.<br /> Why wasn't he changing back, like Max? Would it happen later? Was it because he didn't eat the mushrooms, or Goblin Fruits as they called it?<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks&quot;, he said to Gemini, grunts and bleats more present in his voice than before. &quot;Could we meet again sometimes? We'd like to speak to someone of the Zodiac. The Western One. Just to...compare our experiences, you know? Learn how things work around here?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-17-2014, 03:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T03:28:48-07:00","id":231261,"title":"","content":"&quot;Yes,&quot; Jessica agreed, &quot;In particular, I would like to meet Libra.&quot;<br /> <br /> Despite everything, Jessica had not forgotten her insight about how to escape the contract. However, for her idea to have enan a chance of working, they would need access to someone who could perform marriages. If she remembered correctly, Libra, a robed woman with scales, was something like a judge. If so, maybe she could then marry people. It seemed like a good idea to find out, even if she was far from sure that she would attempt her plan. The thought of betraying Curtis still sickened her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T06:40:54-07:00","id":231409,"title":"","content":"&quot;Whether we meet again or not is up to this place to decide.&quot; the twins answered, &quot;In any case, we can not leave the water, for we are fish.&quot; speaking of which, the women began to crawl their way back into the pool, vanishing under its churning waters and leaving the three companions alone. This seemed to calm the twins as the waters began to grow still once more. How was it that these twins commanded the water in such a way? Until now, the Keeper was the only one who had shown any dominion over this place, yet here were two of his slaves displaying similar abilities!<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Do not listen to Leo, he will only get both Zodiacs in trouble, you for escaping, and us for aiding you. Go back to your ranch, remember your place, and do not disobey further.&quot; Gemini commanded, &quot;You are slaves now, as are we all.&quot; and with that, the pair sank beneath the waters and were gone. Despite the crystal clear waters, it looked like nobody was under now, perhaps there was some caves or merely another trick of the realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T11:58:57-07:00","id":231822,"title":"","content":"&quot;Wait, I still have a few qu...&quot; Aaaaand they were gone. &quot;...Jerks. And I thought<i> I</i> was supposed to be the Sheep.&quot; They creeped him out. Of all the former humans they encountered here, they were the most...other-worldy. Once again, he was seriously glad to have been chosen for the Chinese Zodiac. However, he was intrigued. How did they do this waterwhip thingy? That seemed like a pretty cool trick. Was it because they were obeying the Keeper's orders? They didn't seem like people to trust.<br /> <br /> &quot;We should probably get out of here, and find somewhere to sleep. I'm hurting all over, because of the...you know, fight.&quot; He avoided Max's eyes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":".  Nate's actions were incoherent. 08-17-2014, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T12:25:51-07:00","id":231863,"title":"","content":"The Gemini puzzled Jessica. She had not know that the Gemini were at all aquatic nature. Maybe she was also just as completely uninformed about the nature of the Libra. She felt depressed, but then new thoughts started to take shape in her mind. A beginnings of a new, perhaps better plan was starting to take form in her mind. She just needed more time to think. To Max and Nate, she said, &quot;I think I know a good place for us to camp, if we all want to stay together. If not, it was good to see you two again.&quot;<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T13:14:23-07:00","id":231900,"title":"","content":"Max was too lacking in the wits department to find the goings-on all that significant. He'd just sorta tipped down onto his haunches, Nate's gentle tap being the only necessary thing for that. A dopey, &quot;Aww, c'mon,&quot; and a chuckle was all that got, though, and he probably forgot it a few moments later. He just sat there, watching the rest of the exchange without much awareness. He did think the twin-person was a little hard on the women, though. &quot;But they're just ladies...&quot; he'd mumbled, not really remembering the whole 'attempt on his life' thing. Admittedly, the haze was quickly on the lift. He saw the monster-women and the human women they had been, and both seemed as true. The Goat and the man, the Ox and the woman, the twins who were one... When the last of these claimed to be a fish, he'd mumbled, &quot;But... we're all human...&quot; He could even see his own toes wiggle, as well as his hoof. The rhyme, &quot;This little piggy went to market,&quot; went through his mind, eliciting a grunting, &quot;Heh,&quot; but it didn't seem all that funny.<br /> <br /> Still, while Max's head cleared, he hadn't picked up on anything different about himself. And Nate hadn't been quite right earlier, even if the swine's changes were harder to notice beyond no longer being a boar. He seemed... a tad softer. Cuter, perhaps cuddlier, tusks even harder to spot. His voice had been pitched just a little higher, too. It was as though some cosmic force had forgotten what he'd looked like before the Boar, factored in the hallucinatory cooing earlier, and overshot things a bit on size and shape. He was a little smaller than he had been before, and looked a bit younger than his years.<br /> <br /> &quot;Huh? Oh. Yeah, sure,&quot; Max said at Nate's suggestion. He started to rise, and then gave a quiet, wincing squeal. The bruise on his leg called the host of the others to his attention, and they collectively dragged him back to lucidity. He shook his head to clear the last of it, ears flopping about, and rubbed his leg and arm. &quot;Ugh... R-Right. Th-The fight...&quot; He could remember it all now, the brawl and before it... There weren't many details, really -- though enough that his face would probably be red for quite a while. It was mostly sensation, from the rage to the pleasure, more intense than anything he'd ever known, an ocean to drown him. It had all been so consuming and humiliating and demeaning and horrible and he had never felt so alive. He blinked, a tear rolling from each eye down a bruised face. Max raised his arm to wipe them off, and found some grit on his snout. His eyes fell on a few spots of the ground where it looked like he hadn't cared how much soil he ripped up with a mushroom. Frustrated, he tried to rub all the dirt off his face, whimpering amid a few more tears. &quot;S-S-Sorry about th-that...&quot;<br /> <br /> Drawing a breath and feeling out the best way to move comfortably, the kid rose slowly to his hooves. Max looked to Jessica first. &quot;R-Right. I uh... We <i>need</i> to stick together. Let's get outta here.&quot; Feeling passive -- <i>'If I hadn't brought us here, none of this would have happened.'</i> -- he waited for Jessica to lead them to the spot she remembered. &quot;A-And thanks, Jessica. Thank you.&quot; He was as ashamed to meet Nate's eye as the Ram was to meet his... but as he turned to start out, the Pig's gaze chanced on enough to take a closer look. Eyes widened at the bestial changes. &quot;Nate, your...&quot; He grunted a cough; his voice didn't sound quite right. &quot;Holy shit, what happened to you?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Added a bit in the last paragraph. 08-17-2014, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T14:09:04-07:00","id":231942,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sticking together. Right. Yeah, I don't want to be jumped on by crazy fish women again.&quot; Although he might be the one who would jump on them. &quot;And...I'm sorry for hitting you. Hope I didn't hurt you too much, man. But damn, you're a heavy hitter, you know that?&quot; Nate forced himself to smile, but it looked more like a wince. His head and his side hurt, like he had been hit with a hammer.<br /> <br /> Then Max's question scared him. &quot;I...My horns got heavier, that's all...Right?&quot; No, there was something else. The Pig wasn't focusing on Nate's head, or even his hands. No, he was looking directly at his face. &quot;Oh God, no, no...&quot; He bolted toward the pond, and threw himself on all fours right on the edge. Slowly, he tried to brace himself mentally, and looked at his reflection. The ears hadn't changed. There were still ridiculous though. The horns had gotten bigger indeed, but it oddly comforted him. And then he gasped and froze. Two goat's eyes stared at him. <i>His</i><i> eyes.</i> <br /> <br /> &quot;FUCK!&quot; Nate yelled. &quot;FUCK FUCK FUCK FUUUUUUUUCK!&quot; He began to scream madly. He howled in rage. He smashed his fists on the water's surface, he tore grass from the ground, and grabbed his horns, pulling as if to tear them out of his skull. He rolled on his back in anger, still yelling and now kicking the air with his hooves. After a short time, rage had made room for despair, and tears began to roll from his eyes. The Ram stopped thrashing around and curled up in a fetal position, still sobbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T15:13:07-07:00","id":232007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/205196-ic-zodiac-beasts?p=231863#post231863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Gemini puzzled Jessica. She had not know that the Gemini were at all aquatic nature.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ((The story of Gemini is about a pair of twins who were turned into fish and tied together at the tails. Or at least that's the story I was told growing up.))<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The changes inflicted by the Keeper were not the only ones they would have to deal with, it seemed. The very realm itself was altering them, based on how they behaved. If they continued to act like a bunch of wild beasts, they may end up becoming just that before this was over! It seemed they now had even more reason to cling to their dwindling humanity, and hopefully Jessica would be able to lead them someplace safe from any further molestation while they collected their thoughts. But in a realm such as this, how could an outsider possibly tell what was safe, and what was just another death trap like the one they had been in moments before?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T15:19:19-07:00","id":232010,"title":"","content":"Jessica looked down on Nate, uncertain of what to do. After a moment, she knelt beside him and rubbed his shoulders. She said, &quot;Try to stay calm, Nate. We're alive, and that's what matters.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica tried to sound calm. However, she felt uncertain. Was her thinking even remotely correct. She decided to try an experiment to find out. Could only the keeper make contracts? One way to find out. &quot;Nate, I will tell you what. I promise that if you calm down and stand up within the next minute, you will be able to read my mind. Come on; see if I'm telling the truth.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typoes 08-18-2014, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T16:23:36-07:00","id":232068,"title":"","content":"Max, still crying a bit himself, just stared. He felt directionless. He had hitched his wagon to Nate's and was now unsure to do. The Ram had seemed so strong, but now... <i>'... Strength doesn't matter. Not here. I'm not strong. I never have been. I probably won't ever be.'</i> He sagged a moment. Then took a breath and walked to his side right with Jessica, and lay a shaking hand on his friend's shoulder. The Pig avoided his reflection, as he had since he arrived; there was no way seeing his own face could improve the situation. <i>'I'm weak. But... I can still be a friend. He needs it.'</i><br /> <br /> Max struggled to find words, any words. &quot;Sh-She's right, Nate. W-We're alive. We <i>are</i> still human, however we look. We're still <i>people</i>. We... I mean...&quot; An idea hit him. &quot;Th-This isn't set! There c-could be ways to change back, right? There have to be.&quot; He forced himself to smile and hoped he was convincing himself as much as Nate. &quot;We just have to find them, right?&quot;<br /> <br /> The little guy did take issue with Jessica's proposal, though. It was an idea, but making that kind of promise felt just way too out of left field. &quot;Hey!&quot; he grunted in annoyance. &quot;Jessica! People can't just <i>stop</i> feeling something! This is hard enough as it is! Just...&quot; He took a breath. &quot;I get you've got an idea. Your heart's in the right place. Just... Now <i>really</i> isn't the time. Don't rush Nate. Please.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Adjuuuuustments. 08-17-2014, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-17T21:49:24-07:00","id":232412,"title":"","content":"Nate rejected them, and got up. He had tears stuck in his goatee, which meant that he still had lachrymal glands despite his eyes. &quot;You want me to calm down?! Did you see how fucking monstrous I look now?! We are NOT humans anymore guys! We're something else, we're another race! Look at us! None of us have real feet anymore! And soon I won't even have proper hands too! How much longer do we have before Max goes rolling in some mud, or you Jessica grow some udders to get milked?! You already have extra breasts!&quot; He openly and sarcastically laughed at the Oxen's proposal. &quot;And of course! That was the solution all along, making stupid promises so that we can give ourselves magical super-powers and become the X-men! No wait, I forgot about our condition, X-Beasts would be more appropriate!&quot;<br /> <br /> Once again, he unconsciously bared his teeth in anger. &quot;Well you know what? Go look at yourself in the pond, both of you, and try telling me with a straight face that we're still humans. Go ahead! Do it! And then <i>maybe</i> I will calm down!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-18-2014, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T08:02:06-07:00","id":232827,"title":"","content":"Jessica did as Nate bid her. She saw an ox woman, not herself. &quot;Nate, I might not look human. But you know what? That doesn't matter. What matter is that we can still think. We can still act like human beings, no matter what our situation. Years ago, I took a history class once, and I remember the professor - Doctor Webster - talking about.....&quot; <br /> <br /> Jessica trailed off. What good were words? She said, &quot;I'm sorry. Never mind.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T13:29:57-07:00","id":233189,"title":"","content":"Nate laughed bitterly and also..bleately.. &quot;Are you sure? Did you even see what happened here? I tried to mate with all the blue fem...girls, I wanted to breed them, so they could bear my children. No, my lambs. That's what I was thinking.&quot; His voice got weaker and he seemed to have a lump in his throat. &quot;I...essentialy tried to rape them.&quot; The Goat sat down in the grass and sighed. &quot;I would have never done that before. I don't like what I am becoming.&quot; And he didn't dare say what he was thinking. If he was such a danger to the people around him, should he really to go back to the real world?<br /> &quot;I was ready to hurt Max when he challenged me. In fact, I didn't even know it was you man. For me, you were just an opponent threatening my reign as a male.&quot; Nate looked up and locked into his friend's eyes. &quot;I wanted to kill you. And I know you too.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-18-2014, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T15:49:33-07:00","id":233355,"title":"","content":"For a moment, Jessica was unsure what to say. Finally, she said, &quot;Nate, that professor I was talking about? Well, in one class, he told us that we should remember that history is not just something that happens to other people. All people at times face situations that they can't control, if only death at the end. He said that what matters is how we respond to those times. He then went on to talk about some regular people who lived in Nazi times, and what they did at the risk of their very lives. I know it seems like we have no choices, but we do. Trust me. Nate, your regret now tells me you'll make the right choice in the future. I believe in you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica decided to leave out that the professor she had heard all this from had gone insane and went missing a few years ago. It was important to stay positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typoes 08-18-2014, 06:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T21:22:54-07:00","id":233754,"title":"","content":"Max stood rooted to the spot at Nate's angry demand. He already wasn't feeling so great to see his friend hurting so much, nor some of his verbal lashing out. There were few things he wanted less than to see his reflection. Or the reflection he would see, at least; he didn't want to think of it as his. Seeing something like that... would make it harder to pretend, on some level, that it wasn't really happening. He choked a moment, closing his eyes. <i>'... Just... Just go. Do it. You'll catch a look eventually, so just... Get it over with.'</i> Another few moments passed before the Pig's hooves brought him to the water's edge, eyes still closed and leaking tears. '... <i>Be a man.' </i>Shaking, he forced them open. And saw the Pig's face.<br /> <br /> Max did <i>not</i> think he looked good in pink. His cheeks were a tad plumper than he'd remembered, too. And the ears were as ridiculous as he'd feared; even Jessica's and Nate's weren't flopping over themselves! The snout was still worst. The enormous thing was sniffling and snuffling as he kept crying. It gave an excellent view of the slimy end flexing and contorting, exactly as he felt it doing, all the way at the end of his face. He wanted to throw up. After a sob, he did. He had enough presence to turn from the water and from Nate and Jessica, but there were a lot of part-digested mushrooms that came back up, off to the side on the grass. He breathed a moment. He found he actually felt better. Up until he found it didn't smell half-bad... He threw up the rest of the mushrooms. He turned, fallen on hand and knee, to pant into the water. Puking hadn't improved what he saw. Weakly, he punched the pond into ripples. &quot;So...&quot; he breathed, too quiet for human ears, but not for the other Zodiacs'. &quot;This... is me, now...&quot; It was real.<br /> <br /> He stared for a bit. Then Max splashed water on his face, absently. He kept doing it. He felt cleaner just from that than he had in days (weeks? months?). It got some of the vile-but-not-vile-enough taste out of his mouth. He was hearing a lot of what the other two were saying, even if he wasn't processing it fully. He turned at his name, face dripping, and met Nate's gaze. It hurt to hear, but... Well, it wasn't a surprise. &quot;I... I know,&quot; he croaked. &quot;I... Th-Things were...&quot; He shook his head. &quot;I don't remember. N-Not all of it. I... I tried to kill you, too.&quot; He turned his head away. &quot;Th-There was a reason, a-at first -- stupid, but a reason. Then there was red and...&quot; He took a breath. &quot;Nothing else mattered.&quot; He couldn't look his friend in the eye anymore -- for reasons only tangentially to do with their shape. &quot;I don't blame you. I-I can't. You're still my friend, okay? I mean. At least, I'm still yours. Even if you don't...&quot; Another sob. &quot;God, why did I have to bring us <i>here?</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Max listened to what Jessica had to say. Maybe she had a point. He wasn't sure. He didn't really care to be sure. His mind just wasn't in a state to process it. He did want one thing, though. With a grunt of a sigh, he brought a hand to his forehead. &quot;Can we just... not talk. For five minutes. Or whatever.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 08-19-2014, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T22:03:09-07:00","id":233834,"title":"","content":"Nate raised a skeptical eyebrow at Jessica's advice. &quot;Huh. I never thought we'd invoke the Godwin law in Arcadia. I appreciate the intent, but I'm not sure we can be inspired by History when we're in a freaking magical world that runs on nonsense.&quot;<br /> He looked at Max's reaction with a sympathetic eye, but, as he realized with a pang of guilt, he kinda enjoyed seeing him react with the same disgust as he did. At least, he wouldn't feel weaker than the Pig. The Oxen, however, was unnerving with her calm and self-confidence. How could she be that way? She had to have some weaknesses. The only time he'd seen her falter was when she admitted to being attracted to Leo, but her reaction had been...rather human, despite the object of her affections. Could she...have find some sort of protection? Maybe she did really believe in the words of this professor. <i>Or maybe the Keeper's protecting her to play with us....</i> No, no. That was too far-fetched of a conclusion, wasn't it?<br /> He went to Max and put a hand on his shoulder. &quot;You couldn't have known man. All you did was following your nose, I would have done the same.&quot; He then offered his hand to him. &quot;Now get up. Let's walk out of there, and I promise you to shut up for at least ten minutes, alright?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T01:09:44-07:00","id":233959,"title":"","content":"Jessica quietly started to lead the way to where she had drank and slept. She need nothing, resisting the urge to ask about Godwin's Law or any number of other things. She simply walked, following the path she had taken in reverse. In due time, they reached the place beside the stream where she had drank. The colorful fish still darted in the crystal clear water while secretive crayfish played at the bottom. Jessica stopped, feeling the urge to drink the babbling water. <br /> <br /> Ignoring the urge as best she could, Jessica asked Max and Nate, &quot;Should we stay here or continue onto the ranch?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T08:48:01-07:00","id":234241,"title":"","content":"&quot;Giving up already? Well it didn't take you long to become submissive little cattle.&quot; said a familiar voice, &quot;Maybe I should just eat you right now if you don't care about becoming human again?&quot; the nearby bushes rustled and the face of Leo poked his head out, his fangs gleaming in the light as he licked his muzzle. &quot;Of course if you still want to get back home, I can point you in the right direction.&quot; he offered.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Time's running out for you. Soon you won't have any remains of your humanity left.&quot; he warned, leering at the two males, &quot;I wouldn't recommend wasting the precious time you have left on self pity.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:15:07-07:00","id":234423,"title":"","content":"The stream looked nice. Real nice. But Nate had seen enough water and fishes for the day. &quot;I'd say we go to the ranch. I'd like to see it.&quot;<br /> <br /> When Leo appeared from the bushes, two voices argued in the Goat's mind. One was terrified, and awed at the sight of the king of the beasts. The other voice wanted to confront him, to get violent. Again. But Nate was tired. So he took a third option. His human mind was back in command. &quot;Shut the fuck up, Leo. At least we didn't give up yet.&quot; A cocky smile appeared on his face. &quot;Besides, you couldn't eat us if you wanted to. First up, you're outnumbered, and we're not some little defenseless herbivore&quot; he said, pointing to his horns.&quot;And you know very well that the Keeper would be quite mad if you devoured us, and you really don't want to risk his wrath, am I right?&quot; He flipped him the bird, laughing. &quot;So no need for your empty threats, kitty.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-19-2014, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T21:52:05-07:00","id":235047,"title":"","content":"Max nodded weakly to Nate, and accepted the hand up. He rose just a bit shorter and younger than he'd been before he started crying. Max went along with them back to the creek, listless, but quietly appreciative of the respect and compassion. He thought he could go for a drink by the time they reached the creek, but... Much like Nate, it was a little too soon. He supposed he just wanted to rest somewhere; throwing up doesn't generally do a body good. He felt like he barely had any energy.<br /> <br /> Well, that was quick to change. Max lifted his head, nose snuffling. He was <i>really</i> starting to hate that sound. But it seemed a price worth paying this time: it gave an early warning. This was why he'd taken a step back and faced dead on when the lion emerged, as soundless as before. He cringed, heart racing. <i>'Did... Did he get even bigger from last time?' </i>He wondered if he'd have taken off on all-fours into the underbrush if he'd been caught less aware or been less tired. And how good his odds were if he tried now, even if he was held by the Leo's remonstrations and offer. Still, he was very glad when Nate started mouthing off. Even with the chance it was an act, it took off a lot of the edge and eased his tensions. Never mind the strong points the Goat made.<br /> <br /> Though Max was less sure the 'not some little defenseless' bit quite applied to him. Well, he could at least try to keep the lion from lunging at them. Even with Nate's good arguments against, he knew firsthand how easy it was for the animal to get carried away. He grinned. &quot;You said you're here with an offer, anyway.&quot; The grin faded a smidge; his voice still sounded different. Well, the mushrooms might still be working their way through him. <i>'Just need some time.'</i> He perked up again and went on. &quot;One way or another, doesn't seem like there's reason to fight, here. Mind telling us a bit about this way out, you've got in mind?&quot;<br /> <br /> After a moment, Max realized he had another question. It seemed like it might be important. Though it could take some sweet talk. &quot;Wait. Uh, while we've got you. You've... You've been here a really long time, haven't you? But... But you're so in control! That's... I don't know how you do it. It's amazing! We could--&quot; His eyes nearly darted in Nate's direction. No, the Goat deserved his pride. So did the Ox, even if she didn't seem to need it. &quot;Well, these two are tougher than me,&quot; he forced a grunting chuckle as he gestured at them, &quot;but <i>I</i> could use some tips with managing... well, <i>this</i>. Heh, even just on the way out you're talking about, I'm worried I'll blow it. Like... any ways you've found to keep in control, maybe? Or... Any chance you know how to...&quot; Max wondered if it would be too much of a giveaway who he was partly asking for, but thought up a cover. Even if he wasn't fond of it. &quot;Well... I-I worry I'll wind up making more of a... a p-pig outta myself, right?&quot; More of an attempt to laugh it off, with swinish sound effects. &quot;So, if I do, are there any ways you know to... y'know, change back?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T22:40:56-07:00","id":235066,"title":"","content":"&quot;Or, I could run off and tell the Keeper where you're hiding right now and get myself some tender goat leg as a reward!&quot; snapped Leo at Nate's little back talk. He emerged fully out of the bushes this time, still as naked as the first time he appeared, and got down into a sitting position, resting a hand on one of his paws as he leered at them. His attention turned to Max as he stammered out his questions, giving pause before answering.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The only person I know of who could change us back is the Keeper themselves, and that's clearly not going to happen. Get used to being a pig, because you're stuck with it.&quot; he answered. &quot;As for the subject of remaining in control?&quot; he continued, pausing once more. &quot;Find something to focus on and keep your thoughts directed towards it as hard as you can. This realm is the stuff of nightmares and dreams alike. It will sense your thoughts and feelings, and will prey upon them accordingly. If you can block out distractions, you may just escape with your sanity intact.&quot; he explained.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Of course, there's no guarantee you can maintain it forever, but that's just how I do it.&quot; he commented whimsically, adjusting his posture to sit up straight. &quot;As for how to escape, I don't know why i should bother after the Goat's disrespect.&quot; he shrugged, &quot;Maybe if he came over here and licked by feet clean, I'd forgive him. I've been running barefoot through the forest all this time and my paws get quite dirty.&quot; he sneered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T05:12:25-07:00","id":235317,"title":"","content":"&quot;We're not really hiding, you know. He told us to explore.&quot; As Leo emerged from the bushes, Nate noticed his own nakedness. He had forgotten his shirt at the pond. He felt a little sad, he liked the symbol on it. Sure, he didn't know anymore what it meant, but it seemed important to him somehow, back on Earth. He briefly wondered how could a picture of a mouth and a tongue be so important but he gave up. Oh well. Being naked didn't bother him anymore.<br /> <br /> Nate smiled at Leo's method. &quot;That's exactly what I advised Max to do while eating. It worked fairly well. Of course, the pond was another matter, we weren't aware we were drugged.&quot;<br /> <br /> The little submissive voice in the Goat's mind spoke up at Leo's demand. <i>'Yes, obey the king, and maybe he will spare us!'</i> to which he answered, <i>'Screw you. I'm a ram, not a damn sheep'</i>. He grinned. &quot;Yeaaaah, not gonna happen. I'm pretty sure cats are supposed to be flexible, you could do that yourself. But I still don't understand why didn't you escape, since you claim to have an human mind. &quot; He snapped his fingers, thinking of something. &quot;Oh, and by the way, we ran into Gemini. How can they do this thing with water? Is it only because they're loyal to the Keeper?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-20-2014, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T07:19:21-07:00","id":235387,"title":"","content":"Max had been wearing a pair of jean shorts himself. He missed them, his last traces of human clothing. They'd been comforting, even if his changes and the Thorns had left a big enough hole in the back to put his curly tail on full display. They'd probably been torn to shreds completely when he, er, &quot;Hulked up.&quot; Actually, that raised a counterpoint to what the Leo had said. He'd winced a bit at being called a pig; denying it was hard, but it still stung to be reminded. &quot;I... Yeah, I get that I can't change the... being a pig. But I mean... Back at the lake, I got... carried away. I turned into a boar for a few minutes. I was <i>a lot</i> more of an animal when I did. But I changed back to how I was when he took me.&quot; He ignored a faint doubt that there was <i>no</i> difference. &quot;That's what I meant. Just... if my body changes to be more animalistic, could... do you know if I could turn back to be how the Keeper made me?&quot;<br /> <br /> Still, even as Max cloyed around with the king of beasts, the Leo's demand of Nate nauseated him. The Goat clearly wasn't going to -- and with good cause! Still, if the feline was going to be a dick about answers if he wasn't supplicated... <i>'... Should... Should I just... go over and do it?'</i> He hated even thinking it, but couldn't deny a certain logic. <i>'It... wouldn't even be the most disgusting thing I've eaten or done today...'</i> Still, while his eyes locked on them, he couldn't quite bring himself to do it. Not at the moment, at least. Thankfully. So he tried a different tactic -- though Nate's question did interest him. &quot;I... Is the feet licking really in your best interests, though?&quot; He smiled, back in wheedle mode. &quot;I mean, you want us out, and <i>we</i> want us out, right? Putting up an obstacle just keeps you from getting what you want.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T07:46:00-07:00","id":235418,"title":"","content":"&quot; I simply want you to realize that you have practically no leverage in your current situation.&quot; Leo answered, &quot;I would be especially happy if you all escaped, but catching a bunch of runaways might also garner favor with our master, and that's just as precious as freedom in this realm.&quot; &quot;If you can't escape, the only other option is to make the Keeper happy, or your life will be a living hell.&quot; he folded his arms over his chest, extending one of his feet outward and twiddling his feline toes.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;You were right to second guess my motives when we first met, leaving the ranch was a huge mistake.&quot; the lion commented with a sneer. &quot;Now the situation is a win-win for me. Either you escape and we go back to being master's favorites, or I help capture you and get rewarded for my loyalty.&quot; he turned to Max when asked about Gemini's ability to control water and frowned, pausing before he responded.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The Keeper is the most powerful being in this realm.&quot; he stated, &quot;But he's not the only one who can manipulate it. If you're clever and persuasive enough, the realm will answer your call. Maybe I'll teach you how to do so... once my toes are cleaned of this dried dirt.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T09:48:51-07:00","id":235503,"title":"","content":"Seeing the beautiful Leo again made Jessica's heart catch in her throat. He was such a lovely creature! It took a moment, but she found her voice. &quot;I fear you are wasting your time with Nate. He would never clean your toes, not in the way you suggest. I think you're a stunning creature, but none of us will clean your feet like that. If you want your paws cleaned, we're by a perfectly good stream. I'd even help you, but not with my tongue.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica fought the urge to offer to do other things for him with her tongue. She had to remember Curtis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T11:06:07-07:00","id":235588,"title":"","content":"Nate was struggling to stay calm. The voices were getting louder, but he had to stay in control. &quot;Still not happening. You know, two can play at that game. You're seriously underestimating us. Go ahead, call the Keeper. I'm ready to lie my way out. I'm not afraid of throwing you under the bus.&quot; <i>'Even if I don't remember what is a bus.</i> &quot;We can get dangerous, Leo. So either we cooperate calmly, or either we're <i>both</i> going to suffer an horrible fate.&quot; He leaned toward him, and opened his mouth to phrase another threat, when Jessica interrupted him by essentially declaring her love to the feline. He was seriously shocked, and rolled his eyes. There it was, the girl's weakness. Falling in love with a beast that wants to eat you? Yeah, that was such a good idea. He stepped back, and sat by the stream.<br /> &quot;She's right. You're wasting your time with me. Try your luck with the other two. The Oxen certainly seems eager.&quot; He didn't even realize he hadn't called her by her name. Leo's pattern of speech was starting to rub on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T19:58:51-07:00","id":236103,"title":"","content":"&quot;Well aren't you a polite one.&quot; Leo responded to Jessica, before leering at Nate, &quot;At least one of you realizes when you're up a creek.&quot; he stood up and approached them, wrapping an arm around Jessica's shoulder as he leaned in. &quot;Since you find me so stunning, I'll share a couple of my secrets. But you keep that ram in line from now on, or I'll shove his own horns up his ass.&quot; he promised before pointing off into the distance.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;We call it The Hedge, the border realm between Arcadia and Earth. If you want to get back home, you have to cross through it, and many don't survive the experience... physically or mentally.&quot; There didn't seem to be anything where he was pointing, so evidently this Hedge was quite a distance away from them. &quot;Now manipulating the realm is a bit trickier.&quot; he continued, &quot;You're going to need to sign a contract.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> He released Jessica as he clapped his paws together. &quot;But that can wait until later, I need a bath, and this bovine beauty has offered me assistance.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T21:54:23-07:00","id":236181,"title":"","content":"Max was disappointed not to hear anything on directing any changes. Still, he'd tried, at least; it felt better than doing nothing. Like Nate, he felt a little judgmental about how... interested Jessica seemed, but, well, it was hard to keep up under all the hypocrisy. <i>'Hell, you didn't think it would be so bad to </i>lick the filth from his toes<i>!</i> <i>Just... she's keeping him helpful. That's a lot.</i>'<br /> <br /> He leaned back a bit from the lion's approach. <i>'Not a prey response,'</i> he told himself. And then admitted, <i>'Not </i>just<i> a prey response.'</i> Also not just a prey response was putting a hand on Nate's shoulder and trying to meet his eye. It, admittedly, felt just a bit too much to him like a child seeking comfort from an adult, but a big part of it was to try to keep the Goat from rising to the threat. He'd shown a lot of self-control so far, but the Leo couldn't have been making it easy.<br /> <br /> It seemed best to try to keep the conversation going. It wasn't as though Max was short on questions. This was interesting stuff. &quot;The Hedge... What sorts of things make it so dangerous? And this contract, it, uh... sounds a bit less one-sided than the <i>last one</i> we 'signed,' I hope?&quot; He gave a forced smile. &quot;I mean, what sorts of things can you do, now? Gemini's water thing was, er, sounded really impressive.&quot; He regretted being a bit too drugged to see it clearly. Though one thing crossed his mind. Nor had Nate calling Jessica an ox completely escaped his notice. &quot;Uh... Also, I guess I feel a little silly doing that, using names for the signs. What's hi... he... ...&quot; He gave a grunt of a cough. &quot;What are Gemini's names? And what's yours, for that matter?&quot; A pig he might have been, but it didn't take him long to remember his manners. &quot;Oh! S-sorry. Rude of me to just ask. We never did proper introductions last time. I'm Max.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tweakery! 08-21-2014, 12:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T21:14:22-07:00","id":237744,"title":"","content":"After Max introduced himself and answered a few more questions, Jessica let Leo lead her away to help him bathe. Her heart pounded with both anticipation and dread. Would he only want help with bathing, or did he want more? What would he tell her? Would he harm her? Following Leo, these questions and many others rattled around in the ox woman's mind. However, one quickly occupied her more than all of the others. How far would she go with Leo? Would she betray Curtis? She soon had her answer.<br /> <br /> Once out of Max and Nate's view, Leo gave her a kiss. Butterflies churning in multiple stomachs, Jessica returned the lion man's kiss. At first, so did so almost chastely. However, that lasted by an instant. In turn, Leo swept her up into his arms and carried her down into the water. Jessica's surprised and delighted giggles drifted back toward Max and Nate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T04:17:58-07:00","id":238087,"title":"","content":"When Leo threatened to do something...well...unpleasant with his horns, the Ram felt ready to explode. He couldn't contain his anger anymore. He prepared to lash out at him, when he felt the Pig's hand on his shoulder. He looked him in the eyes, and something felt off. Was the kid shorter than before? It seemed he was, but...nah. It didn't really matter. Although, he felt something in him. Maybe it was because he always called him a kid, but some part of his mind wanted to preserve the piggy. He was kin, and he needed help, he needed the Ram's strength. <i>Protect the young lambs, protect the offspring,</i> said his instincts. Well, the piglet was hardly a lamb and the Goat certainly didn't remember siring him, but he was indeed a young of his small herd. And picking a fight with Leo would only endanger the both of them. And so, he quelled his wrath, and breathed deeply.<br /> <br /> However, the Ox's giggles fired up his anger again. Still sitting, he began to tear down small patches of grass around him, to contain his fury.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-23-2014, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T06:53:05-07:00","id":238154,"title":"","content":"&quot;If you want to use this realm's magic, you need to make a contract.&quot; Leo repeated, licking Jessica on the nap of her neck once they were waist deep in the water. &quot;Like the one you made with your figurines, only much more useful on your side of the bargain.&quot; his paws were trailing over her body as he spoke, clearly he was skilled in divulging information while acting sensual at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I can teach you how to form an contract with animals, you can invoke the powers of an Oxen, instead of just their form.&quot; he offered. &quot;Of course, I'm going to need some incentive first. I can't just give away powerful secrets on a whim.&quot; he winked, resting his paws on her backside and squeezing, &quot;I think you know what I mean.&quot; he licked his lips, his teeth gleaming in the fluorescent light that surrounded them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T15:05:12-07:00","id":238571,"title":"","content":"Jessica smiled back. &quot;I think I do know what you. Let's see if I can give you the incentive that you need.&quot;<br /> <br /> With that, Jessica kissed Leo and returned his attentions. Part of her felt guilty, but it seemed too late to stop. She also promised herself that she would teach Max and Nate anything she learned from Leo. Shortly after making this resolution, Jessica found it harder and harder to think rationally. She just hoped that Leo would refrain from preying on her after he finished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T16:08:20-07:00","id":238647,"title":"","content":"Seduced or not, Leo was not as gentle with Jessica as his previous attention had suggested. He was like a wild beast, strong and primal, more dominating than any human would have been able to mimic. When it was over, he sat upon the mouth of the water, grinning triumphantly to himself, paws clasped together and elbows resting on his knees.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;A deal's a deal.&quot; he said grinning triumphantly, &quot;I'll teach you the Contract of Animals.&quot; he leaned back, moving his paws to prop himself up. Soon, his demeanor changed and he took on a more serious tone as he looked the oxen straight in the eyes, then began to speak as if to the realm itself.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I stand as witness to the signing of this contract. This one wishes to gain the power of the Oxen!&quot; he called out. There was a palpable, shifting feeling in the environment, as if something had heard and was reacting to Leo's words. &quot;If you would gain the powers of the Beast, you must become a Beast.&quot; as he continued to speak, the shifting sensation grew, the environment became deathly silent, and out of nowhere, a long horned ox stepped into view behind Leo.<br /> <br /> &quot;Will you agree to the terms of the contract? To cast aside your human weaknesses and concerns and accept the strength and stamina of the Oxen? Will you agree to live as the Beast's do?&quot; he asked","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T21:14:01-07:00","id":239893,"title":"","content":"Studying the long horned ox and Leo, Jessica wondered what she should reply. On the one hand, it seemed wrong to betray Curtis and gain nothing for it other than a sore body and an incredible memory. On the other hand, the price asked sounded terrible. Live as the beasts do? Give up human concerns and weaknesses? How could she do that? Then an awful thought struck her.<br /> <br /> Jessica answered Leo's question with one of her own. &quot;Lover, have I not done that already? Have I not mated with you like an animal? Without any thought of my boyfriend or any concern for human morality? I would say that I have already meet the terms of the contract!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typoes 08-25-2014, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T22:12:28-07:00","id":239923,"title":"","content":"Leo's eyes closed half way as he leered at Jessica, the ox continued to approach the two, staring blankly at the female as if waiting for her to agree.<br /> <br /> &quot;Actions speak louder than words, so they say.&quot; Leo replied, but it was more to the world around him than to Jessica herself. The shuttering feeling of the world grew still for a moment, as if pondering the words the two of them had spoken. Then it picked up again as the oxen began to change. Its body turned pale and transparent as it slowly lifted into the air, then with a snort, it charged Jessica. But rather than stampede straight over her, the ox was absorbed on contact, being sucked into her body and vanishing completely from sight.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;It is done. You have signed the Contract of Fang and Talon, and the power of the animals is yours to command.&quot; Leo said as the shuttering of the world began to still once more, &quot;The spirit of the Ox has bonded with your soul, you are one in the same now.&quot; he explained. &quot;Congratulations, and remember your agreement. There are consequences for breaking a Fae bound contract.&quot; he explained, before his ears perked up, &quot;Oh yeah, you're half fairy. Probably should have mentioned that at some point.&quot; he laughed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-25-2014, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:31:46-07:00","id":240316,"title":"","content":"Jessica checked out her reflection in the water. Seeing that Leo was telling the truth, she shook her head. &quot;Maybe you should have. No wonder you had your way with me first.&quot;<br /> <br /> After her lame joke, Jessica fell silent. She needed to think about what she had done. She was also in no hurry to get back to Max and Nate. No doubt they would think poorly of what she had just done. She also doubted that she would be able to teach them what Leo had just taught her. She still could not comprehend what had happened.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typoes 08-25-2014, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T13:22:59-07:00","id":240632,"title":"","content":"&quot;Oh that was just a down payment on my end.&quot; Leo answered, &quot;Wanted to make sure I got something out of it before the deal was signed.&quot; he shrugged before turning around. &quot;Teaching the contract is easy. Just let the realm know Max and Nate intend to pledge themselves to the Pig and Goat. They just need to agree with at least one witness present, and that's that.&quot; the lion man explained. He waved to her with the back of his hand as he started walking away into the bushes.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;But I've stuck around long enough, and you'll probably start viewing me as a predator soon. I'll pop back in if things get too complicated for you. But you're on your own for now.&quot; clearly the aspects of the lion were strong in him to leave a girl so soon after having a passionate encounter.<br /> <br /> But then again, was this some manner of Fae prostitution, have sex, pay with power, then leave? Jessica didn't have much time to ponder it right now, she had been left alone, and if their previous encounters with the realm were any indication, that was not something she wanted to be for long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T22:43:39-07:00","id":241103,"title":"","content":"Knowing that she had best not be alone, Jessica set back for where she left Max and Nate. Only when she was part way back did she remember that she had not bothered to redress. While her remaining clothes amounted to little more than rags, she thought she had better go fetch them. Shame at what she had done and her extra hair made her want to avoid nudity around Max and Nate. When she returned to where she and Leo had dallied, she spotted a red fox sniffing her torn garments. When the fox spotted Jessica, it snatched up her clothing and ran off into some trees.<br /> <br /> Outraged, Jessica chased after the fox. In the trees, she quickly lost the fox and her clothes. Defeated, she returned to Max and Nate naked..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  Read the ooc thread 08-26-2014, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T05:57:08-07:00","id":241255,"title":"","content":"The contract had made the environment go silent, and it hadn't been just around Jessica. Nate felt it too. Or, more accurately, the Ram felt it. Something bigger and solemn was happening, and the Beast respected that, which allowed Nate's human mind to surface again. <br /> Why was he so upset? Why did he care so much about Leo having Jessica?<br /> <i>Because it's you. You're Leo.</i> Was he...seeing a bit of his former self in him? The confidence, the cockiness, the masculinity? Could it just be a matter of ego? It wasn't good. He was becoming too much of an animal. An idea formed into his mind, a solution to his... Devolution.<br /> <br /> He looked up at Jessica when she came back. Well, actually, he leered for a moment before meeting her gaze. &quot; There you are. We were thinking about going back to the ranch. So what happened? Did you have a romp with Leo? I hope he gave you something good for that.&quot; He had given her something, he knew that. She had changed, and not necessarily in a good way. She seemed more...wild.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T07:05:20-07:00","id":241305,"title":"","content":"Jessica noticed Nate checking her out. She found herself oddly flattered by his leer. &quot;Leo and I did mate, as you say. It was really something. And I was rewarded for it. I learned to how to use my oxen nature. If either of you wanted, I could teach you how to do the same thing.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T12:20:33-07:00","id":241586,"title":"","content":"&quot;And what, do we also have to screw in the water? I'm not used to doing it outside, but it's better than nothing.&quot; Nate laughed. More seriously, the idea of the contract was scaring him, but it sounded appealing. He didn't like the idea of getting closer to the Ram in him, but he wanted to get stronger. He needed a weapon against the perils of this realm, and he didn't know when he would be offered another chance. Yeah, it wasn't to the level of the power of Gemini, but it was still something. But...would he be able to go back, once he had agreed to this pact?<br /> <br /> He sighed and got up. Something had to be done. He couldn't just endure. He had to fight back, and he couldn't just stay passive, he had to take some risk. &quot;Alright. I'll do it. The Keeper seriously screwed me over with this body, the least I could do with it is to learn how to exploit it. And...better to have all the powers we can get, right?&quot; He looked at Max for support, a hint of uncertainty in his voice.<br /> <br /> Besides, this could work well with his plan. He didn't want to share it with the others right now. He wasn't sure if they would approve of it, and he didn't want them to restrain him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-26-2014, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T21:02:09-07:00","id":241964,"title":"","content":"Max felt some relief as Nate held off on flipping out at Leo and tried to give him a grateful smile. He <i>did</i> believe the Ram's talk earlier of how the three of them could probably have taken Leo if it came to a fight. Mostly. In a fair situation, certainly. That just wouldn't be what they'd walk into. He and Nate still weren't at 100%, and all of them were still getting used to their new bodies -- bodies, for that matter, that weren't really designed as murder machines. He of the Western Zodiac had also picked up some unknown tricks from at least one Contract. At least one of them might not have walked away from a fight. It would have been enough that he really knew his way around his body.<br /> <br /> Judging by the distant sounds that followed, Leo also really knew his way around <i>Jessica's</i> body. Max had told himself she knew what she was doing -- and still did -- but... It definitely unsettled him. He'd had the unfortunate experience once to be kept up at night by some neighbors in the dorm. He would have given a lot to go back there for the moment. Knowing Jessica, having no wall in the way, and hearing some less than human moans from both of them made this <i>much</i> more uncomfortable. <i>'She knows what she's doing. She knows what she's doing. She knows what she's doing.'</i> At least one clenched fist belied his confidence in that mantra.<br /> <br /> Max looked up and looked around a bit as Jessica's Contract was struck. Like Nate, he picked up on the stillness. And it was more than without: part of him stirred, as though to stand at respectful attention. He'd felt it stirring before, but not like this. It had seemed all appetite, craving, and simple pleasures before. It was strange to feel it acknowledge something greater, something he could never put into words. Indeed, words seemed paltry before it. This was perhaps the first time he felt more than disgust and shame at what he'd become. Those two yet predominated, of course, make no mistake.<br /> <br /> On the topic of disgust and shame toward oneself, Jessica returned, a bit less clothed and -- as Nate noted -- more wild. Blushing a bit, he tried to avert his gaze, holding up a hand to assist. Max cringed as he heard the word she used to describe what she'd done, without a hint of self-awareness. <i>'People don't say they <b>mate</b>d unless they're using it in a joke!</i>' Still, he felt hypocritical just thinking it. She'd given up something, something important to her, and was now offering to share what she'd gained by it. Like he had any right to judge. &quot;Nate, please let it go,&quot; he mumbled, not laughing at the Ram's joke.<br /> <br /> Still, the offer definitely disappointed Max as well. Recent new spot of not-disdain he'd found for it, he kind of wanted <i>less</i> to do with the pig he'd become, not more. Though it did make sense to get <i>some</i> greater advantage. Even so, the thought of not only deepening the connection, but of signing onto it with his own hand? Terrified him on several levels. That Nate seemed interested in his take on things put him off-balance, too. <i>'What if the cravings get worse? What if they just feel too good? What could I possibly get that could balance <b>that!?</b></i>' Well, there was one way to find out. Max didn't think himself in a position to judge Jessica, but he did feel in a position to look a gift ox in the mouth. So to speak. What with trying not to look directly at the naked lady.<br /> <br /> &quot;I, uh... Th-Thank you for... for going through what you did for this, Jessica. But, uh... B-Before we say yes, m-maybe you could tell us more about it? I mean... Details? Particulars? What it'll let us do, anything we... might give up? I mean, uh...&quot; He tried a bit of (an apparently grunty) laugh to lighten the mood. &quot;Y'know, not knowing the specifics on a deal got us into this mess, right?&quot; He shivered despite himself. &quot;I-I don't think any of us want a repeat of that. Could you... just tell us more before we think about signing on the dotted line?&quot;<br /> <br /> Max was aware of how spineless he sounded, but not a word was untrue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 08-27-2014, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T22:12:09-07:00","id":241982,"title":"","content":"Jessica looked at Max with compassion. He had far more good qualities than he knew. She replied, &quot;Max, I discovered that the price was to give up human concerns and weakness. When Leo told me that, I was horrified. It seemed too much to ask. I almost declined the offer. Then I realized something terrible. I had already paid the contract price. By going with Leo, I had given up my morality. And what is morality but a hum concern and weakness?&quot; <br /> <br /> Jessica shook her head. &quot;It's funny. I had thought that my desire for Leo was proof that I was still human at heart. What ox would want to sleep with a lion? But I was wrong. The proof of my humanity was being true to my human life, my boyfriend. Sleeping with Leo was the act of an animal rather than a woman. I may have gained something, but I may have lost more. I learned the contract because I had already paid the price for it. Also, don't think I'm noble; I just gave into lust. Still, if you two want, I'll teach you what I learned.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T22:22:49-07:00","id":241993,"title":"","content":"For once, Nate didn't feel like making fun of Jessica. She really was opening her heart there. And her speech resonated with him. He noted the part about her boyfriend though. But still. He had taken his decision.<br /> &quot;Well in that case, I'd say Max and I already paid this price too, back at the pond. I mean...look at us, and look at you. Truth be told, I think you only came to our level of...Beastness. So if I have a chance to exploit that, I'll sure as well will. &quot;<br /> He stretched. &quot;Now come on. I'm in. Feel free to tell me if I'm losing it!&quot; He laughed again in self-deprecation, the bleat stronger than ever in his voice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-27-2014, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T11:20:22-07:00","id":243295,"title":"","content":"Seeing that Nate at least had made up his mind, Jessica tried to remember exactly what Leo had done. She called out, &quot;I stand as witness to this contract. Nate wishes to gain the power of the Ram!&quot;<br /> <br /> It seemed Jessica had managed it. There was again a palpable, shifting feeling in the environment, as if something had heard and was reacting to her words. She continued, &quot;If you want the powers of the Beast, you must become a Beast.&quot;<br /> <br /> As before, the shifting sensation grew. The environment became deathly silent, and out of nowhere, a great ram stepped into view behind Jessica. She asked, &quot;Will you agree to this contract? To cast aside your human weaknesses and concerns and accept the powers of the Ram? Will you agree to live like a ram?&quot;<br /> <br /> As Jessica spoke these last words, she hoped that she was doing it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T13:30:01-07:00","id":243365,"title":"","content":"There it was again, that same solemn feeling. So...they were actually doing magical stuff. Sure, they had been in this fantastic realm for days, weeks, or even years, but it was the first time they were actually harnessing the power around them. The Beast inside the musician's mind was holding its breath, waiting for its host to answer, and couldn't do anything right now. It had been influencing him until now, but the choice was still in his hands.<br /> <br /> Nate gulped, and beads of sweat ran across his temples and got lost in his fur. <i>This is fucking creepy.</i> Jessica had just summoned some kind of ghost! He had to admit, she had guts. He couldn't let himself be one-upped by her. He looked at the Ram, and something clicked inside him. It was like a connection was trying to form. Was he looking at his future? Would he become like this ruminant if they failed to escape? His mind was running wild, but he had to act. No time to go back.<br /> <br /> &quot;...It's done already. Now bring it, you fuckin' sheep!&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, he <i>had</i> to give it a little bravado. However, when the Ram started to charge toward him with a snort, he immediately regretted provoking him, and began to turn around to run, but it was too late. The Beast should have been crashing into him, but it rather <i>melted</i> into him, like ghosts possess a mortal in the movies. Nate fell on his knees, and held his head, panting for breath. The bestial voices in his mind were absolutely delighted, and sang and bleated with joy. He feared he had made a huge mistake, especially when he felt his legs becoming more woollier, but then he realized something. The contract was calming the Beast in him. Yes, it was very pleased with the current event, but it was satisfied. Nate didn't feel the urges anymore, he didn't heard any voices compelling him to act on instinct. He was back in control. He was...free?<br /> <br /> He looked up, and smiled proudly. &quot;This...is freakin' awesome.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-29-2014, 08:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T01:53:37-07:00","id":244680,"title":"","content":"<i>'Already paid the price...'</i> Well, Max certainly couldn't argue their displays weren't <i>at least</i> comparable to Jessica's. But the whole thing still felt fishy. Was making the Contract really just a matter of taking advantage of a price already paid? Or was it committing to <i>continue</i> making such payments? Hearing Jessica's words when issuing the contract only made him sure of the latter. Granted, with strong temptations everywhere, perhaps the difference between taking and not taking was academic. Save that striking the bargain at least gave <i>something</i>. In addition to the knowledge he would no longer resist the dehumanizing humiliations.<br /> <br /> The stillness came again, even more intense for the proximity, and Max felt his bristles stand on end. He couldn't have said anything if he wanted to. The pig in him was attentive and respectful again, as the great Ram came to be. Just being before such a creature... It had a palpable certainty in itself, as though all the mountains in all the world could grind to dust with time, and it would still be there, just as it was. The idea that anything could be lesser than it seemed shot through with doubt. The Pig couldn't remember the last time he had felt so small and petty. The beast before them was a Presence.<br /> <br /> Max saw... something going on between it and Nate, just from being in the same place. He thought he saw something writhing around and within his friend, but could never be sure his eyes weren't just playing tricks. Whatever the case, the kid couldn't help backing up and hurrying to the side, away from the Ram and the Sheep; he was of one mind with the Pig that it was wrong to intrude on this. Though self-preservation might have played a role, given Nate's defiant posture and the Great Beast's charge. He found his voice only long enough to gasp in horror as it crashed into the musician... And then it was over. The mere memory of it kept the stillness for a few moments more. Its pride stayed with Nate.<br /> <br /> The Pig stared for a time. Nate looked a bit wilder, just as Jessica had, all the more noticeable with his other changes. There was a greater surety there, too. It seemed obvious in Jessica as well, in hindsight. It made sense; beasts were less likely to second-guess themselves than humans, and simply were what they were. Given how many years he had fought to win some measure of confidence in himself, the Contract had never seemed more tempting. Though second-guessing came into it again: these were the Ram and the Ox, after all, beasts known for their surefootedness and endurance. What grace could the lowly Pig offer?<br /> <br /> Still, for the sake of saying something, Max asked both of the newly anointed ones, &quot;Wow... W-What's it like? How do you both feel?&quot; True, Nate's words hinted at the answer, but they hadn't exactly registered. Distracted piglet was distracted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T06:14:51-07:00","id":244760,"title":"","content":"Nate let out a small and relieved laugh, and looked at Max through his shaggy hair. &quot;I feel great, man. It's...It's like I just corrected a big mistake. Something was unbalanced in me, you know. As if the Ram wanted to be acknowledged. I think...that's why I got those urges. That was a way to get my attention, you know? To make me listen to him. And with this pact, I...essentialy admitted that I was part beast.&quot; He shrugged. &quot;I feel at peace with the Ram now. I know he'll cooperate with me.&quot; He got up, and looked at his own body, trying to register any different changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T22:58:05-07:00","id":247498,"title":"","content":"Max listened to Nate, nodding a bit. &quot;I... I got it. I'm glad it's stopped fighting you.&quot; His two friends certainly didn't seem to have any issues. They'd gotten a bit more beastly, but given where they'd started... and the changes by the lake... That was barely worth mentioning. Albeit still worth mentioning. Certainly, it seemed a very small price, if freely paying it quelled the animal in their hearts. And as for the rest? Just admitting that one was no longer completely human? Were Max to be honest, he'd have conceded he felt it silly to pretend otherwise. <i>'Let's see. You've rooted mushrooms out of the ground. You've obeyed commands like a pet and felt proud of it. You've eaten from a trough. And liked it. </i>You have a tail<i>. And... and the face you do. You're not <b>all</b>-pig, but who are you kidding here?'</i> Of course, an intellectual realization doesn't always make for acceptance. It didn't here.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well. I, uh... I guess m-maybe we could make this... three for three...?&quot; Max breathed deep, feeling a bit dizzy. From the look of him, the Ox and the Sheep might have worried the Pig was going to throw up again. Still, he took another breath and tried to stand tall -- much as that was kind of not really an option anymore. He was going to do this. &quot;I...&quot; His throat felt dry. He swallowed, for all the good it did. He went on anyway. &quot;I...&quot; Again, nothing. He was trembling more than just a little by this point. <i>'Come on. Come on! You've got a lot to gain and not much to lose! Just get it over with, already!'</i> Max took and held a breath. &quot;I... ... I can't,&quot; he said, exhaling, and seeming to visibly deflate all the more. &quot;I'm sorry, I just...&quot; Gazing at the grass, he shook his head absently, and clenched his fists in frustration. &quot;I can't.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Eh, took out that last line. 09-03-2014, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T07:56:41-07:00","id":247854,"title":"","content":"Jessica said, &quot;Max, it's all right. You don't have to do it, and we can do it later if you change your mind.&quot;<br /> <br /> Oddly, Jessica found herself thinking of Jill, a childhood friend. Years ago, Jessica and Jill had gone to River Hills Mall to get their ears pierced. At the last minute, Jill changed her mind about getting earrings. She was afraid that it would hurt. Jessica herself had still gotten her ears pierced. Even after she had truthfully reported to her friend that it had not hurt, Jill remained fast in her decision.<br /> <br /> There was no need to pressure people to do things, Jessica had decided that day. Years later, she still believed that. Pulling herself to the present, she asked, &quot;What should we do now?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typoes 09-03-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T11:08:02-07:00","id":248018,"title":"","content":"Nate shrugged. &quot;Your call. I won't force you.&quot; But that didn't stop him from judging him. What had happened to Max? Where did the boar go? Now, all that was left was a little small creature made of walking bacon who lacked any backbone. He didn't remember him being that small before, but it felt right : it was only fitting of his demeanor. &quot;But someday, you're gonna have to act if you want to survive in Arcadia. You can't just stay passive. Otherwise, how will you fight back when the Tiger, the Dragon or even Leo will get hungry? I won't always be there for you man, and neither Jessica.&quot; He almost added <i>&quot;And you'll be forced to stay here forever&quot;</i> but he figured that would be too harsh. It seemed that he still had some compassion.<br /> <br /> &quot;I wanna go to the ranch. I'm tired, and I want to sleep in a &quot;safer&quot; place, so to speak. Also, I have something to do there.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:50:58-07:00","id":248860,"title":"","content":"&quot;Thanks,&quot; Max said to Jessica, taking a calming breath. &quot;Right. M-Maybe I just need time.&quot; His frustration fell off a bit, but not much; it would likely stick around to eat at him a while.<br /> <br /> Or it would have, if not for the mention of getting, well, eaten. Nate's casual comments might not have gotten much out of him normally. But already angry at himself and the situation, starting to get very hungry again after puking, and getting a reminder of a three hour period soon after his arrival... &quot;... Then I'll fight back. Because the next time wild animals are clawing at me, I won't have a goddamn <i>hook</i> in my gut.&quot; Max tried to stop there, but an angry grunt said that clearly wasn't happening right away. &quot;And excuse me for not wanting to jump right into the next chance to do something without thinking it through. Because I'm still getting over the last time I did. You remember.&quot; He looked up, then, and his smoldering eyes looked straight into Nate's. &quot;I almost got us killed, <i>and I gave you those eyes.</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> Even with tears starting to well up, there was hard steel there, and Max seemed to stand a little taller. An onlooker might have thought to look for tusks. But only for a few moments. &quot;I-I don't want you all getting hurt because I... I f-fucked up like that. I can't.&quot; He took another breath and looked off, tears falling. He snorted a bitter laugh. &quot;And besides. Let's be serious here. I'd be making a Contract. With a <i>pig</i>. Think about how stupid that sounds. Oxen are strong and enduring. Rams are strong and agile. Pigs are pathetic. I'd get fatter and tastier, and that wouldn't do any of us any favors. So go on.&quot; He looked Nate right in the eyes again, blinking past the tears. There was more pleading there than he wanted. &quot;Tell me what good it'll do. Tell me why it's worth it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T09:46:41-07:00","id":248917,"title":"","content":"Nate rolled his eyes again, and let out an exasperated snort. &quot;Oh, for God's sake. I told you I wouldn't force you, so drop it!&quot; He looked at the tears going down his snout, frowned a little in disgust, before opening his big mouth again.<br /> &quot;You know what, on second thought, I still have things to say. You need to grow a fucking pair man! You say you'll fight? Good! And with what, your meaty and greasy hands? You need a weapon! And yes, you did led us into this trap, I remember it well, thank you. But for crying out loud, stop apologizing for it! Assume your mistakes!&quot;<br /> <br /> He took a deep breath, pondering if he should stop there, but the floodgates were open. &quot;And maybe, just maybe, if you owned to your mistakes and carried on, you wouldn't be so annoying by crying every five minutes! Look at you! I know that you're a pig but have some pride man. Everytime someone else come here you're stuttering at every word, almost hiding behind Jessica or me! How old are you Max, because I've known kids that had more balls than you!&quot;<br /> He breathed again, that was almost over.<br /> &quot;And you're right, you'll be useless if you forge a contract right now in your form and get stuck like this. But think about it : it could have been way worse than that. You could have been the Rabbit, or even the Chicken, forced to lay eggs! At least right now you're pretty stout, and I'm pretty sure you can endure lots of stuff. &quot; The Ram finally smiled smugly. &quot;You know, if you had more pride, you could become the Boar again. Maybe the contract will let you do that!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;And now, could we <i> please </i>go to the ranch?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 09-04-2014, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T18:47:01-07:00","id":250271,"title":"","content":"&quot;I suppose we should get back,&quot; Jessica agreed. &quot;But, Nate, I think you were far too tough on Max. We're all doing the best that we can.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not wanting to give Nate a chance to yell at her too, she started to walk toward the ranch. She still ached from her tryst with Leo. Every detail of it and Leo was clear in her mind. What was less clear was her memories of Curtis. That worried her. She also still felt guilty. She braced herself for whatever might come next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T20:41:13-07:00","id":250384,"title":"","content":"&quot;'Assume my mistakes?' What the hell do you think I'm <i>doing!</i>&quot; Max had thought he was done, but apparently not. &quot;I wasn't cautious enough about that clearing. <i>Of course</i> I'm not going to go diving into something like this after five seconds. We don't actually know a whole lot about the deal, except that it needs us to swear to do <i>the exact thing we were trying to avoid!</i>&quot; He gave an angry snort of his own. &quot;Especially after the 'deal' that got us into this mess in the first place. That sure seems to be sticking. Pretty sure the Contract isn't gonna be happy with just acting like animals the once.&quot;<br /> <br /> The crack about kids stung deep. Max had quietly pieced together that he was definitely smaller than he'd been, even if he wasn't ready to admit it to himself. He might even have conceded he had been crying a lot more than he usually did and drawn a possible connection. His head simply wasn't clear enough, though. It just fed his rage. &quot;Oh, so you knew kids who got dragged off, turned into farm animals, butchered for hours, tried to kill a friend? Or something about as traumatic? And then came out mentally A-OK an hour later? Wow, what a thing not to have mentioned! Yeah, Nate, you are so full of shit.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Goat's last bit was likewise not seen in the most generous of lights. &quot;Oh good. I can get fatter, slower, and tastier, or -- if I 'have some pride' -- I can become a rageaholic who wants to kill everyone! Great picks. I'm sold.&quot; Max grunted out a frustrated sigh, through tusks that had grown a bit more prominent as he'd spoken. A bit of height and faint browning of the bristles had joined them, all very subtly. &quot;Argh...&quot; He shook his head. This wasn't how he enjoyed feeling on the best of days, particularly after everything else. Particularly now that he felt its similarity to that cauldron of rage when he'd been the Boar. When killing Nate had been his one and only thought. He at least recognized he needed to lose some steam.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, yeah, we can head back,&quot; he said curtly. A short pause. &quot;Actually. You guys head on.&quot; He started off a different way from Jessica. &quot;I need some fresh air. I'm taking the scenic route.&quot; Max hesitated after a bit; part of him was aware this was kind of dumb and pointless. Still, being away from the argument was already making him feel a bit better, albeit not enough to turn back. &quot;... Stay safe. See you when I see you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max wasn't really sure where he was going, but that didn't seem so important. If nothing else, his body was good for one thing: if it came to it, he could probably follow his musk back until he found the Ram's and Ox's and then follow them back to the ranch. For now, he just wanted some space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T01:13:30-07:00","id":251342,"title":"","content":"Nate had been clenching his fist during the Pig's retort. Anyone else other than the Ram might have been considering apologizing, or even questioning himself. But he didn't see any reason to.<br /> &quot;Screw you Max. I've been trying to help you all day long because you can't stand on your own, but I can't anymore. Without me, you would be starving. Or, you know, you would have gorged yourself on the slop. I'm tired of taking care of a whiny teenager.&quot; He saw Jessica leaving, and looked at her for a moment. &quot;I also want to be alone right now. Don't follow me.&quot;<i> And don't hold me back.</i> He decided to start off in a third direction. This realm had strange ways to behave, surely they could find three different routes to a big place such as the ranch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T05:33:42-07:00","id":251418,"title":"","content":"Hearing Max and Nate fighting, Jessica turned around. She opened her mouth to try to get them both to come along with her, but saw that neither looked like she could change their mind. She sighed, and continued on her own for a bit. However, before she reached the ranch, she decided to return to the stream. She thought it would be fun to watch the colorful fish dart about in the crystal clear water. It might help her think of what to do next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typo 09-07-2014, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T15:04:09-07:00","id":253616,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, Nate kept grumbling, walking on his own path. <i>Why did I associate myself with those two</i>, he thought. <i>They're stupid and weak. One's a crybaby who sobs as soon as he opens his mouth, and the other can't stop flirting with every male carnivore. If only I was born a Dragon, or a Tiger. That would have been cool.</i><br /> He noticed that the trail he was following went along a rocky hill. It was pretty high, Nate estimated it at 100 yards, more or less. He looked around, and only saw huge mounts of grass and trees that blocked his far vision. <i>I should have a good view of the surroundings up there</i>. He searched for a trail, but the stony landscape didn't seem friendly to wannabe hikers. He was ready to give up, but something in his mind was nagging him to persevere and try. He smiled wryly. That's right, he was part Ram now, and they're known for going up in impossible places. Plus, he still had hands, which meant that he could have a good grip. <i>Yeah. I can do this</i>. He went to the base of the hill, spat on his hands, rubbed them, then flexed his legs before jumping and grabbing a hold, hauling himself on a big rock. &quot;Wow&quot;, he said looking down to the ground. He had never managed to jump this high before. He laughed incredulously, massaging his furry legs. He didn't realize that it was the first time that he didn't shiver when touching his wool. Nate sat up, and resumed climbing. It was exhilarating, like he was discovering something that had been sealed inside him forever.<br /> <br /> About halfway to the top, the young goat-man took a short break, enjoying the scenery. He was way out of the tall grass, and could see for miles away. He could see the ranch, from there. Still, it wasn't enough. He could go higher. He noticed that there was some mountain flowers sticking out of some rocks. Absent-mindedly, he reached out and plucked them before putting them in his mouth. Well, he could give himself a treat after this hard climbing. Although, he didn't find it that hard. He was a natural at this, it seemed.<br /> Soon, he reached the top of the hill, and sat on the highest stone, panting, but immensely proud and happy. He remembered that he wasn't really an outdoor man back on Earth. Well, that certainly had changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 09-10-2014, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T05:27:59-07:00","id":254021,"title":"","content":"(Alright, time to create 3 different scenarios. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> While Nate was busy surveying his surroundings, the ground started to shake. Pebbles and loose stones wobbled every few seconds, and it would soon become clear that they were responding to footsteps. Very... heavy... footsteps!<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Stupid goat ate my crops!&quot; shouted a booming voice as the shaking grew more intense, and an enormous hand, nearly half the size of Nate's body rose up over the other side of the hill, reaching to pluck him from his resting spot and get revenge for whoever the hand belong to!<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> The stream had changed since the last time Jessica had visited it. Perhaps she did not follow the same way back, or perhaps it had been altered by her and Leo's activities previously. Judging by the scene she came across, the later was probably the case! The river had new occupants, but they were not the fish women from earlier. In fact, both the mushrooms and the shrubbery had vanished, to be replaced by men and women looking to bathe.<br /> <br /> But these were no ordinary women, they were cousins of Jessica's! They resembled black and white dairy cows, sporting four breasts, and having large rings pierced through their noses. As they bathed and played in the water, they were guarded over by a single male, a huge looking bull, who's body resembled a minotaur. He was at least twice the size of a normal human, and the prominent, 7 inch horns he proudly displayed was clear evidence that he wasn't going to let anyone else near his cows.<br /> <br /> Wait, were they his cows; just because he was the only bull in the area, did he have claim to them? The whole area reeked of sex and musk, which is likely what the cows were busy washing off. Or perhaps, the realm was learning what sort of traps Jessica could be lured into, after having studied her...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Taking the scenic route through a realm you have never been to before, had no map to navigate, and had the power to change its geography on a whim was probably the stupidest thing Max could have done. Clearly he still hadn't fully realized his situation, but the realm was eager to give him another reminder. It was not long before he came across a large, pit in the middle of his path. The pit was filled almost to the brim with mud, and its depths were impossible to estimate. The mud pit had a sign with the picture of a pig man up to his waist in the mud, arms up in the air, and mouth open wide, facing the sky as if over joyed to be playing in the mud.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-10-2014, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-10T08:18:37-07:00","id":254124,"title":"","content":"Nate's victory got shot down when the gigantic stone hand rose up, and his jaw dropped. He did <i> not</i> expect that. First a godlike being, then some psychos sirens, and now, a fucking hill?! Was everything trying to kill him?! He just wanted one moment of rest, that's all! &quot;Sorry!&quot; He bleated in panic. &quot;I didn't know they were yours!&quot; The hand almost caught him, but he jumped again to evade it. He didn't react quick enough though, as even if the hand didn't manage to grab him, it still threw him off balance, knocking him over the rock. He landed down with a thud on another stone a few feet downwards. He let out a plaintive bleat, and tried to get up, but he was too dizzy, and he couldn't escape the vindictive hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T19:23:22-07:00","id":254942,"title":"","content":"On several levels, Max knew what he was doing was dumb as hell. He was regretting it more and more with each and every hoofstep. Sure, he was exhausted, hungry, and intensely frustrated at how poorly things had gone, but unloading on Nate wasn't a fair or helpful way to deal with that. Even if the Pig had gotten (or imagined) a needlessly holier-than-thou hint from the Ram's tone. That had <i>really</i> rubbed him the wrong way. Only made worse by how the wooly one wasn't entirely without a point. Some time alone would do Max some good, granted, but there was such a thing as doing so in a controlled environment. Wandering around alone somewhere as dangerous as Arcadia was certainly not one of those. Wandering around was itself another stupid decision: the kid was exhausted, and there was little more he wanted than to lie down somewhere comfortable and sleep.<br /> <br /> Lo and behold, then, as a great big pit full of mud appeared before him. With a helpful sign to drive home just how much of a good time there was to be had. Max just stared at it for a good while. &quot;... You have got to be joking...&quot; Max sounded on the cusp of defeat. He couldn't help it. He knew he didn't really want to get in it. He told himself as much, anyway. But it was hard to argue with how the mud just looked like the most comfortable, soothing, satisfying, wonderful place he could possibly be right now, and he'd had such an awful time of it lately, and didn't he deserve a little something pleasant, and he didn't need to be in long or much, even dangling his tired legs in it would be great and he could stop whenever he wanted and even if he couldn't would it really be so awful to get in that muck and never ever want to come out and why would he want to leave really what was--<br /> <br /> Max tried to get ahold of himself. Clamping his eyes shut and turning his back to the mud pit, he took a deep breath through his snout. Even without the loud drawn out snort he didn't enjoy, he regretted it immediately. <i>'Aw, man, it even <b>smells</b> amazing...'</i> Looking even more ridiculous than he usually did, he tried clamping a hand over his snout, and took another deep breath through his mouth. The breathing exercise didn't work nearly so well without breathing through his nose, but it probably beat the alternative. &quot;N-Not interested...&quot; Never mind his quavering tone, his snout's audible snuffling betrayed that for a lie.<br /> <br /> Of course, if Max was truly interested in not giving into temptation, he probably would have been better served hauling his curly tail away from there post-haste. But no. Just stood there about 5-10 feet from the mud with his eyes closed. Still, even if slow on the uptake from fatigue, Max seemed to get that not watching a land that can rearrange itself was the cherry on top of his sundae of stupid. After a moment's worry, he opened his eyes to the path he had taken to get there. With his luck, he'd probably see an even bigger, more appealing mud pit. With an even happier-looking pig on a neighboring sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T20:03:56-07:00","id":254978,"title":"","content":"The hand just barely missed the goat, as the fingers wrapped around the stone he had been resting on. The hand gave a tug as if pulling it's owner up, and soon a head emerged over the side of the hill, along with enormous shoulders nearly twice as wide as Nate was tall! The creature was enormous, yet vaguely human in its appearance, and as it placed a second hand on the ledge, it became clear that the rest of its body would soon follow.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Those flowers were exotic Goblin Fruits!&quot; the giant boomed, &quot;They're extremely hard to cultivate!&quot; apparently the creature wasn't interested in Nate's excuses, it just wanted to punish him for the theft.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> As Max began showing disinterest in the mud puddle, it was almost like the mud sensed his intentions. A churning gurgle could be heard as bubbles popped along the mud's surface. It was almost as if the mud were trying to call out to him, which knowing this place, it probably was! From behind him, a cold, filthy hand clamped gently upon his shoulder.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Come play with me.&quot; said a voice, barely above a whisper, yet right in his floppy ear. But almost immediately afterward, the hand and the voice vanished, leaving nothing but a muddy hand print on the pig's skin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T21:04:32-07:00","id":255028,"title":"","content":"Max's ear flopped a bit at the sound of the burbling and... giggling? <i>'... I really need a rest...'</i> Not because he'd written it off as all in his head -- though that concern did still exist. He just... wanted to be much better rested if he was going to have to deal with stuff like this. And he was quite right to feel that way. Given the actual physical contact. And whispered temptation. The little pig gave a terrified squeal as he ran a few steps off, and whirled around to see... just the mud pit. <i>'... <b>Really</b> need a rest...'</i><br /> <br /> He panted, each breath drawing in more of the disgusting, foul, cool, tantalizing stench of the mire. Max was starting to feel kind of hot, now that he thought about it, the way one often does when upset. He brought a hand to his forehead to wipe away the sweat... and found only his dry, bristly flesh. He put two and two together. <i>'Oh... No wonder I feel hot so often...'</i> And he did. Also very tense, all over his body. With one, solitary, hand-shaped exception. It felt <i>very</i> good where the mud had touched. It had felt good where the nymphs had caressed him, too, but this was that and more. The pig then noticed his head was at an angle, as he'd absently rubbed the side of his head and face into the bit of mud, giving a grunt of satisfaction. He was revolted at what he was doing, yes, but... damn, it felt fantastic. He was at a loss for a time when he'd felt better. <i>'And that was just a touch...' </i>His curly tail swished away behind him, his eyes full of longing, want, and need.<br /> <br /> Not that Max went charging in then and there. Make no mistake, the parts of his brain worried about pride and human dignity -- at least for the moment -- were drowning under the refrain of <i>how amazing</i> <i>it was going to feel</i>. But a certain amount of self-preservation was just managing to keep its head above the rising tide. Someone had touched and spoken to him. Someone was there. And likely someone interested enough in his going for a mud bath to make a sign about it. &quot;Is... Is s-someone there...?&quot; Not that the answer was likely to matter. Unless it revealed itself to be very obviously dangerous and very, very quickly at that, what sense the Pig had left was not going to hold him back much longer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T04:31:49-07:00","id":255188,"title":"","content":"Nate panicked at the sight of the mountain man, and he crawled to the edge on the rock he was on. Nope, couldn't jump from there, or else he would surely break his neck. He could try to climb down, but he doubted that he would have the time to do that. He'd have to get past the monster and go back the way he came up, he knew he could jump down safely there. His eyes darted around, looking for a cover, but no avail : there was only stones of different sizes. Against a normal opponent, this could work, but against something that is <i>made</i> of those same stones? It would be useless.<br /> Still, the hill had answered his apology, which means that it could be talked to. He had to try it this way. He briefly wondered what were those Goblin Fruits. The last time he heard about those, they were mushrooms. Back then, he didn't notice, but it seemed that the term Fruit wasn't really correct. However, those shrooms caused him to attack Max under an hallucination. Could this mean that this stoneman would be a fragment of his imagination? <i>Do you really want to take this risk?</i> Yeah, no. If he was mistaken, he could be squashed, flattened to death, or just thrown down from a great height. On the other hand, if he was right, he would just look like a fool, alone on a hill.<br /> He also remembered that the cages had been made with people, which meant that this hill could effectively be one too. A former human, transformed into landscape...And the Pig thought he had it bad. However, that gave him an idea. He raised his hands in a gesture of peace : &quot;Listen up, you mighty mountain. I'm the Ram, and I'm part of the newest collection of our master the Keeper.&quot; If he had stopped to listen to himself, he would have thrown up in disgust. But...acknowledging the omnipotent being as his master felt horribly <i>right</i>. &quot;Which means that I'm new here, but especially that right now, I'm one of his favorites. He has gone to great length to have me in Arcadia, you know. Do you really want to displease him by killing me? I'm sure he could easily crush this hill of yours with just a thought. So...let's be civil, alright? I'm sorry for those Goblin Fruits, but you should have put a warning on it, or something. Now please let me go, and I promise I won't eat anything on the way down. Or better, that I won't ever come back. Deal?&quot; While speaking, he was slowly circling the mighty being, hoping to keep him so busy with his speech that he wouldn't notice the Goat getting closer to his escape route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":".  Minor mistakes 09-12-2014, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T21:12:00-07:00","id":255805,"title":"","content":"After watching the cow women and minotaur for a bit, Jessica decided that she should head back for the ranch. She had no more desire to add to her guilt than she did to become part of a harem. To add to that, she was still sore from her vigorous encounter with Leo. It would be best to catch up with Max or Nate.<br /> <br /> As she crept away, the minotaur noticed her. &quot;Get in the water with the other cows!&quot; he bellowed. &quot;Now!&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica thought of running, but turned around instead. &quot;I am no cow,&quot; she retorted. &quot;I am an ox. Now leave me alone!&quot;<br /> <br /> The minotaur gave no answer, but simply charged after Jessica. Again, she thought of running, but held her ground. As the creature neared her, she launched herself at him. The two tumbled to the ground, wrestling from dominance. She matched up with the minotaur's amazing strength poorly, but she sought as best as she could to give a good account of herself. After perhaps a minute of struggle, she felt herself weakening.<br /> <br /> Fear of what the price of losing might be inspired Jessica to make a move that one would never expect from an ox. As the bull man tried to hold her down, she bite as hard as she could into his exposed neck. While her ox woman teeth were not ideal for biting flesh, she used every bit of strength that she could bring to the grisly task. She savagely shook her head as she bit, trying to rip the bull monster's tough throat open. Jessica tasted blood, but her foe seemed no weaker for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typoes 09-14-2014, 12:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T09:39:12-07:00","id":258238,"title":"","content":"&quot;Then you can explain to the Keeper, why you stole from me!&quot; the hulking giant shouted, once more swiping towards the goat, intending to snatch him into the air. To think anybody would get this pissed off over simple flowers was hard to imagine. But then again, not many things made sense in this realm. Maybe breaking the rules was taken more seriously here?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Max was answered with more bubbling from the mud pit, and finally it began to shift and churn. Once more the voice whispered out, inviting him to jump in. Even as the mud began to rise into the air as a sludgy mess. Arms began to form out the sides, and eye sockets began to form. Beneath them, a massive hole opened in the tower of mud, like a toothless maw. A maw which looked big enough to swallow the pig whole if he tried climbing inside.<br /> <br /> &quot;Come play with me.&quot; it invited, &quot;I&quot;m so hungry!&quot; and then it lunged forward, dragging itself with the newly formed arms.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Clearly surprised from the bite, the minotaur backed off for a bit. She hadn't drawn any serious amount of blood, so it couldn't have been the attack itself that drove him back. Rather it was the shock of having a bovine attack with its teeth, something that clearly went against its nature.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Oath breaker...&quot; the Minotaur grunted, before his eyes zeroed in on her with rage. &quot;OATH BREAKER!&quot; he roared at the top of his lungs. The cows began to join in, chanting the phrase over and over, pointing at Jessica as they did so.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Oath breaker! Oath breaker! Oath breaker!&quot; their voices rising in volume as they closed in around her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T17:27:39-07:00","id":258584,"title":"","content":"&quot;But I didn't --&quot; Nate was cut short by the giant lunging at him. He ran, or rather bolted toward the edge of the hill, ready to jump off, trusting his new legs. He had to admit it, he was faster now, and with those hooves, he didn't feel any pain from running naked on stones. He dodged the big hand quite easily, thanks to the Ram's agility. It was as if his mind had stepped back a little bit, letting the bestial part of it in command. <i>Get us out of there, hurry! </i>He could hear the giant roaring, and the stone rumbling all round. He assumed that it was simply in anger, and it was slightly proud to have annoyed such a big creature, like a mosquito tormenting a human. However, he had been overconfident, once again, because something hard and cold suddenly grabbed his left leg, tripping him against the hard floor with a surprised and desperate bleat. Turning his head, Nate saw the giant's hand clenching his leg, while the monster itself was still at the center of the hill, but his arms seemed to have sank back in the ground. The Ram was kicking the stone in panic, and the hand started to slowly drag him back to his tormentor. Soon, annoyed with the beast's struggle, the other hand came out to hold the other leg.<br /> Nate was frantically searching around him for a solution. His first instinct was to butt heads with the mighty being, but it was quickly deemed stupid by all the voices in his mind. He looked around, and grabbed a nearby stone, throwing it at the mountain's eyes. of course, it didn't work. The stone simply got...absorbed by it. Raising his arms in a defensive gesture, the man cursed himself for what he was going to do, but it was his only option.<br /> &quot;Keeper!&quot; he shouted as loudly as he could. &quot;Please, Master! Someone's trying to kill me! Help me, I beg you!&quot; He hated himself. The pleading, the bleats. He was pathetic. He hoped his plan would work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 09-17-2014, 08:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T20:49:05-07:00","id":258635,"title":"","content":"As the cow women started to close in around her, Jessica tried again to flee. Her effort proved futile. One of the cow women shoved Jessica back into the minotaur. As the bovine women continued to chant oath breaker, the enraged monster seized her. She struggled as hard as she could to escape his grasp, but the minotaur easily lifted her over his head. &quot;Let me show you what happens to oath breakers!&quot; he bellowed. <br /> <br /> With that, the minotaur slammed Jessica hard into the earth. All the air was forced from her body, and she could not move before the minotaur straddled her. &quot;You should have just went in the water like I told you,&quot; he said. &quot;We might have both had a little fun, cow. Now all the pleasure will be all mine.&quot;<br /> <br /> As the cow women continued their chanting, Jessica struggled and cursed, but she could not move the minotaur atop her. Before the minotaur could do any more to her, the chanting stopped. Something was happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  fixing word flow 09-16-2014, 11:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T22:16:27-07:00","id":258722,"title":"","content":"Well. <i>That</i> certainly met the &quot;very obviously dangerous and very, very quickly&quot; criteria. Max's wagging tail slowed its tempo to a dead stop as the color drained from his mud-smeared face. Understandably, he was too stunned to do much more than gawk, even as his fear built to a fever pitch. It was like a bucket of ice water, returning his rational mind to the fore. A mind that was horrified at how badly that had almost gone... and even more horrified at how a part of him still wanted to wallow in the mud badly enough to brave the danger. The prey animal in him had joined the &quot;Get the hell away from the mud&quot; lobby, but it worried him that, if that wasn't the case, the hedonist's calls of &quot;How bad could it be?&quot; might just get him to commit that bizarre and pathetic form of suicide, after all.<br /> <br /> Of course, it was hard for the fear of being eaten <i>not</i> to win out, especially when the awful thing lunged at Max. The pig started squealing in even more terror than before, throwing himself away from the mud pit and turning to run. In his haste, he turned at an odd angle and lost his balance, ending up on all-fours. It dazed him a moment, but the adrenaline was still flowing and his bestial side seemed to prefer the new posture, starting to charge off. The Pig being nearer the forefront worked against him, though; the mud creature managed to brush a naked leg and oh... It felt as wonderful as he'd hoped and feared. The tingle of relief and pleasure made him pause for a moment, even halting the non-stop squealing. During which the monstrosity managed to move in for a tighter grip. That resumed the frantic struggle to get away from the avatar of death on the mire, but things did not look good. Desperate, Max squealed out to it: &quot;Please! <i>Please!</i> <i>Don't eat me!</i>&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T03:23:51-07:00","id":258895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/205196-ic-zodiac-beasts?p=258635#post258635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the cow women continued their chanting, Jessica struggled and cursed, but she could not move the minotaur atop her. Before the minotaur could do any more to her, the chanting stopped. Something was happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>As suddenly as the chanting surrounding Jessica stoped, so did the momentary silence broke by a loud bellow of pain and rage coming from the minotaur. The harem cows gasped in horror at the sight of their stud with the best part of a foot of sharpened wood going through one of his bobine eyes.<br /> Taking advantage of the commotion, Derek quickly pulled his improvised spear out of the minotaur's socket in one strong movement accompanied by a disgusting and liquid sound of suction. &quot;<i>C'mon, we don't have much time!</i>&quot; he shouted to the still dissoriented cow (or was her an ox?) while he tended her the large leathery palm of one of his long fingered hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 09-17-2014, 06:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T05:22:13-07:00","id":258932,"title":"","content":"Jessica took the offered hand and ran off with the monkey man. In short order, they were in relative safety among the trees. As she followed her rescuer deeper into the forest, terror at the vile fate she had nearly suffered almost made her physically ill. &quot;Thank you so much,&quot; gushed Jessica. &quot;I owe you so much! I'll never be able to repay you. I don't even know your name!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T08:08:05-07:00","id":258982,"title":"","content":"&quot;<i>Oh, don't worry, everybody would have done the same</i>&quot;. The monkey left the distressed ox woman plenty of room to recatch her breath and calm down. &quot;<i>My name is Derek... just Derek now, I've recently trade my last name for... something</i>&quot;. The monkey looked both embarrased and worried. He looked around, incapable of meeting the ox eyes for a while. He took a look at the uneven sharpened head of his spear still wet with the minotaur's blood and vitreous humor, and droped it in disgust.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>I've ne-never had to do so-something like this be-before</i>&quot;-He sttutered-&quot;<i>I mean, back in college I organized some patrol groups to prevent asaults in campus</i>&quot;-he explained, regaining his composure-&quot;<i>Some of those entitled jerk jocks could get violent from time to time when they get a no from a girl they put their eyes on... and being drunk as hell didn't help either</i>&quot;-he took another look at the spear lying in the ground and shivered-&quot;<i>Nothing as <b>intense</b> as this, though</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Some awkward silence fell over the two beasts until the monkey spoke again, matter of fact.&quot;<i>Weren't you with some other, err... people later? Where are they now</i>?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 09-17-2014, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T09:05:59-07:00","id":259005,"title":"","content":"&quot;I was with Max and Nate - the pig and the ram - earlier,&quot; Jessica replied. &quot;We sort of had a group fight and each of us went off on our own. Most likely, a bad move. I hope that they're both all right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica fell silent. She shuddered again, thinking of what the minotaur would have done to her if Derek had not rescued her. She could only hope that Max and Nate had fared better. After a couple of seconds, she turned her attention back to Derek. &quot;I think I've seen you before, both in the cages and when we first got to the ranch. I have so many questions. Have you gotten to know any of the others? Where did you go to college?&quot;<br /> <br /> As she asked her first two questions, Jessica remembered with a start that she had lost her clothing. Despite remembering this, she realized that she felt comfortable around Derek. Maybe it was the fact that he had actually organized patrol groups during college to prevent women from being assaulted, or perhaps it was because he had saved her. She hoped it was one of these two reasons. Sadly, she knew that it might well also be a result of her having become even more like an animal and less like a person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T15:05:55-07:00","id":259274,"title":"","content":"What answered Nate's call was nothing short of deafening. A monstrously deep voice roared out from the sky, it's tone saturated in anger.<br /> <br /> &quot;FOUND YOU!&quot; and a second later, something dropped from the sky with enough force to shatter the stone giant into thousands of pebbles. In its place stood the keeper, hands clenched into fists, and flames radiating from his eye sockets. The image of the old, asian store owner had almost completely vanished, replaced by some manner of demon. Long, sharp teeth lined his mouth, and the skin on his face was stretched and creases into a snarl.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;YOU RAN AWAY, AGAIN!!!&quot; the voice boomed, the Keeper not even moving its mouth as he spoke, but the words being projected directly into the goat's mind.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> The sign that had originally been depicting the happy pig had changed, or perhaps Max had misinterpreted its original meaning and it was becoming clearer now. The pig wasn't throwing its arms up and cheering, it was flailing its arms and screaming. Something was dragging it beneath the mud, and it had been struggling to get back to safety before it drowned!<br /> <br /> With each &quot;step&quot; the mud monster made, parts of its body would splash to the ground, leaving tiny mud puddles in its wake.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Get in my belly!&quot; The creature shouted once it had trapped him, pulling one of his legs into its mouth and licking it with a huge tongue formed out of soaked leaves and tree bark. But before it bit down upon him, an object flew towards it and struck the muddy creature in between the eyes. This made the mud monster dissolve enough to free him as it cried out and began receding back to its pit. It was spewing curses even in its liquid state as it moved like water to a drain.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Unbelievable, do we have to do everything for you people?&quot; said an unfamiliar voice, before the sound of clopping hoof prints reached Max's ears. A few moments later, a proud looking centaur came into view, a bow slung over its shoulder. &quot;My name's Sagittarius, and I just saved your bacon.&quot; he introduced himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T16:13:12-07:00","id":259327,"title":"","content":"Well. It certainly did <i>not</i> went as planned. The Keeper's voice was searing the words into his mind, and Nate writhed on the ground, curling into a fetal position, clenching his horns as if their weight was somehow reassuring to him. Between screams of pain and plaintive bleats, the man managed to form some words, crying out. &quot;I'm so sorry M-Master! I wanted to go back t-to the ranch, I swear, but I got lost! I got up on this mountain to get a baaa...&quot; He gulped, and forced himself to breathe deeply. He was going to die. No, worse. He knew that the Keeper had a myriad of crueler ways to punish him.<br /> &quot;I, I got up here to get a view of the realm so I could get back to the ranch but I got attacked...I...thought I'd listen to the Ram in me! I thought that was what you wanted, for me to become a...a Beast! Master, I never wanted to displease you, I'm begging you, please forgive me!&quot; He didn't dare looking up at the demon in front of him. Technically, he wasn't lying, but what could he do but plead? There was no other options.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 09-17-2014, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T22:10:29-07:00","id":259520,"title":"","content":"Max had tried making a go for that sign, whether for leverage to pull himself free or -- if poorly secured -- a weapon. The thing caught up with him too quickly. It wrapped what could charitably be called its mouth around him. The little pig just stared at its maw. <i>'This is it,'</i> he thought bleakly. This was how his story was going to end. Eaten by a monster made of mud. And, as a last kick to his human pride, he was going to die squealing.<br /> <br /> But then he didn't. An arrow caught it dead in the &quot;face&quot; and Max's struggles managed to get him somewhere. And that somewhere, as Sagittarius clip-clopped into view, was breaking free and bolting on four legs toward the centaur. And then hiding behind him, of course, looking around the equine legs at the flailing mud-beast. The disparaging quips weren't welcome -- Max took particular issue with the word choice on that last one -- but he was certainly not looking <i>this</i> gift horse in the mouth. He just panted back there, heart still racing, but managed to grunt out a, &quot;Tha... Thank... Thank you... So... So much...&quot; Even with his staggered breaths and bestial voice, the pig's gratitude was obvious.<br /> <br /> And Max hadn't looked like much more of a pig than he did at that moment. On all-fours, naked, trouble speaking, coated from the chest down in mud -- and with heavy splotches above that, even... But at least he was alive to feel the humiliation and shame of it. After all, someone had come along to save him. <i>'Again...'</i> he thought, just a mite bitter. He wondered if he'd ever get a chance to save anyone, or even save himself. It had bothered him a while, how far off this was from expectations he hadn't realized he'd had. Max read a lot of fantasy. Someone from &quot;the real world&quot; winding up in a fantasy land and becoming a hero was a cliche. But that cliche had featured in some daydreams. They were about as far from his present state as one could get.<br /> <br /> To underscore this, with the immediate danger over, part of him <i>really</i> wanted to roll that mud over the rest of him while it was still nice and gooey. Max fought back the urge. If all he was good for was getting saved, he could at least make his savior feel he had saved a remotely respectable person, not a filthy animal. He tried to calm himself down as he brought himself back up to two legs. He also tried not to think about how nice and <i>natural</i> four legs had started to feel, there. He tried for conversation to take his mind off that. &quot;So... Just, uh... Just in the neighborhood or... were you... keeping an eye on me?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T01:51:41-07:00","id":261158,"title":"","content":"&quot;Leo said you turned down the Contract of Fang and Talon. So he thought you might need a different approach.&quot; the incarnation of Sagittarius answered, resting his hands on his hips. &quot;And considering what I just saw, I think he's right. You're going to die here over and over again without some kind of contract to keep you safe.&quot; he turned around, getting a better look at this pig who had nearly been swallowed whole by the mud.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;So... I'm going to teach you the Contract of the Wild.&quot; the centaur declared, &quot;It won't make you a deadly predator, but it will make your journey through the forest easier.&quot; he smiled as he beckoned him to follow before clip clopping away from the mud pit.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;SILENCE!&quot; the keeper roared, flames exploding around him as he did so, before they receded into an aura concentrated around his body. &quot;If you were a good beast, you wouldn't have left in the first place!&quot; the fiery aura that surrounded the Asian demon was unnatural. It did not give off the sensation that earthly fire would have, but rather felt like it was the concentrated essence of the Keeper's rage given form.<br /> <br /> &quot;IF YOU WANT MY FORGIVENESS, SLAVE...&quot; the Keeper's voice bellowed, &quot;You're going to have to EARN IT!!&quot; he reached a hand forward and grabbed the ram by one of his horns. &quot;We're making a CONTRACT!&quot; he commanded, before rocketing off into the sky with Nate in tow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T03:42:06-07:00","id":261181,"title":"","content":"&quot;<i>I worked there, I am... was a proffesor at the university</i>&quot;. He corrected mid-sentence. Derek was clearly very uncomfortable about her companion's nudity, and even more about the aparent non issue it was for her. He recovered the spear he had previously droped and offered it to Jessica without looking at her. &quot;<i>There, you keep that one. We will need protection here and if they see you porting a weapon that already spilt blood, the potential threats may think twice before confronting you</i>&quot;. It was almost true, though part of Derek couldn't stand the sight of the dark stains on the sharp pole.<br /> <br /> The monkey wandered around looking for a tree, he had something in mind. He continue talking to Jessica to ease the awkwardness of the situation. &quot;<i>I did hang around with the Snake in a tree for a while after we were brought to the ranch, but that woman seriously freaked me out. She seemed way too used to her situation for my comfort. Maybe she was sort of a viper even before getting that figurine, who knows...</i>&quot; Finally he found what he was looking for, a big tree with strong branches and big leaves.<br /> <br /> Derek grabbed one of the branches and it simply detached from the tree as on its own. He closed his hand around it and made a pass all along its length. All the leaves and sprouts just fell, leaving the surface mostly smooth. The stick even seemed to straighten, now looking more like a staff than a recently cut branch. He them proceed to sharpen one of its extremes by hand alone, sawdust falling with each pasing of his hand until he ended up with a spear not much different from which he had offered Jessica not a moment ago. &quot;<i>Well, one thing left to do now</i>&quot;. Derek then took a bunch of leaves and started to tear them in fine regular strips. He was at it for quite a while, utterly concentrated on the work at hand. When he was satisfied with the amount of material he collected he sat on the ground in front of the strip pile and started weaving them with all of his four hands. It was not long before he had another tunic similar to the one he was wearing.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>For you</i>&quot;. He said, handing the clothes to the ox woman. &quot;<i>Clothes is part of what makes us human</i>&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T04:48:41-07:00","id":261208,"title":"","content":"After thanking Derek, Jessica put on her new clothes. To her surprise, they fit perfectly and felt far more comfortable than she had expected. She then examined the spear. While she had grown used to her nudity, she felt much better dressed. She said, &quot;I think you're right about clothes being part of what makes us human. I can't think you enough.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica wanted to ask Derek just how well he had gotten to know the Snake. However, it did not seem like the time to ask. Instead, she said, &quot;I see us having two basic options. We could set up camp here, or try to return to the ranch. If it's all the same to you, I myself would like to go back to the ranch, if only to see that Max and Nate made it.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T04:50:47-07:00","id":261210,"title":"","content":"Nate tried to crawl back futilely, shielding his face from the flames. Why was this happening?! He had just done what he had always done, trying to sweet-talk his way out of conflicts, and it had always worked for him until now. So why wasn't it working? He had begged, he was crying, he had said what the Keeper wanted to hear...Wasn't it enough?! He didn't leave on his own, he had only followed the others! <i>It is so unfair!</i> That was their fault he was here! <i>I am a good beast!</i> Why was he the one who was punished?! He hadn't been the one trying to escape! He wanted to take the long road and to wait for an window of opportunity, but everything and everyone had been after him. He should never have let the others trick him into leaving the ranch.<br /> <br /> The Ram tried to protest when the Keeper grabbed one of his horns, but he was cut short by the pain he felt when he pulled him into the sky, only holding him by a side of his head. It felt as if the horn was going to be ripped out of his skull. Of course, he would probably plummet to the ground after that, but it sounded way better than what the Master had in store for him. The only way for him to alleviate the pain would be to hang onto one of the Keeper's finger to spread his weight, but he feared what would happen if he only dared touching him. However, curiosity got the better of Nate. &quot;Wh...What k-kind of contract, M-Master?&quot; he shouted, hoping to be heard while flying at high-speed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T11:53:17-07:00","id":261387,"title":"","content":"Max sighed. &quot;Yeah... I agree with that much. I need <i>something</i>. I feel like I barely get a chance to catch my breath before something else horrible happens.&quot; He shook his head and started to follow along, his movements dropping thick dollops of mud off him as he went. He fought down the desire to rub them back on and tried to tell the part of him that mourned their loss to shut up (with mixed results).<br /> <br /> &quot;Thanks for the help, again. Uh, on shooting that thing <i>and</i> on the Contract. I don't know that... Fang &amp; Talon would have done much for me. Especially with the price. But the Contract of the Wild does sound better. Better than the Contract of the Domesticated, right?&quot; Max gave a small smile, figuring the self-deprecating joke might help the mood. &quot;But what's it like, though? What sort of things can it do? ... And what's it going to ask?&quot; The Pig hoped his tone made clear he didn't intend to wriggle out of making it: knowing its demands would help him brace himself. Even if the terms were worrying, he didn't suspect another member of the Western Zodiac was going to come along with another chance. Actually, with that thought, a question had been bugging him.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, uh. I was wondering. You said you're 'Sagittarius.' You and Leo and Gemini... You all just call yourselves by your signs.&quot; Max paused, concerned this might be treading into too personal territory. &quot;Umm, don't feel like you have to answer, but... Why? You were taken just like the Eastern Zodiac. Why don't you use your real names anymore?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T14:05:26-07:00","id":261466,"title":"","content":"&quot;As I said,&quot; the Centaur began, &quot;It will allow you to travel unhindered by the wilderness, but in exchange, you must respect the wilds.&quot; he stopped when he felt they were far enough away from the other creature, and turned to Max once again. &quot;Respect the ground, the trees, the plants, the air. Treat the wilderness like a sentient being that has thoughts and feelings, and it shall offer you safe passage.&quot; he went on before smiling. &quot;Over time you learn new tricks, and the wilderness will begin to hinder those who hunt you. Sounds like a pretty sweet deal, does it not?&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As Max asked his next series of questions, the centaur folded his arms and looked at him sternly before responding.<br /> <br /> &quot;This place... messes with your head. I'm sure you've already noticed.&quot; he answered, &quot;We've been here too long... we don't remember our names. I don't even know how many years I've been here, the days and nights come and go at complete random.&quot; he uncrossed his arms and relaxed, &quot;We're doing this to stay as the Keeper's favorites, so that we have at least some measure of comfort in this mad house.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> The speed at which the Keeper traveled was beyond mortal comprehension, and probably broke several laws of physics in the human world. In less than half the blink of an eye, they landed back at the ranch, as was made evident by the rest of the Chinese Zodiac being present. The demon grabbed Nate's horns with both hands and they shattered into tiny fragments, leaving him with two broken stumps that would shame a proper Ram.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Your horns shall return to you when the rest of my collection does the same!&quot; The demon commanded, releasing Nate from his grasp finally. &quot;Now these are the terms of the contract...&quot; his form began to change once again, returning to the innocent looking shop keeper he had been previously.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;You will take responsibility for your betrayal. You will hunt down and capture the rest of my collection who have left without my permission. You will bring them before me or my agents. If you refuse to follow my orders for any reason, you will spend another hour in the Slaughter House for every order you reject.&quot; he leered at the goat, &quot;If you break this oath... if you attempt to betray me and escape once more, I will cast you into the Slaughter House for 100 years!&quot; he threatened. &quot;Now, let us shake on the contract!&quot; and with that, he extended his hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T15:25:26-07:00","id":261538,"title":"","content":"The Ram...no, Nate cried out at the loss of his horns. All the voices inside his mind howled in pain, as if a piece of his soul had been ripped off. He fell on his knees, devastated. How could he compare himself to the others Beasts when...wait. Why should he have to compare himself to beasts? Why...did it seem so important to him?<br /> He listened to the Keeper's offer without moving an inch, paralyzed as he was by the horn loss. And then, he began to laugh nervously. Softly, but he couldn't contain himself. He was going to suffer, oh yes. &quot;Keeper&quot; he said in a distant voice devoid of the terror that previously plagued him. &quot;I'm no predator. I'm the Ram. It's not in my nature to bring the lost lambs to the ranch, it should be the Dog's task! &quot;He laughed incredulously. &quot;I can't do what you ask of me in my current state. This is how you made me, mind and body.&quot; <i>This is going to hurt like hell.</i> He knew that, of course. But at this point, what could he do but go on? Strangely, he didn't care anymore about his fate. He had given up the tricks, the flattering, and even his pride.&quot;I don't want to escape, Master. I don't want to go back to my world with a body like mine. &quot; He swallowed. &quot;I could serve you in different ways. I know music. I wanted to make you a surprise present by creating an instrument so that I could show you my talent. Let me do this instead, Keeper. &quot;<br /> <br /> And with that, he raised his head, eyes looking at the Fae. There wasn't any defiance, hate or fear. Just plain... Resignation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 09-21-2014, 07:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T19:43:07-07:00","id":261676,"title":"","content":"Max listened carefully to the words of Sagittarius, and then returned the smile with a nod. &quot;It does. I really like the sound of that.&quot; The very thought made him a bit more hopeful. This wasn't the flashiest, most ground-breaking magic, maybe. It wouldn't give him much of a sword. But it was a shield, and it sounded like quite the shield at that.<br /> <br /> Though the centaur's other answers brought down the pig's mood. &quot;Oh. ... I'm... I'm sorry.&quot; Face full of sympathy, Max looked up at the half-horse man and nodded at the last bit. &quot;I can't fault you, there. Thank you for just taking the risk to help. I hope that it <i>does</i> make things easier for you all, here.&quot; A thought struck him after a moment. &quot;Just... Just in case I do make it out in the end... I mean, maybe you can't think of anything, but... If I get out, if there's something you want me to do, a message you want to give someone or... or anything else, well. Just let me know. I owe you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max took a deep breath. &quot;And I guess... No time like the present for the Contract, right? That should make me less of a burden.&quot; He tried to stand ready, with as much dignity as a pig with a body at least three-fourths covered in drying mud (with a fair bit all over his snout). <i>'... I could have used a bath before, but maaaaan...'</i> He gave Sagittarius a nod. &quot;I'm ready.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T08:48:48-07:00","id":263811,"title":"","content":"The Keeper glared at the goat who had not immediately complied with his terms, before responding to him.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;You are not here to play, you are here to be displayed.&quot; he told him. &quot;I will give you your chance, but if your music is not to my liking, you will be sheared in front of everyone here!&quot; he went on, a pair of farming shears materializing in his hand. &quot;Proceed, slave.&quot; he ordered<br /> <br /> <br /> The rest of the Zodiac seemed to take notice and gathered around to watch the show, or at least the goat attempt to perform one.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Don't worry&quot; Sagittarius told Max, &quot;Forming a contract is very easy. You just need a witness who can confirm both parties agreed to the terms and conditions.&quot; and with that, he spread his arms out slowly and looked up to the trees that surrounded them.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I stand witness to one who wishes to sign the Contract of the Wild!&quot; he called out, and with that, a strong gust of wind blew through the forest, causing the trees to sway and the bushes to rustle. &quot;Do you agree to honor and respect the wilds in exchange for the protection it offers?&quot; another gust of wind and again the trees swayed, although this time in a different direction.<br /> <br /> The grass around Max's hooves began to grow unnaturally, wrapping around his body. But it was not a tight or aggressive hold. Rather it felt more like the plants were embracing him, offering their comfort if he agreed to the terms. They gently spread across more of his body, entwining around his legs, chest, arms, but not his face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T09:21:18-07:00","id":263842,"title":"","content":"It worked. It actually worked! He had managed to delay a punishment! Nate seemed to regain some life with this small victory, but then, he remembered that he didn't have the chance to craft himself a guitar. He could do some backup voices, but...he did not trust his voice, he feared that he would suddenly bleat in the middle of a verse. Looking around to the other Zodiac, he was slightly pissed at their passivity, but also somewhat flattered to have an audience of more than one person.<br /> Gulping, he spoke to the Keeper once again. &quot;I am truly grateful for your mercy Master, but actually...my surprise was not quite ready. I'm primarly a guitarist, and I was hoping to craft an instrument once I would be back here. I...could proceed with only my voice if you desire so, but it would not do my songs justice.&quot; He gritted his teeth, hoping that he wasn't pushing his luck too far. He didn't even notice how easy it was now to call the being Master.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 09-23-2014, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T22:26:58-07:00","id":264393,"title":"","content":"Still a bit jumpy, Max's shoulders jerked as the grass started up him. He relaxed quick enough; it felt... nice. Peaceful. He took a deep breath, grunting out a contented sigh. He'd smelled the grass, trees, and other greenery about, but they all seemed fresher to him now, more lively, and more friendly. It all had an interesting contrast with the mud that still clung to him. That still felt nice, of course, but the grass and the air were different. More genuine, that feeling, with a firm undercurrent of affection. He chuckled; the grass tickled a bit as it climbed. The muck suddenly didn't seem as appealing as it had -- though the pig would probably still have to hold himself back at the next chance. He just felt more refreshed than he had in what felt like ages.<br /> <br /> Max was certainly tired, but wasn't nodding off. There was still some trepidation, but it was overpowered: he was focused, committed, and even a little excited about this. <i>'This is where it all turns around. Things'll get better. I can feel it.'</i> Body embraced by the grass about him, no doubt seemed to shadow him as he answered. &quot;I swear. I will give the wilds all respect and dignity that is their due.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T10:42:44-07:00","id":266853,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'm losing my patience...&quot; the Keeper answered in a low voice as Nate once again came up with an excuse. He flicked his wrist and seemingly out of thin air, an object smacked the goat in the head before landing on the ground in front of him. It was... a pan flute of all things!<br /> <br /> The keeper squeezed the shears twice, eliciting a series of clipping noises as if reminding Nate of what would happen should he fail, and glared at him impatiently to begin.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> &quot;Then the Contract of the Wild has been signed, the centaur declared, and the grass fell away from Max's body, receding back into the ground as the realm acknowledged the pact. As long as the pig honored his end of the deal, the forest would no longer attempt to harm him. He could now protect himself without having to bloody his hands, or his spontaneous growth of tusks if they ever reappeared.<br /> <br /> &quot;Congratulations, you've just signed your first contract!&quot; Sagitarrius said, patting Max on the shoulder. He then looked around cautiously before whispering to Max, &quot;Remember the Hedge is your way to freedom. I won't lie to you that it's going to be painful, but you must have the courage to plow through when the time comes.&quot; and with that, he turned and galloped off into the forest at full speed, leaving Max to fend for himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T13:31:25-07:00","id":266968,"title":"","content":"Max nodded and smiled back up at Sagittarius. &quot;I understand. Thank you for your help. I won't forget it.&quot; His smile faded a bit as the Hedge was mentioned. Having signed a Contract only made the phrase seem more ominous, somehow. As though it gave him some small insight into the extent of his bargain, enough to know that the Wilds could only do so much to guard him from that place. Still, he gave another nod. &quot;I understand. I-I'll be ready to face that. When the time comes.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then Max was alone again. But the place certainly felt less hostile. Oh, his nose and ears still brought him smells and sounds of danger, but it made a huge difference that <i>the wilderness itself</i> was not against him, now. He'd scarcely realized how oppressive things had seemed before. Now it felt almost like he was in his own backyard. Max felt freer to focus on more important things than an ever present panic.<br /> <br /> Not the Hedge quite yet, though. As the earlier adrenaline faded, his stomach reminded him that he was famished. Yes, throwing up those mushrooms had probably been a net gain, but hadn't done his hunger any favors. Nor had the intervening time. He resented his swinish nature showing; he couldn't remember when he'd been so hungry.<br /> <br /> <i>'Ugh... I can't wait for the Ranch. I have to eat something. Soon. Well... Maybe the Contract will help. Keep me from finding trouble. Or... Or anything too disgusting...' </i>So, hoping for better fortune than last time, Max perked up his snout. He had big misgivings, but a much bigger hunger. The little pig started on a search for his next meal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor tweakery. 09-27-2014, 06:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T18:03:26-07:00","id":267092,"title":"","content":"Nate had to restraint himself from bursting in anger and throwing insults at the Keeper. That would have been an... unfortunate move to make. He gritted his teeth and rubbed his head, before taking the pan flute. <i>Oh, you must feel so clever, you crazy fucker. </i> Since his transformation, he had realized that he kinda looked like a satyr, but with this instrument, the association couldn't be clearer. Looking at the instrument, he wondered if he should be even trying, if admitting his defeat wouldn't be less humiliating. <i>Yes it would. But you're going to suffer anyway ,stupid. Try it. </i> He examined it, and blew tentatively on it. The small sound produced wasn't so encouraging. <i>Alright, it's like blowing on a beer bottle. How hard could it be?!</i> He looked around to his audience, and smiled wryly. It was stage fright all over again!<br /> He breathed deeply as he tried to remember songs that should be easy to perform. Unfortunately, his mind was blank. Did...Did he even knew songs other than his own? And his composition were mostly hard rock, nothing that could be reproduced with a simple wind instrument. And so, the Ram would have to rely on pure improvisation. <i>This is gonna be terrible.</i><br /> <br /> Closing his eyes, he began his recital. He tried to stick to a tune : better to look confident than just admitting that you don't know what you're doing. To his surprise, it sounded...coherent? It wasn't horrible to hear! He opened his eyes in shock, pausing for a second. He still had a chance! Instinctively, he decided to play something whimsical and sweet, relying on his innate musicality. The flute seemed alive in itself : as he blew his notes, the instrument made his hands move on their own, instantly matching his mouth with the right pipe for the right note. The Ram wanted to laugh incredulously, but the staring of the audience kept him from breaking his performance. The happiness of his tune was contagious : he saw two other Beasts tapping their feet (or rather, their paws and hooves) in rythm and Nate even had to restrain himself from dancing!<br /> He ended his song on a high note, and couldn't stop himself from smiling proudly. He didn't know how long he had been playing : It had felt like an hour to him, but it might have been the pressure speaking. Looking up at the Keeper, he instantly lost his smile, his eyes drawn to the shears. &quot;Was...Was it to your liking...Master?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 09-28-2014, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T09:20:10-07:00","id":267448,"title":"","content":"Derek snaped out of his own thoughts at the question from Jessica. &quot;<i>If you want to go back to the ranch to check on your friends I'll follow you</i>&quot; He didn't feel safe at all going solo in that crazy place and the expectation of meeting yet more potential allies in an escape plan was certainly enticing. He looked around, stretching as tall as he could with his upper hands firmly grabbing his spear. &quot;<i>Ok, which way?</i>&quot; he finally asked &quot;<i>I've never had a particuarly keen orientation, could you lead the way?</i>&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T07:51:03-07:00","id":268264,"title":"","content":"&quot;I think I know the way,&quot; Jessica assured Derek.<br /> <br /> With that, Jessica, followed by Derek, left the trees and started back to the ranch. For a bit, she was afraid that she had gotten lost. Based on her memories, she expected a shorter trip, yet the ranch remained stubbornly out of view. Just as Jessica considered admitting defeat to Derek, the ranch came into view. From their nearby destination, the monkey and the ox could hear the faint strains of music that matched the beauty of the ranch created by the keeper. When the two of them finally set foot in the ranch the music ended.<br /> <br /> After a moment, Jessica said, &quot;We had better see if the others made it back.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T03:52:14-07:00","id":268925,"title":"","content":"&quot;<i>Was that... a Pan's Flute?</i>&quot; Asked Derek trying to hear the tune better.<br /> &quot;<i>Curious thing about pan's flutes is that they were mostly called </i>siringues<i> back in Greece due to the legend of the homonimous naiad that was turned into a cane plant. The god Pan have fallen in love with her and used her metamorphosed body to fashion the first of these musical instruments</i>&quot; The monkey gesticulated widly while talking, like he did in class with his students. &quot;<i>Of course the asociation with Pan as one of the most known pieces of his regalia is what caused the current most common name. Another weird fact is that the name Pan is also the root of the word </i>panic<i>, wich was originally an adjective of a type of fear: </i>panic fear<i>, that is, a kind of fear provoked or related to the god Pan. As with anything it evolved and turned into a name unto itself for a kind of irrational fear. That asociation with fear was probably what caused early christians to model his devil after him and other greek gods. Most iconic representations of Satan picture him as a sort of half man-half goat like Pan, living and ruling and underworld like Hades while wielding a trident that was one of the attributes of Poseidon. The flames and fire maybe related to Haefestus. So yes, Pan... Fear. You should read The Great God Pan, terrific and terrifying piece of literature...</i>&quot; Derek slowly realised he was rambling and stoped. &quot;<i>Sorry about that, I may be more nervous than I initially thought</i>&quot;.<br /> Despite being part of the Zodiac, Derek have had no direct contact with the Keeper yet and having seen what that did to others he was quite glad. The idea of facing him now was driving him mad. &quot;<i>I tend to pour trivia like crazy when I'm nervous</i>&quot; He said as a kind of explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T08:30:29-07:00","id":269113,"title":"","content":"The keeper stared at Nate, absently clicking the shears every few moments. After a time, he began to speak.<br /> <br /> &quot;That was an unusual melody.&quot; he said, &quot;I could feel your terror and pain mixed with whimsy and joy. It reminded me of those projects humans refer to as creative art.&quot; another couple of clicks from the shears before he tossed them aside and they vanished into thin air the moment he released them from his grasp. &quot;Your creation has amused me for a time, but it was still lacking in quality. You should work on it more.&quot;<br /> <br /> With that, he patted the goat on the head before looking to the rest of his collection that had still assembled. At some point his monkey had also decided to go missing, which began to spark his anger again before he turned quickly back to the goat.<br /> <br /> &quot;Again!&quot; he commanded, &quot;I need a distraction, right now!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> True to Sagittarius' words, the forest did seem much kinder to Max than before. roots sank into the ground to prevent tripping, and shrubs swayed out of the way to give him a clear path. In fact, it almost seemed like they were opening a path for him, showing him the true way to navigate towards his destination. As if reacting to his hunger, the path would open to a small clearing, where a young apple tree grew in the center. There were no mud pits, no sexy monster, no apparent dangers of any kind. Just a tree, baring fruit for a hungry traveler.<br /> <br /> Or at least it looked like an apple tree at first glance. But these were not any apples Max had seen before. They were nearly as big as his fist, and their coloration was unnatural, a vibrant blue with dark purple speckles on one side, while being completely blue on the other. At the trunk of the tree was a sign that read in an alphabet that appeared to be a jumbled mess of squiggles, yet at the same time was perfectly legible. It was as if the sign was communicating in every language simultaneously, so that all could understand it.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;If you would partake of my fruit, I ask you spread my legacy.&quot; the sign said, &quot;resolve to plant my seeds, and you may eat your fill.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-30-2014, 12:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T10:19:35-07:00","id":269232,"title":"","content":"Nate released a sigh of relief at his Master's reluctant approval. <i>You made it. The plan worked.</i> The criticism was harsh to hear and quite chilly, but it had done the trick. &quot;T-Thank you Master. I'll work on it.&quot; He shivered when the omnipotent being patted him on his head, and cringed when he asked for an encore. Once again, he brought the flute back to his lips, and started to blow on it. The Keeper liked his emotions? Fair enough, he'd show them to him. The song was much slower this time. The Goat had decided to focus on his experience in Arcadia : the pain he felt, the horror of his transformation. His losses, his loneliness. At first, he didn't want to open his heart this far, but there was something in this flute that compelled him to lay out his emotions. However, it wasn't cathartic, really : it only served to bring back the painful feelings to the surface. He remembered the stock-market. The shop with the figurine. The slaughterhouse. Valerie. The fight at the pond. The loss of his eyes. The fight with Max. Being jealous of Leo. The loss of his beautiful horns. His kid.<br /> All of this fueled Nate's song. He didn't notice the tears running down his cheeks into his fur. Once again, he had lost track of the time, and when he finally ended it, he sat down on a nearby rock, completely spent emotionally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T10:59:51-07:00","id":269266,"title":"","content":"&quot;Again.&quot; The keeper said, &quot;AGAIN!&quot; he barked, sounding more angry than pleased. &quot;I want something to put me in a good mood, and you only made it worse!&quot; The Keeper didn't seem to realize two members of his collection were growing closer to the Ranch, for if he did, he would have surely stormed their location by now to vent his anger. Instead, Nate seemed to be the outlet for his frustrations.<br /> <br /> &quot;I said again!&quot; he demanded, his teeth becoming sharpened once more.<br /> <br /> The music Nate had been playing was not like the musical performances in the human world. It wasn't merely strumming notes together, it was a combination of mental imagery and sound, blending together. The music told a story through pure expression, it had no need for lyrics. Unfortunately the story had been one about pain and suffering, not the cheerful distraction the Keeper had been desiring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-30-2014, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:32:10-07:00","id":269308,"title":"","content":"Jessica smiled at Derek. &quot;I'm sure you're terrified. I can hardly blame you. I'm afraid too.&quot;<br /> <br /> Thinking of Derek's nervous reaction to returning to the ranch made her more clearly realize her own terror. This led her to decide that she would betray Curtis. After all, she already had with Leo. The time had to come to escape. As she needed help to escape and since Derek had saved her with a minotaur, she decided she would try to escape with the monkey. She could just hope Max and Nate would find their own way home. The thought of abandoning them hurt even more than the thought of betraying her boyfriend. After a moment, Jessica said, &quot;Derek, there's something I should discuss with you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Blushing, Jessica began trying to explain her idea of using marriage to escape their present problem. Before she could make herself understood, Nate resumed his music. Unable not to listen, she fell silent. Without thought, she reached out for Derek's hand, awed by the unearthly music washing over her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  Typo 09-30-2014, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:51:49-07:00","id":269319,"title":"","content":"The Keeper's shouts were a brutal slap to Nate's mood. He was slowly beginning to realize that his plan was flawed from the beginning. Of course, no one cared about his feelings. No one ever did. He wiped his tears with the back of his hand. This was all because the other animals had gone away. This was their fucking fault.<br /> <br /> He wanted to lay down and rest, but he couldn't. Nothing's ever comfortable in this Realm. You can't have a moment of rest. Of happiness. Or...can you? There were the small joys. The ones you may experience when interacting with others. The ones when you're overcoming an obstacle. <i>Damn, I sound like a buddhist or something. All about zen and all this stuff.</i> It was hard to keep the sadness away, and in truth, he didn't completely manage too. But as he already knew, for all the pain and madness in Arcadia, there was also wonder, and that's what his next song was about. He thought about Max, and their budding friendship. He thought about the pride he felt when he managed to climb the mountain all the way up. The sensuality of the pond's illusions. And of course, the joy of simply playing music. <br /> <br /> It was a jaunty happy tune at first, but slowly, the song was twisted into another meaning. The Goat was feeling the pressure to please his Master as to escape punishment, and it echoed through the performance. It was unintentional, but the story that was thus told had gained a moral : obey the Master, and there won't be any suffering. He'll take good care of you. And Nate couldn't even protest as he played. Everybody could see that those were his true feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T22:06:05-07:00","id":270611,"title":"","content":"Max was pleasantly surprised at the wilderness helping him on his path. He'd known the terms of the Contract, and even felt some ease from them, but everything here had just been so... horrible and dishonest. From his transformation and abduction, to the spores and &quot;nymphs&quot; at the lake, to the mud pit that tried to eat him... Forces in this place acting toward his <i>benefit</i> was new. <i>'I guess direct deals are the only thing you can trust here.'</i> Still, an empty belly didn't leave him much space to ruminate on that nor appreciate the kindness. He was too focused on following the path that the land set before him and his snout urged him down. Wherever the pig was heading smelled wonderful.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the sight of the blue apples was every bit as delicious as their fragrance. Absently wiping his salivating mouth, Max almost missed the sign. The recent thoughts on deals crossed his mind again, and his Contract with the Wilds to boot. He'd have to keep to this one, too. Truly, though, it almost didn't matter that the terms seemed so reasonable; the starving porker might have done much the same if it meant promising a firstborn son. &quot;Deal,&quot; he told the tree -- with a hint of delirium and his curly tail awag -- before he lost it. Max plucked a fruit from its branches and took an enormous bite from it.<br /> <br /> It was better than he'd dared hope. The juice, skin and pulp danced across his tongue, bringing an apple to mind, but only for wont of a more apt comparison. He wasn't sure he had the words to describe it. If any food could be called sublime, this was it. The moment seemed to stretch on for Max, even though he hungered. And then it was over. Delighted swinish sounds made their ways out through full mouthfuls, polishing the first fruit off quickly and reaching for another. He absently spat out the single large, round seed from each -- not due to thoughts of his agreement, simply for their being slightly too hard and cumbersome to eat. Yes, he made quite a pig out of himself, juice and pulp splattered all over his face, hands, and stomach, as who knows how many of the delicious fruits disappeared into his mouth and down his throat.<br /> <br /> In time, the Pig's belly filled and he started to slow enough for actual thought to rise up. <i>'Heh, definitely didn't need Nate's tips for <b>this</b>'</i>. This made Max pause in his chewing, and in bringing another fruit in for a landing.Nate's advice <i>had</i> been a life-saver during his more embarrassing and nauseating meal. He remembered how much he appreciated it, now. Not all of the Goat's other counsel had been <i>as</i> useful, but that wasn't the point: they were given with the best of intent, from a friend with a clue to a friend sorely in need of one, as Max remembered. For Jessica's sake, too; she'd tried to include him on a plan or two to get out, and had saved both of their lives before. Introspective as the Pig was, he'd felt bad about the fight earlier than this, but was now <i>very</i> guilty indeed. <i>'... I have to keep a better handle on things. They deserve better.'</i><br /> <br /> Max swallowed his current mouthful and looked at the fruit in his hand. He thought of an earlier chat with Nate, and found himself laughing a bit. <i>'Ha. Guess this stupid thing finally found a fruit tree after all,'</i> he thought, bonking the side of his snout. Max was done eating. Not that the hunger had completely abated, but he felt full. He could stop. And he would. &quot;I'm not a pig,&quot; he said aloud. And then licked his chops, slurping up all the juice and pulp around his snout, giving a small squeal of pleasure. &quot;... Not <i>really</i> a pig...&quot; he mumbled weakly to no one, his blush reddening the purple juice stains across his cheeks.<br /> <br /> Max looked to the small pile of seeds in front of him, each with an opalescent sheen, like a pearl in the sun. He remembered the deal. Luckily, there actually weren't as many as he'd thought, given his gluttonous rampage. Perhaps they were just more filling than they looked? Still, he definitely had some gardening to do. &quot;Thank you,&quot; he told the tree, giving it a small bow, &quot;I'll keep my word.&quot; He began to cradle the seeds between his arms. After a thought, Max added two more fruit to the third he'd plucked earlier: Nate and Jessica could use these. &quot;I'll be sure their seeds get planted, too,&quot; he reassured the tree. Then, departure! <i>'Hm... I'd like to head back to the Ranch... But I could see these pissing off the Keeper, if he really wants us to eat like animals. They'd just get torn down.'</i> He'd risk a few, just in case, and could even get off following the letter of the deal planting all of them there. But Max owed it; he'd honor the spirit, too. Speaking of which... &quot;Um... Hey there, uh, Wilds.&quot; He turned from the tree, then paused, and bowed somewhere at the wilderness -- careful not to spill any seeds. &quot;Thank you for bringing me here. I really needed it.&quot; He wasn't sure he really needed to <i>talk</i> to it, but, well... It felt respectful. &quot;So... I hate to ask again right away, but... could you help direct me, here? As long as I'm planting seeds, where would you most want 'em to go? I'd love to honor two bargains at once.&quot; The pig waited for the wilds to give him a clue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T13:38:31-07:00","id":271717,"title":"","content":"As Eva sat there with the other beasts of the Zodiac she looked somewhat bothered by the scene as it unfolded before her... The goat was clearly broken and the Keeper seemed to care more about it's own first world issues than how it treated them all. Still, despite her slightly screwed up face, trying to hide her disgust over their mutual master, she stayed silent. The tune coming from the goat's pipe (why a pipe? Clearly the goat wanted a guitar... Is that beyond the powers of their 'all-powerful' Master that he could only muster up a simple pan-pipe? Eva was sure she could carve a better looking thing at high-school wood class) was just too sad for her to enjoy. It was full of emotion and to her it was good... But despite not caring much about the goat before now, she could see that he had enough.<br /> <br /> Not enough that she thought about putting herself in the firing line of course, though when the goat had finally finished his tune, she gave him a slight nod and a sympathetic look crossed her face, which was quite an unusual sight given her new serpentine appearance. The look probably looked less than sincere thanks to her new appearance, but she made an effort in silence over to the broken piper either way, which was enough for her to feel better about not doing more. Still, she noted how the Keeper despite his threats and rants wasn't as all-powerful in her eyes as he'd like to think he was. Soon, their time would come. But not yet. She knew that whilst they could do much together, she knew well enough they likely wouldn't be able to out-number and defeat their Master as is right now... But the Keeper worked on whims, follies and generally spur of the moment things, never really concentrating fully on much at all past their own amusement... They would drop their guard at some point, then their chance would be there for them all...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T10:30:26-07:00","id":274833,"title":"","content":"The keeper seemed amused by the first portion of the melody, and less so by the second half. Leering at the goat, he materialized a pair of shears once again and then fell upon him with an inhuman shriek of rage. He swung the shears back and forth like a crazed slasher, the shears snipping with each pass. By the time he stopped his assault, he pulled back to check his work. Nate's upper body from his waist to his shoulders had been sheared bald, save for tufts of curly hair on his chest and forearms.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;I'm bored!&quot; the Keeper snapped, before flying off into the sky once again, presumably to look for new ways in which to entertain himself, gods help whoever he managed to bump into.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> The forest appeared to hear Max's request, because once again the plant-life moved to clear a path. Not only that, but it seemed to be illuminated by isolated sunlight, while the surrounding forest turned darker like night had befallen it. Clearly he was supposed to follow the illuminated path, and at the far end was what looked to be another grassy clearing like the one he was standing in now. Except this one had no tree in the center. Max's goal was obvious, reach the clearing and plant the seed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T14:51:14-07:00","id":275006,"title":"","content":"Eva moved with a slithering motion of her hips to where Nate was left standing, &quot;I sure hope I don't get picked next for that thing's amusement... Luckily I have scales though, so I'd sure like to see what he could do with me...&quot; she smirked, before patting Nate on the back with some measure of sympathy, though there always seemed to be something unnerving by the way Eva acted nice, like as if she was doing it to get something she wanted. She of course did resort to such tactics in her old human life at times, but here it was more genuine... The pair were in this cage of a realm together, so small comforts like this pushed them on. At least Eva tried to think so, she was cracking herself, but she'd never wish to show it. No, she was the serpent now and she'd like to think she was still one step ahead.<br /> <br /> &quot;That Keeper is more like a petulant Lord Fauntleroy than an actual... Well, whatever the heck it's supposed to be. Sure isn't no fair folk I've ever heard of...&quot; Eva whispered, staring out into the sky as she watched the Keeper fly away. She took another slithering step back and looked over Nate, who had been sheared. &quot;Hey, you don't actually look too bad... I mean you looked pretty cool with the fuzz... But you got this kind of cool satyr look now... A bit scruffy... But not bad, I guess...&quot; she nodded, with a sly smirk and went by towards the other animals. &quot;If all of us were together here we might have been able to do more...&quot; she sighed, narrowing her eyes at everyone else for a moment. Of course she felt bad for not being able to do more herself and she knew more than the rest that noone was kicking her down more than she was herself right now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T15:43:58-07:00","id":275028,"title":"","content":"Nate barely had the time to drop the flute and raise his arms in a defensive gesture before the keeper fell upon him. He was way too fast, and he did not intend on shaving the musician painlessly. The shears didn't exactly cut his hair : it was more like an aggressive waxing, complete with howls of pain from the Ram, that were echoed in his mind by the Beast inside him. He panicked, trying to escape from the Keeper's grasp, but it was futile : the shears left first degree burn behind them and many superficial cuts. Sure, it wasn't much compared to the traumatic experience in the slaughterhouse, but this time, the punishment was directly hurting Nate's soul. He felt the Ram inside of him bleating in distress as parts of his identity were shaved away.<br /> <br /> When the Keeper finally stepped back and left, the Ram was panting from exhaustion and pain. He looked at his upper body with a wry smile. <i>I...I did it? </i>He cringed and gasped when the he felt a scaly hand patting him on his back. Turning abruptly around, he was relieved when he saw that it was the Snake. He didn't know that woman well and she creeped him out, but at least she wasn't a natural predator of the Goat, even if it was weird to admit it. Still, her eyes made her look...cold. As if they were watching the world with a pragmatic curiosity.<br /> However, she made some compliments. Nate brought his smile back, and even chuckled a bit, adjusting his mess of hair : &quot;Thanks. That's...very nice of you, actually.&quot; <i>But you still didn't do anything to stop him.</i> He didn't say it. No sense in angering them right now. Right now, he wanted some peace, some rest, and a bath. He picked up the flute, examined it again, and decided to keep it. <i>I'm gonna need a strap or something... Guess I'm stuck as a satyr for now. At least I'm not a beast anymore.</i> He strutted to the Snake. &quot;Say, do you know if there's a pond nearby, or at least some water? It could really do some good for my skin right now...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 10-07-2014, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T02:49:48-07:00","id":275286,"title":"","content":"Derek's feelings of dread were quickly washed away by the sudden awkwardness of the situation. Being there with a woman, almost a girl for old Derek's standards, holding hands and listening to that eerie flute concert have taken him more by surprise than any of the previous weird ocurrences. Trying to keep his mind busy he gave a thought to Jessica's plan. There was no way he could feel comfortable agreeing to it, of course, and maybe this was what made him look more thoroughly to all the little details the ox woman have shared with him.<br /> &quot;<i>The first customers to buy the Zodiac figurines agrees to come to Arcadia and take on their forms</i>&quot; He whispered to himself remembering the words from Leo. &quot;<i>... agrees to come to Arcadia and take on their forms</i>&quot; He focused on the last part as Jessica already tinkered with the concept of &quot;first customers&quot; and how to spin it, her plan depended upon that.<br /> &quot;<i>Wait a moment! Jessica, Jessica, it is already solved, it was a trick!</i>&quot; he whispered, unable or uncomfortable to raise his voice pating her hand with his. &quot;<i>We never agreed to remain here in this... Arcadia. There's nothing in the contract forcing us to remain here, no mention of any minimum or maximum period of time to do so!</i>&quot; He was geting more excited for moments, he didn't even notice when the music stoped and the goat started bleating in agony at the Keeper's ministrations.<br /> &quot;<i>Technically, we already fullfilled our part of the contract, we are free to go... if we find a way out!</i>&quot; The Keeper flew away, geting lost in the ranch's sky while Derek gesticulated wildly and jumped up and down, happy as kid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T14:32:56-07:00","id":276653,"title":"","content":"Eva looked Nate over again, &quot;Heck if I know, despite my new lack of blinking... I haven't spotted anything like that at the moment, though I'm sure if we can find some water big enough, we can sort you out.&quot; she explained, looking to spot any real way she could call a path. The landscape was confusing to her, she was a city girl anyway, but the Arcadian countryside wasn't exactly welcoming to those not of the Fae, seemingly taking an animistic pleasure from making wanderers get lost in it's lands. &quot;Best thing we can do is keep walking and we'll likely find one, sooner or later...&quot; she mumbled before slithering off. A second later she looked back to Nate, &quot;Well, you coming or what, Mr.Satyr?&quot; she smirked before moving on again. The motions of her legs were fluid and she was more slithering across the ground as she took steps than truly walking. She didn't seem to care or struggle with this though, her smirk was constant.<br /> <br /> &quot;As far as I can tell you need to beseech the water with some kind of contract for it to actually clean you though... Was the thirtiest you could think of earlier... Had to talk to the water and make it a deal for it to quench my thirst... Such a pain...&quot; Eva sighed as she moved on, hiding her dismay and negative feelings behind her confident front... Which is exactly what it was, a front. She only differed from the emotional pain Nate felt in that she was able to hide it better. This gave her some power with the Keeper, as she was seemingly tough to break, though this wasn't the case, she just refused to show that side of her. The main thought that kept her strength up was that 'Things could always be worse'. She didn't want to even conprehend that she was more suited to this land than she'd like to admit...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:33:55-07:00","id":276772,"title":"","content":"Nate became flustered when the Snake woman talked about exploring for a bath. &quot;Y...You know what? On second thought, it's not that bad... I don't want to make another deal out of desperation anyway and... you know, I just came back here to the Ranch. I...&quot; <i>I don't want to displease the Keeper anymore.</i> &quot;I just want to rest for a bit. I've had a really long day...if it was even just a day. Hell, for all I know, I could have been awake for a whole year.&quot; It was weird to be called &quot;Mr. Satyr&quot;, but it was still better than &quot;Goat.&quot; &quot;But thanks for the concern.&quot; He said, sitting on a nearby rock. &quot;You know, while I was out there, I met some other prisoners. The Keeper has another collection of people like us, except they're the Western Zodiac, so some of them are still human. I've ran into Leo and Gemini, and the latter could control water. They even made some sort of whip with it! Did you pass this sort of deal with the water, or were you just allowed to drink it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T16:51:52-07:00","id":276810,"title":"","content":"Jessica considered Derek's words. After a moment, she said, &quot;i think you're right. The problem is what is to prevent the keeper from re-taking us?&quot;<br /> <br /> Then it occurred to Jessica that the same risk existed in her own plan. Nothing here is without risks. There was no safe way to escape. Yet remaining had its own risks. She forced a smile. &quot;I guess the wedding is off,&quot; she joked. Then she added, &quot;You're a smart guy, Derek.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T11:05:15-07:00","id":279904,"title":"","content":"Max smiled, gave the path a nod, and started down it. He could see it was a ways to go, but that the clearing ahead seemed wider than the one he was leaving. Given the number of fruits he'd eaten, there were quite a few seeds to plant; he wondered if he would wind up spacing them all out in the one clearing, or if the Wilds had several locations in mind on top of this. He was sure the helpful lights would give him an idea. <i>'Hmm... Gotta be sure I don't lean too heavily on it, though. It's a big help, but I don't want to take advantage.'</i> Presuming nothing stopped the Pig, he just focused on putting one hoof in front of the other, careful not to drop any fruit or seeds, and then set to digging one or more holes to plant the pearl-like things.<br /> <br /> Really, it was just very refreshing to Max to have such a simple, clear objective to carry out. Especially for that which had saved him from starving. <i>'I could get used to this partnership.'</i> Indeed, thinking about it, a notion struck him. He gave it a snort of laughter. <i>'Wow.'</i> Sagittarius had mentioned that, in time, the Wilds might grant him capacities beyond protection. <i>'Possibly by doing MMO quests to &quot;level up&quot; my Wilds rating. That's... I don't know what that is.'</i>Still, it made a degree of sense, albeit not best couched in those terms. <i>'Or maybe I'm just exhausted.'</i> Well, first things first: Max could catch some Z's after planting some seeds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T04:01:39-07:00","id":292848,"title":"","content":"Encouraged by Jessica's words, Derek started to ponder the next step of the plan.<br /> <br /> He wouldn't want to leave anyone behind in that strange and crazy place, but on the other hand was painfully aware that a large group would be way more easier to spot if they went for a sneaky escape. They could try to use the numbers on their benefit, though. Creating some confusion and looking for different avenues of escape at once may very well make it more difficult for the Keeper to catch them all. That didn't exactly make Derek happy. Potentially using some of the other prisioners (and Derek had no illusion about them all being anything else) as bait so other could make it to safety was a bit too much to bear on his conscience.<br /> <br /> Then he remebered about Leo and the other members of the Western Zodiac that Jessica had told him about. Maybe they could help, after all they seemd to be completly institutionalized already and he didn't had the time or the means to help them break with that dependency they had adquired to the place. They could get back the attention of the keeper and him and the others that were still savageable could have a shot at regaining their freedom. Yeah, that sounded about right.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Jessica</i>&quot;-he said-&quot;<i>We need to join your friends as soon as posible, and do you think you could find Leo? I need to talk to him</i>&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-26T21:22:59-07:00","id":293378,"title":"","content":"&quot;I agree joining my friends as soon as possible,&quot; replied Jessica. &quot;As to Leo, I can try. But I had the feeling that after he had finished with me, that he had finished with me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Remembering, Jessica almost blushed. She wondered if what she had said was true. After all, Leo had seemed interested enough in her at the time, and at least not unhappy with how things had worked out. Maybe he would want to see her again. Could she please him twice? She had no idea, and was unsure if she wanted to find out. However, she realized that a part of her did. This insight made her feel guilty.<br /> <br /> After a moment, Jessica continued, &quot;Like I said, I can try at least. But first we had better find my friends. And maybe your snake lady friend too&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica added this last bit with a teasing smile for Derek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T17:14:58-08:00","id":301581,"title":"","content":"Max indeed found his way to the clearing without any trouble. That nearly wasn't so, but a helpful beam of light pointed out a hole just before it had a chance to trip him up. Safely arrived, he watched the central light split itself up into several smaller ones and scattered. It left him with a central sunbeam with a circle around it. <i>'Well, I guess that's that.'</i> He set down his little collection of seeds and fruit, picked up one little pearl, and started digging where light marked a spot.<br /> <br /> The going was messy and a bit slow; the ground was thicker than he'd have guessed. And he kept running into networks of roots under the ground. All the exertion gave Max a bit of a grunting pant by the end of the first hole. <i>'I can see people don't just buy garden soil for the nutrients, now...'</i> he thought as he put the seed at the bottom and got it buried. He took a deep breath and started on planting the next seed. He went on this way until he'd covered almost half the seeds. By which point his arms were screaming with fatigue.<br /> <br /> <i>'C'mon... Just a few more. Just... Take a breath, wipe your brow and get through this.'</i> Max forced his arm up to wipe the sweat off his forehead, forgetting too late that 1) his hands were coated in dirt and 2) it wasn't like he had any sweat to wipe off, anyway. It gave him a moment's pause. <i>'Because the muck hadn't quite gotten everywhere, yet.'</i> But feelings of his own daftness quickly made way for how nice it felt. He hadn't realized how hot his face had gotten -- nor the rest of him -- until he touched the cool dirt to it and felt the instant relief. He briefly recalled a childhood field trip to a farm, and the sight of pigs rooting in the dirt, plunging their faces in practically up to their eyes. They made holes very quickly and seemed to have enough stamina to do it all day. So, with some reluctance and no small embarrassment, Max weighed the pros and cons of putting his snout to work.<br /> <br /> He tried to start the hole with a hand, but the sharp twinge across his arm drew out a wincing squeal. The Pig took a few breaths. He looked at the last pearl before him. He looked at the site of the last hole. And he looked at the small pink blob always at the bottom of his vision. He looked to his left, and to his right, and sighed. &quot;Aww, what the hell...&quot; Max got on his belly before the site of it. With one last breath, he started digging in the dirt with his snout. And he really began to wish he'd done it sooner. Sure, he was ecstatic nobody could see him now, but this was just like night and day. The shovel-like shape of his new nose and the neck muscles made for doing exactly this made the digging so much easier, the cool dirt offered some welcome relief, his inner pig was squealing with elation inside to lend him a sense of rightness about it (albeit an unsettling one), and hey, free grub. Yes, he'd felt briefly conflicted after eating the dirty roots without thinking about it, but, well, done was done, he hadn't been completely full, and it would have been a hassle to pull them up, so he rationalized his way past that one. That they'd been tastier than they ought hadn't hurt.<br /> <br /> In this way, Max wound his way through the rest of the holes in about half the time and a quarter the effort he had on the others. He was probably blushing furiously, but there was no way of knowing with all that dirt on his face. <i>'That... wasn't so bad, really.'</i> If he wound up needing to every now and then, he wasn't sure he would mind. Just so long as nobody ever found out, of course. It didn't even concern him that he was pretty okay with rooting in the dirt like an animal: it seemed exhaustion had finally left him too tired to care. As though to make this case, after he'd moved away from the planted seeds to check up on his fruit, an ear flopped at a rumbling sound and he lazily turned his head in time to catch his gardening sprout a new little orchard. Max gave no reaction, other than to smile and decide the base of the largest and most central tree looked like a good place for nap. The pig curled up beside it and was out like a light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T12:25:26-08:00","id":304878,"title":"","content":"The Snake Lady was definitely too weird for Nate. Cold and detached. He <i>knew</i> that this was his instinct speaking, but he couldn't get over it. He mumbled a quick excuse, and got up, away from the other Beasts. He was still uncomfortable from the concert. He...needed some time alone. The ranch had some wooden outhouses, suitable from a big farmhouse. Maybe he could find some amenities in here, even for a Goat like him. As he went toward them, he couldn't shake the feeling that those were big buildings. Too big. He felt like a child in there. And it looked too...pristine. As if someone was taking great care of the wood, it had a sheen to it, which looked weird on a ranch. He tried and pulled the first door, but it wouldn't bulge. He heard a snort, which came from the lock. &quot;Try as long as you might, but you can only enter where is your right!&quot; Nate sighed. A riddle, again? &quot;So what, I need a permission to come in here?&quot; The lock didn't answer but... the Goat could swear that the knob just....shrugged. &quot;Fine! I'll find my spot, if that's what you're saying!&quot; He stepped back, and looked under his hooves when he heard a soft crunching sound. He had stepped in...grain? It seemed that...it was coming from the building. So this place was a granary, huh? He looked around him, and found that the Rooster was watching him from afar. Oh... So, this place was the Rooster's &quot;apartments&quot;, it seemed. Nate waved at him, and got away from the building. <br /> <br /> It sounded like a trap. Or rather, something destined to lure them over, to separate them, and to appease their anguish and their dreams of escaping. But...right now, Nate wanted only one thing, and it was comfort. Besides...he seemed that he was back to being part human now. Surely, he could afford this respite. And thus, he explored the ranch. He passed a few outhouses, including one that strongly smelled of milk, a kennel, and a locked fence that seemed to guard the entrance to a big pond of mud. It made him think of Max, and he bit his lips, hoping that the kid was okay. And...he also hoped that he was still there, and he didn't escape.<br /> He was puzzled when he finally found a door that opened smoothly for him. When he opened it, his nostrils were assaulted by a very strong and earthy aroma : it smelled of wine. In fact, once his eyes were accustomed to the darkness of the building, he could see that it was a whole winery, located in some sort of warehouse. Nate didn't know a lot about wine, as he was more of a beer guy, but it looked like it had the whole package: barrels, bottling line, tanks... <i>Why is this my building? This isn't very goat-like...</i> He entered the small factory, and made a tour of <i>his</i> building. It seemed like the production was already well on its way, as there was already a lot of filled bottles, without a label, however. In the back of the winery, there was another door, which led to a small outdoor vineyard. Weird. How did he not see it from the ranch outside? The grapes seemed fine, and very juicy. He picked one, and popped it in his mouth. It was an explosion of flavor. <i>Oh man, it's so good!</i> He took another bunch, and quickly devoured them, not caring if the juices were staining his face and goatee. The aroma was so rich and fruity! He almost went for another grape, but he stopped himself : he needed to keep some for later. Besides, how could the winery function without fruit? He went back to the building, still entranced by the smell... He needed to taste it. It was his building right? And even if he didn't bothered to lock the door behind him, it was in his charge. But...how could he help make the wine if he didn't even know how good it was? Surely, no one would miss a bottle...<br /> <br /> And that's how, after a while, Nate had emptied his third bottle. He was drunk, with spots of red wine on his body and fur, laughing merrily and dancing and playing jaunty tunes on top of a barrel with his flute. Weirdly enough, it seemed that his music was even better than before, and the melody could be heard in the entire ranch. Wine and Music, was it his new life? For now, he didn't care. All he wanted was to drink more of this delicious wine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-09-2014, 10:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T15:31:51-08:00","id":306957,"title":"","content":"((Aaaaaand, I just realized it was Pisces who became the two fish, not Gemeni.. So let's go ahead and Retcon their name, shall we?))<br /> <br /> With it's newly planted trees, the forest seemed more pacified than it had been previously. At least around Max, anyways. The sounds of the wilderness went very quiet, as if trying to let him rest after his hard work. Any sounds that continued were too far off to be much of a disturbance. And hey, this time nothing emerged from the ground or the trees or the water to try and eat him! Unfortunately, the environment wasn't what he had to worry about, because as he lost consciousness, another entity casually approached him.<br /> <br /> &quot;You should have listened to Pisces, slave.&quot; the figure spoke with a woman's voice, before clasping a pair of shackles to his wrists and ankles.<br /> <br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Despite Nate's fears, the supply of berries seemed limitless, as did the bottles that were being churned out of the machine. The room seemed to be able to contain the limitless supply, almost as if the interior was getting bigger with each bottle added to it's storage! Of course in his drunken stupor, it's not likely Nate could appreciate the magic behind it. Suddenly, the sounds of high pitched giggling and gentle moans could be heard from nearby. A trap door Nate hadn't noticed before hung open at the back of the wine storage, and the feminine sounds were coming from below. It seemed his private room had a basement level, too!<br /> <br /> <br /> As if responding to his music, some guests began to ascend from the trap door, and launched into playful dancing as they emerged. True enough, they were all female, and they were all stark naked. They seemed to be gathered from a variety of different races including forest nymphs, elves, and even goat people like himself. Some resembled his previous form being almost entirely goat, others were satyrs having the upper body of a human.<br /> <br /> <br /> Having an endless supply of wine, the girls began uncorking bottles and showering each other with the fluids as they danced and drank, and partied with Nate's music! They even began cheering him on, begging him for more entertainment. Complimenting him as being the best party thrower they'd ever seen, and even making sexual advances. If Nate wasn't in paradise before, he certainly was now. It seemed everything in this room was designed to enthrall him!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T18:14:29-08:00","id":307038,"title":"","content":"Max was really tuckered out. His ears flopped at the approaching footsteps and the voice, but he couldn't really register them. Certainly not as a threat. The click of the shackles and the resulting discomfort merely roused him a bit. Ditto the strange tingling they sent through the former human's body; there was some manner of enchantment upon them, and Max was unlikely to enjoy it. For now, exhausted as he was, he simply felt them an inconvenience to sleep through. With an annoyed grunt, the pig tried rolling onto his other side, to see if that helped things. It didn't, so he simply accepted them. He tried to nod off again with a murmur of, &quot;Five more minutes...&quot;<br /> <br /> The woman seemed unlikely to grant him that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Tweakery. 11-08-2014, 09:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-08T18:24:00-08:00","id":307052,"title":"","content":"Where did those girls come from? Did it even matter? They were here for his party, and he was going to be the best host ever! He had quickly given up on trying to remember each girl he met, it seemed that they were...all different, but all similar either. <i>Must be the wine.</i> This delicious, intoxicating wine. It seemed that he couldn't ever have his fill of drinks, he had drank like what, five, six bottles of wine? He wasn't even thirsty, but...not having this taste in his mouth seemed just wrong.<br /> Guests were still coming from the trap door, and there were now some men among them, enjoying the party. He wasn't even feeling jealous, and why would he be? Everybody here was having the best of times, thanks to him! He needed to entertain them, He laughed at a stupid joke told by one of the women, and put an arm around her, taking a mouthful of wine before kissing her playfully, chuckling as the red liquid overflowed from his mouth and dripped on his torso. Stepping back, he took the flute that always seemed to be near his hand, and began to play a joyful and sensual song, that resonated into the whole winery, and even outside. Weirdly enough, it looked like he didn't even need to have the flute in his mouth, the music was still playing even when he was taking a break from it to drink, or to kiss another guest. He mingled with his guests, decided to be the most awesome host ever. He hoped that some of the other Zodiacs would come. He wanted them to have some fun, and he was ready to give it to them! He thought about Max, or Jessica. If they saw this party, surely they would be more inclined to stay here with him... But right now, he was hanging out with people that looked like him (oh, was Aries among them?), and...well, if the building was designed to enthrall him, it was certainly working perfectly!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-08-2014, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T17:32:52-08:00","id":307638,"title":"","content":"Max's reluctance was met with a swift heel to the face as the woman tried to awaken him. Her hands were on her hips and she did not seem happy.<br /> <br /> &quot;I am Libra, the Zodiac of justice!&quot; she exclaimed. The woman wore a blindfold over her eyes and was garbed in a pure white robe. &quot;You have broken Master's laws, and I'm here to bring you to judgement.&quot; On second thought, the blindfold wasn't worn over her face, but rather sewn into it. The edges along the top and bottom had stitches that indicated the blindfold could not be removed easily, if at all!<br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> The party was a level of euphoria that could scarcely be comprehended by humans without dropping some serious acid or ecstasy. The wine and music seemed to crush any worries or fears it's party goers had, leaving nothing but the joy and contentment of staying in this room... forever... where the Keeper could find them easily!<br /> <br /> Suddenly the crowd seemed to part subconsciously, as if they weren't even there, formed a path. At the end of the path was another satyr girl, but she was familiar. Very, very familiar, and even in his drunkeness, her appearance was crystal clear to Nate's eyes. It was Valerie, only she seemed much more beautiful than he remembered, at least from the hips up, where she was still human. Her beauty was almost fae-like, too perfect to be humanly possible. The Keeper's voice whispered behind the musician as invisible fingers creeped along his shoulders.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;She can be yours forever, Nate.&quot; the Keeper said, &quot;They all can, you'll never have to worry about your old life again. Just wine, music, and sex... for eternity.&quot; the weight of the Keeper's presence seemed to shift to the left, but nothing was there. &quot;I can give you immortality, but only if you submit. I can give you the girl you left, but only if you submit.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The music of the party seemed to fade away to barely above a whisper and Nate's vision began to narrow into a tunnel that specifically focused on the familiar face at the end of the room. The Keeper awaited his response, as did Valerie","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-09-2014, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T18:56:27-08:00","id":307728,"title":"","content":"&quot;Who...Why are you...&quot; In his inebriated state, Nate squinted his eyes at the girl. He couldn't form a coherent answer right now, <i>Something is wrong.</i> What was her name again? &quot;Ve...Val? Valerie?&quot; He needed to be sure that it was really her. He tried to get to her, but he stumbled, still drunk.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm c-coming, Val...&quot; He got back up on his hooves, and staggered again toward the girl. <i>God, she's so beautiful. </i>Her freckles, her curly red hair, her ample bosom, her wooly legs, her shapely hips...&quot;V-Valerie, did you buy the figurine too?&quot; He slowly made his way to her, although it seemed like those few steps took him forever. The deal was tempting alright. She was offering herself to him, after she had left him. <i>Wait, did she?</i> No, that's right he...<i>I dumped her.</i> But she was coming back! She didn't have any hard feeling, she still loved him and they could be together again, for a life of party and sex and...<br /> <br /> <i>Why...what is missing here?</i> She came here, to the Keeper's kingdom, just for him... Why did it sound weird? It was just the two of them here, the guests didn't matter. Two satyrs, they were going to be the best party throwers ever, king and queen of the party, the sexiest beasts on the ranch, and they would play music, drink wine, and mate all day long, like they should have done before...<i>Hey, that's right... </i>&quot;V-Val, what happened to our baby?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T21:35:00-08:00","id":307892,"title":"","content":"The kick did it alright. Max snapped wide awake with a loud squeal of pain, bringing his shackled hands up to his poor snout. &quot;Oww...&quot; he whined, barely sounding human. And then tried to get to his feet as quickly as he could. He hadn't fully processed what was going on, but he understood removing a reason for her to kick him. He massaged his throbbing face, cracking off some of the dried dirt in the process. The pig caught sight of his hand after a moment, and found a little blood mixed in with the dirt.<br /> <br /> &quot;Zodiac of... Wait, no!&quot; The knowledge of facing the Keeper's justice finally hit home. &quot;Y-You don't have to take me back! I-I was going to head back to the Ranch right after I'd woken up! Really, I was! I swear!&quot; It was true, but it was a question whether she would believe it. Or whether it would matter to her. He tried thinking fast, though at least one thing was distracting him, even beyond his scarcely relieved weariness. &quot;I-I just got lost earlier. Out looking for food because, um, well...&quot; The Pig supposed the end of that thought was self-evident. &quot;But I've, uh, got my bearings now, so can I... just...?&quot; It finally registered that the veil was sewn on. Max trailed off and gaped.<br /> <br /> And his mind turned down a new path. All the Zodiacs, Eastern and Western, had a pull toward embodying their signs and archetypes. Max knew he was having enough trouble not acting like a pig, and the other Zodiac animals were in a similar boat. But with the Western members, time seemed to have more thoroughly etched the signs' identities into their own. More so than the Eastern set -- for now, at least -- they were what the Keeper had made them to be. If she an instrument of the Keeper's justice was blind, she wasn't going to be easily swayed. <i>'Knowing him, that veil probably lets her see everything clearly. As long as it doesn't look anything like <b>real</b> justice.'</i><br /> <br /> It struck Max as an important insight, albeit a discouraging one. It was depressing, too. For all that she had kicked him and intended worse, he couldn't help feeling a little sorry for her, and it showed in his expression. Still, the Pig was mainly preoccupied with, well... saving his bacon. <i>'There's gotta be something I can do... Just... keep talking. Stall until I think of it.'</i> He asked the first question that came to mind. &quot;H-How much did it hurt? Er, when he sewed on the veil.&quot; He then hoped the stupid personal question wouldn't score him a black eye to match the nosebleed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T10:23:27-08:00","id":309279,"title":"","content":"&quot;Sold it to a barren couple!&quot; the altered Valerie answered cheerfully. &quot;You were right, kids just weigh you down. And hey, I got some good money off it in the process!&quot; she laughed, wrapping her hands around Nate's hips. &quot;How about I let you throw it at me while I dance for you?&quot; she flirted. The other party goers continued dancing silently in the background, their bodies lost in some kind of trance as they didn't register the conversation between the two of them.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;All yours... if you submit.&quot; the Keeper's voice whispered yet again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Max's question was met with another kick to the face in a manner that suggested the answer to the question was blatantly obvious. I mean, how would <b>you</b> feel if somebody sewed a cloth into your face?<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;This is not good cop, bad cop!&quot; Libra declared, &quot;Do not try to befriend me!&quot; she forced him to his feet, or rather hooves, and issued an order for him to start marching whilst she held him by the back of the head, one of his ears clutched between her thumb and index finger in case he tried to struggle. The forest did not seem to be attempting to stop her, that would have been trying to interfere in Keeper's agent of justice. And that... that would have been ill advised, to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T18:49:34-08:00","id":309728,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;</i>But you...you said you wanted that kid...&quot; <i>How...</i><i>Why did she... </i>He opened his mouth to ask a drunken question, but was stopped by the touch of her hands on his hips. It was so sensual, electric, it was pure bliss. &quot;Oh Val, I missed you so much...&quot; He ran a hand through her hair, caressing her cheek, not even troubled by the horns on her head. He smiled, a little confused at her question. &quot;You're silly, babe... There's no need for money, here.&quot; He softly sighed when he felt her breath touch him. <i>I...Yeah. This is what I want.</i><br /> <br /> While Nate was far from sober, it seemed that the alcohol was slowly fading, becoming nothing more than a nuisance in the background like the party goers. <i>&quot;</i>Submit, huh...&quot; <i>I'm so sick of struggling alone... </i>He hugged Valerie, holding her close. He needed her warmth. Still caressing her hair, he raised his voice, looking over her shoulder. &quot;Keeper? I...I'm tired of fighting you.&quot; He closed his eyes, breathing deeply, hating himself for his weakness. &quot;I'm ready to... to submit. Could we maybe...discuss it?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-12-2014, 07:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T21:36:20-08:00","id":309857,"title":"","content":"Max, having wisely gotten to his feet before he said a word to her, managed to block the kick. Between the block and his general exhaustion -- never mind her own skill -- he couldn't keep Libra from getting a hold on him. He drew a sharp breath at the grip she had on his floppy ear; he knew it didn't take much force to do some serious damage there. Needless to say, his level of sympathy for her dropped a bit. &quot;Urrgh, sorry for the stupid question. I just... don't think clearly when I get woken up by <i>a kick to the face.</i>&quot; Honestly, the little pig sounded too anxious for it to come across as the crack he meant it to be. This was probably for the best Failed snark aside, he did start walking. Not quickly, but enough not to provoke her. He needed to buy himself time to think up a way out.<br /> <br /> Max noted the lack of help from the wilds. That was disappointing, but, well... He certainly couldn't blame it. He couldn't really blame anyone for not wanting to get between the Keeper's agent and her mission. <i>'... Unless,'</i> it suddenly struck him, <i>'<b>I</b> give a good reason.'</i> A plan started to form. Which opened with a mental beseeching of the wilds. He didn't even know if he could reach out to them like this, or if they could or would comply. But it was certainly worth a shot. The porcine prisoner sent his will out through the contract. <i>'Wilderness... Please, hear me. Please make it... easier for our words to carry, so anyone at all close can hear us. It's... In a way, you'll be doing Libra a favor. It's important for people to know an agent of the Keeper has a mission to carry out, right? They'll know how dangerous it is to interfere, so that might make the trip run smoother.'</i><br /> <br /> Hoping his plea did as needed, Max tried for conversation again. &quot;So, uh... H-How long did you know I was away without leave?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T11:41:03-08:00","id":310413,"title":"","content":"The forest did not speak back with human words, but a gentle breeze passed through, causing the leaves to flutter and branches to sway before it went still again. Was that the forest's attempt at nodding? It didn't seem to matter, one way or the other. If somebody came, his plan would have worked. If they didn't, then it failed. Max was forced to play the waiting game and hope somebody arrived before they returned.<br /> <br /> Or then again, maybe this was helpful, after all. He had been separated from the others and almost died at least once since doing so. Maybe he should just go along and regroup, he could start the journey over with better odds of success! Or the Keeper could lodge another meat hook in his back... that was always a possibility.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> At Nate's words, the entire party faded away. Not into the background, but completely faded, Valerie too! The winery, the music, everything was a black, empty void save for a single spot light shining down on the satyr. Out of the darkness came the image of the Keeper in his demonic form, levitating through the air like a wraith as flames danced around him. The flames gave off no light of their own, for when he vanished into the darkness, they did too.<br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Yesss, let's trade words.&quot; his voice hissed in an alien pitch. It had never been heard by human ears before, and therefor was impossible to describe. The Keeper floated in and out of the darkness, circling around the satyr in a spiraling motion, appearing above and beside him at random intervals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T13:12:52-08:00","id":310477,"title":"","content":"Nate stumbled when Valerie disappeared, losing his support. He <i>knew</i> she was fake, but...this emptiness had twisted the knife in the Goat's heart. This sea of darkness was stirring some primal fear in the musician's guts. He had nothing, he was completely alone, at the mercy of this twisted being. Why did he agree to this? <i>In a way...he made a mistake.</i> Now that Nate wasn't surrounded by distractions and pleasures, his mind was clear, and while he was still reeling from the humiliations he had endured all day long (if it had even been just a day!), it looked like he wasn't influenced by some drug or temptation. It was only the two of them.<br /> <br /> There was something deeply unsettling in the Keeper's voice. Nate didn't know if he wanted to puke, run away, or simply cry. He got up, but opted for lowering his head and holding himself in his own arms, as if he was cold or afraid. He thought that this would please the sadistic alien being, and he hoped that this would prompt some pity in the Fae. <i>Yeah, right. As if he even knew what pity is.</i> He had been foolish. He couldn't step back now, he had to discuss some pact with his &quot;master.&quot; Either he'll manage to trick him into a loophole or he'll accepte his fate, forever embodying the Goat in his master's collection. He wondered how long it would take for him to be stript of his old identity, how long before he would forget his name for good and just be a figure.<br /> <br /> Still looking at his hooves, in a submissive posture, he spoke in a shaking voice. &quot;So...Y-you want me to submit. What does this entail? It would be a p-pact, right? Everything here works with pacts...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 11-12-2014, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T22:01:50-08:00","id":310925,"title":"","content":"Max considered just riding this back to the Ranch, but... <i>'No. &quot;Zodiac of Justice,&quot; she said. She <b>might</b> just take me back, but she's probably going straight to the Keeper. No, I've gotta at least try something.'</i> He was indeed limited in what he could try. Still, broadcasting anything the two said was a good start -- if indeed the wilds were giving him a hand. It very much increased the chances his plan had of working. No, he couldn't do much. But he could talk. Even if she wasn't in a chatty mood -- that last question about how long she'd known hadn't gotten <i>any</i> response -- Max could pick up that slack. And that's just what he opened his mouth to do--<br /> <br /> Until he spied the pieces of fruit on the ground. &quot;Ah! Wait!&quot; he said, starting to twist his head, and then strangling a squeal at the pain where she gripped his ear. &quot;Th-That fruit,&quot; he gestured, &quot;I-I picked it as a gift. Please, let me take it.&quot; Plucking those fruits and then not planting their seeds <i>was</i> a concern, but a distant one. The Pig wanted to at least add a little bright spot to his friends' stays in Arcadia; he owed them that. As well as a peace offering, if things hadn't yet cooled down. And, whatever else, he wanted to prove to himself he could do <i>something</i> under his own power. Er, even if &quot;his own power&quot; technically involved the wilderness's power after a bargain brokered by someone else's power.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Max realized after a moment that his plea would fall on ears as deaf as her eyes were blind. He grunted in annoyance. &quot;I really mean it! This is <i>not</i> a trick.&quot; After a moment's pause, he started to facepalm at having said that, but, well, he a) didn't trust the shackles, b) thought Libra might not take kindly to the sudden movement, and c) ... really wasn't sure how stupid it would look with his snout in the way. &quot;Okay, that was dumb to say. So... Argh...&quot; He took a deep breath. And held it; an idea to make her believe suddenly hit him. It seemed like the sort of fairy tale business that would actually work. He breathed out. &quot;... I swear on my name that I'm telling the truth about them. And that letting me get them won't interfere with your goal. And that I'll come back to your grip if you let me grab them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max felt an odd ripple run through him, not unlike when he'd forged his first Contract. It was... less grand, maybe, but perhaps more personal, and no less significant. Specifics were foggy, but it became very intuitive to this little piggy that he <i>did not</i> want to break his oath. He swallowed hard. Now, granted, there was a bit of a gulf between 'believing' and 'giving a damn,' but it was probably a better place than he'd been. &quot;... Please?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor edit. 11-13-2014, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T02:21:05-08:00","id":314342,"title":"","content":"Derek tried his best to ignore the smile of the ox lady but he could not avoid a sudden warmth filling his chest. Trying to ignore the issue he remained silent and started to walk towards where he thought he heard the music a while ago.<br /> <br /> The place was now empty but several footprints, hoove marks and so on remained as a testimony of the gathering. They were right on track.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Where could have everyone go?</i>&quot;-asked Derek more to himself than to Jessica, though expecting some kind of answer from the Ox. The monkey took almost no time to notice the row after row of strange buildings that where no far away from their postion.<br /> <br /> &quot;<i>Maybe we could try there?</i>&quot;-he pointed to a big wooden structure, almost like a barn from whence came sounds of laughter, music and other undeniable signs of a wild party-&quot;<i>Maybe they moved the concert or whatever that was to the inside</i>&quot;-propossed Derek. It was as good a guess as any.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T10:05:08-08:00","id":315500,"title":"","content":"Jessica followed Derek's led into the wooden structure. Inside, they found a wild, fantastic party that defied description. Before it could really register, a strange man with long blue hair and clad in golden chains pulled the ox woman into a dance. As they danced, he showered with kisses. Jessica tried to gather her thoughts, and take in all that was going on around her. However, before she could manage it, the entire party faded away. Not into the background, but completely faded. The winery, the music, everything was a black, empty void save for a single spot light shining down on a satyr Jessica recognized as Nate. Out of the darkness came the image of the Keeper in his demonic form, levitating through the air like a wraith as flames danced around him. The flames gave off no light of their own, for when he vanished into the darkness, they did too.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yesss, let's trade words.&quot; his voice hissed in an alien pitch. It had never been heard by human ears before, and therefor was impossible to describe. The Keeper floated in and out of the darkness, circling around the satyr in a spiraling motion, appearing above and beside him at random intervals.<br /> <br /> Jessica, standing seemingly alone in darkness, wondered if Derek had vanished with the party. &quot;Derek!&quot; she cried out. &quot;Are you still here?'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T04:32:05-08:00","id":362303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nate</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still looking at his hooves, in a submissive posture, he spoke in a shaking voice. &quot;So...Y-you want me to submit. What does this entail? It would be a p-pact, right? Everything here works with pacts...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Keeper</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Yesss, let's trade words.&quot; his voice hissed in an alien pitch. It had never been heard by human ears before, and therefor was impossible to describe. The Keeper floated in and out of the darkness, circling around the satyr in a spiraling motion, appearing above and beside him at random intervals.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;But no more sloppy pacts, no more rogue contracts being signed left and right and left again&quot;-as it spoke, the Keeper changed once more and so did the barn. He appeared as an old chinese man clad in a red silken robe embroided with gold threads woven depicting each of the Zodiac figurines. But not all, the place of the Horse was painfully empty, only the sewing marks where the silouette had been carefully unravelled out of the robe as testimony of its previous location. The Keeper may have appeared as the living image of the villain of those old and cheesy Fu-Manchu movies if it werent for the jade tinge of its skin or the flaming orange of its inhuman eyes.<br /> <br /> The Barn twisted and expanded, its roof so far up it was imposible to see. A dozen columns, also adorned with gold and red and jade sprouted from the floor as if trees, their top lost in the imposible heights of the room. Several figures, too tall and thin to have been human, stood at both sides of the room in perfect formation clad in chinese imperial guard uniforms, holding spears. Their faces where completely featureless, save for a single, big, round eye as big as a fist. The Keeper sat now in a throne. At its feet another figure, smaller than any other, hold a long Scroll whose lenght made it cover the &quot;secretary&quot; up to its waist in paper.<br /> <br /> &quot;Only a little detail left, your Incomparable and Gracious Lord Collector&quot;-the servile secretary pointed out-&quot;It will be proper protocol if all the members of the Zodiac where here to act as witnesses&quot;.<br /> The Keeper looked down from its throne to the secretary-&quot;Is that so?&quot;-it hissed. The secretary, aparently unafected by the obvious anger of its master, limited himself to nod. &quot;So be it, then&quot;-growled, and clapped his long nailed hands, once, twice, three times.<br /> <br /> On the floor of the room appeared 12 small circular platforms, disposed in a semi-circle in front of the throne. One by one in pufs of smoke the members of the Chinese Zodiac appeared there, dressed for the ocasion with oriental looking formal robes. Again, all save for the horse, whose platform remained empty and akward.<br /> <br /> &quot;Better?&quot;-hissed the Keeper to its annoying secretary. The secretary mostly ignored the question save for a quick nod, focused as he was cheking the list on his Scroll.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, then&quot;-the Keeper smiled and got up from its throne, bidding the Goat to aproach.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-08-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-07T14:40:57-08:00","id":362888,"title":"","content":"Well, that was terrible. This had been such a huge mistake. He had been tricked into giving in, and he thought he would be smart enough to trick the Keeper...there was no way for him to do that. Who was he kidding? <i>I'm gonna be forced into eternal servitude...</i><br /> He stood in awe when the palace was created. This was amazingly beautiful, no one could deny it, not even Nate. A shame that it was populated by such scary monsters. The Goat turned around to face each of the Zodiac with a panicked look on his face. Why were they here? No, they would judge him! They would judge him for his weakness! He tried to avoid looking at Jessica : he had ridiculed her before, and now he stood there, devastated, about to betray his humanity. And Max... He tried to meet his gaze, but he didn't have the courage, or the strength to speak. He just hoped that his eyes alone would express his thoughts.<br /> <i>I'm sorry for failing you.</i><br /> <br /> The Goat breathed deeply, eyes closed, before stepping down from his platform, solemn as a prisoner facing execution. &quot;So...&quot; He breathed again, his mouth furred with fear. <i>At least, try to show some fight. Don't give up now, so easily! </i>&quot;Incomparable and Gracious Lord Collector, Keeper and Master.&quot; He bowed, thinking that at least, forcing himself to be polite couldn't hurt. In fact, it could even ease the being. &quot;As I asked earlier... what does this pact entail?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T03:54:22-08:00","id":363326,"title":"","content":"The Keeper, the Collector, smiled at the polite words and bowing of the Goat-&quot;Niiiiice, then let's set the terms of your new Contr...&quot;-its discourse was suddenly interrupted by the sound of the Secretary loudly clering his throat.&quot;Arghhhh, what now?&quot;-it growled, dangerously cosing its eyes down to a flaming slash.<br /> <br /> &quot;If I may interrupt your Gracious and Magnificient Lord Collector again&quot;-proceeded the Secretary-&quot; the order of the meeting demands that the previous Contracts agreed upon by all the members of your most recent collection be adressed before any new Contract is written or signed by any part, my Lord&quot;. The anger of the Keeper was palpable, emanating in heated waves from his persona. Yet again, the Secretary remained either oblivious or unnafected by such displays.&quot;This way&quot;-he continued-&quot;the previous Contracts may be offcially aknowledged, rendered invalid or ratified as needed in each case, my Lord&quot;-he tapped the Scroll twice with his quill-&quot;It is all here&quot;-he assured.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 01-08-2015, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-08T22:34:18-08:00","id":364128,"title":"","content":"Now out of the darkness, Jessica kept quiet. The sudden change had jarred her. However, she now came to her senses. The words of the Secretary rang in her mind. Fighting down her fear, ignoring her pounding heart,she asked the secretary, &quot;Sir, is the Collector the only one able to render contracts invalid?&quot;<br /> <br /> In her mind, Jessica berated herself for speaking. However, she knew that someone had to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T02:38:58-08:00","id":364190,"title":"","content":"The Secretary looked down on his Scroll, looking for something. After a little while he made a little nod to himself and started reading aloud-&quot;Jessica Sparks, owner and owned of the zodiac figurine representing the sign of the Ox.... cheked&quot;-he made a quick mark with his quill on the Scroll next to Jessica's name.<br /> <br /> &quot;Our Sublime and Magnificient Lord Collector is in its right to call into doubt the validity of any Contract performed without the participation of its Gracious presence&quot;-the Secretary explained before the Keeper had time to react-&quot;That said, it is a matter to be discussed between all the parts involved in each relevant Contract and to make sure the appropiate protocols had been observed, which would render the Contract invalid otherwise, and that the agreed upon terms of the Contract had been diligently obeyed by both parts&quot;. The Secretary tapped the Scroll twice again with his quill-&quot;It is all here&quot;-he assured.<br /> <br /> The Keeper's anger had given pass to utter bafflement-&quot;You... you remeber you work for me, don't you, maggot?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T14:30:39-08:00","id":364788,"title":"","content":"Maybe this wasn't over. Maybe there was still hope. A faint glimmer of hope, provided by the Secretary. Who was this guy, Nate had no idea, but right now, he just wanted to thank him. A plan started to form in the Goat's mind. It was risky, and it would certainly qualify as playing with fire, but it was his chance to get the better out of the Keeper. So...he needed to thread carefully to not ruin his solution by being too greedy. <i>Here goes...</i><br /> <br /> The Goat cleared his throat. &quot;Sublime and Magnificent Lord Collector, if I may? As your secretary-guy just pointed out, this would be the occasion to pass a few Contracts.&quot; He didn't notice that he was gradually to lose his polite tone. &quot;See, I know that you granted powers to some...pieces of your previous collection. Like Pisces, and their control over water for instance. And it's only logical that they possess this ability, it's very thematic and fitting. After all, what sort of fish can't even swim, am I right?&quot; He checked the assembly as if he expected a laugh, but this wasn't exactly open mic night. <i>This guy knows what I'm talking about, right? Nate out!</i><br /> &quot;That's why I took the initiative of agreeing to the Contract of Fang and Talon, even if honestly, it could have been named differently, given that I have neither of those.&quot; He snorted. &quot;Anyway, thanks to that, I've come to term with my new Goat-ness. But...&quot; He paused, pondering his words. &quot;if I'm to distract you with my music,&quot; he began, frowning a bit as he discovered that the pan flute was inexplicably in his hand, &quot; I could use some new powers to inspire me, to make me a master musician, and I'm sure my tunes will only please you better then!&quot; He smiled and bowed a bit again. <i>Please, make this work...</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T16:04:03-08:00","id":364848,"title":"","content":"&quot;Well, well&quot;-grinned the Keeper-&quot;isn't this a pleasant and polite request?&quot;-it looked down from its high throne to the Secretary-&quot;So, what are you waiting for?&quot;-it demanded-&quot;Proceed with all the proper protocols&quot;.<br /> <br /> &quot;It will only please me to obey your magnanimous orders, oh Your Most Incomparable Lord Collector&quot;-answered the Secretary in a monotonous tone that seemed to show he didn't care one way or another. &quot;Ok, let's see then.... Nate Davis, owner and owned of the zodiac figurine representing the sign of the Goat... checked&quot;-he made a mark next to Nate's name with a quick motion of his quill-&quot;...&quot;-the Secretary mumbled to himself reading more information on his Scroll for what seemed like an eternity to Nate, was it possible there was something wrong?-&quot;Here is stated that you already had signed a Contract with The Goat, is that correct?&quot;-he asked after a while looking directly to your eyes. &quot;And it also says that who acted as witness was no other than Jessica Sparks, another member of the Zodiac, that's highly unnusual&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-09T17:52:39-08:00","id":364928,"title":"","content":"Nate blinked, unsure of the right thing to answer. &quot;Uh...yeah. That's what I just told you. Jess was the witness, she had passed the same kind of contract with the Ox just before mine. With Leo as a witness by the way.&quot; He shrugged. &quot;Why? This is unusual, but it's not irregular, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T14:03:15-08:00","id":365735,"title":"","content":"With a few grunts of confusion, Max brought a dirt-crusted hand to his head. Blinking, he looked around him, and at himself. He was relieved to be dressed again, for the first time in what seemed a great while. They were... exotic, and likely looked out of place on a mud-splattered pig, but comfortable; they seemed meant to fit one of his shape. As did the costumes of the other elev-- ten zodiac animals in the room. And what a room it was. The universe had apparently changed venues from his being apprehended in a forest to standing in a grand, palatial court of law. <i>'Oh. Well...'</i>The Pig found his heart briefly lifted on noting he didn't seem to be the defendant, but dipped on spotting the Goat who was. <i>'Nate... What happened?'</i> He tried to give his friend an apologetic smile, but the... well-shorn fellow tried and failed to meet his gaze. It puzzled Max, but left his confidence ebbing low. He then gave them up entirely, with a little squealing gasp, when he saw the &quot;judge.&quot; Any court over which their Keeper presided could hand down no positive verdict.<br /> <br /> <i>'... Or maybe it can...'</i> Unsure as he was about what to say or do, the Pig said and did nothing, simply trying to get his bearings together. And he got the impression that the real power in this room was not the &quot;Sublime and Magnificent Collector,&quot; but the small and unflappable figure at his feet. Or at least the endless document. It was clear there were rules here, and the Keeper either couldn't or wouldn't likely go against them. <i>'Okay, this place is still crazy. And I don't think the rules'll be <b>fair</b>. But at least he can't just change them because he wants to.'</i> Max had felt moments of hope since he'd been in Arcadia, of things being okay or getting better, or even of their getting away. However, this was the first time part of him wondered if it might just be possible to <i>win.</i><br /> <br /> The Pig's ears flopped a bit at a phrase the Secretary had twice used. <i>' &quot;Owner and owned...&quot; That's interesting...'</i> He filed it away, in case it mattered. For the moment, Max couldn't think of anything that might improve the situation, so he simply wracked his brain, mouth shut and ears open. Snout open, too, evidently, as he sniffed at the air. The Court had a certain austere grandeur that even seeped into its smell, and of course each Zodiac animal had their own natural musks to them, but there was an unexpected sweet -- and familiar -- scent, too. Very, very close. Max looked down and saw, next to the spot his robes met the ground, the apples he'd meant to bring with him. The blue fruits seemed to blend in with his robe and had thus gone unnoticed. <i>'... Well, I guess that's something else going for me. Maybe...'</i> The Pig returned his attention to the trial, hopeful something would hit him. He wanted to know where things were going. Particularly now that Nate had brought the Western Zodiac into things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T14:57:47-08:00","id":365760,"title":"","content":"The Secretary seemed to ignore Nate's last question with the same detached disdain he reserved for his Lord. He noded to himself as he read and made quick notations on the Scroll.<br /> <br /> &quot;Everything seems to be correct, oh Most Exquisite and Terrible Lord Collector&quot;-the Secretary looked up to the throne-&quot;Both Contracts have been explained in terms that the recipients could understand, both parts had agreed to them by their own free will, there had been witnesses that corrobored that it was so...&quot;-he made more notes on the Scroll-&quot;...the payment has been made effective as the two of them had abandoned whatever little human restraints they originally had and followed their animal instincts... and the rewards of the Contract seemed to be enjoyed by the recipients&quot;- The Secretary looked alternatively to Nate and Jessica-&quot;Or is that not so?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T15:32:05-08:00","id":365803,"title":"","content":"<i>Ouch.</i> Nate didn't know what hurt more : the unpassionate tone of the secretary or the truth of his words. He waited a moment to answer, as he considered what he had lost. it didn't seemed like much, back in the Ranch, but here, in this court, where Beasts like him were out of his element? He finally realized what dangerous game he was playing. Still, he needed to press his luck. &quot;Yeah, I...I enjoyed the rewards, as you say. Can we move on now?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-10T19:23:21-08:00","id":365919,"title":"","content":"For her part, Jessica replied. &quot;I wouldn't really say that I enjoyed it. Or maybe I did. Whatever. If my contract needs to be undone in my case, so be it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica had more to say, but fell silent. This trial confused her too much. Even in the normal world, she was no lawyer. She worried that anything that she might say could make matters worse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T04:22:29-08:00","id":367196,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hmmmm&quot;-mumbled the Secretary making too fast to follow notes on the Scroll. For his part the Keeper seemed to have reach the limit of its patience and beratted his far too formal servant. &quot;Yes, yes, yes, everything is perfectly clear. I have some things here to discuss with my dear Goat, isn't that true, <i>Goat</i>?&quot;-The Keeper put especial emphasis in that last word, piercing Nate with its flaming orange eyes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course, oh Superlative and Exquisite Lord Collector&quot;-he conceded-&quot;But, may I take into account the posible complaints the rest of the collection may have with their Contracts, my Lord?&quot;-It seemed Nate would have the complete attention of the Keeper, at least until they managed to formalize a new deal. On the other hand, the Secretary was open to questions and complaints, so maybe it was the right time to make some indiscrete questions, now that the attention of your tormentor is focused elsewhere, on poor Nate. You cannot avoid feeling a pang of guilt to leave Nate on their own to deal with your Keeper, but on the otherhand he brought this on himself by choice. Poor consolation as it is.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, so, my little Goat, you aspire to be a more pleasing piece of my collection, isn't that lovely?&quot;-the Keeper clapped his long nailed hands, obviously delighted-&quot;If only all of you were as compliant&quot;-he added, firing a spitefull gaze towards the Pig and the Ox. It seemed it still resented them for their initial escape attempt, horribly failed as it was-&quot;Well, and what I could do to you to make you better? What would make you a more aesthetically pleasing piece?&quot;-it asked, more to itself than to Nate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T04:51:36-08:00","id":367215,"title":"","content":"The Secretary took the sudden change of focus of his Lord as an agreement-&quot;Let's see, we have the Contract that both Mr. Davis and Ms. Sparks signed with their respective animals, of wich Ms. Sparks seems to be disatisfied&quot;-as he spoke, he made more and more notes on the Scroll.<br /> <br /> &quot;We have the Contract that Maxwell Layton, owner and owned of the zodiac figurine representing the sign of the Pig had made with the Wilds with Sagittarius acting as witness, of wich the payment on Max's part have been interrupted&quot;-he looks at Max from above his Scroll-&quot;My apologies about that, if everything is deemed correct we will make sure you can continue with your services to the Wild undisturbed, we don't want them to be angry, right?&quot;-Max wasn't sure if that was supposed to be a joke, as the secretary used the same monotonous and tired tone for everything.<br /> <br /> &quot;Finally we have the Contract of Derek ********&quot;-the surname of Derek was substituted by a sound like the rustling of leaves-&quot;...owner and owned of the zodiac figurine representing the sign of the Monkey with the elemental forces of Wood, in exchange for his Family Name and everything asocciated with it, with me as its witness&quot;.-he tapped the Scroll twice-&quot;It's all here&quot;-he asures you all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T13:32:53-08:00","id":367782,"title":"","content":"Oh great. The Keeper was alienating him even more from the rest of the group. And now they would surely think that he was a traitor. He needed to pull this off, or they would hate him.<br /> &quot;If I may, oh Magnificent and Grand Lord Collector, I have a suggestion. You already gave me this awesome flute as a gift, and I'm honored, really,&quot; Nate answered in his most servile voice. &quot;And I think I know another way to put this gift to good use : you... made me the perfect party thrower, with this...this amazing form&quot;, he said, gesturing at his changed body. &quot;But the other Zodiacs, unfortunately, are reluctant to understand what an honor it is to be a willing part of your collection.&quot; The Goat paused, and breathed a bit. <i>I want to vomit right now...</i> &quot;Give me the power to enthrall them, to show them how beautiful this realm is, through my tunes or by any other meaning. It will only make your collection better.&quot;<br /> He did not look at the other animals. He knew that if he did, if they heard him (and he was pretty sure that at least one of them did), they would insult him, hate him. To hell with them! He was trying something for their own good! <i>And if I fail, well, at least I'll have a way to protect me from their stupid wrath.</i> He hastily added a bow, the Keeper liking politeness. &quot;Please...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 01-12-2015, 11:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T04:44:28-08:00","id":369666,"title":"","content":"&quot;I see...&quot;-the Keeper stroke its long, thin moustache and goatee, showing interest in each and all the words of his collection's piece-&quot;And will you vow to do that, <i>Goat</i>?-again, the demeaning inflexion on that word made Nate feel even more uncomfortable-&quot;Will you promise and swear on your Name to enthrall your fellow Zodiac signs on behalf of me, the Lord Collector, your Master and Owner?&quot;-It rose from the throne as it spoke, one of its long nailed hands cutting a yet unwritten piece of the Scroll off. Surprisingly the overall length of the thing didn't seem to be reduced by this, even if the piece cut by the hand of the Keeper was a good five feet long.<br /> <br /> The Keeper was wielding a quill in its other hand, not much different from the one the Secretary was using except for its enormous size. It sat down again and started to frantically write on its Scroll, pausing only from time to time to dip the quill in the dark saliva covering its serpentine tongue. After a long while, apparently done writting, it started to read to itslef the whole document, start to finish. Obviously satisfied, it let the scroll unroll towards Nate.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sign here... your innitials here and here&quot;-it explained, pointing to several dot lines at the end of the document, far away from the corpus of the text-&quot;You can use this, <i>Goat</i>&quot;-and with that it threw the quill towards Nate. The quill quickly reduced its dimmensions to acomodate to the size of the Goat, but not its speed. As if an arrow its sharp point buried itself in the chest of Nate near the heart, dipping in his blood, adding injury to insult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-14T07:26:42-08:00","id":369730,"title":"","content":"Nate fell to his knees with a surprised cry, groaning in pain. A thousand insults almost came out of his mouth, but the shock of the attack managed to keep them under control. He grabbed the quill but gasped again, as it seemed to be very comfortable here in his chest, even burying itself a few inches deeper. The Goat then used his two hands, and pulled it out slowly, with another groan. <i>Felt like I was Excalibur's fucking rock...</i><br /> The quill now seemed to have found its own ink with the goat's blood. Of course, could it be more twisted? Speaking of twisted, Nate looked as his Keeper, thinking of how his words, and how they could be twisted against him. And maybe it was because of his exhaustion, but the Goat couldn't find any loopholes to his disadventage. It seemed too good. Almost... too easy, which was ironic considering that he just took an arrow in the chest for that.<br /> <br /> He took the quill and paused, breathing deeply to stop himself from shaking. This was a big mistake, he knew that, and he hated himself for pushing his luck that far. <i>But it's too late to turn back now. </i>He then slowly signed the document, after pausing a bit to remember his initials. When did it get so hard to write? Had he forgot already how to do it? Once the deed done, he got back up, and held the quill high so his... Master, apparently, could take it back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 01-15-2015, 12:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-15T07:44:31-08:00","id":371030,"title":"","content":"After trying to understand all that was going on, Jessica threw up her hands. To the secretary, he said, &quot;I admit it: I don't understand what is going on. I have no idea if the contracts we're discussing are valid. I thought I sort of understood it, but now I don't. I guess what I really want - what I think we all really want - is a contract to go home! Is that possible?&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe I should also try to get a nice car, thought Jessica.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-16T20:04:21-08:00","id":373246,"title":"","content":"&quot;Uh, y-yeah,&quot; Max nodded, when the Secretary mentioned his Contract of the Wilds. &quot;I'm satisfied with the terms. I don't contest them. I'll-I'll keep to my obligations.&quot; He scratched nervously against the side of his snout, cracking free some dirt it had picked up while he was 'keeping to his obligations.' &quot;Er, though, if if there's anything about those terms that weren't explained to me -- anything else I owe or anything else I'm owed -- I'd be glad to understand it better. I-If you please.&quot;<br /> <br /> He was also interested in that mention of the Mon-- Derek's Contract. The Pig had been present or informed for all the others described; if there were any more, the Secretary was keeping them to himself for now. Giving up one's 'Family Name and everything associated with it' seemed like a pretty big deal. <i>'From what Sagittarius said... Wow... I hope the poor guy can still make it out of here.' </i>Max turned a few platforms down to the simian, and gave a look of sympathy. Briefly, at least.<br /> <br /> The Pig got a sense of something ominous going on with the Goat and the Keeper, but he'd split his attention too many ways. He was too distracted by the Secretary to make out any terms discussed. Still, it was hard for a great quill stabbing into his friend's chest to escape him. &quot;Nate!&quot; he half-squealed. Still, after recovering, the Goat signed the scroll he'd been offered. <i>'Well... Here's hoping that comes out well...'</i><br /> <br /> Max turned as the other horned ungulate spoke up, almost on the other side of the zodiac platforms. And appreciated that she charged straight to the heart of the matter. Drawing a breath, the Pig decided to back her up. &quot;R-Right. I mean, uh... Only makes sense we'd all be...&quot; His eyes darted to the Keeper, and he chose his word carefully. &quot;... curious about possibilities for leaving. And we haven't all been gathered for a talk like this before, right? S-Seems like a good time to go over things.&quot; Max coughed. &quot;On a related note... We've heard some mentions before, but... Seeing we're in a formal setting, could we also go over the contract that brought us here? Like, formally and in-depth?&quot; Another glance at the Keeper. &quot;I-I-I mean, b-best to reassure us all e-everything's in order with the terms.&quot; He gave a not-so-convincing smile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T02:58:46-08:00","id":375085,"title":"","content":"The Secretary looked at both the Ox and the Pig with confusion in his eyes. It was only a flash of emotion, almost subliminal, but you are almost sure you saw it. &quot;Let's see the terms of the Figurine Contracts&quot;-he said again in that monotonous tone-&quot;... first customers... comming and taking on the shape of... aha, aha...&quot;-he read on the Scroll.<br /> <br /> &quot;You seem to have already commited to the terms of the Contract that brought you here, as the first customers who bought each of the figurines you have come to this place and have taken on the appearance of your respective signs as agreed&quot;-he made some more notes on the Scroll and continued-&quot;Apparently there is no set period of time for you to remain here as part of the Collection, at least I can see none especified here on the original Contract&quot;<br /> <br /> The air got still and the room fell silent.<br /> <br /> &quot;I suposse that means you are free to go&quot;-he finally added.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T10:03:43-08:00","id":375333,"title":"","content":"Nate had expected something more flashy with his contract. Last time, a ghost appeared and collided with him, but now... well, he had taken an arrow to the chest and signed a giant scroll. That felt a bit underwhelming. He had to trust the contract, and he hoped that he did in fact gain musical talent, but he couldn't really test it right now. Especially since Max and Jessica seemed to have figured it out.<br /> <br /> The Goat turned to them, and a big smile slowly crept on his face. He didn't even feel jealous that he wasn't the one to point out the technicality. They had won. Still sporting this grin, he cleared his throat, and adressed the Secretary. &quot;Hey, lawyer-guy. I too signed the same contract as the two of them, like the rest of us. I want to get out too. I'm free to go, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T11:23:25-08:00","id":375405,"title":"","content":"&quot;Awhahahahahahaha... no&quot;-cackled the keeper, taking the recently signed contract and adding it to the length of the main Scroll as if it was never separated from it-&quot;Secretary!&quot;-it screamed-&quot;Have I not properly fed these creatures? Have not they voluntarely partake of the fruits of my realm?&quot;-it asked, grinning like a maniac.<br /> <br /> The Secretary navigated the Scroll, looking for the information demanded by his master-&quot;Ah... yes, here it is&quot;-said at last-&quot;It appears all of you have been offered food. Furthermore, all of you accepted and ate it&quot;-he looks at all of you-&quot;My apologies&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T11:42:02-08:00","id":375426,"title":"","content":"&quot;Whaaat?!&quot; Nate bleated way too loud in surprise. &quot;That's complete bullshit! What if we ate this food, this has nothing to do with the original contract! You can't just make up your rules!&quot; He snorted with anger at his Master. <i>Wait, master? I meant Keeper, yes. Keeper. Oh no.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T09:26:26-08:00","id":377273,"title":"","content":"Jessica nodded at what Nate said. It occurred to her that the Keeper may have made a mistake. She said to the secretary, &quot;Back on my world I was a locksmith. The company I work - worked ? - for used contracts all time. They couldn't just change them. Also I think I should point out at this time that Max and I left our cages before we ate anything.at all provided by the keeper. From what you're saying, it sounds like that we had the right to leave, at least at that time. Yet he and I were punished for it. I think this means that the keeper was the one not to keep the contract. Shouldn't he be punished now?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T21:01:22-08:00","id":377753,"title":"","content":"Max's outlook ping-ponged from hopeful, to horrified, and then back to... well, mildly hopeful again. He honestly couldn't believe he'd forgotten about their early ill-fated jailbreak. <i>'I guess it does feel like it happened ages ago...'</i> Still, even without any sort of real plan, he tried his best to pitch in on defense. &quot;Sh-She's right! If h-he's claiming he got the right to keep us here when we ate the 'food' he gave us,&quot; -- the Pig gave a derisive snort -- &quot;then he violated <i>something</i> by k-keeping us here when we tried to leave before that.&quot; He didn't think it was just Jessica and himself, either. He'd been overstressed and very out of it in those early days before (and shortly after) the Ranch. But even then, Max was sure he remembered at least a few of the other Zodiacs disappearing from time to time and not generally looking much enriched when he saw them again. He thought <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/205196-ic-zodiac-beasts?p=215677#post215677\">the Goat had been among them</a>.<br /> <br /> Steeling himself, the little pig tried to reach still further. &quot;And... And given those... f-false pretenses... C-Couldn't that mean any bargains we st-struck afterward were... were...&quot; He managed a glance at Nate, still bleeding from his quill-wound. He drew a breath and forged ahead. &quot;Th-They were made under d-duress. Sh-Shouldn't we be able to void them if we f-felt coerced?&quot; Max didn't have high hopes for this. Aside from the whole 'it would be fair,' thing, coercion didn't usually count for much when it came to bargains and oaths in stories he'd read. Still, a court like this -- mad though it was -- gave it a chance, especially in light of the Keeper's apparent error. All the Pig could do was hold his breath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T12:14:06-08:00","id":378265,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hmmmmm&quot;-pondered the Secretary, reading the Scroll up and down-&quot;It is customary and part of the rules of this place that you tacitaly agree to remain here if you accept and eat anything originated in the realm, those are the ancient rules, that is the Wyrd and that cannot be averted&quot;-he sentenced.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, well my little <i>things</i>&quot;-the Keeper said, pleased-&quot;You heard my diligent Secretary here, you have agreed to remain here for my own amusement&quot;-he paused-&quot;I wonder what kind of display I should use for such naughty pieces of my collection as you have demonstrated to be...&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That said...&quot;-interupted the Secretary-&quot;...the Ox is <i>thecnically</i> right, the best kind of right if you ask me&quot;-he finally conceeded-&quot;The Wyrd has already been violated and it must be amended, least the integrity of this realm gets irreparably compromised&quot;.<br /> <br /> This was the second time the unflappable fa\u00e7ade of the Secretary had been broken by a display of emotion, in this case a very brief flash of utter anger and acusation directed to his purported Master.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, oh Grandiose and Incomparable Lord Collector, what is your decision regarding our current predicament?&quot;-he asked, his voice once more devoid of emotion or inflexion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T06:27:41-08:00","id":380065,"title":"","content":"Something else occurred to Jessica. There might be a way to help Nate, maybe even some of the others. She said, &quot;Sorry to interrupting, but I should point out that it wasn't just Max and I who tried to leave before we first ate. I was thinking only of the escape from the cages. However, after we were moved to the ranch, Nate was with Max and I. I'm almost positive we were outside the ranch before we all first ate. Some of the others might have been too. In at least Nate's case, I think - if understand this rightly - he was punished for having left. Again, sorry to interrupt.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":". 01-24-2015, 09:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T12:15:28-08:00","id":385444,"title":"","content":"&quot;Well, well, well...&quot;-said the keeper tapping the arms of the throne with its long, spidery fingers-&quot;Neither of us want things to go awry, now do we, <i>Secretary</i>?&quot;-the tone of its voice changed for a moment but you feel unable to point out what exactly does it remind you all.<br /> <br /> &quot;Of course not, Unasailable and Inconmesurable Lord Collector&quot;-the Secretary conceeded, noding ever so slightly.<br /> <br /> &quot;So be it, then!&quot;-the keeper growled-&quot;Let's give the offended party the chance to take what they see as an appropiate compensation&quot;-saids gesturing to you all, tracing a wide arc in front of him with its overly long and thin arm.-&quot;What is it do you want, <i>Goat</i>, <i>Pig</i> and <i>Ox</i>?&quot;-As it spits your names it looks each of you in the eye with its flaming and piercing gaze.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T11:41:30-08:00","id":386529,"title":"","content":"Jessica did her best to meet the Keeper's gaze. She had to compose her thoughts. She had to say things just right, or she might makes matters worse for herself. After taking a breath, she said, &quot;I would like to be return safely to my home in Mankato within a couple of day.&quot; Nothing ventured, nothing gained. She could only hope for the best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T16:59:06-08:00","id":386848,"title":"","content":"What did Nate want? Well, the answer was easy. He wanted what was his due. And what more could he want? He had already been greedy, and he started to feel like it had been a bad choice. So, he pondered his words, wondering if he really could ask for home : he had an apparent free wish from their Keeper, this could be the chance to win it all. Or...he could waste it, by angering the Master. Jessica's request brought him out of his reverie. This seemed pretty reasonable. And even fool-proof. He could ask for something similar, right? &quot;What I want, oh noble Lord Collector, is to be allowed to leave your realm, with safe passage and a clear path.&quot; He even added a little bow, as a mark of politeness, even if it could be taken as a mockery. Screw him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T22:53:18-08:00","id":391067,"title":"","content":"Max naturally flinched at the Keeper's gaze. His heart raced. Well, more than it had been doing since he'd arrived in this room. The poor little Pig was shaking like a leaf. He had been putting together some sort of plan behind that ridiculous face of his, but those eyes on him just dashed his hopes. That look held such wrath, disgust, and condescension toward him. <i>'And how couldn't he! He's right!'</i> Tears started to well up, even as Jessica and Nate made their requests. <i>'Even with a chance like this, I can barely stand! I <b>am</b> just a stupid, pathetic little p--!'</i><br /> <br /> Max stopped mid-thought. With the rude awakening and surprise court proceedings, he'd forgotten something until that moment. A dream he'd had after his meal. It was a bit fractured, but he remembered the spirit. And it gave him something. The swine swallowed, still shaking. He was tempted to match Jessica and Nate's requests, but... No, that felt too easy. Like a trap. Maybe Max was just paranoid, but he couldn't feel comfortable walking into that. <i>'No... I need something he can't see coming. I've gotta catch him. ... Go big or go home, I guess. Heh,' </i>he thought, without mirth, but with a kind of crazy optimism.<br /> <br /> The Pig's trembling hooves clacked forward on the surface of his platform. &quot;I-I...&quot; he stuttered, keeping his eyes low and head slightly bowed. He snuffled a bit, from the tears. Max hated making that sound. But he made sure he made it loudly, looking as pathetic as he could. &quot;I-I... I-If you w-would allow it... I... I want to... to...&quot; He gulped. &quot;Keeper, I want to r-reset my Contract with you. I-I want to state the new terms myself. A-as though that's what they'd always been. I-If you agree to the new Contract, th-then that'll be that. A-Anyone with t-terms like th-the old ones can switch. P-Please, I...&quot; With a squeal of a sob, Max felt the tears fall and dabbed at his face with a sleeve. &quot;I-I swear it'll say... say th-that you really own me. C-Completely. Heart and... s-soul.&quot; He gave another snuffle, the very picture of pathetic. &quot;I... I just want this to stop. B-But I can ask f-for something else, instead...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T05:03:08-08:00","id":392507,"title":"","content":"The Keeper listens, grinning to himself. After each one of the Ox and Goat had made their request, the creature nods, aproving. Meanwhile the Secretary is lost in a frenzy of scribling in the ever so long Scroll.<br /> <br /> When the pig finally makes his declaration, the Secretary stops abrutly, and the inhuman face of the Keeper twist in... confusion? The two Fae looked at each other for a brief moment and after the Keeper nods to the Secretary this one retakes his notes, putting everything said to paper.<br /> <br /> &quot;You want to, and I quote: <i>To return safely to your home in Mankato within a couple of days</i>. Is that correct, my lovable Ox?&quot;-the keeper's attempt at niceness results even more akward and disturbing than its displays of anger.<br /> <br /> &quot;... aaaand, you want to <i>be allowed to leave my realm, with a safe passage and a clear path</i>, uh?&quot;-the Keeper repeats, like making a list-&quot;That can certainly be worked out, my dear, dear Goat&quot;-it tries to asure you with a wide smile that splits its face in two.<br /> <br /> &quot;And you...&quot;-his forced smile dwindles for a second-&quot;You, my beloved Pig&quot;-says recovering what passes for composure for that creature-&quot;You want to re-set the terms of our original Contract, and not only that but made it retroactive! What ingenuity, don't you think, my Secretary?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I am amazed beyond belief, oh Gracious and Incomparable Lord Collector&quot;-he answered in his trademarked monotonous tone.<br /> <br /> &quot;And there's even more! He want me to allow any of the pieces of my collection to switch to that, I supose more favorable, Contract if they want to!&quot;-it's smile was widening by the second, soon its head would fall off.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have been taken note of everything, oh Insurmountable and Exquisite Lord Collector, the Pig is the only one that saw fit to offer something in exchange, my Lord&quot;-he tapped twice the Scroll with his quill-&quot;<i>I-I swear it'll say... say th-that you really own me. C-Completely. Heart and... s-soul</i>, where his exact words, my Lord-points out the Secretary using Max's own voice.<br /> <br /> &quot;Fair enough&quot;-says the keeper, its smile disappearing under an expression of profound concentration-&quot;You have managed to intrigue me, Pig, well done. So, may we hear the terms of that new Contract?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T07:38:11-08:00","id":392580,"title":"","content":"Fear ran through Jessica when the scribe said only Max had offered something in return. Perhaps that would make her request fail. She said to the scribe, &quot;Not to interrupt, but I need to make something clear. I am offering something in exchange. Or rather I already have. When I was punished unjustly, I was used to feed any number of the Collector's creatures. During that process, I lost a tattoo that I had. So I would say that I prepaid as it were. The temporary use of my body and my tattoo were what I paid.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  typo 02-04-2015, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-04T17:11:58-08:00","id":393200,"title":"","content":"Nate didn't answer to the Keeper. He couldn't, even if he wanted too, as he was frozen in fear. <i>This is it. I messed up. I'm gonna be a prisonner, tortured for the rest of my life, until I forget who I really am.</i> But Max, this adorable kid, tore nate out of his trance. &quot;Max?! What the fuck are you doing?!&quot; Nate yelled in shock. &quot;You're giving up?! Come on man, not you!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T00:32:13-08:00","id":393491,"title":"","content":"Max cringed at the sound of his voice from the Secretary's lips. It was unexpected and Max, just like so many people, hated hearing the way he sounded. Well, probably not 'just like:' most people don't have to hear themselves sobbing, with hints of grunt, snort, and squeal underlying every bit of it. That and the stutter brought him a fact to focus on, one that was bizarrely petty, given the gravity of his situation. <i>'Oh no... I... It's like I'm Porky Pig...'</i><br /> <br /> But that thought was quickly forgotten. The unpleasantness felt like a day at the beach after what came next. Max felt his stomach knot with shame as Nate shouted at him. He didn't think the poor Goat could <i>sound</i> more horrified. Or more disappointed. <i>'Nate... No, I. I have to. I have to...' </i>For a few moments, Max held his breath, and then gave a few sobs, human and animal vocal chords mingling. He turned his head toward Nate, but couldn't meet his eyes. &quot;N-Nate... I... I'm sorry. I'm s-so sorry, but...&quot; Another snuffle. &quot;I have to. Th-This is the only way. I-I-I mean...&quot;<br /> <br /> The Pig took a breath, tears falling from his eyes. And a bit of anger came out with them in his words, anger at the whole desperate situation. &quot;Y-You saw it in his face when y-you and J-Jessica asked. He's th-thinking about how to give you wh-what you asked for, but n-not what you want! Y-You know that! And he'll do it! H-He's pr-probably been at this l-longer than we've been alive, all of us p-put t-together!&quot; Max swept his hand around the other assembled animals. &quot;Y-You'd have to be stupid to tr-try to get one over on him!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Y-You two are in trouble! Big trouble. Just... Just admit it. A-A-And...&quot; The anger had been subsiding, but left him completely. &quot;... And you're both better than me.&quot; He'd meant everything he said, but that last bit was especially heavy with truth, bitter twist at the end. It hung there for a bit. &quot;If you're stuck, then... Wh-What else is there for a... a worthless pig like me to try? I n-need to try to m-make him happy... A-And if the Keeper takes my terms, then... Th-That's at least <i>something</i> I could finally do for you. Y-You'd get a choice. I-if you don't like what he gives, you could s-switch. M-Maybe he'll even show m-mercy...?&quot; Max had believed most of what he was saying. The thought of the Keeper showing mercy was not among it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Just... P-Please don't hate me for this. And... And...&quot; The Pig trembled. &quot;I-I don't know if I'll still b-be me after, so... Th-Thank you. For being my friends.&quot; And then he dipped into his breathing exercises to get more of a grip, and tried to put those friends out of his thoughts.<br /> <br /> Max looked up hesitantly, still not daring to meet the Keeper's eyes. &quot;I-I-I'm s-so s-sorry for the w-wait. ... M-Master.&quot; There was that nauseous feeling again. &quot;Uh. Right. M-My terms.&quot; He took another deep breath. He tried to clear his thoughts again; he needed all that emotion out. This was going to be hard enough as it was. &quot;I-It's... Just like you said. A-Anyone with a C-Contract like us can sw-switch to the new terms if th-they want. And it's retroactive. A-A-And...&quot; Another breath. &quot;Yes. If you meet the terms, y-you'll own me, j-just like I said. I-If you agree to the n-new terms altogether. So...&quot; The little pig dabbed at his eyes with his sleeve again. Unfortunately, the dried mud on his face was by now wet with tears, and smudged terribly, making him look even more pathetic. A blush was evident, even through it.<br /> <br /> So, with one last breath, Max cast a glance up at the little pig statue near the Keeper that started all this. He took a few shaking, clopping steps toward the center of the court and plunged in. &quot;The new terms. It's still the first person to buy a given figurine as in the old terms. In this case, it's me, so I'll just keep referring to me. So, when you sold it to me, you... W-Well, it's a sale: you agreed it c-couldn't be yours anymore, and, and that sole ownership would be mine. 'cause... Th-That's how sales work.&quot; He coughed into his awkward flailing. &quot;A-Anyway. At the same time... You...&quot; A gulp. &quot;Instead of getting permission to bring me here and change me, you... You took ownership of me, m-my heart, my soul, my... my everything, in the broadest sense, and not a bit less. Th-The kind of ownership that would let you do all you've done to me, and... anything else.&quot; The Pig fell silent, feeling very ill, and hoping he hadn't just made a huge mistake. &quot;... That's all,&quot; he said, mouth dry. &quot;If all that's true, the Contract holds.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I-If th-that meets with y-your satisfaction, M-M-Master.&quot; Max gave an awkward bow, and waited nervously to hear the response. It would decide how this was all going to shake out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T19:53:58-08:00","id":395776,"title":"","content":"Nate didn't know what was going in his mind, it was such a flurry of emotions. Anger, shock, anguish, relief... A coherent sentence barely escaped his lips : &quot;No...no, you can't be doing this, no...&quot;, and like some twisted madness mantra, the goat repeated this for a few minutes, as if to convince himself. But the worst part of it? <i>He's right... You screwed up. And you're taking him down with it.</i> The pain he felt when hit by the arrow was nothing compared to this : Max had been like a little brother to him, and he only realized just now. &quot;Screw you, Max...&quot;, the Goat said quietly, not daring to look the Pig in the eyes. &quot;I'm no better than you. Don't you even dare thinking that,&quot; he continued, almost spitting the words in disgust. He wasn't angry against the little piece of pork, but mad with himself.<br /> <br /> See, a good man would have protested against a friend's sacrifice. Nate should have begged the Keeper to take him, instead of Max. He should have taken the burden of his mistakes, and sacrificing his fate for his inmates' freedom. He should have done all of that, and he knew it.<br /> <br /> But he couldn't. He couldn't speak up, protest or beg. He didn't have the will to move and physically stop Max from speaking further. The opportunity for freedom was just too good, the chance to get back to the real world... Nate couldn't pass it up, even if it meant condemning the kid to a lifetime of sloth and filth in the mud. The offer was still too good to turn away, and Nate<i> hated</i> himself for it. <i>This fucking pride.</i><br /> <br /> The Goat was even aware that this act would be a terrible burden to carry. To know that he would be saved because of an act of cowardice that doomed his only friend... How could he live with that? But even that realization didn't give him enough strength to protest. So instead, he got back to his mantra, adding some insults in the mix, directed to Max (for playing the noble hero) or to himself (for not being one).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T05:59:32-08:00","id":401792,"title":"","content":"&quot;Please, wait for your turn to speak, thank you&quot;- the Secretary admonished Nate dispassionately. -&quot;If your Incomparable Majesty the Lord Collector has no further comments to make on the compensations demanded, we can proceed&quot;- he said making the last notes.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Perfect, perfect!&quot;- clapped the Keeper. It got up from its throne and discarded his playfuness for a short while entoning its oath seriously-&quot;Let's it be heard by all those present, and with the Wyrd, my Secretary and all the members of the Zodiac as my witnesses that I, the Lord Collector, agree to give the Ox, Pig and Goat what they demanded... provided they manage to cross my Garden!&quot;.<br /> <br /> And with that it claps its long nailed hands again: once, twice, three times and the Pig, Ox and Goat dissapear in a puf of smoke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T15:21:32-08:00","id":407062,"title":"","content":"*puf!*<br /> <br /> Nate found himself suddenly stranded in front of the biggest hedge labyrinth he had ever saw. The entrance was marked by a stone arc with a symbol carved on the top front stone, he recognized it as the symbol of Aries from the horoscopes of the newspaper.<br /> <br /> The sound of trembling earth took him out of his stupor as the remnants of the cloud of smoke dissipated, revealing a great figure standing between him and the entrance to the garden-labyrinth. The creature seemed like a giant, better fit version of Nate himself: furry goat legs under a muscled human torso, all topped with a horned head with the face of an angry man. The most notorious difference besides the face, obviously, was how pale the figure was, alabaster skin covered by snow-white fur.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Who are you and what brings you to the House of Aries?&quot;-the creature remarks his question trampling the ground with its enourmous hooves, causing the earth to tremble again.<br /> <hr /><br /> *puf!*<br /> <br /> Jessicca saw with surprise how the whole hall and everybody inside disappeared in a cloud of smoke around her. As the smoke settles on the ground, she manages to make out the shape of an enormous stone archway leading inside what appears to be one of those hedge-mazes she saw in some period films. The archway has a single symbol carved in the most prominent spot, a round circle with a pair of horns that she recognizes as the zodiac sign of Taurus.<br /> <br /> Having nowhere to go but inside, she enters. Is no long after she had taken a couple of turns that she hears a known harsh voice behind her:<br /> <br /> -&quot;Now you are in my place and you'd better run. An eye for and eye, so the saying goes...&quot;<br /> <hr /><br /> *puf!*<br /> <br /> Max almost dropped all his remaining fruits when he was rather unceremoniously teleported again by the Keeper. The smoke was dense and smelled sickly sweet, making him cough for a long while until it got away in the wind. It seemed he was on the open again.<br /> <br /> Before him, an archway, before the archway, Libra.<br /> <br /> The stone structure had not one, but two openings, each of them leading in oposite directions as far as Max could see behind the cold and serious figure of the zodiac of justice.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Choose now, and choose wisely, Max of the Pig, Max of the Boar. Choose your Destiny and accept your Fate&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T18:59:31-08:00","id":407222,"title":"","content":"Nate had raised his arms in defense when the smoke engulfed him, crying in surprise. And he yelped once again when he saw Aries. <i>Of course. Of course it's not a cute chick. What were the odds!</i> His eyes wandered on his opponent's muscles, and he gulped, not only in fear, but also... in jealousy? <i>I wish the Keeper had reshaped me like him... No, wait. Scratch that. I shouldn't be thinking like this... </i>The big guy was guarding the archway. There was absolutely no way Nate could pass him by force, or even by speed. <br /> <br /> &quot;Hi there, fellow Zodiac. I am...&quot; Nate hesitated. Better to sound compliant. &quot;I am the Goat, one of our Master's latest additions. I'm so glad to finally meet you, you know!&quot; He said, flashing a big grin. &quot;Maybe it's because of our forms, but I really think we could be friends. Maybe even join the same flock!&quot; he added despite himself. <i>Okay, that was... a weird sentence to say.</i> &quot;But first, our Master has me playing a game. See, this is a race. I must cross his garden, and apparently, well, your nice house is supposed to be my entrance. So, can I pass, my friend?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 02-16-2015, 10:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T21:34:56-08:00","id":407379,"title":"","content":"Hard as his words to Nate had been to say, Max felt like he'd been punched in the gut by Nate's reaction. A hopeless and desperate anger, but one turned inward, with words of self-loathing. Max stared a few moments. He genuinely didn't think he could have that kind of impact on anyone. He bit his tongue to keep from offering a reassuring word or two. <i>'Be tougher than that. It's not for much longer.'</i> The Pig choked out another mostly animal sob, and turned his snout toward the ground, waiting for the &quot;judge's&quot; decree. When it came, it brought a moment's relief. The terms were accepted: one way or another, he'd be able to give his gambit a try right away. Or... maybe, if he managed a maze. &quot;Wait, wh--&quot;<br /> <br /> *puff*<br /> <br /> &quot;--at?&quot; Max coughed into the smoke. He couldn't see a thing. He also hadn't realized how much he'd come to rely on his snout; with that sickly sweet smell, he really did feel blind for a bit. <i>'Ohhh, not good...'</i> After a few tense moments, it parted, and he gave a gasp of a squeal when he made out a sight -- and scent -- he'd have sooner done without. He reflexively took one step back, slipping into a defensive stance. Mostly, anyway: one hand went to the floppy ear she'd grabbed earlier. Whatever happened, this little piggy wasn't getting taken unawares a second time.<br /> <br /> At least, that was the plan. Libra's words left him a little off-balance. Trying to ignore how plain the puzzlement must have been on his face, Max tried to think it through. He turned his head between the left gate and the right. Without meaning to, he took a few speculative sniffs from each direction. While this unthinking animal behavior was worrisome, he'd at least grant it a point: he wanted to know more before he decided. So, in addition to whatever news his nose brought him, the little oinker decided to also try a more human method. &quot;Um... I... I don't suppose you could tell me more about what each choice means?&quot; Max thought fast, and, recalling the title Libra had given, he added, &quot;I-I mean... P-Probably works out better for justice if I know my rights, a-and the laws here, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-16T08:49:44-08:00","id":407810,"title":"","content":"Jessica swore when she heard the minotaur's voice again. She doubted that she could not outrun the beast. Last time, the minotaur had charged her. This time, hoping to gain the element of surprise, she charged the minotaur. The seven foot monster lowered his head, hoping to impale the charging Jessica on his horns. Jessica skidded to a stop. As she did, she side kicked the minotaur in the nose. Bellowing in pain and showering Jessica with vile threats, the monster tumbled backwards into the leafy walls of the maze. His eyes blazing with fury, the minotaur rose up.<br /> <br /> Knowing that she could never win anything like a fair fight, Jessica kicked the incoming minotaur in the groin absolutely as hard as she could. This brought the minotaur to his knees. Knowing that price of failure would be death after having been subjected to something even worse, the ox woman kicked the Minotaur in the head as hard as she could. When the minotaur fell, Jessica continued to offer kicks, as hard and fast as she could. She felt sick to her stomach, but she knew she had to try to kill the minotaur. Derek would not be around to save her this time. This time, she had to save herself.<br /> <br /> Tears running down her face, Jessica pressed her attack, seeking to finish the grim task she had set for herself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  Word Flow 02-16-2015, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T04:16:26-08:00","id":409880,"title":"","content":"&quot;She is breaking my collection!!!!&quot;- the Keeper complained looking the brutal beating up Jessica was providing Taurus.<br /> <br /> The Collector, the Secretary and the remaining members of the Chinese Zodiac (with the notorious absence of the Horse) where standing in circle around a big scrying pond that depicted the whereabouts of each of the three participants in the Keeper's challenge. Derek the monkey was clapping like crazy with both sets of hands at the Ox reaction. He was pleased she could handle that bull(y) on her own.<br /> <br /> &quot;So it seems, oh Magnificient and Incomparable Lord Collector&quot;- the Secretary nodded, dispassionetly.<br /> <br /> The skull of the bull-man was thick and hard, but it found a perfect match on the strong-muscled legs and hooves of Jessica's new form. Blow after blow, the bone dome of Taurus' head started to chip and crack with a disgusting crunching sound, before starting to cede and collapase into itself. Finally, Taurus stoped making any sound or move, lying still, a bloody mess for a head.<br /> <br /> Jessica didn't wait more and continued to advance through the maze at good pace, following the sinuous path before her. After many turns, some of them apparently making her go back, she finally arrived at an intersection.<br /> <br /> The path here divided in two. To the left was a rather open path, the hedge leaving room to patches of very tall grass, some green, some dried by the sun. To the left, a thorny path looking an inch too narrow, with flowers of vivid colors (red, blue, yellow, purple, pink) blooming among the pointy and sharp spines. <hr /><br /> &quot;Let's see what the Pig is up to&quot;- said the Keeper with a sigh, pasing its hand over the pond. The waters weaved and trembled, the image they depicted changing a little more with each motion.<br /> <br /> Max was before Libra, sttutering a question.<br /> <br /> &quot;You have to choose who you are and who you want to be, Max of the Pig, Max of the Boar...&quot;- Libra answers, extending each of her arms to one of the doors remarking each of the titles, making her look more like a balance.-&quot;...and you must accept the consequences of your choice, same as all of us here&quot;. It may be the tension of the moment but Max almost noticed a sad tone in Libra's voice in that last remark.<br /> <br /> &quot;Choose&quot;- she adds after a long silence, an offering, not an order. <hr /><br /> &quot;Booooooring!&quot;- complains the Keeper, the emotional intensity of the situation completely lost to it.-&quot;Ah, the Goat, the Goat has never failed to amuse me&quot;- it remembers, grinning.<br /> <br /> The waters change once more, showing two horned figures confronting one another.<br /> <br /> &quot;Friends? Hahahahahaha!&quot;- Aries' laughter is a low bass like the rolling of rocks, it kind of reminded Nate his fight with that sentient mountain. -&quot;You <i>do</i> are funny, I now see why the Master wants to keep you. How could you ever compare to me? Aries! First among the Zodiac!&quot;<br /> <br /> He calms down and regains his composure.<br /> <br /> &quot;A race you say? Yes, maybe, but not one of speed but endurance. No need to hurry, is there, little Goat?&quot;<br /> <br /> Aries starts to circle around Nate at a slow, steady pace taking his measure.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, why are you so eager to reach the end of your journey, what do you think will be waiting for you at the other side of this garden? You have already sold yourself to the Master, that I can see. You and I are more kin that you would imagine. You picture it will just forget about it and let you go? Just like that?&quot;<br /> <br /> Aries laughter and trampling shook the earth again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 02-18-2015, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T05:18:19-08:00","id":409934,"title":"","content":"<i>Alright, he didn't attack me on sight, so... I guess it's a good thing.</i> Nate crouched down just a bit to keep his footing (his hoofing?) through the trampling. Apparently, Aries was also the boasting sort : trying to outboast him would only lead to a brutal beating, Nate was sure of this. Fortunately, he didn't look that bright. &quot;Hey, now now Aries, I never said I was your equal. I mean, look at the both of us, you're so much stronger than me! Honestly, I'm even a bit jealous, but I'm sure the Master had his reasons.&quot; Suddenly, Nate realized something : this wasn't even a lie. Lies had made his life so easy, denying the truth and getting people to do his bidding. He used to picture himself as a manipulator.<br /> <br /> That's why he answered Aries' own laughter by another laugh, incredulous and nervous. The Goliath's words were only underlining his own folly. &quot;Fuck if I know, man!&quot; Nate had to take a break, laughing too much to form a coherent sentence. &quot;I've been tricked! Of course I have, I know that! The Master must be... I don't know, centuries older than me... Maybe he's immortal. Maybe he's a god or something, who am I to know?!&quot;Again, laughter. &quot;You're right, I'm no different than you... I'm just a dumb fucking Beast...&quot;<br /> <br /> A sad smile formed across the Goat's face, as he sat on a nearby rock. Going back home was hopeless. Aries certainly looked happy, and Pisces... well, they didn't look too miserable. If that was his fate, that was as good as any. Although... back at the trial, the Pig seemed to have an idea. Of course, the Goat knew better, and it would only lead to disappointment. But... his life was already miserable : trying one last mean of escape couldn't hurt. And if he failed, he would submit for good, and take his rightful place in the Zodiac. Yeah, that sounded right and comforting. <br /> <br /> The Goat was still smiling at Aries. &quot;Thanks. You made me realize that... well, it hurts to say, but I'm just a idiot. I've struggled for far too long. If the Master wants it, maybe we'll talk again sometimes, I really think we can be friends.&quot; A chuckle escaped his lips. &quot;God, this is so sappy. Forget this. Hey, maybe I'll get to throw parties for everyone here : I have wine, cute females and music. I hope you'll come.&quot; After a resigned sigh, he added : &quot;But if I want to do that, I'll still need to cross the maze. Please, I just want to get this over with, let me pass through, so I can get to the end and then go back to the Ranch.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":".  Minor mistakes 02-18-2015, 10:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T09:21:14-08:00","id":410168,"title":"","content":"As she pondered which way to go, Jessica felt herself become sick. She found herself shocked by what she had done. Her hooves, her entire body was splattered with blood. She had purposely taken a life, albeit in self-defense. She was a murderess. After some reflection on this, Jessica set off into the narrower, flower-adorned path. She did not trust a path in this place that looked too easy.<br /> <br /> Before she went very far, Jessica found herself swarmed by insects of all descriptions. The vermin, colorful and diverse, seemed drawn by the minotaur's blood. All over her body she felt the insects landing and tasting the blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T18:10:02-08:00","id":414682,"title":"","content":"Max gulped, but nodded to Libra. He trusted she had told him all she could. &quot;I-I see. Thank you.&quot; He had a hunch about what each might mean, and an inclination picked out. But he was reluctant: it meant choosing and declaring himself to be <i>that</i> of all things. Max shuddered. Besides, he might well be wrong. After all, it was being wrong about what buying that little pig meant that had gotten him into this. To say nothing of what it would mean for the Keeper to formally accept his proposal. Thoughts of that did help a little; if he was right about the terms, this choice might not matter at all, and if he was wrong... well, Max could hardly be any worse off.<br /> <br /> <i>'Nothing ventured, nothing gained, I guess... Okay. Just... one more sniff.'</i> He'd gotten nothing but more of the sweet-smelling mist before, it had slowly dissipated as he'd mulled things over. Now his snout picked up rather distinct smells and odors from each direction. With a few more snuffles to take their measure, he felt he understood -- or at least felt his subjective understanding crystallize. More than that, whether through some nature of the pathways, some subtle magic of Libra's, or simply his keen sense of smell, Max beheld visions of the futures down each path.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">To the left, Max of the Pig. It was nearly overpowering: the stench of an animal that may have never left its muddy sty nor known a bath. A great hog, at least thrice Max's size -- not counting the layers of mud to cake on over years of wallowing. The creature was content to laze and sleep in his mire, and to gorge himself even fatter on the unmentionable substance in his trough. In terms of size and contents, said trough made the one Max had eaten out of earlier seem like a thimble of fine wine.</div> <br /> The little pig in his robe found it all repulsive, even as it seemed so alluring; he suddenly noticed how his mouth had watered at the &quot;meal,&quot; and how his skin itched for a dip in that soothing mud. Who needed complexity? He could be happy and content with so little... And there was so little he'd have to change... He'd taken two steps before he caught himself with a gasp that was half-squeal. He turned his head sharply, hoping whatever awaited him to the right would at least balance it.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">To the right, Max of the Boar. This, too, nearly overpowered: the stench of sweat and musk, but mingled with incense and perfume from other bodies. A boar in the shape of a grown man, brown bristles coating a well-muscled and exceptionally athletic build, with a large and wicked set of tusks. The boar-man dressed in loose robes of exquisite threading, and sat in a grand palace at the head of a golden table. The table offered a meal of tantalizing food, a rich meal shared with persons of power and prestige, though clearly less than the boar's. Beautiful women of every exotic description attended upon him, perhaps finding his company pay enough. The wealth, the respect, the affections -- the boar had earned it all through his power and skill alone.</div> <br /> Max drank in the heady smell of power. He found that he <i>wanted</i> it. How could he have ever thought of contenting himself with slop and a small sty? No, no, the boar? <i>That</i> was who he wanted to be. The little piglet could scarcely see a bristle of his weak, pathetic self in that future. Nothing to fear from anyone, nothing but the finest for him, and nothing but the desire to be or to be with him for all others. Max gave a grin, barely visible tusks growing more prominent. Bristles browned with every eager step he took. <i>'Yeah... Just like back at the pond. The boar was so </i><i><b>powerful</b>! And that was just a taste! It could be like that all the time. <b>I</b> could be that all the time! Nate was right, I could...!'</i><br /> <br /> The Pig stopped suddenly, tusks and bristles receding in their growth, as the memory of hurting Nate broke the spell. And the fury and rage he felt in doing it. With a sniffle, the vision continued, with an acrid scent and something like iron.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">One of the boar-king's attendants tried to feed him a grape, but was caught unawares when he turned his head suddenly. She cut herself on his tusks, and some of her blood spilled onto his robes. His eyes glinted in fury at her and he easily broke her unbloodied arm. This brutality earned gasps or screams from all assembled, including an outraged shout from a lordling across the table. After very little angry discourse, the boar-king cleared the table in a leap, swiping an ugly gash into the guest as he went, before flinging the young man roughly to the ground. Before the plates, platters, and chairs he had scattered settled down, the poor youth was very still. All others in attendance now began shouting protest all at once, drawing their weapons. The boar silenced them with a great bellow that shook the room. They were cowed, but no, not good enough. Particularly as one of his favored art pieces fell from where it rested and shattered. With another cry of fury at what they had made him do, the boar-king hefted up the great table itself and broke it in the course of breaking everyone in the room. Servants and soldiers had come at the commotion, gawked at the scene, and then attacked the Boar. Why wouldn't they? There was nothing of the lord of the palace in him.<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Hours later, the Boar stood on a hilltop, composing himself. He was covered in wounds that would have instantly felled lesser creatures, as the flaming and crumbling shambles of his estate continued their collapse in the distance behind him. The blood-soaked Boar gave it a contemptible snort. He walked off with the easy grace of one who has built and destroyed a life of splendor for himself many times, with no aim to change.</div> <br /> Max felt quite sick and shaken. Just a few more steps would have brought him through to the path of the Boar. Had his wits been more about him, perhaps he might have reasoned his way around it. Perhaps he might have cleverly thought up some manner of third option. All he knew was that a choice between the two destinies was no choice for him at all. Max gave Libra a nod, and walked past her, through into the path of the Pig.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T04:20:39-08:00","id":420042,"title":"","content":"The path Max decided to walk started pretty normal, almost suspiciously so. Walls and an arched ceiling carefully trimmed from a wild hedge, floor of dark, pressed earth.<br /> <br /> It was quite beatiful in its simplicity and its openess made it very comfortable to walk trough... at first.<br /> <br /> Max couldn't tell at wich time the earth he walked on started to get progresively wet, then outright muddy, and finally just short of becoming foul-smelling quicksand. The wide passage provided by the hedge archway also became more and more narrow with each step and the ceiling seemed to close on him, like trying to crush him under.<br /> <br /> He found himself forced to crouch slightly to be able to advance until he had no choice than to get on all fours and walk like that on the mud. Part of him didn't find this as humiliating and inconvenient as he probably should.<br /> <br /> As with the transformation of the passage, the progressive and subtle aceleration of his advancement went almost unoticed until too late. It seemed the path had turned into a slope and Max couldn't avoid to slide down on that slippery mud, faster and faster and faster and...<br /> <br /> Max looked with horror at the edge he was unavoidably aproaching at insane speed and growled in horror.<br /> <br /> A figure, barely a silouette cut against the open end of the path, cut his slide short. He found himself on a gargantuan open clearing, a sort of muddy hole several stories deep occupying almost the whole space save for a small and too thin cornice around it. Max and the figure he had just run over where at oposite sides of the opening of the tunnel he had enter that place through, doing their best to not slip into that muddy abyss. Several other such openings (and so, tunnels, he thought) where disposed around the cornice of the clearing. On the bottom of the mud pit, the Pig from his vision.<br /> <br /> Something that his vision had lacked, Max thought as a shiver went down his spine, was perspective. In his vision the hog already seemed big and fat, but this creature was the size of a great building. From time to time, things and creatures fell through some of those other tunnels into the pit, where the eager open muzzle of the hog awaited. Always hungry, never stoping eating, the house-sized teeth of the giant pig crunched vegetables, wood, flesh and bone alike, gorging in his disgusting feast.<br /> <br /> -Collector almighty, dude! That could've been me! - said the figure next to Max.<br /> <br /> Now that he got to see it?, him? he seemed like what Max could only describe as a goblin. Long nose and ears, big round amber eyes, small and skinny, his skin a mutted green color.<br /> <br /> -I'm talkin' to you, man! -the goblin shouted to Max, annoyed -At least you could apologize or sumthin' ya know? &quot;<i>Sorry for almost turning you into pig's food, Summernickel!</i>&quot; would've been nuff'.<br /> <hr /><br /> It took a while for Jessica to notice her growing weakness.<br /> <br /> As she forced his passing through the thorny path she didn't realize that the blood she was covered in had stoped being Taurus' a long while ago. The bugs did a great job at drinking and laping it with their miriad of different-shaped proboscides, tongues, trunks and suckers, yet there was always more. The thorns were literally killing her by a thousand cuts, each step opening a new dozen minor wounds that in themselves wouldn't be life threatening, but they were quickly adding up.<br /> <br /> She felt her forces leaving her, the strength that had fell Taurus but a shade of its former glory. Even her thoughts were in shambles, her sight muddy and unfocused and she was soooo tired, soooo tired...<br /> <br /> She fell to the ground on her face, the trembling sound frightening the bugs sending them flying away in all directions. She had somehow reach the end of the hedge.<br /> <br /> Jessica found herself in a great round clearing. It was open, no ceiling covering the place so she could see the strange sky of the Keeper's realm, but she could see no other exit but the path she went through, but she couldn't see much anyway, her vision was permanently blurred by blood loss.<br /> <br /> In the middle of the clearing stood a great closed flower. Its shape was alien and beatiful, its purples, reds, yellows, blues and pinks were striking. The smell, sweet as happy memories.<br /> <br /> It seemed as if the flower realized Jessica was admiring it, because it bloomed and opened as if in response. Inside she could see a familiar figure she thought she could see never again, there was her boyfriend, calling her with open arms, she did it! She actually did beat the maze and she could reap her reward!<br /> <br /> She was so happy.<br /> <hr /><br /> -I'll do more than that, I will go with you.-Nate's hysterical laugh gave pass to dibelief -What? Don't look at me like that, as I say there's no hurry. -Aries laughed.<br /> <br /> He made a mock bowing still grinning and invited Nate to enter through the archway.<br /> <br /> -So, tell me, <i>genius</i>, how did you get into this, uh?- he asked Nate, walking behind him. -Maybe as you will remain here for eternity we could get to know each other. You <i>do</i> are a mess -Nate didn't like one little bit how Aries managed to enfatize key words to hurt and bring him down, he sounded just like the Keeper. Was that his fate? Was that what future had him in reserve? To became a puppet and mouthpiece of that bastard? -But then again, so where others the first time they got here- continued Aries.<br /> <br /> -Let's do this, <i>Goat</i>- there was that tone again...-I'll teach you a few things and you don't make me look bad in front of the Keeper, ok? But first I want to know things about you. What do you do well besides being pathetically funny? Are the rest of the Chinesse Zodiac.... <i>like you</i>?- he made a derisive gesture signalling all of him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T05:12:07-08:00","id":420061,"title":"","content":"It was a nice change of pace. It was the first time Nate could freely talk to one of the Western Zodiac : Leo had been a jackass, and Pisces were too busy splashing people around. Sure, Aries was way too condescending, but his presence was reassuring in this labyrinth : at least, if they were to encounter danger, Nate could count on the big guy's muscles. He figured that the big Ram was behaving this way because of his form, maybe the Keeper shaped him like that. He mentally shrugged : <i>I'll find out soon enough, when I'll submit later.</i> &quot;Thanks. Trust me, I've learned my lesson, I'll just play my part from now on,&quot; the Goat confirmed with a nod. &quot;I&quot;m a pretty badass musician : the Master gave me an instrument, and I guess he'll order me to distract him from time to time. Other than that... Hmm... Well, I'm the best party thrower ever,&quot; he added. He sounded quite sure of that : seems the illusions from the vineyard had stuck to him.<br /> <br /> He winced and sighed at Aries' last question. The big guy was right to make fun of him, the Goat looked so tiny and weak next to him. &quot;Yeah, I guess. They're still adjusting, I haven't really met most of them, though, and a few think they can still escape. The Snake, the Oxen, and maybe a few others. Man, you should see the Rooster, he looks so fucking ridiculous. I can't believe he hasn't been eaten by the Tiger yet... The Pig sounds like he has given up too, which is good, because he's a good kid, and I don't want him to get hurt because he's disobeying the Master.&quot; The Goat smiled sadly. He truly hoped that the P...Max would soon see the light. Sure, he would certainly have one last idea to escape, and the Goat would indulge him, but they couldn't keep that hopeless game forever. &quot;Watch out for the Oxen by the way, she's brutal. But she did seduce Leo for power, so maybe she will adjust in time.&quot; The Goat rubbed his horns uncomfortably. Of course, they were so small compared to Aries', but still, their presence reassured him. Hopefully, one day, he'll have Aries' confidence and might, if the Master wants it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey, you mind if I ask you some questions too? What do you do all day, usually? You can't just be standing in this house, right? We met Leo and Pisces outside the Ranch, so I'm guessing you're left to wander the realm? Because if that's my fate, that sounds... alright.&quot; He shrugged, scratching his scruffy beard. &quot;And what are you going to teach me? More Contracts?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T07:39:28-08:00","id":420154,"title":"","content":"With what remained of her strength, Jessica made her way to Curtis. The two kissed. Trying not to think of Leo and what had happened, Jessica kissed her boyfriend again. Curtis returned the kiss, and one thing led to another. Some measure of Jessica's exhaustion left her as she made love in the shade of the strange flower. After she and Curtis had finished, she felt herself drifting off to sleep. Just before her awareness slipped away, she remembered that she was trying to reach Mankato, not Curtis. She had won nothing; instead, Curtis had lost his freedom.<br /> <br /> Jessica fell asleep before she could reflect any further on this terrible revelation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-28T11:39:37-08:00","id":423147,"title":"","content":"Max panted, eyes having trouble focusing on one thing for a moment. His heart threatened to tear a hole through his chest, but he finally got under control enough to speak. &quot;What is that!? How could...? It almost...!&quot; Still shaking, but gradually getting a grip, he shook his head and turned his eyes back from the pig to the goblin surprise-rescuer. &quot;I-I'm sorry. Th-Thank you for the save. S-Summernickel?&quot; The pig gave a shaky incline of his head in appreciation. &quot;Just a little... o-out of sorts.&quot; His eyes began drifting back toward the gargantuan swine, but he jolted them back. &quot;W-What with the almost... d-dying,&quot; he finished lamely. Max gave a worried grunt with no words behind it.<br /> <br /> It had indeed been a pretty sudden transition. One moment, he was thankful Nate and Jessica couldn't see him like this, pointedly resisting the temptation to roll around in it a little, and found it worrying how little walking on all-fours worried him -- including an idle, terrifying thought that it sure would work better if his arms and legs were the same length. The next, his hand slipped and he almost went down the rest of the world's most harrowing mudslide. The sound of that awful gorging, crunching, and chewing from below had been drowned out only by his terrified squealing, until he hit a muted green obstacle.<br /> <br /> Clutching desperately at the wall, and never more aware of the tactile information his new hooves weren't giving him, Max tried to keep steady. &quot;Really, thank you. But... Where is this? How do we get out?&quot; When he thought he had as decent a grip as he could expect, he tried to take a look around the new environment, mostly centered on the other openings (<i>'Not out through those... They're like little mudfalls.'</i>) and anything that lay above. As he pressed his belly against the wall, the piglet occasionally stole glances down below. Still eager for information, Max's snout worked the air, much as it brought him little other than the overpowering, nauseating (<i>'And unreasonably appetizing...'</i>) odors from below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T07:40:30-07:00","id":432617,"title":"","content":"-How do <i>we</i> get out?- Summernickel asked puzzled -I didn't realize <i>we</i> were a <i>we</i> already, little piglet. Summernickel doesn't even know yer name! I was trying to get trough that tunnel, but it seems is as muddy as the others.- he said gesturing towards the hole Max had appeared through.<br /> <br /> The goblin scratched his head and seemed to try to think really hard, wich made his pitiful face contort as in performing a great effort.<br /> <br /> -Uh- he sighted- Maybe the little piglet can help Summernickel if Summernickel helps the little piglet, yes? -he finally saids, hopeful. -Summernickel doesn't want to get back trought the thorns alone.<br /> <br /> He looks around, nervous.<br /> <br /> -So, will the little piglet help good Summernickel? -he smiles, tending Max his little, thin hand.<br /> <hr /><br /> Jessica shifted in his weary sleep. She felt horrible, having cursed Curtis to share her imprisionment. The guilt felt like bile in her mouth, disgusting and bitter. The emotional pain almost physical, as if her skin was melting....<br /> <br /> Jessica woke up to the sound of his body hair sizzling. The flower was slowly closing around her and sweet smelling liquid was starting to fill up the cup-like body of the plant.<br /> The pain of the vegetal acid took her back to her senses, she now remebered her sexual tryst with Curtis without the clouding effect of the flower's hallucinogenic aroma. Knowing that it all had been a product of her drugged mind made her both relieved and scared, she could never be sure of her senses again while in this terrible garden.<br /> <br /> She had, though, more pressing concerns now. If she didn't find a way out of the carnivorous flower she would get digested sooner rather than later...<br /> <hr /><br /> Nate was starting to calm down. Even in his current circumstances, faced with the decision of finally bending to the will of the Keeper or keeping a shred of hope in whatever the Pig had planned, the casual conversation with Aries and the relaxing walk were making wonders to ground him. Hell, it almost felt normal, for a very wacky definition of the term.<br /> <br /> Aries walked by him, not before as a leader or guide, not behind as a threat, <i>besides</i> him almost as a pal. A towering, pale, inhuman pal, but a pal nonetheless. Nate felt Aries on his side, and that granted him a feeling of security that was like a balm on his cracking ego. Thanks to this he could actually enjoy the ride, admiring the alien beauty of the garden, its flowers and small insects of all the colors of the rainbow, and quite more he didn't have names for.<br /> <br /> Before he could get bored, the garden changed once more to show the Goat and Aries previously unseen wonders. Why could anyone want to leave a place like this? The world where tha Goat has come from seemed grey and ugly and cold in comparison.<br /> <br /> *chop* *chop*<br /> <br /> Uh? Nate looked down to his hooves and realized the floor has turned from stone tiles to pressed earth and lately to wet mud. Aries didn't seem to notice, despite his strong steps his hooves didn't seem to sink in the mud as Nate's. Aries remained clean and unblemished even above that muddy floor.<br /> <br /> Nate was not that lucky, getting more and more complicated to walk, his legs getting more and more dirty. In a effort to move, the mud from one of his steps splashed in all directions.<br /> <br /> *splosch*<br /> <br /> A shiver went down Nate's spine even before turning his head to his right and seeing the mess, Aries' alb fur stained by a dash of dark brown mud.<br /> <br /> -You, dirty creature! How do you dare to do this to me! Aries! First of the Zodiac! -He was completely out of his mind. -You want to get soon to the end of your journey? So be it, Goat! -and with that he kicked Nate out through the slimy mud. He started to slide and slide, faster and faster...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T13:55:45-07:00","id":433083,"title":"","content":"A thousand insults came to Nate's mind, but all that came out of his mouth was a choking sound, as the former musician swallowed by accident spoonfuls of mud. <i>How did that happen?</i> The question was soon replaced by <i>Oh shit when is this thing ever gonna end?!</i> It was the worst waterslide ever, Nate didn't have time to reflect on Aries' reaction, he was too busy crawling during his fall, tumbling and hitting his head on the low ceiling. This was going way too fast : each time he tried to find a grip in the walls surrounding the chute, his fingers got scraped against the stone walls.<br /> <br /> But soon, despite the mud that got in his eyes, he finally saw a light at the end of the tunnel. Unfortunately, it came with a gigantic boar-monster. &quot;NOOO! Fuck fuck fuuuuck no! Don't eat me Max!&quot; He didn't even thought there could be another pig in this realm, it was the only thing that made sense to his panicking mind : his buddy had been tricked by the Keeper and transformed into this huge monster. He tried to get on his belly and futilely crawl upward, but soon was thrown in the pit...<br /> <br /> Or not. Finally, his fingers had found something to hold on. Two of the stones forming the cornice was missing, allowing Nate to hang on the lone one that was still there. However, despite his relief this unexpected grip brought him, there was still a huge pit with a gargantuan beast at the bottom. And the torrent of mud was still pouring on Nate, who felt his grip weakening by every second. &quot;HELP!&quot; he yelled, coughing as he got another mouthful of the vile stuff. &quot;Someone please help! ANYBODY!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 03-08-2015, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:16:46-07:00","id":433506,"title":"","content":"With great effort, Jessica crawled out of the hungry flower before it closed completely. Almost mad with pain, she rolled on the grass, hoping to clean off at least some of the burning acid. It took a few minutes, but rolling in the grass seemed to help. Once it did, she got to her feet. Fearing that remaining near the planet would mean death, she set on, heading back into the maze. She was still alive. There was still a chance that she could reach Mankato and home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:50:02-07:00","id":433548,"title":"","content":"&quot;It's Max,&quot; the 'little piglet' explained, after cringing a bit at each utterance of the phrase -- mostly from how accurate it had become. &quot;Please call me Max. S-Sorry for not introducing myself, Summernickel.&quot; Keeping himself steady on the wall was still a tricky endeavor, but getting easier: the mud on his palms had dried enough to be less slick than sticky, and his hooves were in a similar state.<br /> <br /> Max turned his head, spying the goblin's outstretched hand and nervous smile. He felt a relieved smile cross his face, on learning that Summernickel was open to the idea; the swine had worried he'd burned a bridge by following up his bad first impression by being presumptuous. Then again, it was also a sign of how desperate their plight was in there; the disgusting sounds from below served as a constant reminder. Still, Max's experiences had taught him caution before making an agreement, even now. &quot;I... I agree. I'll help you get out of here if you help me. W-We'll work together.&quot; Taking great care, he began reaching his hand toward the goblin's...<br /> <br /> ... but didn't reach it. The Pig's ears rose and flopped at a familiar scream and a cry of his name, and Max pulled back his hand, the better to help him whirl his gaze in that voice's direction. &quot;Nate!?&quot; His eyes widened and his jaw fell open. &quot;Nate!&quot; he half-squealed and half-shouted, hoping to be heard, &quot;H-Hang on!&quot; Max began shimmying along, away from Summernickel, and nearly slipped in his haste. Grunting as he resettled his grip and footing, the little piglet remembered the goblin. He gave the long-eared needle-nosed figure as apologetic a look as his snouted face allowed. &quot;I-I'm sorry.&quot; Max turned back to watching carefully where he was going as he moved along. &quot;W-We'll work on getting out together, but I have to save my friend first.&quot; Max paused in his speech and, much as he felt a little too manipulative, added, &quot;M-Maybe all three of us can f-find a way together.&quot; The Pig continued to thread the long, thin path toward the Goat, calling out, &quot;J-Just a little longer, Nate! I'm coming!&quot; Granted, &quot;Just a little longer,&quot; was overselling his pace. But as long as it helped Nate keep focused, Max would keep up that sort of chatter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 03-08-2015, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:57:30-07:00","id":434107,"title":"","content":"Nate was pretty sure he was just imagining voices now. Besides, they weren't very helpful. <i>Just a little longer?!</i> <i>Easy for you to say!</i> The torrent of mud continued to pour all over Nate, he was pedaling in vain : he tried to find a find a surface for his hooves to fit underneath the mudfall, but each time he even touched the earthy liquid, it only threatened to pull him down to his doom. As much as he didn't want to look down, that was the only way for him to breath and speak without his face being covered in filth. &quot;Please!&quot; He yelled at the top of his lungs. &quot;I'm gonna fall!&quot; His eyes darted around, and he caught a glimpse of a form moving on the corniche, toward him. Something was coming! Maybe one who could help!<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this welcome sight caused the Goat to lose his focus, and soon he lost the grip on his right hand. Yelling in panic, he frantically tried to get it back on the stone, but the current was too strong. <i>Fuck that, I'm not gonna become pig food!</i> What did the voice say? Hang on just a little longer? Yeah, that's what he would do. Nate stopped wriggling, and instead focused all his strength and stamina on his left hand. Finally, those beast muscles were put to good use!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T15:34:54-07:00","id":441891,"title":"","content":"It was rough going, making the crossing, but Max actually thought he was doing quite well. At least until the point his muddy grip slid and a mud-caked hoof did likewise. His arm flailed as his heart jolted into overtime. It's unclear if he would have made it, had he been in the large gap between tunnels. But the Chinese Zodiac says pigs are lucky, and perhaps there's some truth to that: he was near to one of those tunnels, and managed to wrap his arm around it. Max grunted as his head thumped against the wall from the angle, but he maneuvered his wayward hoof back to solid ground... in time for it to be swept away in the mudflow. Another mad scramble amid a strained squeal brought it back just outside the opening.<br /> <br /> The Pig stared, and began to despair. Forget rescuing Nate; at that kind of speed for the mud, there was simply no getting past it. The coursing river was up past his shin! <i>'Hock,'</i> Max recalled at once, from that grisly butcher's diagram. He trembled for reasons aside from being splattered in cold wet earth. <i>'Wait... Earth...'</i> He eyed it speculatively. <i>' Well, worth a shot.'</i> Even in this unnatural place, the mud <i>was</i> natural. And therefore... &quot;W-Wilds. I-I could use some help with all this mud.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max felt the difference immediately, the small of a fresh breeze in his snout, while his body felt as though he'd been sunning himself for much of an hour. Make no mistake, it was still tricky gripping the wall and balancing on such a narrow strip -- on hooves, no less. But he hadn't realized just how badly the stuff had been slicking his efforts or muddling his sense of touch. Hesitant, the piglet tried again for the raging mud current. His hoof went into it as easily as if it were a still pond. Nor did it slip when it reached the solid surface below. It was odd to feel the mud rushing past his bristly leg, but the Pig would take that over being carried off by it any day of the week.<br /> <br /> Pleased, Max turned back to maneuver the rest of him off of the wall and paused on spying Summernickel. The goblin was a ways back, having begun to follow reluctantly -- given the treacherous distance to travail, Max could hardly blame him -- and appeared to have stopped. The long-eared creature stared at his porcine companion. And then grinned, as though an old coin he'd stopped to pick up turned out to be a doubloon. &quot;'Wilds,' the litt-- 'Wilds,' <i>Max</i> says,&quot; Summernickel remarked, correcting himself as he began to make double-time across. &quot;A handy Contract, is that. Perhaps Max might... extend its Clause to ol' Summernickel, too?&quot; The goblin's grin turned ingratiating as he neared the piglet. &quot;Summernickel promises to help Max -- and Max's friend -- escape if they help Summernickel. And that Contract is no small help.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max considered this a moment. <i>'Wilds, would that even work? Can I ask you to spread your protection around?'</i> He felt a mythic presence stir slightly with a dull wind, not elated, but not disagreeing. <i>'Hmm... It </i>would<i> be a help. And... Maybe if I ask him to swear to respect and honor the wilds while you protect him?' </i>The wind swirled again with more enthusiasm, its misgivings much allayed. <i>'And... Can I do the same with Nate?</i>'The wind brushed one hand, and then blew in the Goat's direction; the Pig got the sense that distance was the obstacle. <i>'Okay. All the more reason to hurry.'</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Well?&quot; Summernickel asked, having reached Max. The piglet looked at the outstretched hand, and nodded, adjusting his grip and extending his own, slowly. &quot;Okay. I-If you help us make it through, w-we'll give you some help. J-Just swear to honor and respect the Wilds, and they'll protect you as long as you do.&quot; The two hands clasped, and shook, and Max then felt the warmth and wind from the other side. As well as something else. The promise, perhaps? Regardless, Summernickel seemed pleased. They shared a quick smile, and then Max went back to the matter at hand, traversing the mud. <i>'Kinda pleasant, actually,'</i> he thought of the flow. <i>'Might be nice, later, to just lie back and let it flow over--'</i><br /> &quot;Stop, piglet, stop!&quot; came a screech from behind. Max stopped just in time for a large rock to plow through where he would have been if he hadn't. He gaped, soundless, until he heard the crunch of the rock in the swinish maw below. Summernickel gave him an encouraging tap on the shoulder from behind. Shaken from his daze, Max stammered a, &quot;Th-Th-Thank you,&quot; and hurried across. A little optimism was a good thing, but he made sure to mind his caution as well.<br /> <br /> The rest of the way was much less eventful. A couple of scares, but with some care and the aid of the Wilds, they made much better time, with Max shouting periodic encouragement to Nate. And, at last, they made it. With little preamble, the Pig crossed over to where the Goat dangled and reached down. Even as he did, though, he realized how exhausting his trip had been; he was giving a grunting pant. Summernickel looked to be doing better, but not by much. Even working together, this was going to be trouble. So Max tried a different track. &quot;N-Nate! I... I need you to-- to s-swear to h-honor and resp-pect the Wilds. J-Just trust me, and we'll make it! N-Now!&quot; He forced his weary, muddy arms to grab one of Nate's, while Summernickel did likewise with the other, cursing in a language neither beast knew. They were going to depend on the Goat and that Contract. Or else all three of them probably wouldn't even manage to be plaque on the massive, unceasing teeth below.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T06:05:26-07:00","id":442443,"title":"","content":"Jessica advanced trought the maze, weak but resoluted. She felt grateful that for the last hundreds of meters nothing out of the ordinary (at least, ordinary for this crazy place) had become a new obstacle for her. Her determination was stronger than ever, the trick using a false Curtis and her own guilt as bait had hit too close home, but the same could not be said about her body. Burnt in places by acid (thankfully, very minor wounds all things considered), still in haze due to the massive loss of blood and the quickly disipating effects o the drugs, she's been quite better.<br /> <br /> Finally, she arrived at an intersection, and such an intersection it was! Before her stood three paths, each of them forking from the way she were on away from each other. They were equally spaced, giving the place the shape of an oversized fan or a duck's foot.<br /> <br /> Directly in front of her, a path of pressed earth that seemed to go right into the center of the maze. Jessica could almost swear she heard the desperate bleats and growls of Nate and Max calling each other and asking for help coming from that direction. Another trap, maybe? She also felt more than heard another sound in the background, like the crunching of rocks.<br /> <br /> To the right a similar path, but this one was covered by artfully cut stone tiles disposed in two parallels rows, as if if two differnt paths going together for a while.<br /> <br /> To the left, the path of earth beared the mark of hoves all along its visible length, the direction of the footprints going in both directions, as if some animal or rider had been patroling the place up and down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T07:07:00-07:00","id":444133,"title":"","content":"Jessica considered her three options. Did Nate and Max really need her help, or was this another trap? For long minutes, Jessica pondered this question. She almost took the right path, the one paved with parallel rows of cut stones. Then it occurred to her that it would be just like the Keeper to set it up for her to pass by her friends in peril just after she had encountered an illusion. How amusing the sadist would have found that! No, she could not take the risk. As fast as her present state allowed, Jessica started to run down the path.<br /> <br /> Jessica cried out, &quot;Max! Nate! I'm coming!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":". 03-17-2015, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-16T11:29:43-07:00","id":444602,"title":"","content":"Nate couldn't see anymore, the torrent of mud was just too strong, and he had to focus on hanging on. So when he felt something grab his arm, he almost fell in surprise. He then gesticulated with his free arm, hoping that Max could take the both of them, and pull him more easily, but instead it was a different set of hands, much smaller, that grabbed the other arm. Right now, he didn't care. He heard the piggy yell something at him, but the downpour was awfully loud, and the crunching noises of the behemoth below didn't help. &quot;I can't hear you Max! JUST PULL!&quot; He yelled, panicked. <i>Is he saying that he can't do it?! Is.. What if it's not Max?! What if it's someone else?!</i><br /> The voice, who was definitely masculine, although it wasn't much help, repeated his sentence, louder. This time, Nate understood a few words : &quot;need to swear&quot;, &quot;make it now&quot;. <i>What, I have to swear again?! That's complete BS, does it really look like I want another contract or trap on my head?! </i>For all he knew, this could be another trick from the Keeper. But then again, he had already decided on given up his freedom, so where was the harm?<br /> &quot;Yes! Yes, I fucking swear on it, to do whatever you just said! Now pull me up for god's sake!&quot; It seemed to do the trick, as the Goat felt a gust of wind brush his fur. Immediately, it seemed that the current was getting weaker. He thought that something had closed the tunnel he came through, but Max and the goblin could easily see that the mud ceased to &quot;attack&quot; Nate, allowing them to pull the musician as easily as if he was in a mundane pool. Once dragged on the corniche, The Goat dropped to all four, coughing spats of mud. But as soon as he cleared his eyes, he finally saw his saviors, and if he quickly ignored the little creature, the sight of his buddy was a miracle. That's why he promptly pulled Max in a bear hug and break into sobs, desperately clinging to his best friend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T17:10:45-07:00","id":446740,"title":"","content":"Jessica emerged from the path she had taken to find herself at the edge of a vast pit. What she saw in the pit almost overwhelmed her with awe. She then spotted Max, Nathan, and a strange creature. She made her way over to them, keeping a wary eye on the huge monster in the pit. When she reached them, she said, &quot;It seems we're reunited. Who is your friend?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:14:09-07:00","id":453141,"title":"","content":"Max's arms had felt as though they were on fire. He could feel his hoof slipping and was briefly, desperately terrified that all three of them were about to head over the edge. He didn't hear it, but did feel Nate accept the terms. The supernatural &quot;tingling&quot; wasn't even needed; the Goat came up just that easily. The Pig then felt the relief coursing through him, but all he could do was pant, exhausted. The next thing he knew, his friend snatched him up into an incredibly tight hug. The piglet was stunned a moment. With all the petty cruelties and bizarre contractual rules in this place, something as simple, honest, earnest, and <i>human</i> as the gesture... He gulped down that breath of fresh air like a drowning man. Max hugged Nate right back, just as tightly as he could, and bawled alongside him, letting all the stress and rage and sorrow of this out at once. Summernickel, whether from politeness, practicality, or both, hung off to the side, and let the two friends get it out of their systems.<br /> <br /> Max wasn't clear on how much time went by or anything else that happened, but when next he was aware of the world, Jessica was in it. He shook his head to make sure he wasn't more out of it than he felt. &quot;Jessica?&quot; He snuffled a moment, from all the crying. &quot;I-I guess we are. H-How did you get here?&quot; The piglet sniffed again, rubbing at his muddy, tear-stained face with his muddy arms, squinting for how exactly she came in. He then remembered his manners. &quot;O-Oh! Nate, Jessica, this is Summernickel. He kept me from...&quot; A gulp. &quot;From hurtling off the edge and helped me get over here. Summernickel, these are Nate and Jessica, the two best friends I've had here.&quot;<br /> <br /> The goblin nodded his long-eared head in recognition of his achievements, and then to the two new ungulates, perhaps seeming a bit overeager. &quot;Yes, it is Summernickel's pleasure to meet Max's friends. Per Summernickel's agreement with Max, only we three will help each other escape,&quot; he noted, gesturing to the Goat, the Pig, and himself. &quot;Certainly Jessica wishes to take part as well...?&quot; The fellow looked hopeful, but also perhaps a bit impatient. &quot;Reunions and greetings are fine things,&quot; he added, in a note of diplomacy, &quot;but escape is finer.&quot; Summernickel then tensed and gave a shriek as what looked to be a chair came flying down from the tunnel above. Thankfully, it was nowhere near hitting anyone, but it did make his point: this was not the safest of places.<br /> <br /> &quot;Right, right.&quot; Max stood there dumbly. &quot;... Um. <i>D-Do</i> we have a plan...?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T19:05:46-07:00","id":453590,"title":"","content":"Yes, there was something human in that hug, indeed. And that's why Nate refused to let go. His brain was simply overflowing with emotion, and he could barely register what was going on. Jessica was here, somehow. There was also a small being, that seemed friendly, but nothing was certain in this realm anymore, except the presence of his buddy. The Goat continued to sob during the introductions, his tears getting mixed with the mud covering his whole face. Even his once proud horns were now caked with the vile liquid! All his pride was gone. He didn't care that he was almost childishly clinging to Max's arm while they were discussing an agreement of some sort. For once, he had a respite, and he was safe. After what seemed like days of fighting alone, bringing the trio back together was a godsend.<br /> <br /> But while the presence of his two friends was appreciated, Nate wasn't eager to face danger once again. &quot;We don't.&quot; He said quietly, his voice shaking. &quot;We don't have a fucking plan. And we never will. The Master's just too smart and powerful for us.&quot; He took a few deep breaths, to control his sobbing, but still didn't let go of the Pig's arm : in fact, he even put all his weight on it, he looked barely able to stand on his own. &quot;We barely escaped this... but one day, we won't be lucky enough. He's a fucking god, there's no other way! We can't fight him, there's no way out... We should... We should just let go and submit, we'll be happier this way...&quot; he concluded, his voice cracking at the end as he fell to his knees, whimpering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T20:37:17-07:00","id":453738,"title":"","content":"Jessica looked at Nate. She understood how he felt, but she herself had no intention at all of giving up. &quot;Nate, I can't and I won't tell you what to do. All that I can say is that I don't plan to give up. I might die, but so be it. I will die fighting. With what I did to get here, I can expect no mercy. If I surrender, I am confident I will suffer a fate worse than death. Worse, I will have done something....&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica trailed off, almost overcome with the memory of what she done to the minotaur. She had killed one of the Keeper's creatures. While it had been in self-defense, Jessica had no expectation of the Keep er being fair. Jessica continued. &quot;I won't give up, but I would understand if you two and your friend did.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-23T22:16:57-07:00","id":455415,"title":"","content":"Max wasn't exactly eager to let go of human contact himself. Though the little guy did grunt a bit, and had to put in some effort to hold up both himself and Nate. Really, even more than the Goat's words, that sagging really made it clear there was a serious problem. &quot;Nate...&quot; the Pig said, note of sadness in his voice; such a good friend locked in the grip of despair... To put it mildly, this didn't do his own less-than-rosy outlook any favors. To put it more honestly, it broke his heart. With the added weight of guilt behind it, as well. After all, Max hadn't said much different in the courtroom, and it had clearly affected his friend. Except even then, the piglet had clung to one last feeble, desperate hope. Nate lacked even that much.<br /> <br /> Jessica's words encouraged him. Max was glad she still hadn't lost her resolve. Even so, a small bitter part of him found it a little naive. Like she was a dashing hero prepared to face down an impossible danger, like something straight out of a fairy tale. Which... didn't seem quite so stupid, after a moment's thought, given all the storybook overtones shot through everything here. In more than a few stories he'd read, it was exactly that kind of determination that led directly to victory. Max was actually a little envious, now; even thinking it, he couldn't bring himself to the same level of heroic resolve. It stung a little. He'd sometimes idly imagined he could manage it if he were suddenly pulled into a fantasy land like this. <i>'Probably shouldn't cling too hard to how you imagined things'd go. You didn't imagine you'd end up with a curly tail, either.'</i><br /> <br /> Still, perhaps Max was being too hard on himself. Whether or not it worked, he'd put the Keeper off-balance with his request. Even if it failed, and even though he'd whimpered the whole way through, there was some brazen trickery to it. And if it worked, it would get them all free. Big 'if,' but still. This little piggy was at least making a hell of a try at heroism. That chance of his weird angle actually working was probably what kept him going. Max had to at least see that through, for himself and everyone. <i>'Maybe... Maybe hearing that'll help snap him outta this.'</i> He cleared his throat. &quot;Nate... I-I know how y-you feel.&quot; He snuffled noisily, dabbing at his own tear-streaked face again. &quot;There's n-not much hope or m-much of a chance. B-But I want you to know--&quot;<br /> <br /> Max stopped very suddenly. If not for all the mud, the other three would have seen him go very pale at the thought he'd just had, and at what he'd just done. &quot;The Keeper's watching,&quot; he murmured after a moment, meant solely for himself and too quiet for human ears to have picked up, but, well. None of the three nearby sets were human. He gulped, even more sure of it now that he'd said it. He rocked on his hooves a moment, dizzy. <i>'And you almost gave the plan away! You... You can't tell them...'</i> The Pig breathed deep a bit, not getting anything like fresh air in that mucky hellhole. &quot;I-I... W-Well...&quot; He fumbled for something to say, and trembled; unable to lean on Nate, Max rested a free hand against a wall. Another breath. Two. A deep one. It bought him time to come up with something else to say, though, something else that might work.<br /> <br /> And he came up with another bit of trickery. Just as when he'd kept his plan secret from Nate and everyone in court, he felt filthier than if he'd been completely submerged in the mud flowing past his hooves. But Max forced himself to go for it anyway. It seemed the best chance they had. &quot;N-Nate, J-Jessica. W-We can't stop.&quot; He gulped. &quot;Y-You know how b-big he is on his handiwork. I-I bet you ran into s-some... t-trials tailored for you, j-just like me.&quot; Against his wishes, he turned his gaze toward the monstrous hog below. &quot;L-Lovingly c-crafted,&quot; he added, with a sharp twinge. &quot;I-If w-we don't keep going, our Kee-- Master w-won't be able t-to show them off. A-And he won't be happy about w-wasted effort. I-It won't go well. Y-You know it won't. W-We can't stop, e-even if we want to.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not that he'd said anything untrue, but he felt like a manipulative little sneak. Max looked directly into Nate's eyes, not having to fake the tears welling up again. He sniffed. &quot;I-I'm sorry...&quot; And looked for all the world like the child he was in shape. &quot;B-But I-I know you.&quot; He said smiling a bit at the Goat. &quot;Y-You're d-down now, b-but y-you're tougher than y-you think. You've... Y-You can keep going. Y-You can take it.&quot;<br /> <br /> As for what the goblin made of all this... Well, he gave no input, for the moment. Whatever his goal and intent, that was for Summernickel to know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T04:00:42-07:00","id":455642,"title":"","content":"*<b>Rooooooaaaaaarrrrrr!!!!!!</b>*<br /> <br /> The Keeper let out a blood curling scream of rage that made everybody in the chamber to hide in fear. Well, except for the Secretary that looked unamused at the furious tantrum of his master, as always.<br /> <br /> &quot;What it is <i>him</i> doing here <i>again</i>?!?!&quot;- it howled- &quot;That thrice dammed goblin smmugler was suposed to be living bait for Pisces!&quot;<br /> <br /> The Secretary took a look to the scrying pond over the massive Scroll and then focused on reading.<br /> <br /> &quot;It seems to me, oh Incomesureable and Gracious Lord Collector, that he escaped&quot;- he noted, stating the obvious to the chagrin of the Keeper.<br /> <br /> &quot;I can see that, incompetent bureaucrat!&quot;- the creature walked around the pond in a vain attempt to calm down- &quot;He already stole some of my pieces! I cannot afford loosing three more!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;No. You do not&quot;- said the Secretary looking down on the Keeper .<br /> <br /> The creature became silent and still as a shiver went down its spine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T06:06:54-07:00","id":455746,"title":"","content":"&quot;Stop! Both of you, stop!&quot; Nate cried, letting go of the pig and stepping back. &quot;Stop saying you know me, stop saying I'm stronger than I think, because I'm not! I'm not like you Jessica, I'm not ready to fight to the death, because this isn't who I am! Stop indulging me, stop lying to me! I know what I am, okay?! I am a fucking coward!&quot; The Goat began to shout despite himself (maybe trying to cover the behemoth's roars?), adding bleats among the words. &quot;I never had any difficulties in my life, I always ran away from responsibilities, and I used people to get what I wanted! When we first met, I wanted to use the both of you as tools for my escape! That's it, that's who I am, a terrible person! A grade-A asshole! I dumped my girlfriend because I got her pregnant and I didn't want to assume my responsibilities and become a father, AND on top of that, she was becoming fat and annoying! See?! I'm shallow as well!&quot;<br /> <br /> His voice gradually became hysterical : &quot;And you know what?! I'm starting to think that this,&quot; he gestured all around him, &quot;this place, this realm, this plane, whatever the fuck that is, well, I DESERVE IT! This is purgatory, my punishment for my jackass ways! Maybe Master is a demon, a god, an alien, I don't know! But this is clearly something to torment me, and every escape I'll attempt will fail because I don't have the strength and the willpower to go away! So now there's only one solution for me, and it is to assume the Goat's role : it's the only logical explanation!&quot; He futilely directed his anger at the gigantic boar, shouting at him : &quot;And I can't even commit suicide to escape this, because I'm too scared and too afraid to die! So go you two, escape if you want, but I can't fight anymore! I'm...&quot; He grabbed his horns, as it sometimes reassured him. However, it didn't seem to work this time, as he almost choked on his next words : &quot;I'm just gonna go to the end of the labyrinth and submit. I'm so tired, and I deserve this. Master will make me better like he did with the others.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-24T11:27:52-07:00","id":456029,"title":"","content":"Nate's revelation about his girlfriend took her by surprise. She felt a rush of anger. What he did her really was terrible. However, now was not the time to judge him for it. Instead, she exclaimed, &quot;Nate, you don't understand! I'm not brave. Not at all! I am just more afraid of surrendering than dying. You see, for what I did to get here, I cannot even imagine how the Keeper will punish me. For merely leaving my cage and helping Max do the same, I suffered hours of being butchered and eaten! The agony of it! The penalty for killing one of his creatures? I would rather die than find out! You do what you need to do!&quot;<br /> <br /> With these last words. Jessica realized that she had just admitted to having killed someone, and turned away in shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T09:01:17-07:00","id":467438,"title":"","content":"Nate didn't expect this kind of revelation. &quot;You... killed?!&quot; He stepped back, his face showing a mix of shock, disgust, but also fear. &quot;That...that's what you're willing to do to get out?! You understand that they were people too, right? How... How could you do that, Jessica?!&quot; His voice was still broken by all the previous shouting and he was still bleating randomly, but the Goat was no longer focusing on his worthlessness. &quot;I can't... I can't stay with you anymore. Master will think that I'm an accomplice. And who knows what you might do next... I don't understand, you're the Ox, you passed the same contract I did with your animal! You're not a predator, you're not supposed to kill!&quot;<br /> <br /> He grabbed Max's arm, pulling him back with him. &quot;Max, we shouldn't stay with her. It's for our own good, you understand, right? Let's go, let's find the exit of this maze.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 04-03-2015, 12:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T10:02:55-07:00","id":467544,"title":"","content":"Jessica wanted to defend herself. Neither Max nor Nate was a woman. How could they understand the fate from which she had saved herself? Yet Jessica also saw that Nate had a point. Her presence could put them in danger. She said, &quot;Max, I think that Nate might be right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Saying this, Jessica started to walk away, hoping to spare Nate and Max whatever fate awaited her.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-04T22:33:29-07:00","id":469179,"title":"","content":"Max felt as though he'd taken a fist to the gut from Nate's reveal. <i>'He... But he said she lied to him...'</i> The knowledge that he'd been betrayed by a friend made the already abhorrent act seem all the more so. He leaned a hand against the wall to steady himself. A part of him felt hypocritical for focusing so much on the lie, given how he'd hidden his plan from Nate in court, but, <i>'No... No! It's not the same! I had to lie or I'd give the plan away. He lied to make himself look better.'</i> While true, this didn't stop the pig's guilt from muddying the emotional waters a bit.<br /> <br /> Still reeling, Max then felt the second fist of the confessional one-two punch. &quot;You... What...&quot; His gaze fell on the Ox, bewildered. Even with the mud and... other fluids that had left her at least as filthy as the Goat or the Pig, there was red Max could see, and he finally placed the sharp coppery smell of blood on her. &quot;How...&quot; His hooves sloshed back a step from her through the mud. <i>'She seemed so... How could she...?'</i> Perhaps he'd held her to standards too high; he'd once bitten off a woman's hand, for crying out loud. But murder...<br /> <br /> Max didn't know what to say. That foundational shaking of his worldview left him paralyzed. He stayed so through Nate's tirade, and as the mud-coated goat began to tug him away. The piglet needed time and peace to think about this, to make it all make sense. But both were in short supply. Part of him felt betrayed; that part wanted nothing more than to leave them both behind without a word. In the end, though... Since the Pig's arrival, &quot;Nate and Jessica are my friends,&quot; had been the only positive constant of Arcadia. He wasn't ready to throw out that compass, just because it occasionally didn't point true north. How much forgiveness, understanding, and acceptance factored in was hard to say: Max <i>needed</i> that axiom to stay true.<br /> <br /> He reached his left arm across to Nate's grip on his right. The loss of human feet and flummoxed his footwork, but Max's training was just as valuable in escaping a hold. The Goat's grip wasn't even something as firm and efficient as that. He reversed it into a firmer grip of his own and shifted his footing, painlessly putting the brakes on Nate's departure. Technique could only matter so much if the wooly one was strong enough, but Max hoped it wouldn't come to that.<br /> <br /> &quot;W-Wait. Jessi--Jessica. It... That's just... It's awful. But... Th-Think about the... the... slaughterhouse.&quot; The Pig had a hard time resisting his own advice, flashes of horrific imagery and searing agony coming to mind, as his free hand began tracing the cuts on that diagram on himself. He pushed through. &quot;H-How many times did we die? How many times did we... did we come back? U-Unless the Keeper wants it, nobody here's really dead and gone. And... And h-he's watching all this. He set it all up. H-He might be...&quot; Max felt sick. &quot;He might think you gave him a good show.&quot; He swallowed. &quot;We're not in danger with you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max turned back to the other ungulate, still in his grip. &quot;Nate... What you did... A-And what you said you had planned... I just...&quot; His hand holding the Goat's shook a likely a bit painful for Nate. Part of him was furious enough to do a hell of a lot worse than that, while another just struggled to keep it together. Perhaps emblematic of his choosing the Pig over the Boar, fury lost out. His grip loosened completely and tears started down his muddy face. &quot;H-How could you...? How c-could you even...?&quot; Max squeezed his eyes shut and shook his head. Eyes still clamped closed he took a breath. &quot;I-It doesn't matter. N-Not right now. I... I still need to... to take it all in. But Nate?&quot;<br /> <br /> The piglet opened his eyes again, looking directly into those horizontal pupils. &quot;Whatever you meant to do, y-you kept me going. I-I'd've given up a while ago, i-if you hadn't. Y-You <i>can</i> do more good than you think. And w-whatever you planned, y-you're not going to use us now. And you wish you n-never had. And... And you wish you hadn't done...&quot; Max trailed off. &quot;... What you did before all this. You regret that. B-But maybe y-you can make it right, if you get out of here. I mean... 'Fat and annoying,' you said.&quot; A brief twinge of anger flickered through that, but he forced it down. &quot;W-Well... With the hug you gave a... a c-crybaby pig like me, I-I think you're p-past that.&quot; Max forced a vaguely goofy smile, but couldn't keep the hurt he'd done himself out of his eyes, nor the fresh tears that slipped from them.<br /> <br /> &quot;And...&quot; Max took a breath, after his voice cracked, followed by a snuffle. &quot;And... you don't deserve this. You don't. I... I don't think there's anything anyone actually <i>can</i> <i>do</i> that's bad enough to deserve all <i>this</i>.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T15:02:35-07:00","id":469631,"title":"","content":"Even if Nate wanted to break the hold, he would have been too weak and broken to succeed. So he simply listened to the Pig, lowering his head in shame. Finally, he was getting the treatment he deserved. Finally, they were rightfully disgusted by him.<br /> <br /> &quot;Nate... What you did... A-And what you said you had planned... I just...&quot;<br /> <i>Just want to puke? Just can't believe it? Yeah. That's what I inspire to people.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;H-How could you...? How c-could you even...?&quot;<br /> <i>Told you. I'm shallow and stupid and immature and a complete ass. I still love her, dammit. I .. I ruined everything.</i><br /> <br /> But when Max looked directly at him, forcing him to listen closely, it hit home. While he knew the pig depended on him, he hadn't realized... well, that he had really made an impact on him. That's why Nate gulped a few times, trying to get rid of the mud caking his mouth : &quot;Max... no, both of you. Jess, Max.&quot; He threw a glance at the goblin, remembering him : &quot;Sorry for the scene buddy, but it's not over&quot;, he weakly grinned.<br /> <br /> His voice was calm now, his nerves were under control now : &quot;You're wrong about one thing Max. It does matter. And it matters right now.&quot; He took a few deep breathes. &quot;I'm pretty sure you're feeling it too, but I'm slowly starting to lose myself. I have trouble remembering a lot of stuff from my previous life. Hell, I can barely remember my last name or even what I looked like. I don't know how much longer I have, so I have to tell you what I am. Who I am. You're both stronger than me mentally, and I know that. You'll hold on longer than me.&quot; He sighed, wiping the mud and tears from his face.<br /> <br /> &quot;Everytime I fail Master, my punishment takes away another part of me. Shit, see? I automatically call him Master. That's a fucking insidious process... That's why I have to tell you. I'm gonna be completely honest with you from now on, so reject me if you want to, but at least, know who I am. 'cause that way, if I have to lose my mind, you'll know whether to mourn me or not. Hell Max, if you hadn't saved me from your big villainous twin down there, you'd still be thinking I'm a nice guy,&quot; Nate snorted. &quot;So here's my story. If you have questions, ask away, I want you to know what a loser I really am.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Alright...&quot; He didn't wait for them to protest, and continued : &quot;I'm Nate D. Only remember D, forgot the rest. I think I live in LA, which I remember being in America. Only child, spoiled kid. I just had to manipulate my folks to get what I wanted. I whined, I cried, I flattered, I used my smarts... I don't think I ever actually worked in my life.&quot; The Goat was shaking his head, as if he couldn't believe what he was saying. &quot;I was in a band, playing... Shit.&quot; He burst into a incredulous laugh : &quot;Woah, I'm even more broken than I thought! I don't remember any of my bandmates, and I see myself playing every instrument! In my mind, I'm a fucking musical genius. I don't even remember the style, I just see the satyr version of me playing in front of a delirious crowd. And I know it's wrong, but it's the only thing I remember from my concerts so eventually, I'll believe it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Now...&quot; He looked at the two of them, facing their glares. <i>As I thought : this is hard.</i> &quot;Yes. I did dump Valerie. I know she lied to me about something, and that sparked the dispute, but I did leave her when she told me she was pregnant. Didn't want to burden myself with this. For me, people are tools to get what I want, like with my parents, and I throw them when they become annoying. That's... That's what I wanted to do with you two.&quot; Another deep breath. &quot;Initially, I was trying to suck up to Mast... The Keeper.&quot; The Goat slapped himself angrily. &quot;Fuck, The Keeper, dammit, it's not THAT hard!... I was trying to suck up to him, and I planned on using you two as my scapegoats,&quot; he snorted ironically, &quot;in case something went wrong. Besides, I... I liked the fact that you seemed to admire me, Max. Jess, I was afraid of you because you're strong and independent. I still am, actually. And... well, I tried to play smart, but Master is too strong for me. I can't compete with him. And he's slowly winning. But you two... you have a chance. If you have a plan, and you still want me along for this... I'll help you. I want to believe in you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Once again, his eyes watered, but he wiped them immediately. &quot;If you don't want to, however... I understand. Go and leave me behind. You deserve it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":".  Minor mistakes. 04-05-2015, 09:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T15:40:33-07:00","id":470440,"title":"","content":"&quot;May Summernickel speak? Yes?&quot;- interrupts the goblin, nervous- &quot;Little piglet and I have an agreement, we should help each other get out of here, so I am bound to point out we should be moving. This place is very dangerous, yes? Yes?&quot;<br /> <br /> The little creature looks around trying to find the best route out, but he reaches the same conclussion as all of you, all the exits seem the same.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hmmmm&quot;- mumbles the goblin- &quot;If we have to choose I would prefer to keep the Ox woman around, she could come in handy, there may be more skulls in need of crushing&quot;-he looks at the pitiful mess that is Nate at the moment-&quot;We could probably do without the undecided turncoat, too dangerous... That said, Summernickel was once even worse than him now and Summernickel would have loathed that the good people had given up on him then&quot;- he shrugs, letting Max do the choice.<br /> <br /> &quot;I do have good news, yes?&quot; -he continues- &quot;You want to end that Keeper, yes, yes? The Collector is this one, yes?&quot; -he asks without waiting for any of you to answer- &quot;You can not crush the skull of that one, but you can not be much of a Collector without a Collection, yes, yes?&quot;- he smiles, widely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T15:01:25-07:00","id":485747,"title":"","content":"Max frowned and thought as the Goat made his confession, eyes softening in places. Part of him still felt betrayed, and Nate definitely hadn't been in the running for Person of the Year. Even so... Max remained convinced of what he'd thought in the guy's defense, and in his own need for his two friends to remain such. Never mind that nobody could be horrible enough for such a fate as this; he hadn't realized just how much Nate had felt himself slipping. The Pig thought he had his answer.<br /> <br /> And it was good that Max reached the decision quickly, as there was not going to be much more time to think it through. With an unhappy grunt at the reference to him by species, he mumbled, &quot;Max...&quot; in correction, again. &quot;But right. W-we shouldn't stay here longer than we g-gotta.&quot; The awful sounds and stench from below were constantly bearing down on him, nevermind the occasional detritus that came hurtling down one of the tunnels.<br /> <br /> &quot;J-Jessica,&quot; Max corrected again at 'Ox woman.' His eyes also narrowed a bit at the implication that skull-crushing was her biggest contribution. They did so again at 'undecided turncoat.' &quot;We're not leaving Nate,&quot; he told the goblin, firm delivery surprising even himself. &quot;I-I... I'm still taking it all in, but... But h-he deserves better than this. I'm sure of that.&quot; The piglet turned back to the pitiful Goat. &quot;Nate. I mean... Let's just...&quot;<br /> <br /> An idea struck him. He'd sworn oaths before; he could do it again. Hell, they'd done it moments before . If Nate swore not to betray them, well, that could have it all settled! But... <i>'... No. I-I don't wanna force anyone into something like that. Not when lives don't depend on it. I-I'm already keeping secrets about my plan. I... I want to just do this honestly.' </i> The Pig took a breath, and decided to go ahead with some modifications. &quot;L-Let's try this. I... I want you to make me a p-promise. N-Not like... Not one of these... these <i>stupid</i> magic oaths, just... A real promise. S-Something <i>human</i>.&quot; He put on a small smile. &quot;P-Promise me that we're friends, a-and we can trust each other. A-And that you won't give up on on getting out of here.&quot; Max thought of one last addition while he was at it. &quot;... And that if... <i>when</i> you get out...&quot; He forced the smile a little wider. &quot;You'll do... Well, whatever you can to make things right with y-your girlfriend.&quot; He extended a mud-coated hand, for a handshake as well as to help the guy up. &quot;Okay?&quot;<br /> <br /> Then Summernickel made his last remarks got a flop from the pig's ears. &quot;... G-Go on. P-Please. W-What do you have in mind, Summernickel?&quot; Max remained with his hand outstretched to Nate, not turning back to the goblin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-22T18:32:57-07:00","id":488914,"title":"","content":"Nate breathed in relief. He didn't think he deserved a second chance, but he wasn't too proud to refuse it. &quot;Thank you Max,&quot; he answered, trying to keep his voice under control. He took his hand and used it to get back up. &quot;I... I want to promise this. We're friends, and I trust you... you two&quot;, he forced himself to add as he looked at Jessica, still unsettled by her confession. &quot;I'll make things right for Valerie, yeah&quot;, he continued as he restrained a sob, taking a few deep breaths. &quot;And not giving up... I...&quot; <i>Nope. No more lying, you said. They have to know that you're a liability.</i> &quot;Look, I'll try. But Master's influence is insidious, and I'm already further down than you guys. I want to believe in you, and I hope I doesn't break this promise, but...&quot; his voice trailed off. No need to complete the sentence, it was clear enough. Still, Nate shook weakly Max's hand. &quot;I'll... I'll keep the breakdowns at a minimum too,&quot; he snorted. <br /> <br /> &quot;What do you mean, little guy?&quot; Nate asked Summernickel. &quot;We're a bit tired for riddles right now...&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T01:08:15-07:00","id":505133,"title":"","content":"The little goblin seemed concerned about how much to tell, that was obvious. He looked at Nate suspiciously, pondering if he could be trusted after all as the piglet asured.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ok&quot;- he said at last.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, you know how your keeper has these long winded barroque titles, right? Gracious and excelsior, whatever and whatever, right? Right?- he asked ansiously. -&quot;They are not just adorments and nonsense, they are in very literal way, their very being&quot;- he let the concept sink in for a while before continuing -&quot;It is the Lord Collector because of his Collection, that is, you, your other pals and the other zodiac-people that guard this maze. It won't like to admit it, but his western collection is incomplete, that's why it is scatered and everyone of them is roaming the realm instead of being exposed, the missing pieces would be too obvious.&quot;<br /> <br /> Summernickel looked around, nervous, like if he expected the creature to jump on him at any moment.<br /> <br /> &quot;I helped them escape this place...&quot;- he added in a whisper- &quot;...and can help you out as well&quot; -he looked at Nate again, like waiting for him to call the guards or something. After a while without any sign of treason, he went on. -&quot;See, he can do whatever it wants with you here because it is the Collector and you are its Collection, you are both it's playthings and slaves, but also the source of its existence and power. A Collector <i>needs</i> a Collection by definition, if it lacks one she wont be a Collector anymore, and as it can <i>only be that</i>...&quot; he gasped -&quot;...he would cease to exist if we managed to take enough pieces from him. I beliebe these new collection of yours, chinese Zodiac, was an atempt to hold onto that title after the wound I dealt him by taking away almost half of the previous collection.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T07:53:01-07:00","id":505497,"title":"","content":"Nate nodded, listening to the goblin. This... actually made a lot of sense, in a fairytale sort of way. But they had to think this way now, so it wasn't really surprising. He decided to ignore the globin's suspicious looks : frankly, how could he blame him? But the Goat didn't want to be a burden now : if the little weird dude was right, this would soon be over and they would be back to the real world and he would see Valerie. <br /> <br /> <i>Also, mental note : find a therapist.</i><br /> <br /> &quot;Okay... So, this is great news, because that means if he ceases to exist, then we get rid of him forever! And that means everyone in his realm will be free, not just us three! The other Zodiacs as well, or even the cages, trees, mountains and stuff!&quot; He smiled, not quite believing it. &quot;But... how can we take pieces from him? I mean, except for killing...&quot; Nate pondered, glancing at Jessica. He couldn't help it, that revelation was still very unsettling. &quot;Wait, never mind, you said you helped them escape this place, so you have a mean to take people away from him. How do you do that, exactly?&quot; Meanwhile, he tried to scrap as much mud as he could off his body, throwing the excess in the pit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T12:03:04-07:00","id":507080,"title":"","content":"Jessica took in these new revelations as best she could, puzzled by them. Then she started to understand, or least thought she might. She shivered. &quot;Maybe I did the right thing. Maybe I hurt the Collector. Well, not really. At best or worst, I destroyed a piece of the broken set.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica fell silent. It was a piece of her own set that needed to be destroyed. Trying to kill either Max or Nate was out of the question, ans she had no current access to any of the other members of her set, even if she would be willing to do something so vile. With a stab of dread in her stomach, Jessica worked out what she needed to do.<br /> <br /> Jessica exclaimed, &quot;I need to break our set!&quot;<br /> <br /> With that, Jessica raced toward the massive pit and hurled herself at the giant, devoring pig that called it home.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T17:04:35-07:00","id":507396,"title":"","content":"Sure, Nate didn't agree at all with Jessica's epiphany. He was even ready to call her out on it.<br /> <br /> Sure, her own confession was terrifying, and Nate's trust in her had been broken.<br /> <br /> But to commit suicide? <i>Oh hell no!</i> The Goat didn't even think about it, he was acting on instinct here : they needed to stay as a group. Or a flock, his caprine part would say. He grabbed her arm, but she was clearly stronger than him. His other hand quickly went into a crack in the wall and he clung onto it, yelling in pain as he was holding the muscled Ox by one arm, stopping her from falling to her death. &quot;What the hell are you d... Gah!&quot; He gasped, teeth gritting in effort. &quot;Max, quick, help me!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T00:29:51-07:00","id":508809,"title":"","content":"Max nodded to Nate's admission that things were and might not be completely rosy. He smiled back sadly as they shook on it. That the Goat would try did encourage him, believe it or not. Perhaps the Pig was too trusting -- as the zodiac sign is said to be -- or perhaps there was just some relief at having cast the die, whatever way it turned up. But Nate's trying counted for no small amount to Max.<br /> <br /> Speaking of dies he'd recently cast, as Max listened to the interesting insights Summernickel provided, he found his mind turning to the gambit he'd laid out in court. <i>'So that's how it is... That means if my plan works, then... Then it's even better than I thought! But... If it doesn't work out... Oh...'</i> He had admittedly been surprised the Keeper seemed accommodating of the request he'd made. With this new information, though, the Pig had a new grasp of how highly the Collector valued what he'd put on offer.<br /> <br /> Max wasn't alone in rolling these revelations around in his head. Of course, Nate and Jessica touched on a somewhat... darker possibility. One which the Ox quickly jumped toward, in a horrifyingly literal fashion. Before the Pig even let out a squeal of a gasp when he realized what was happening, the Goat was already trying to keep her from that mistake. Without a word, Max was right behind him, even before Nate had finished asking for help. &quot;Jessica, don't!&quot; He grabbed her other arm and tried to pull. For all the good it did. Max was plumper than he'd been, but his body weight was nearer to a piglet's than a full-grown hog's, and nowhere near that of an ox. Likewise, even beyond lacking Nate's greater strength, Max had no nearby wall to grab: the other arm was all him. Between learning just how terribly suited porcine hooves were for the task and how forcefully oxen could go where they wished, he found himself getting dragged ever so slowly along. There was only so much difference he could actually make.<br /> <br /> At least, physically. It struck Max that he and Nate were trying to hold her back on a slick muddy surface. If not for the Wilds' blessing on the Pig and Goat, all three beasts might have probably already gone careening down into the gargantuan jaws below<i>. </i>And there was more than one way the Wilds could help. With no thought for whether it would even work, Max focused on his Contract and called out, &quot;Wilds! D-Do something! H-Help hold her back!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T13:25:29-07:00","id":509213,"title":"","content":"And the Wilds answered.<br /> <br /> The mud dried and hardened in response to the pig's call, keeping his hooves and those of the goat firmly in place while a new cornice of stable earth and not slimy sludge erupted some feet below to catch the Ox.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, that was impresive...&quot;-said the little goblin.-&quot;You are certainly a bag of tricks Pi... I mean, Max. Yeah, Max, that's it, right?&quot;.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T13:47:17-07:00","id":516433,"title":"","content":"Well. Max certainly hadn't expected <i>that</i>. The pig's eyes widened, and he felt light-headed; he couldn't say whether the latter was from feeling drained in some way or simply from the rushing energies that had used him as a conduit. Nonetheless, he wasn't about to let the surprise slip by him. &quot;Now!&quot; he said to Nate and pulled with all his might.<br /> <br /> He had no articulate response to Summernickel, his mind focused on tugging the Ox back through the sudden light wooziness, and his voice giving only grunts and snorts in his exertions. But a certain small part of him did take pride on the goblin actually using his name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-21T09:23:48-07:00","id":523337,"title":"","content":"Saved, Jessica looked up and said to her rescuers, &quot;Thank you. I wasn't thinking clearly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Saying that, Jessica pondered her next move. She felt so tired. She had expended so much energy to reach this point, and had lost so much blood. Her body screamed for sleep, but Jessica did her best to ignore it. However, her best proved unequal to challenge. The ox woman passed out on the cornice of stable earth created by Max.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":790,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","user":"Cire","date":".  Bad word choice 05-21-2015, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T05:14:42-07:00","id":528726,"title":"","content":"Nate fell back on the cornice, panting from the effort, and actually blinked in surprise at Jessica passing out. He only realized now he couldn't remember the last time he had slept, or even taken a nap. And yet, he felt that he could still keep going, for the sake of his friends. Time was a strange thing, here in this realm. Days and night were meaningless, as if events and trials happened in a succession, with no regards for temporality...<br /> Or maybe he had slept before, and his brainwashed mind had forgotten it. Who knows, but it wasn't a place to take a nap. The cornice could crumble at any moment. The Goat sat up, took a few breath, and spoke again in a cold voice. &quot;We need to get her out of here. Hey, Summerknightsomething?&quot; He asked, &quot;What do we do now? Do you have a safe place we could use to rest a little or something?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-10T01:51:43-07:00","id":548162,"title":"","content":"&quot;Safe?! SAFE!!!??? Not here, no. There's no true safe place while we remain in its domain, but there are places more dangerous than others. This one for instance. Crazy dangerous. Bad Place, we should totally go out of here as soon as posible&quot;- the goblin whrited nervously and focused his atention back on the pig.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ok&quot;- he finally said- &quot;We may have our exit ticket right here. We should stick togheter and maybe I can take you back home... most of you I hope&quot;- he gives you all a sad apologetic smile that breaks your heart. Is obvious that the poor thing has seen his fair share of pain at the hands of his own keeper and is broken beyond repair. Despite that, though, he managed to make the best out of what he got left and even get back at it and others like it, like this Collector. In sadness you have found hope.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you think you could create a burrow, crossing the walls?&quot;- he asks Max- &quot;We cannot play by its rules, we should get creative and cheat as much as we can. If we create our own passages trough the maze we may take it off guard and have a chance to escape before it realizes it, the last time I smuggled some of his captives it seemed quite slow to react to sudden and unexpected changes&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T11:04:41-07:00","id":553251,"title":"","content":"Max fell back next to Nate after pulling Jessica up, panting away. His body felt like it was on fire. But at least the flames were receding and Jessica was safe. Much as 'safe' was a relative term in this place, Summernickel reminded him. With a grunt, the Pig forced himself to sit upright; even with his mud-drenched robe, lying on his back in the new mud sliding down was <i>far</i> too comfortable. Never mind the ever present danger of more things hurtling down from above.<br /> <br /> Max gave a sympathetic look at Summernickel's sad little smile and then heard him out. The plan made good sense. And now that he knew how much the Wilds could do down here... &quot;I... I can try.&quot; He pulled himself to his feet. Turning to the nearest wall, his hooves made audible little clicks against the dried earth as he went. He wondered when he'd get used to that. Regardless, he set his hand against the muddy surface. He paused.<br /> <br /> A few things ran through his mind. The piglet had his plan waiting for him if he made it to the end. It might become voided if he didn't reach that end as agreed. And with what the goblin told him, he didn't think he'd get another chance like it. Of course, the same could be said for leaving now. It was like he'd cast the dice when he had nothing left to lose and, before being told the result, was informed that the stakes were much higher than he'd thought -- and was offered a chance to take a lesser, safer gamble. But it wasn't just Max's life he'd be chancing: that &quot;lesser&quot; gamble might mean a better chance of freedom for Nate and Jessica and someone who had come to help. Did he have the right to risk all that?<br /> <br /> <i>'Well... Maybe I can hedge a little.'</i> He took a deep breath. &quot;W-Wilds. I-If you would...&quot; Max closed his eyes and pictured his desire, a burrow like Summernickel described, opening as a side-path for them to use or not, not simply a new chasm down which to slide. &quot;M-Make a new tunnel, safe and b-big enough for all of us.&quot; -- <i>'Or just most of us.'</i> -- &quot;T-Tear a path out t-to the Hedge.&quot;<br /> <br /> Just as the little pig made his request, he went rigid. Summernickel's plan hinged on the Wilds cooperating. But Max had gotten the sense that while they would obey him, these were still the <i>Keeper's</i> wilds: requests too far out of the Collector's wishes might be denied. Or worse. And even if it could work, he was calling on it so soon after it had saved Jessica. The Wilds struck him as reasonable, and he had done his best to make it well-disposed to him. But Max dreaded that he might offend it by simply asking too much, too soon. &quot;P-P-Pleeeeease! Please!&quot; His voice was scarcely more than an animal's squeal, plainly begging for mercy. They would find out soon enough if his fears were off-base or terrifyingly well-founded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-21T15:47:34-07:00","id":563456,"title":"","content":"Nate just watched his friend work his magic, literally. It was impressive, how Max had been looking up to him at first... and now, he was there leading the group, having learned so much about the workings of this world. Nate frowned, a bit confused as he felt a pang of... something. Not jealousy but... pride?<br /> <br /> He took a few step forward and placed his hand on the pig's shoulder. &quot;Hey. Stop doubting yourself, you're doing fine,&quot; he said quietly with a genuine smile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T20:45:27-07:00","id":568703,"title":"","content":"Jessica was unaware of any of the drama going on around her. Instead she was lost in a dream. In that dream, she was watching herself buy the oxen figurine from the keeper. She wanted to warn herself, but she was immaterial, like a ghost. Maybe she was a ghost now, forced to review her life. In any event, her earlier self simply could not perceive her. Even so, Jessica felt like the keeper could see her and was enjoying her helplessness. It was then notice a strange face with sparkling purple eyes in the floor of the shop. It winked at her, smiling. &quot;This is only a dream,&quot; it said. &quot;You'll be all right.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica wished she could the face, but felt that she had better not take the risk.<br /> <br /> Still smiling,said the face with smiling purple eyes, &quot;You will wake up soon.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T11:33:31-07:00","id":571712,"title":"","content":"As the seconds ticked by with no apparent response from the Wilds, Max settled into hyperventilating. And without a paper bag in sight. Fortunately, Nate's reassurance and support did the trick, coming as a huge relief. &quot;R-Right.&quot; He took a deep breath, and smiled back at the goat. &quot;Thanks.&quot; It settled things for him; if his friend had enough trust in him to take care of something like that, he couldn't justify letting his plan go to waste.<br /> <br /> At that moment, the chamber wall began to shake. Max jerked away from it with a short squeal, and watched as the filthy wall began to reshape itself. Like a curtain of filth rising before a christening ceremony, it revealed a tunneling path, winding off, down, and away. The floor was mostly dry, though muddy fluid pooled in places and drabs of mud dripped down often. Bits of vine, and luminescent little crystals and mushrooms poked out from the curvature of the ceiling and walls, just enough to see by for those with beastly or goblin eyes. The pig heard his stomach rumble and tried to ignore how tasty the little fungi smelled. He certainly couldn't live with himself if he let something like <i>that</i> change his mind.<br /> <br /> Max sighed in relief. &quot;Thank you, Wilds. A-And this'll lead to the Hedge?&quot; He felt no stirring from the primordial force. A gulp. &quot;A-A-At least as close as you c-could?&quot; he stammered, anxieties rising. A pleasant breeze of confirmation blew down the tunnel. &quot;O-Of course. Thank you again.&quot; He gave an awkward bow toward the tunnel and started breathing again, not realizing he'd stopped.<br /> <br /> After a few deep gulps, he went for the next step, eyes turning to the dreaming ox. &quot;N-Nate, w-would you take Jessica? It's, uh... I'm not strong enough to help carry her, y'know?&quot; Their respective physical showings while she'd tried to kill herself had made that plain. Max looked away after a few moments and whispered, &quot;Wilds. P-Please show me the way to... t-to the end of the K-Keeper's path.&quot; He spotted the green easy against the brown and gray, as a vine sprouted from the mud and extended up the way Nate had come. He frowned at it, almost hoping he'd have an excuse to take the easy way out. <i>'Well... Guess I'd better break the news...'</i><br /> <br /> But he'd miscalculated, and wouldn't be breaking it like he wanted. Max's words had been too soft for human ears. The little piglet had forgotten there <i>weren't</i> any human ears among the assembled.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T03:03:12-07:00","id":572487,"title":"","content":"The path did not stop extending, first in the direction Nate came from as Max already noticed, but then it grew also in the oposite direction and moments later a third path going away from the other two carved itself out of the mud walls of the Pig Pit.<br /> <br /> The Wilds have answered Max's plea, but that reminded them that if they wanted to play by the Keeper rules and gain each of their rewards they had no option but to split again and go their separate ways, hoping each of them succeeded and none of them betrayed the others. Of course they may also follow that Goblin, Summernickel, and directly break their own path together through the Hedge, to home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-29T18:11:47-07:00","id":573377,"title":"","content":"Nate watched all this magic happen, too tired and now too accustomed to it to be surprised. He grumbled when Max asked him to take Jessica, and was about to ask her for help, but found that strangely, she wasn't as heavy as she looked with her Oxen body. <i>Or maybe I'm just stronger... I did hold on for my life earlier for a long time...</i> He put her on his back : this might have been the only time in his life that a woman was pressed against him and he didn't have any lustful thoughts about it.<br /> <br /> The Goat frowned a bit at Max's questioning : despite leading them, he still was very nervous about it. If only... there was a way to make him bolder, or more confident. They'd spend less time reassuring the pig that it's going to be fine... &quot;What news then, Max? What's your plan? Look, Iet me help with this...&quot; He grunted, readjusting Jessica. &quot;It'll be easier if we're cooperating on this. You had a plan with the Keeper, right? Although... it might be hard to do so if Jessica is knocked out...&quot; he pondered. The Goat was feeling a bit frustrated to be left out of the plan : his previous ideas had been failures, and now... they distrusted him. <i>Can't blame 'em, really.</i> Still... he had to regain that trust. He couldn't just let them down after they showed him mercy...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T22:27:34-07:00","id":576037,"title":"","content":"The Wilds had been more generous than he'd hoped. It confused Max. &quot;The Hedge... Me... Nate...? Jessica...!&quot; he said to himself, pointing and reciting the sense the Wilds had given of each new path as it opened. <i>'Wait, their paths, too? Nooo...'</i> Max frowned. He didn't even want Jessica or Nate to have the option of going to the Keeper. And now he'd paved their ways. <i>'Then again... Maybe that's not my call.'</i> He'd been iffy about their requests -- or the Keeper's resulting amusement, at least. But if they wanted to turn down a path to the Hedge, didn't they have the right to choose for themselves?<br /> <br /> The little pig got lost in his thoughts, and turned with a surprised grunt as the Goat asked about his plan. &quot;... P-P-Plan? Whaaaat?&quot; Max put on an innocent smile. &quot;W-Why would you...?&quot; It was as believable as a kid who's been caught with his hand in the cookie jar and crumbs on his face. His childish physique made the likeness even stronger. And he knew it. The smile slowly shrank, giving way to a pained expression. His face then cycled through a range of contemplative, unhappy looks, his eyes darting from Nate, off and away, to Summernickel, or to some empty spot in the chamber as he wrestled with himself. To tell his friend the truth, or keep it from prying ears? Finally, eyes and face scrunched up, the piglet seemed decided and eased a bit, sighing.<br /> <br /> Max looked at Nate. And began to act. Poorly. &quot;I-I... I d-don't know why you'd think <i>I</i> had a p-plan. Heh... Y-You heard me in c-court: I-I'm just a st-stupid... pig.&quot; The last word remained hard to get out. He trembled a moment, about the only genuine and believable part of this 'performance.' The grin he faked was about as convincing. &quot;Ha ha, m-me with a plan. Ha.&quot; He shook his head a moment, and then inclined it toward his path. &quot;N-No wonder I'm g-going t-to...&quot; The swine swallowed dry. &quot;T-to t-tie m-myself even c-closer t-to the C-Collector.&quot; he trembled as the full danger and risk of his plan crossed his mind; he'd tried so hard not to think about it.<br /> <br /> Changing tracks, and taking a few breaths to calm himself, the little pig raised a hand to his chin.* &quot;O-Of course... I guess if I d-<i>did</i> have a plan...&quot; He began, 'speculatively.' &quot;W-Well, like I said, n-no d-doubt the Keeper's w-watching all this. I-It'd be dangerous t-to talk about it, right?&quot; Max then looked right into Nate's transformed goat eyes, earnestly. Everything fake fell away for his last bit, leaving his regret bare. &quot;N-No matter how much I really, <i>really</i> wanted to.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Pig held his gaze, fixed on Nate, hoping the Goat would understand where he was coming from.<br /> <br /> *<s>ny-chin-chin</s> couldn't help it ^_^o","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T04:04:14-07:00","id":576258,"title":"","content":"Nate seemed shocked for a moment... not by the 'revelation', but by Max's incredibly bad lies. He rolled his eyes in an exaggerated fashion, groaning. &quot;Oh my god, Max, next time you want to lie, don't repeat at least six times that you sure as hell don't have a plan. Just say 'I can't tell you right now' or just 'Trust me', it'll work too. Take it from a consummate liar,&quot; he sighed.<br /> <br /> The Goat approached the vines, examining them. &quot;Besides,&quot; he continued, &quot;you're under-estimating the Ma--the Collector&quot;, he quickly corrected himself. &quot;The moment we decided to play his game, he knew we would try to trick him. So... if you have a plan, fine, I'll follow you. But believe in it then, stop doubting everything. You need to be confident and bold if you want a plan to work,&quot; he said casually. <i>Oh look at me, going all sappy and mentory on him!</i> &quot;Alright. So, Hedge, or our respective paths?&quot; He asked, unusually calm about all this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 07-02-2015, 07:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T09:10:41-07:00","id":578859,"title":"","content":"Max looked understandably abashed. &quot;Ah. R-right. Thanks for the tips.&quot; He scratched at the back of his neck, flaking off some dried mud. &quot;R-Really didn't know what I was doing, there...&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>'He's right. I've gotta be confident about this. At least, confident enough.' </i>He took a deep breath, trying to borrow Nate's evident calm. &quot;Okay.&quot; At the last question, he hesitated, and then said, &quot;Well, k-kind of... both. I-I want you to take Jessica with Summernickel down the Hedge path, and find a way out from there. A-And you need to go quick. Like S-Summernickel said, catching him by surprise helps, s-so the longer you wait...&quot; Max shudders. &quot;I need to get to the end of my own path. I-I'm willing to bet my own life on this, but I'm n-not willing to bet anyone else's. I... I can't stop you if you want to come with me, but...&quot; The pig's eyes settled on the ox, slung over Nate's shoulder. &quot;J-Jessica's still out like a light. And you're the only one strong enough to carry her.&quot; He was being honest, but felt a little manipulative here, and his discomfort showed. &quot;I n-need to trust you to get her out of here, okay? I don't know what's down there, but I know you can take it. &quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Get yourself out, too. Heh, and k-keep that promise you made me when you do.&quot; Max forced a smile. &quot;I sh-should see you again. A-A-And if my plan doesn't work, it... I'm glad I met you both.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":". 07-04-2015, 12:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T16:36:32-07:00","id":580335,"title":"","content":"Nate answered by a bleating and weary laugh, shaking his head in disbelief : &quot;I can't believe this...&quot; He kept laughing at the irony, amazed at the turn of events. &quot;Fuck you Max, for making me do this choice... I'm the one who should play the sacrifice card...&quot; The Goat sighed : he had prepared himself mentally since the trial, prepared to lose his freedom, his mind or even his life to let Max and Jessica escape... And now the pig was taking his place? He laughed again at the Pig's 'flattery' : <i>Sounds like I did teach him something...</i> &quot;You know the worst part about this? I'd like to say the truth : that you're wrong, that I should take your place, no, you deserve to get out more than I do... But your plan actually makes more sense. This... I think you've been planning this for a long time, and you have a trick up your sleeve... and even if I do think you have the strength to carry Jessica, my willpower would just crumble before the Keeper. And since she's out, we can't go on our separate ways...&quot; <br /> <br /> The Goat glanced at the Goblin, then the Ox, and sighed anew. &quot;Dammit Max, you better get out of this mess, or I'll get back here to bust your piggy ass out!&quot; He approached him and freed one arm to pull him into a friendly hug. &quot;You're the best of us three, buddy. We'd be dead or hopeless if it wasn't for you... Thank you&quot;, his voice broke a moment, and he breathed deep to keep his speech in control. &quot;I don't know what you planned but... look, you'll have to face Aries to get out of here. This guy's a ... a massive version of myself, with a huge ego : he can't stand to be less than perfect, you'll need to trick him. I succeeded by flattering him and belittling myself...&quot; <i>Even if I actually didn't have to lie... </i>&quot;I wish I could give you more advice,&quot; he continued, &quot;and... I wish I could help you more...&quot; He whispered, finally pulling away, and he faced the path to the Hedge. &quot;So... here I go, right?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T21:03:10-07:00","id":583152,"title":"","content":"Unexpectedly, Jessica said, &quot;Your eyes! They sparkle!&quot;<br /> <br /> After saying this, she came awake with a sudden jerk. She found herself alive and slung over Nate's shoulder. Not sure of what else to do, she made a joke. &quot;You could at least buy me dinner first, you know.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T15:49:59-07:00","id":588524,"title":"","content":"Max gave a sad smile to Nate's first response. &quot;J-Just... The way it has to be.&quot; He was doing well at keeping himself together, he thought; he kept back the tears. <i>'Gotta put those aside.'</i> He gulped. &quot;W-We made different deals. That's all. I-I have to go.&quot; The little pig still shook a little, but was determined not to let that show, either. He looked bashful at the talk of his plan, murmuring, &quot;I-It's noth--&quot; before catching himself. <i>'Confidence, remember. And not just for you.'</i> One cough later, he corrected himself: &quot;Something. I-It's something.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max had a hollow laugh of his own when Nate suggested he was strong enough to take Jessica. &quot;M-Maybe you didn't notice. W-When she ran, I did so little -- n-not the Wilds, just me.&quot; He then decided he probably wasn't alone in needing some encouragement. &quot;L-Look at you, though. Sh-She'd have j-just dragged me with her. But y-you're stronger than you think. B-Better than you think. I-I hesitated, when she ran, but you jumped right to her. I-I trusted you, and you proved why I should.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then Max chuckled at the comment of rescue. &quot;I don't doubt. Not for a minute.&quot; Though paired with the hug, Nate's next words left him speechless. The Pig's mouth moved, but nothing came out. <i>'That's not true. You <b>are</b> better than you think. We all brought something. We wouldn't have made it here alone.'</i>* He believed it, but it was like his throat was swollen, as eyes watered. He could at least return the hug. Finally, he managed to croak out something. &quot;... Th-Thank <i>you</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> The advice and guidance was very welcome. Max had had no idea what was up there, but knowing Nate had faced it helped. Not that he knew how he'd get past Aries, but the advance notice for planning was huge. The piglet smiled up at the Goat. &quot;Thanks. That... That <i>does</i> help a lot. I-I might just make it through, now.&quot; As Nate turned, he nodded and added. &quot;R-Right on through. It'll go a-as far as the Wilds could manage. J-Just... Keep respecting them like you promised, a-and they should still help where they can.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then there wasn't much left, but the last goodbyes. <i>'Just for now,'</i> Max told himself. &quot;Summernickel, th-thanks for c-coming to help, a-and for saving my neck earlier. Nate... Th-Thank you for everything. T-Tell J-Jessica the s-same, a-alright?&quot; He cleared his throat. &quot;G-Good luck. And good-- No, not goodbye. Just... S-See you after all this is over.&quot; And with a smile, Max turned, beginning his ascent toward Aries.<br /> <br /> Only to pause in his tracks at Jessica's voice. <i>'No... No, not now...'</i> Max turned to look back behind him, bewildered. His throat made an odd sound of disbelief as he processed what she'd asked; at another time it might have amused him, but things were just too heavy for him to know how to respond to it. In any case, his mind wildly changed gears from clever plans for getting past Aries to clever plans for keeping Nate and Jessica safe. And this little piggy had none. &quot;I-I...&quot; He took a breath to get a grip on himself. And decided to just deny that anything had changed, re: the plan. &quot;I-I'm glad to s-see you w-wake up before I head out, J-Jessica.&quot; That, at least, was genuine, as was the smile that joined it (tinged with his worry as it was). &quot;G-Go with Nate and S-Summernickel to the H-Hedge. <i>Please.&quot;</i> There was more yearning there than he meant. &quot;Th-Thank you for... For everything. I-I'll see you all l-later.&quot;<br /> <br /> Max felt cold. Very cold. There was more he wanted to say to Jessica, more he felt his friend deserved to hear if this didn't work. But he'd barely kept himself together with Nate. One more round and his nerves would be shot completely. And so, wiping with his muddy hand at the few tears that had finally slipped past him, he took off at a run toward Aries, and the path the Collector had picked for him.<br /> <br /> * Which, given &quot;here&quot; was a muddy hole with a giant monstrous pig indifferent to whether it ate them, was likely best unsaid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T19:48:18-07:00","id":588740,"title":"","content":"Surprised by Jessica's sudden awakening, Nate lowered her carefully to the ground. This brought a dilemma : she has been a good excuse to go along with Max's plan, but now that she was awake... The Goat looked back to the Pig, who had already understood the situation and scampered off. <i>Figures. At least he's taking charges...</i> But now that the three of them were awake... was splitting up really their best bet? <i>If I let him go to his death or enslavement... It's all about trust...</i><br /> <br /> After a look at the different paths, Nate explained to Jessica in a tired voice : &quot;We have a chance to run away right now if we follow our little friend here,&quot; he said nodding to the goblin. &quot;But... there's no saying Max will make it. He has a plan and I have no idea what it is... We might be a burden and screw him up if we go after him... or we could end up saving his ass. I honestly have no idea which one is more likely.&quot; <i>As much as I'd like to play the hero...</i> One hand went to grab a horn, as he often did when he was in turmoil. &quot;I hate to say this, and I don't want you to think I'm trying to betray you because that's really not the case, but... we should run away. I think Max can pull this off. I placed my bet on the little guy. So come with me, please,&quot; he pleaded, offering her his hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T21:11:13-07:00","id":595345,"title":"","content":"Jessica took the hand that Nate offered. &quot;I hate to leave Max, but maybe this will have the same effect as what I tried to do. It seems we can do little other than hope for the best.&quot;<br /> <br /> Despite saying this, Jessica felt almost ill from the choice that she had made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T05:40:21-07:00","id":598196,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hurry, hurry!&quot;- Summernickel abruptly interrupted the emotive farewell bringing everyone back to their current predicament-&quot;the more time we spend here, the more time we are giving The Collector to react, and believe me, we can't afford giving that thing even more advantages&quot;.<br /> <br /> Demonstrating both the disposition and the expertise of an experienced pathfinder, the little goblin guided Jessica and Nate away from the brave piglet. As in the transition in a dream, the way openend by the Wilds soon changed the scenery around the trio, the mud pit and the slicky slides-tunnels disapearing behind them, substituted by increasingly thick vegetation as they marched to an uncertain destination. <hr /><br /> Max was alone.<br /> <br /> It was not only his three companions which had been spirited away from his side, the mud pit itself and the great pig that representend him in the sick mind of the Keeper have grown silent, when he decided to take a look he actually found the pit empty. What that meant, if indeed anything had a hidden meaning in this crazy place, Max didn't know.<br /> <br /> The Path to Aries, to his Goal and hopefully to the freedom of his friends extended before him, inviting.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T07:05:18-07:00","id":598294,"title":"","content":"As the vegetation thickened, the way forward became more and more difficult. It soon became clear that the vegetation around them had sharp thorns. As the path that the little goblin led them on became tighter and tighter, Jessica found herself wishing that she still had her original size. Even so, she pressed forward. Little other choice existed. <br /> <br /> In time, the trio reached a small clearing. A tree with strange pink and stranger still glowing green fruit leaves in the center of the clearing. Sleeping under the tree was another another goblin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-21T22:02:58-07:00","id":599032,"title":"","content":"Max had put only some small distance between himself and the others, and then stopped to try to get a hold of himself. <i>'Calm... Get calm... C'mon, you can't be all panicked and fidgety. Not.. Not until it's over.'</i> Though that wasn't the only reason he stopped. The little pig left a floppy ear cocked in the direction he'd come. He heard the steps of four hooves and two feet. Moving away from him. <i>'... Guess they listened to me.'</i><br /> <br /> It was bittersweet. Part of Max had hoped all three of them would be facing the end of all this together. He missed them already, snuffling a little and wiping away a few tears. Other parts knew this was selfish: Nate and Jessica reaching the end wouldn't win more than his bargain could, and they deserved to get out if his gambit didn't work. From what Summernickel said, it would do the Collector harm either way. <i>'This is how it needs to be,'</i> he told himself.<br /> <br /> Still, aside the loneliness and the practicality he saw, there was a swelling of pride in the piglet's chest. &quot;They... They trust me... Th-They didn't just <i>say</i> they did. They really... They think I can do this.&quot; Whether right or not, Max wasn't sure he'd ever believed anyone felt that sort of confidence in him, but now when he couldn't deny it... He rested a hand against a muddy wall to steady himself. He hadn't realized the weight it could carry. The Pig drank a few deep breaths of the air, his heart rate slowing to something comfortable. He coughed, feeling a little choked up, and wiped away some fresh tears. &quot;S-So I'm gonna,&quot; he said, rare determination crossing his face, as he stepped free of the wall and stood as tall as he could.<br /> <br /> It was then that Max noticed something. <i>'When did it get so quiet...?'</i> The disappearance of the great insulting behemoth of a hog had gone unnoticed. He wondered what it meant. Though not for long enough to worry: he became aware of something new, a scent quite a ways ahead. At first he wondered how Nate had gotten up there, but no, definitely not; Nate's musk was just the closest word for it. The poor little piglet then had a brief panic at associating his friend with scent so unthinkingly. He hadn't even noticed. <i>'H-How human am I actually going to <b>be</b> by the end...?'</i> He shook his head to clear it of those unhelpful thoughts, and started walking. The Pig would find out when he got there. <i>'The sooner the better, whatever the case... Just... Focus on thinking up how to handle Aries. As long as I don't run into too many more... animal things... It should be okay.'</i><br /> <br /> And so Max gave a frustrated squeal on noticing that his tunnel was narrowing, the roof getting lower. It would force him to all-fours, just as when he'd entered. He considered calling on the Wilds again, but... <i>'I've asked a lot lately. I <b>needed</b> it then, but now... This would just save some... humiliation. That might insult it. So...' </i>With a resigned grunt, the piglet began crawling through. And tried not to think about how much more <i>natural</i> it felt to move this way than it had before, nor how nice the muddy walls felt brushing against his face as he went. Yeah, Max wasn't having much luck with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T11:46:45-07:00","id":599666,"title":"","content":"Sure, the vegetation was thick and difficult to navigate, but this was a welcome respite from the mud pit. And actually, now that he was thinking about it, Nate didn't have the same problems as Jessica with his surroundings : he was smaller and his body was more nimble. Plus, he had passed a contract with the Wilds too, and after having observed Max's way of asking help, he decided to try his hand at it, without the squeals and stutters. He whispered his request, and the plants parted way for him, although he did prick his skin on a few thorns. Before, he would have complained, but now it seemed trivial.<br /> <br /> The trio seemed to be mostly silent : it was hard to make small talk after parting with Max and leaving the Pig to his potential death. Which left Nate to focus on his escape... until he became aware of his body's needs. Unlike Jessica and Max, he had been awake for a very long time, running on adrenaline and stamina since... Why, since they had arrived in the ranch! So much had happened since then, and he suspected something magical allowed him to hold on : maybe the laws of his realm, maybe his contracts, or maybe just his new body. He was tired, but the prospect of getting out was beating the need to rest by a long shot.<br /> <br /> However... being surrounded by foliage brought another vital need : Nate was starving. His stomach rumbled, as a reminder that his last meal had been the hallucinogenic mushrooms, and they hadn't been really nourishing. He could feel his saliva thickening as the tentalizing smell of the leaves got stronger... <i>I can't just stop and eat them, or I will lose the group. </i>He tried to reject the idea, but the more he thought about, the more eating those leaves made more sense : it'll give him more strength to escape, and it would also honor the Wilds and his animal contract, keeping his word on the both of them! Which is why he finally gave in, grabbing a bunch of stalks and ripping them off to chew while walking to keep up with the Ox and the goblin.<br /> <br /> It tasted so wonderful, so green and delicious! His flat teeth were perfect for chewing on them, releasing all the juicy sap in his hungry mouth. The Goat was still enjoying his meal when they stumbled in the clearing, and those glowing leaves caught his yellow eye : they looked perfect. He made his way to them, avoiding the sleeping gobelin, and started to munch on a branch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T16:46:43-07:00","id":599983,"title":"","content":"Jessica watched Nate munch on the glowing leaves. She wondered if that was a wise thing for him to do. She noticed that the sleeping goblin was starting to stir. In a moment, the goblin sprung to his feet, alarm etched on his face. <br /> <br /> &quot;How long was I sleep?&quot; the goblin asked. <br /> <br /> Jessica replied, &quot;I can't say; we just got here.&quot;<br /> <br /> The goblin turned his attention to Nate, smiling. &quot;Good, right?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-23T17:05:57-07:00","id":601068,"title":"","content":"Nate barely stopped to glance at the goblin, trying to evaluate if he was aggressive... but since it wasn't apparently, he resumed his task, acknowledging his question with a nod. They were truly delicious indeed, calming, even. Just what he needed : once his belly is full, he'll be ready to carry on his escape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T04:39:39-07:00","id":601599,"title":"","content":"&quot;You lazy mongrel, Winterdime!&quot;- Summmernickel berated the sleepy goblin- &quot;We have no time, It already took me more than expected to reach to these two, and the third... the third is a brave one, let's leave it at that. I hope he's fine&quot;- he aded, a hint of sadness calming his mood.<br /> <br /> Now that you are able to take a look at the other goblin (Winterdime his name, apparently) you realize is almost a mirror image of your goblin companion, same features, colors and even voice tone, though certainly more cheerful and easy going than the bag of nerves that is Summernickel.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ok, ok, Summernickel,my old friend&quot;- the other goblin says, getting up from below the strange fruit tree- &quot;But what if you let them eat in peace? There's a very demanding path before us and they could very well not make it whole if they are weak and hungry&quot;- That said he takes one of the strange fruits from a nerby branch and handles it to Jessica. <hr /><br /> Meanwhile in Aries path:<br /> <br /> Max continued moving as fast as he could on all fours, constantly reminding himself that despite his feelings this was not the proper way for a person to walk. He didn't even realized the tunnel had opened up, revealing a strange sky above, so focused was on the muddy path he was traveling. His run apbruptly stoped when he went full speed against a pair of white columns.<br /> <br /> *THUD!*<br /> <br /> Max head hurted from the hit and he remained a little fuzzy for a few seconds afterwards. When his senses cleared he could made out some words directed at him.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, well, look who has finally come here! And you are already grovelling, as you should! It seems your friend told you well&quot;- Max looked from the floor up the columns that seemed to be made of marble covered in fine white fur, only to meet the smug smile of superiority of Aries, First among the Zodiac.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-24T15:22:17-07:00","id":602299,"title":"","content":"Recalling how eating food offered by the Collector had led to trouble, Jessica shook her head. &quot;Thanks, but no thanks.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You better eat it,&quot; Winterdime advised. &quot;You cannot last forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jessica took the fruit, but did not eat it. &quot;I will think it over. Thank you.&quot;<br /> <br /> Winterdime smiled. &quot;That is all that I ask.&quot; He then turned his attention Summernickel. &quot;I hope you are willing for us to go through that Goblin's Market on the way; There are a few things I have been thinking of getting.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T10:42:51-07:00","id":603066,"title":"","content":"No doubt to Aries's satisfaction, Max had even bowed his head after the collision, clutching it with a hand. On noticing the Ram properly, he squealed in alarm and whirled around to run a short distance. He turned back with a wary eye to Aries. The poor piglet still stood shaking on all-fours, all thought of this impropriety and humiliation in remission. Once his head cleared and he calmed down from the threat of this mountain of a goatman, it would return. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> Panting a bit, he looked up at Aries. Nate had <i>not</i> been kidding about the size of this guy. <i>'Guess it says something about how big <b>I</b> am, too...'</i> Still, the Goat had found success by way of flattery and self-deprecation: the Pig could follow that trail. He cleared his throat with a grunt. &quot;I-- I-- I'm s-sorry f-for-- A-and y-yes, N-Nate t-told me about you. J-Just...&quot; Max cringed at his awful stuttering, even worse than usual. He drew a few breaths, trying to focus on clarity. &quot;W-Words just c-couldn't do you justice. W-Which I'm sure d-doesn't surprise you.&quot; He tried flashing a conciliatory smile up at the ovine powerhouse. &quot;'s-specially next to me. Ha, d-down here in the muck, I can b-barely make out the tops of your horns!&quot; The piglet tried to work as much admiration into his voice as he could.<br /> <br /> He didn't have a plan, but buttering up the big guy seemed as wise a course as any. When he did come up with something, being on Aries's good side was the best position he thought he'd have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T08:06:07-07:00","id":606588,"title":"","content":"After a moment, Summernickel replied to Winderdime, &quot;Fine. It might be there are some things we might need to.&quot;<br /> <br /> For a long time after Summernickel spoke, Nate simply continued to eat. For her part, Jessica reflected on all that had happened to her and the others. She also reflected on her decision to let Max face the collector by himself. She asked herself how could she have been willing to give up her life only to show such cowardice later. She shook her head. Even if she had changed her mind, she doubted that she could have found her way back to the maze. She could only hope that Max knew what he was doing.<br /> <br /> Eventually Summernickel said, &quot;We had better get a move on.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-29T16:27:59-07:00","id":607250,"title":"","content":"After a while, Nate's hunger subsided, his caprine impulses calmed down by the taste of the leaves. As he munched a few times to fully digest, he noticed that unlike every other times he had succumbed to the tentalizing scent and sight of this green food, he didn't feel bad about it. Maybe... Maybe he was accepting his new body afterall. Doesn't mean he would turn back and turn himself to the Mast--Keeper, but the goat was a part of him now. Sure, it wasn't the most glamorous animal, but it was his fate. And who knows, perhaps once they're safe and far away from the Keeper, their changes would reverse and they'll be human again. But no way to know until they got there...<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, sorry,&quot; he cleared his throat as he noticed everyone was waiting for him. &quot;I really needed it. Let's go.&quot; But as he said this, his eyes glanced at one of the pink fruits, and he decided to pluck one from the tree : he could at least get a dessert, right? He took a big bite and munched on it, waiting for the goblins' instructions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T01:58:21-07:00","id":607556,"title":"","content":"&quot;Haha, good, good&quot;- Winterdime aproved Nate's disposition-&quot;Come this way. Summernickel could you do please watch our backs?&quot;- the goblin asked heading out of the clearing and further away from the Collectors realm, or so everyone hoped.<br /> <br /> &quot;Make no mistake&quot;-Summernickel pointed out-&quot;The path ahead is no less dangerous than the one we are leaving behind. The Thorns will rend at your very soul, not only your flesh and skin, and the Hedge will play tricks to your mind brought from your own fears and desires. The limited comprehension of human nature of the Keeper limited it a great deal, no matter how omnipotent it may have been while in his home ground, here you will have to face your own twisted insecurities and emotions, be careful&quot;. <hr /><br /> &quot;Aren't you a lovely piglet?&quot;- Aries sneered at Max's debasing- &quot;I DO NOT like lovely piglets. They are no sport&quot;<br /> <br /> The sharp head of an oversized spear pierced the ground next to Max's head with such strength the ground trembled. Aries was casually leaning most of his considerable weight on it, as if a cane, looking down on the sudenly shocked pig.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, you thought to just pass me by with meliflous flattery?&quot;- Aries inquired, bending his knee to lower himself to be able to talk Max face to face- &quot;Is one thing to enter the maze, we want you to after all, but getting to the other side? Just like that?&quot;- Aries started to laugh out loud, rising again to his full height- &quot;No, my little <i>prey</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> At the command of that word, Max changed yet again. Dark brown fur, hard as wire covered his body. His considerable weight turned from soft fat to raw muscle and a sharp pair of tusks protuded out of his lips. He was yet again the Boar, and he was to be hunted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-30T16:41:21-07:00","id":608608,"title":"","content":"Maybe it was an effect of the plants, or just because of his acceptance of how this realm worked, but Nate didn't feel especially scared by the goblin's words. <i>Insecurities and emotions? I think I already covered this, thanks...</i> He glanced at Jessica : he had no idea of the trials she faced when they were separated, maybe she would be especially vulnerable to the... Hedge? <i>Yeah, that's what he called it,</i> to the Hedge's manipulations. It would then just be up to him to lead her to safety.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, it's not like we have any other choice, don't we? Let's press on.&quot; Max had sacrificed his freedom and maybe his life to allow them to escape, and they sure as hell wouldn't spoil this chance. The Goat headed after Winterdime, intent on surviving these ordeals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-01T11:03:52-07:00","id":611083,"title":"","content":"Max had expected some mockery, but his heart leaped into his throat when the spear came down. As Aries lowered himself, the Pig stood, shaken and speechless. He'd soon regret not finding his voice quicker. &quot;I-I-I, n-no, of c-course n-not, I just--&quot; Aries talked over him, cowing him into silence. Still, he'd begun getting together an idea, one that just might let him talk his way past this. Max drew a breath to steady himself and went for it when the First of the Zodiac began to laugh. &quot;N-No! Look, I-I think this isn't what it seems. I--&quot;<br /> <br /> And then that word struck. Max stood there, stunned, grunting in discomfort as the changes raced over and through him like a fire. The pink flesh and scattered white bristles gave way to a sweeping ocean of hard brown bristles, while his large floppy ears shrank to a smaller, narrower pair, perked and alert. His body exchanged fat for muscle, and that wasn't the only structural change: his stature went from small and childish to the size and build of a much more mature animal. The now-filthy robe in which he'd been dressed hadn't been sized for this and tore like tissue paper. This revealed that his curly tail had straightened and lengthened slightly, a small dark tuft crowning its tip. After a few panicked seconds of confusion, Max spotted his new tusks, gleaming proudly, and realized what was happening. He squealed in alarm. And found that even his voice had groan deeper and huskier.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait! Stop! This...&quot; He paused, puzzled at the sound. It was growing more guttural with every word. By this point, the tingling fire had mostly begun to recede, but still simmered in Max's throat and jaw. <i>'... Ohhh, no...' </i>The thought sent a chill through him. &quot;I made a deal! He's rrroing groo--!&quot; <i>'No no no...'</i> &quot;Wrree neeeeed groo grryyy--!&quot; <i>'No please no no...'</i> &quot;Grink, runk! Roink! REEEEEE!!!&quot;<br /> <br /> It was no use.<br /> <br /> He looked up from the ground, past the end of his snout and his new tusks, and locked fearful eyes with Aries. Even the perfect words couldn't get the Boar out of this one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T05:12:32-07:00","id":618689,"title":"","content":"Meanwhile, mirroring Max's own transformation, Aries started to change. His marble white skin turned deep dark grey, almost black in the dim light of the maze. His horns grew even more majestic and sharp and a cowl fell over his face, obscuring his features save for the pinpricks of light of the eyes. As Max the Boar growled in distress a powerful steed with unnatural proportions entered the scene. The Hunter jumped on its back with ease, spear firmly held in one hand while he blew a hunting horn with the other. <hr /><br /> The four companions haven't walked for more than a minute or so (or at least that was the consensus among them, time run strangely too in this place) when the whole hedge around them seemed to shake and vibrate. After a short while, like the sound of distant thunder, the deep sound of a horn reached the group.<br /> <br /> The two goblins stoped dead and shivered, exchanging a worried look.<br /> <br /> -&quot;This is...&quot;-started Summernickel- &quot;...very bad&quot;-ended Winterdime.<br /> <br /> The sound of several blood curling howls answered the call of the horn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T06:10:00-07:00","id":618746,"title":"","content":"There was no need for the goblin's warnings : Nate could feel it to its core. They call it gut instinct, and he knew why, as terror grew in his very core. Something or someone terrifying was hunting, and no one was safe. The beast part of him stirred and panicked as he heard the Goat's plaintive and scared bleats. <br /> <br /> &quot;We should run, right? Let's run guys, please?&quot; He pleaded, throwing nervous looks around. Nate was struggling to stay in control, one word from the goblins and he would be ready to dart away. But he couldn't let the Goat take full control yet, what if this was a trap?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-07T08:38:41-07:00","id":618964,"title":"","content":"Jessica shook her head angrily. &quot;They expect to run. We have to do the unexpected. We have to hide!&quot;<br /> <br /> Having said that, Jessica tried to crawl into the nearby dense, thorn-laced leaves. She did the best that she could to crawl through and conceal herself. However, the thorns pricked her far more painfully then she thought possible. The plants also seemed to bent on repulsing her back. Even so, Jessica struggled forward. She would not be caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T00:05:17-07:00","id":620956,"title":"","content":"Max was not in his clearest frame of mind. He was terrified of losing his voice. He was terrified of Aries's hunting plans. And he was terrified the boar's rage would consume him again. Max remembered those thoughts of fury and bloodlust from when he'd wanted to tear Nate apart. Already, he could feel a flame simmering in his throat as he looked up at Aries. The premonition from Libra had crystallized for him his worst fears about it. There was so much senseless brutality and destruction he could wreak if he lost control. And part of him <i>wanted</i> to; amidst the fear, it was starting to hit him how angry he was at the Zodiac hunter for doing this to him. The Boar wanted to tear Aries into pieces too small for anyone to ever find. Feeling that way frightened him so much.<br /> <br /> Only... it wasn't his biggest fear. Nor were his fears of never speaking again, nor of being brutally hunted. No, it struck Max that his biggest fear was betraying the trust that had been placed in him. The thing that scared him most was was falling short of who and what he needed to be to reach the end, to save himself and everyone else. In a moment of clarity, it all seemed so obvious. He realized something about those other fears? They were all subordinate. They would not beat him because he could not allow them that.<br /> <br /> Max couldn't speak? He would make himself known, however he must.<br /> The Boar's rage flared? Max would <i>not</i> let it rule him; he would channel it instead.<br /> Aries had already written roles for them both in the script? Well then. Fuck. That. Script!<br /> <br /> In the spirit of the third, Max would not become the hunted, and would not allow a hunt at all.<br /> In the spirit of the second, Max would do Aries great injury, but only as needed.<br /> In the spirit of the first... Well. That would be a matter of course.<br /> <br /> He felt his fists tighten. Hands! He hadn't been made a complete beast. And those early days of martial arts practice in his newly porcine body... Max decided on his course and something like a plan. &quot;Something like&quot; because a proper plan would need longer than he could give. He needed to act <i>now</i>. So it was fortunate his transformation had made of him a creature adept at charging headlong into danger.<br /> <br /> The Boar gave a swinish bellow, not matching the horn's volume, but just barely. Mid-cry, before Aries could set down the horn and otherwise fully prepare himself, Max hurled himself up at the First among the Zodiac. The new muscle in his legs had more than enough power to carry him there, and the strength of his arms -- and the wire-harsh bristles -- promised a hell of an impact from the fist he threw. At the same time, he leaned his neck forward, riding his body's momentum and letting the Boar guide his tusks to where they would leave the most debilitating gash of a wound. His other hand stands ready to seize at the wrist of Aries's spear hand, perhaps to kill his grip on it, but mostly to ensure the combined massive weight of both beasts fell agreeably on either that arm or the spear itself.<br /> <br /> If it worked, the element of surprise would end things in seconds. And Max was truly playing every card in his hand: much as Aries might take that animal cry to mean Max had lost all reason (welcome bonus though this would be), it held a different purpose. It was a call to the Wilds. In a voice it surely knew better than his usual stutter. With its aid, the ground itself would lift sharply under the Boar as he jumped, adding even more speed and momentum, and cutting down the window of a reaction time. Nor was it the sole request: Aries's steed would find its footing thrown into chaos as the earth bucked and trembled wildly. Even an experienced rider and hunter would have enough trouble staying steady in the saddle, much less trying to aim a weapon at a sudden attack.<br /> <br /> Still, while he had done what he could, Max was not just dealing with a regular steed and an experienced rider and hunter. These were supernatural ones. It was an open question how well this was going to go for him. One way or another, this question would have its answer very, very soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-10T14:42:35-07:00","id":622682,"title":"","content":"&quot;Hide?! Last time I checked, I was a Goat, not a chameleon!&quot; Nate whined, looking around in panic. Where could he hide in those bushs?! The thorns seemed to make it too painful for anyone to hide in there, he knew his skin was tougher than before, but surely that wasn't enough. <i>Come on, think, think!</i> They had to do the unexpected? Like what, fighting? Go and look for these hounds? <i>Nope, I don't see any scenario where this would be a terrible idea...</i> Okay, then what about using other abilities? He had no equipment except his flute, his hooves and horns... <br /> <br /> <i>Take a page from Max's book, idiot.</i> That's right, Nate had passed contracts too! The Wilds already helped him avoid most of the thorns, but could they help him hide at all? As for Fang and Talon... He blinked as the answer dawned on him : the Goat looked for the tallest tree around and ran toward it. <i>Okay hum... Goat spirit? Do your thing, please?</i> That thought just switched something in the musican's mind, and his feets and hooves quickly climbed on the trunk and onto the branches of the tree, balancing his weight with surprising ease. The human part of Nate had relinquished the control to his bestial side, accepting that it was for the best for now. They headed for the highest branch, hoping to be undetected there, or at least, out of reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T13:53:35-07:00","id":626946,"title":"","content":"Max's unexpected attack took Aries by surprise. The sharp tusks of the Boar backed by his powerfull muscles (and no short deal of anger and fear) pierced deeply into the Hunter's side before the steed, wildly off balance due the intervention of the Wilds, could react to avoid it. The roots protuding from the soil at Max's command dropped the unnatural horse to the ground where it was pierced by several nasty-looking thorns. A stream of purplish-pink blood sprayed from the wounds, filling the clearing with a sweet fruit-like smell while both steed and horseman screamed.<br /> <hr /><br /> As Jessica entered the Thorns by force and Nate managed to climb his way up to the higest bramble around, several figures poured into the place.<br /> <br /> There were half a dozen of them, all vaguely lupine-looking with long, sharp fangs and all too human eyes. They started to circle and hound the pair of scared goblins, ignoring for now the Ox and the Goat nearby. They finally prepared to pound on their prey frozen in place by sheer terror when an inhuman shriek pierced everyone's ears.<br /> <br /> The briarwolves left the goblins alone and continued to run once more towards the scream.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 08-16-2015, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T15:02:33-07:00","id":631599,"title":"","content":"Nate shivered at the scream, cringing in pain, but still, it was a stroke of luck. He felt guilty that he hadn't thought of saving the goblins as well, his instincts were so focused on saving his person... <i>Dammit, I said I wouldn't do it again...</i> Well, at least everybody was alright. He allowed himself to breath in relief, his fear slowly receiding. In fact, he was even amazed at his newfound balance : it seemed so natural and simple to him now, but he used to be so clumsy! <i>Hell, I would have been scared to be that high before...</i> Maybe the Goat wasn't so bad after all. <i>Thank god I wasn't born a rooster...</i> <br /> <br /> He looked around him : since he was in the canopy, he had a good viewpoint here. And if he couldn't really find the path ahead of them due to the lush and thick forest, he could make out some huge ruins in the distance, overgrown with vegetation. &quot;Hey guys,&quot; he called after he got down from the tree, &quot;sorry, I thought you were right behind me... Hum... I saw some ruins from up there, is that where we're heading?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T15:25:01-07:00","id":631653,"title":"","content":"-&quot;Ruins?&quot;- the two goblins asked in unison after recovering from the sudden scare<br /> <br /> -&quot;Like... chalk white stone covered in vegetation, about this tall?&quot;- Winterdime jumped on Summernickel and held his hands up as far as he could to represent a really tall structure.<br /> <br /> -&quot;If that's true *ugh*, that's good news *ugh*-Summernickel tried to say under the weight of his partner-&quot;It *ugh* means we didn't deviate *ugh* too much from the path&quot;- He looked angrily up at Winterdime-&quot;He already *ugh* understood the *ugh* size of the place!- he said dumping the other goblin to the ground.<br /> <br /> *Stomp!*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T09:41:41-07:00","id":632402,"title":"","content":"It took Jessica a bit of time to work out that no one had followed her into the thorns. This revelation was closed followed by seeing that the thorns had actually closed up behind her. Jessica called out, but had the horrible feeling that the thorny plant life all around her was consuming any noise that she might create. Fighting a growing dread, Jessica struggled to crawl fee from he thorns that she might. She just hoped that she was going in the right directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-20T15:26:46-07:00","id":633846,"title":"","content":"&quot;Not sure if it was chalk white, since it was kinda far, but yeah, I guess it's the same ruins. Are we heading there?&quot; He stretched a bit, looking around. &quot;It did seem to be important... And by the way, where's Jessica? I swear she went in that bush...&quot; Indeed, Nate hadn't heard any of her calls, and the thorns were disturbingly silent : absolutely no rustling of leaves, no cracking branches, nothing.<br /> <br /> &quot;Jessica? You can come out now...&quot; he tried, hints of worry in his voice. Where was she? <i>I can't just leave her here... Even if we're closing on the ruins which could be the exit. </i>The idea of running through those thorns to find a cow wasn't really appealing, considering that he had the feeling that those thorns would try to lead them astray. <i>Stop. You said you wouldn't betray them. You promised, idiot.</i> Nate called her name again, anxiously shifting to one hoof to another. &quot;Hum... hey, guys? Do you know what's behing these thorns, or inside them?&quot; He asked the bumbling duo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T02:38:16-07:00","id":634383,"title":"","content":"Winterdime got up and cleaned the dust from his clothes.<br /> <br /> -&quot;I beliebe we told you this place was dangerous&quot;- he grunted.<br /> <br /> Summernickel gave him <i>a look </i>and aproached Nate.-&quot;Don't worry, we'll find her, she couldn't be that far away&quot;-he reasured the nervous goat-&quot;Even here there are rules and although time runs in strange ways I don't think she's been absent for more than we have noticed&quot;-he added patting Nate on the back.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Ok, bring the Sccissors, Winterdime!&quot;-the goblin ordered aproaching the thorns were Jessica had dissapeared-&quot;We have some trimming to do!&quot; <hr /><br /> The steed was convulsing on a syrupy pool of its own strange blood and The Hunter was next to it, trying to get up using the spear as a cane while holding his own wound with the other hand. The horn hanged by his side on a strap of leather and the howls that have answered the call, after a brief moment of silence, sounded closer and closer by the second.<br /> <br /> -&quot;Hahahahahaha&quot;-The Hunter laugh echoed from his cowl as he got up-&quot;Very, VERY, nice. That's more like it, <i>Max</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> As if his name was the sign, a dozen wolf-like figures entered the clearing positioning between Max and the Hunter.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:21:17-07:00","id":640876,"title":"","content":"<i>Scissors?!</i> This was ridiculous. Sure, it was believable for goblins to use that sort of cartoony stuff, but it didn't make sen... <i>Hold on... It does actually...</i> This realm, the whole plane, world or whatever seemed to have very strange rules, nothing was logical here but rather... fake. That was why the Ma--The Keeper was so... evil, why he had no redeeming qualities and couldn't be swayed by any remotely logical arguments or even emotional pleas... <i>Or maybe you're just a terrible liar.</i> Yeah, that was also a possibility, but it didn't lead anywhere. The Keeper was as wicked as a Disney villain, or a fairy tale monster : he was a dick to them just because he could. <i>That's how this whole place works, there are no explanations for anything here, it's almost random...No, that's not right. It works on symbolism, but nothing else.</i> Was this why the Keeper was so obsessed with having people to fulfill roles, like the Goat for instance? Because this... this is just a giant story. That's basically it...<br /> <br /> The snap of the cissors brought him back to 'reality' : maybe he was entertaining a foolish idea, but it seemed like a good insight. However, this didn't help in the slightest : what could he do now? He had been assigned with the Goat : sure, he could eat the thorns, but he didn't want to bleed profusely from the mouth. What else could he be of use? He didn't have a weapon, and was just an animal... Although... he had something else. Max showed them the way : sure, he hadn't listened to the spirit of the Pig and refused to pass a contract with it, but it seemed he had gained mastery over plants. <i>Damn, he even fits the story as the unlikely hero.</i> He had flipped the script, and broke the labyrinth's walls in the process, showing them that they could, in some way, improve their own role...<br /> <br /> <i>And i'm not gonna be the pathetic buffoon anymore.</i> If Max could do it, well so could he, dammit! Nate stomped his hooves on the ground, taking a solid stance, and raised his arms to the bushes. &quot;Hold on, I'm gonna try something.&quot; He had no idea if wizardry moves could help, but he was already covered with mud, plants, and half-goat, so who would ridicule him? How did max do it again? &quot;Hem... Spirits of the Wild,&quot; he calls out with his bleating voice, &quot;I... I ask you to uphold our pact and... er...&quot; <i>And what? WWMD, What Would Max Do?</i> &quot;...And provide us a path to Jessica, the Ox!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T18:58:14-07:00","id":640965,"title":"","content":"Still lost, Jessica heard no answers to her cries, and had fallen silent in despair. Not long after that, she stopped struggling against the thorns. She came to believe that she had reached the exact place where she was going to die. More than a part of her was glad it was almost over. Then she felt the thorns gently pulling away from her. Dazed, Jessica got to her feet, and started to walk along the new made path. She somehow knew which direction to go to meet Nate and the goblins. Walking soon turned to running.<br /> <br /> Before long, she was again with Nate and the two goblins. She noticed the scissors, but them little attention. It was Nate that was the focus of most of her attention. Somehow she knew he had saved her from the thorns. &quot;Thank you,&quot; she said, before surprising the goat with a kiss.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T11:54:33-07:00","id":641916,"title":"","content":"Nate's mind was currently busy with three thoughts : <i>&quot;It worked! It fucking worked! I'm awesome!&quot;, </i>then &quot;<i>Oh thank god she's okay</i>&quot;, and finally a very loud &quot;<i>WAIT WHAT IS SHE DOING</i>&quot;. The old him would have immediately enjoyed the attention and even reveled in it, but the Goat now was more confused than anything. And worse, he was starting to feel his lust rising, reminding him of his time at the pond and in the vinery. He gave into it for a quick moment, reaching a hand to Jessica's face (which, admittedly, was quite weird with her bovine features), before he abruptly stopped, breaking the kiss and gently pushing her away.<br /> <br /> &quot;Er... Glad you're okay,&quot; he said, clearing his throat and stepping away. &quot;Let's stick together next time, alright? I caught sight of some ruins nearby, that's where we're going,&quot; he added, eager to change the subject, at least for the moment. It wasn't that Jessica wasn't attractive (although with this ox body, she was certainly unusual), but he didn't want to fall prey to his basic instincts, fearing that they would drive him back to the M-- Keeper, or at least, not before finding a safe haven. Plus, he didn't feel very sexy covered in sweat and dried mud... &quot;So... shall we?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 08-27-2015, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T18:37:29-07:00","id":642313,"title":"","content":"Jessica blushed. &quot;Yes. I look forward to seeing this city.&quot;<br /> <br /> As she and Nate followed the two goblins, Jessica pondered why she had kissed Nate. Was it only that he had saved her, or was it something more? She shook her head, unsure. She had to get a better grasp on her emotions. She had no doubt that she would need her wits in the ruins ahead. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T18:25:04-07:00","id":644807,"title":"","content":"Glaring, Max snorted. He had hoped his sneak attack would completely debilitate Aries, at least disable a limb or two. Much as part of him took pride in (and another part felt sick at) the deep injury he'd dealt the Westerner, it would be of only so much use unless the fight dragged out. That was something the Boar preferred to avoid. Still, he couldn't be too disappointed: he could have been spitted, after all, and he'd cost Aries his mount. Max hadn't expected the fierce brambles -- though couldn't deny they felt right -- and regretted the beast's death. For all he knew, it had once been human as well. He put this from his thoughts: he needed to survive this. <i>They</i> were counting on him.<br /> <br /> As much as the hunter was going to be on his guard, the element of surprise might not be completely lost. Max hadn't allowed himself any time to plan something more precise, and still wasn't quite used to his new body -- much less to goring someone. He had practiced his martial arts as the Pig, so there was at least some familiarity with fighting in a porcine shape. But there was a vast difference between practice and combat, and, he found, between being a domestic hog and a wild one. It distantly struck him just how reckless it all was. Even so, now with a better chance to get the hang of his form, it seemed he'd come out ahead.<br /> <br /> Well. Except for the pack. Max sniffed the air, taking their measure -- tinted by Aries's blood all over his snout. He found their eyes unsettling. He willed himself to stand firm, despite how much he wanted to bolt. This was a <i>hunting</i> pack, after all, and letting them harry their prey just as they'd been bred and trained seemed unwise. Not that this occurred to Max at first, mind: the Boar's simmering fury at that affront was what kept him from running. Only then did he get a chance to size up the situation. And with those numbers, never mind Aries... running was starting to look wise. <i>'If the Wilds runs interference, maybe I can reach the end before they--' </i><br /> <br /> Max stopped suddenly. A thought struck him. And not just that he had no idea where &quot;the end&quot; was. He saw another way, and one more on his terms. Rising to two legs, he set his hooves and bellowed a warning cry to the beasts. And his commands to the Wilds. The first briarwolf that made a move forward was going to be removed from the fight by the land itself. Max would use the moment of surprise to fall on the closest one and likewise disable it. <i>Then</i> his plan would really get going.<br /> <br /> Not a mind in that clearing could doubt that he would soundly crush any of the briarwolves if they came at him singly -- they <i>needed</i> their pack tactics. So he was going to take those off the table: the Wilds would raise writhing, thorny barriers at his back and sides. They would move around the clearing as Max moved, and leave an opening <i>just</i> wide enough at his front. Their numbers meant much less when they could only attack one at a time. And of course the Wilds would keep whichever one stood before him off-balance, harrying it, and making disposal all the easier for him. If for some reason they showed reluctance to approach a cornered boar in a bottleneck, the Wilds were also welcome to nip and strike at them, unless they actually fled the field. Not very sporting, all told. But Aries could talk to Max about &quot;sporting&quot; when he ditched the wolves and spear.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Aries, the Easterner was going to do his damnedest to keep an eye on the Westerner at all times. That spear could put a big ugly hole in his plans -- and his hide. And that was <i>if</i> the horned hunter had no other tricks up his white-furred sleeves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Minor wording tweak. 08-29-2015, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T03:12:10-07:00","id":666666,"title":"","content":"The air was tense and charged, like filled with static electricity ready to arc at the merest change of pressure. Max the Boar and Aries the Hunter stared at each other from opposite sides of the clearing, measuring their rival, looking for a weakness or an opening to strike true.<br /> <br /> The briarwolves growled with impatience, muscles tensing like the cord of a bow, eager to pound and bite and shred. But not yet.<br /> <br /> Max's mind rushed, animal preservation instinct and human logic working in unison to prepare for the incoming fight. And then it started.<br /> <br /> One of the hound's bloodlust overcame its loyalty and darted towards the Boar like the proyectile of a ballista... but Max was ready. The Wilds answered his command and a thick wall of thorns sprout from the ground between him and his attacker. The strength of the hound proved its bane as it impaled itself on the wood's barbs.<br /> <br /> One less, thought Max. Five to go.<br /> <hr /><br /> -&quot;Should we give them some time alone?&quot;- Winterdime asked his partner.<br /> -&quot;Don't be ridiculous&quot;-he answered packing the sccisors back-&quot;We don't have time for this, everything is already in motion&quot;<br /> <br /> Without waiting for anyone to react, Summernickel started to advance towards the ruins. Winterdime shrugged and smiled to the two beasts before following the other goblin. Nate and Jessica quickly rushed behind the pair, trying to concentrate on finding a safe path to ignore the sudden akwardness of the situation. Fortunately, the path and the thorns provided plenty of distraction even if you weren't actively looking for it.<br /> <br /> The vegetation seemed to change every now and then. Sometimes vibrant and verdant. Others dry and arid, but always thick, though and sharp as knives. The Sccissors proved neccessary more than once to open even the slightest hole in the packed hedge. But finally, they reached the ruins.<br /> <br /> The first thing that caught their attention was the size. It was gargantuan, way bigger than Nate had anticipated. He wondered if he had misscalculated the distance that they have traversed and that if his original assesment of the ruins size was a trick of proportions.<br /> The ruins were basically a round plaza, the whole floor a single disk of stone, polished but matt. Distributed all along its circumference were several tall arcs of the same polished stone and encased in each one a metal-rimmeed mirror. There were thirteen of them in total.<br /> <br /> The mirrors were weird, looking more like vertical ponds of quicksilver than cristal. Nate, curious, dared to touch one with his finger and was shocked when it efectively created ripples on its surface. He steped back and realized his finger felt numb and impossibly cold, but the sensation faded before he could panick at the idea of loosing it to frostbite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T08:28:08-07:00","id":671990,"title":"","content":"If Nate had been well-rested, he would have been wary of Summernickel's last comment. But the prospect of reaching a new and possibly safer place was his first and foremost concern, especially since it could possibly be the exit they had desired for so long.<br /> <br /> Shaking his hand to get rid of the numbness, he stepped back, awed at the majesty of the place. Their hooves had made quite the noise when they walked in, as the ruins were otherwise eeringly silent. Looking back at the mirror, Nate noticed that it didn't seem to reflect his person very well, the image was blurry. A glimmer caught his eye, and he looked up on the arc, to a small emblem embedded in a little disk of black obsidian the size of a grapefruit. It seemed to be the symbol of a snake, which wasn't especially helpful, Nate thought. It could easily look like a dragon as well, and a very obscure part of his mind reminded him that the Western Zodiac had thirteen signs, including the Ophidian.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are we still in the Keeper's realm?&quot; The Goat wondered out loud, &quot;it looks so different...&quot; He slowly started to walk around the ruins, looking for a portal with a goat symbol on it. Maybe it would be his, maybe it would be Aries'... But he wanted to find it. He was drawn to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":2016,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","user":"Evilmarmelade","date":". 10-08-2015, 03:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T10:51:29-07:00","id":672210,"title":"","content":"The Boar didn't hesitate. Just as planned, once the first beast brought about its own end, Max blazed a trail at the closest briarwolf in the confusion. Goring it, stomping it, hurling it at the wall of thorns... His human side hesitated at the brutality, but instinct guided him with a fearsome squeal. The creature scarcely got to react; drunk on adrenaline, Max wasn't sure if it even managed to attack him. He couldn't feel it, anyway<br /> <br /> The bristly Easterner then turned and ran off on all-fours, exposing his back as he made a large circle. The pack would surely pursue; even if their instincts and training weren't to dart after prey that ran, the Wilds lashing at their heels would do the trick. Max's ears stayed pricked and alert as he ran. Snarls, pawsteps, hoofsteps, even the telltale whistle of a spear in flight... All kept the Boar abreast of every actor on the field, informing his own moves. After the first one, he didn't expect any to leap at him, but the Wilds were ready to spring up for a repeat impalement if the wolves did -- and he deliberately picked a slower lope of a run to tempt them.<br /> <br /> If allowed his circuit, Max made sure to note where Aries was, and took the measure of the wolves around him. He threw himself at the least wary of them if removed enough from its fellows, hoping to remove it from the hunt. If at any point they surrounded him, wherever he was, he tried to whirl and get Aries in line of sight. Either way, when the time was right, he went with his plan. The Boar called on the Wilds to guard his back and sides, forcing the beasts to attack from his front -- and hopefully slashing at them if they'd tried to nip at his heels. The thorns lashed them forward and as the challenging bellows called to them. <i>'Come on! Come at me!'</i> Human swept up with the animal in the rush of battle, the Boar that was Max thought only of inflicting every injury he could on the fools that came at him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T21:58:04-07:00","id":693485,"title":"","content":"Jessica watched Nate study the mirror. &quot;Be careful,&quot; she warned. &quot;We have no idea what that thing might do.&quot;<br /> <br /> After making this warning, Jessica looked around, surveying the city. She wondered how long it been abandoned. She wondered why it had been abandoned. Yet, oddly, she felt as much wonder as dread. Was this place built by people, or something other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/790-cire","name":"Cire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T14:14:52-07:00","id":892768,"title":"","content":"(Rest In Peace, Zodiac Beasts... *puts flowers by the grave*)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}